const DENEME_YDT_INGILIZCE_OZEL_5 = {"1": [{"id": "ydtozg5-rc-detail-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (DETAIL/RESULT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Some coral colonies exposed to brief episodes of unusually warm water later prove more resistant when a larger heatwave arrives, a phenomenon researchers call coral 'thermal memory'. Corals host microscopic algae that supply them with energy through photosynthesis; when water temperatures rise even slightly, this partnership can break down, causing the coral to expel its algae and turn pale, a process known as bleaching. Corals that have previously survived a mild warming event, however, appear to adjust their internal chemistry in ways that make them less likely to bleach again. Genetic studies suggest that certain stress-response genes remain switched on for weeks after a mild heat episode, effectively priming the coral for future stress. Reef location also matters: colonies living in naturally variable, shallow lagoons tend to develop stronger thermal memory than those in stable, deep water. This built-in resilience works like a rehearsal, allowing corals to ready their defences before the real crisis strikes. Understanding thermal memory has become central to conservation efforts aimed at helping reefs survive a warming ocean.\n\n29. According to the passage, what happens to corals that have previously experienced a mild warming event?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "They undergo internal changes that reduce future bleaching risk"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "They stop relying on photosynthesis for energy altogether"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "They lose the ability to host symbiotic algae permanently"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "They become more likely to bleach during subsequent heatwaves"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "They tend to migrate to deeper, more stable waters"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen bilgiye göre doğru seçenek 'They undergo internal changes that reduce future bleaching risk' ifadesidir. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-rc-ref-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (REFERENCE/ILLUSTRATION)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Some coral colonies exposed to brief episodes of unusually warm water later prove more resistant when a larger heatwave arrives, a phenomenon researchers call coral 'thermal memory'. Corals host microscopic algae that supply them with energy through photosynthesis; when water temperatures rise even slightly, this partnership can break down, causing the coral to expel its algae and turn pale, a process known as bleaching. Corals that have previously survived a mild warming event, however, appear to adjust their internal chemistry in ways that make them less likely to bleach again. Genetic studies suggest that certain stress-response genes remain switched on for weeks after a mild heat episode, effectively priming the coral for future stress. Reef location also matters: colonies living in naturally variable, shallow lagoons tend to develop stronger thermal memory than those in stable, deep water. This built-in resilience works like a rehearsal, allowing corals to ready their defences before the real crisis strikes. Understanding thermal memory has become central to conservation efforts aimed at helping reefs survive a warming ocean.\n\n30. The author's reference to 'a rehearsal' serves to illustrate ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "how prior mild stress can prepare corals for a larger future threat"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "why algae abandon corals during a heatwave"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "how conservation programs monitor reef temperatures"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "how corals in deep water avoid bleaching entirely"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "why bleaching events have become more frequent worldwide"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Yazarın 'a rehearsal' benzetmesi, parçadaki ilgili mekanizmayı somutlaştırmak için kullanılmıştır; doğru açıklama budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-rc-purpose-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (MAIN PURPOSE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Some coral colonies exposed to brief episodes of unusually warm water later prove more resistant when a larger heatwave arrives, a phenomenon researchers call coral 'thermal memory'. Corals host microscopic algae that supply them with energy through photosynthesis; when water temperatures rise even slightly, this partnership can break down, causing the coral to expel its algae and turn pale, a process known as bleaching. Corals that have previously survived a mild warming event, however, appear to adjust their internal chemistry in ways that make them less likely to bleach again. Genetic studies suggest that certain stress-response genes remain switched on for weeks after a mild heat episode, effectively priming the coral for future stress. Reef location also matters: colonies living in naturally variable, shallow lagoons tend to develop stronger thermal memory than those in stable, deep water. This built-in resilience works like a rehearsal, allowing corals to ready their defences before the real crisis strikes. Understanding thermal memory has become central to conservation efforts aimed at helping reefs survive a warming ocean.\n\n31. The main purpose of this passage is to ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "explain how prior mild heat exposure can improve corals' resistance to future bleaching"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "describe the process by which algae photosynthesize inside coral tissue"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "criticize conservation efforts for focusing on the wrong reef locations"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "argue that coral reefs cannot be saved from climate change"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "compare the resilience of shallow-water and deep-water ecosystems"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçanın geneli, belirtilen olguyu açıklamaya odaklanmaktadır; bu nedenle doğru seçenek parçanın ana amacını en iyi yansıtan ifadedir. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc25-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (SUBORDINATE CLAUSE - MIXED CONNECTORS)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "----, the small bakery still attracts customers from across the city every morning.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Despite having no advertising budget whatsoever"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "As it opened its doors only two years ago"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "While its owner trained originally as an accountant"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Even though it closes early on weekends"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Since it uses locally sourced ingredients in every recipe"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "'Despite having no advertising budget' ile 'yine de müşteri çekmesi' arasında gerçek bir zıtlık kurulduğundan A doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc26-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (REASON CLAUSE - BLANK AT END)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Many people focus on correcting others' mistakes; however, examining one's own errors first is far more valuable ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "since genuine improvement begins with self-awareness"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "when colleagues are unwilling to accept criticism"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "because most errors are ultimately harmless"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "even though self-reflection can be uncomfortable"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "if it is done publicly to set an example"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "'since genuine improvement begins with self-awareness' cümlenin ana fikrini destekleyen doğrudan gerekçeyi verdiğinden B doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc27-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (VARIED CONNECTOR - BLANK AT END)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The Roman road network extended over 400,000 kilometres at its peak, ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "even if many sections have since been buried beneath modern cities"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "for it allowed troops and goods to move rapidly across the empire"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "yet some stretches remain visible and usable in parts of Europe today"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "as it connected distant provinces to the capital"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "whereas railway networks would not appear for another two thousand years"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "'even if' bir gerçeğe rağmen geçerliliğini koruyan bir durumu ifade ettiğinden A doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc28-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (CONDITION/TIME CLAUSE - BLANK AT START)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "----, many cities have begun redesigning public spaces to prioritise pedestrians over vehicles.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "As long as car ownership continues to rise in urban areas"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Given that traffic congestion has worsened significantly in recent decades"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Whether residents support the change or not"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Though many drivers oppose reduced parking availability"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Until public transportation becomes affordable for everyone"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "'Given that' şehirlerin gerçek bir gerekçeye dayanarak harekete geçtiğini ifade ettiğinden B doğru tamamlamadır."}], "2": [{"id": "ydtozg5-rc-detail-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (DETAIL/RESULT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Each autumn, monarch butterflies in North America travel thousands of kilometres to a handful of mountain forests in central Mexico, even though no single butterfly has ever made the journey before. The migrating generation is typically the great-great-grandchild of the monarchs that flew south the previous year, meaning the route must somehow be inherited rather than learned. Scientists have found that monarchs rely on a time-compensated sun compass, adjusting their flight direction according to the sun's position and the time of day, which is tracked by an internal circadian clock housed in their antennae. When researchers disabled this clock experimentally, the butterflies still flew, but in the wrong direction, as though their compass had lost its calibration. Genetic factors appear to encode the general direction and distance of the journey, functioning much like a passed-down map that each new generation consults without ever having seen the destination. This combination of an inherited sense of direction and a finely tuned internal clock allows monarchs to complete one of the most remarkable migrations in the animal kingdom.\n\n29. According to the passage, why is the monarch migration considered unusual?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The butterflies travel only short distances within a single generation"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The migrating generation has never previously made the journey itself"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "The butterflies rely entirely on visual landmarks to navigate"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "The migration route changes completely from one year to the next"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The butterflies migrate without using any internal biological clock"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen bilgiye göre doğru seçenek 'The migrating generation has never previously made the journey itself' ifadesidir. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-rc-ref-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (REFERENCE/ILLUSTRATION)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Each autumn, monarch butterflies in North America travel thousands of kilometres to a handful of mountain forests in central Mexico, even though no single butterfly has ever made the journey before. The migrating generation is typically the great-great-grandchild of the monarchs that flew south the previous year, meaning the route must somehow be inherited rather than learned. Scientists have found that monarchs rely on a time-compensated sun compass, adjusting their flight direction according to the sun's position and the time of day, which is tracked by an internal circadian clock housed in their antennae. When researchers disabled this clock experimentally, the butterflies still flew, but in the wrong direction, as though their compass had lost its calibration. Genetic factors appear to encode the general direction and distance of the journey, functioning much like a passed-down map that each new generation consults without ever having seen the destination. This combination of an inherited sense of direction and a finely tuned internal clock allows monarchs to complete one of the most remarkable migrations in the animal kingdom.\n\n30. The author's reference to 'a passed-down map' serves to illustrate ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "how monarchs learn their migration route by observing older butterflies"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "how genetic information can convey a route never personally experienced"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "why monarchs sometimes migrate in the wrong direction"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "how the sun compass is calibrated during flight"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "why migration distances vary between different butterfly populations"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Yazarın 'a passed-down map' benzetmesi, parçadaki ilgili mekanizmayı somutlaştırmak için kullanılmıştır; doğru açıklama budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-rc-purpose-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (MAIN PURPOSE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Each autumn, monarch butterflies in North America travel thousands of kilometres to a handful of mountain forests in central Mexico, even though no single butterfly has ever made the journey before. The migrating generation is typically the great-great-grandchild of the monarchs that flew south the previous year, meaning the route must somehow be inherited rather than learned. Scientists have found that monarchs rely on a time-compensated sun compass, adjusting their flight direction according to the sun's position and the time of day, which is tracked by an internal circadian clock housed in their antennae. When researchers disabled this clock experimentally, the butterflies still flew, but in the wrong direction, as though their compass had lost its calibration. Genetic factors appear to encode the general direction and distance of the journey, functioning much like a passed-down map that each new generation consults without ever having seen the destination. This combination of an inherited sense of direction and a finely tuned internal clock allows monarchs to complete one of the most remarkable migrations in the animal kingdom.\n\n31. The main purpose of this passage is to ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "criticize scientists for disabling the monarchs' internal clock"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "explain how monarch butterflies complete a multi-generational migration without prior experience"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "compare monarch migration to that of other insect species"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "argue that migration distances have increased in recent decades"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "describe the geography of the monarchs' wintering grounds in Mexico"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçanın geneli, belirtilen olguyu açıklamaya odaklanmaktadır; bu nedenle doğru seçenek parçanın ana amacını en iyi yansıtan ifadedir. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc25-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (SUBORDINATE CLAUSE - MIXED CONNECTORS)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "----, the small fishing village has managed to preserve most of its centuries-old traditions.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "As tourism has grown steadily over the past decade"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Despite growing pressure from modern development nearby"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "While its harbour was rebuilt after a storm"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Since the village council meets twice a year"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Even though the population has remained stable"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "'Despite growing pressure' ile 'geleneklerin korunması' arasında gerçek bir zıtlık kurulduğundan B doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc26-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (REASON CLAUSE - BLANK AT END)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Companies often prioritise short-term profits; nevertheless, investing in long-term research is ultimately more rewarding ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "if competitors choose to do the same"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "when quarterly earnings reports are published"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "because it leads to innovations that sustain future growth"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "since most researchers prefer stable funding"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "even though shareholders may expect quicker returns"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "'because it leads to innovations that sustain future growth' doğrudan gerekçeyi verdiğinden C doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc27-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (VARIED CONNECTOR - BLANK AT END)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Early printing presses could produce only a few hundred pages per day, ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "even if the type had to be set by hand for every page"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "for they still transformed the spread of written knowledge across Europe"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "yet modern presses can print thousands of pages within minutes"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "as each press required a skilled operator to function"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "whereas handwritten manuscripts could take months to complete"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "'for' bir sonucun nedenini/gerekçesini sunduğundan B doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc28-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (CONDITION/TIME CLAUSE - BLANK AT START)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "----, several airlines have started offering fully refundable tickets on domestic routes.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "As long as fuel prices remain stable throughout the year"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Whether passengers request it explicitly or not"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Given that customer complaints about cancellations had risen sharply"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Though the change increases operational costs"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Until a new pricing model is fully implemented"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "'Given that' havayollarının gerçek bir gerekçeye dayanarak harekete geçtiğini ifade ettiğinden C doğru tamamlamadır."}], "3": [{"id": "ydtozg5-rc-detail-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (DETAIL/RESULT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "An octopus can transform the colour, pattern, and even texture of its skin within a fraction of a second, a feat made possible by thousands of tiny pigment-filled sacs called chromatophores embedded beneath its surface. Each chromatophore is surrounded by tiny muscles that, when contracted, stretch the sac and expose more pigment, and when relaxed, allow it to shrink out of view. Beneath these lie additional layers that reflect light and produce iridescent or metallic effects, adding further depth to the disguise. Remarkably, octopuses appear to achieve this without relying primarily on colour vision, since many species are thought to be colour-blind; instead, they may sense light patterns directly through photoreceptors in their skin. The entire system operates like a living projector screen, instantly displaying whatever pattern best conceals the animal against its surroundings. This extraordinary camouflage not only helps octopuses avoid predators but also allows them to ambush prey without being detected, making their skin one of the most sophisticated visual systems in the animal kingdom.\n\n29. According to the passage, what role do the tiny muscles around each chromatophore play?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "They regulate the octopus's body temperature during camouflage"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "They allow the octopus to sense light without using its eyes"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "They control how much pigment is exposed, changing the skin's appearance"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "They produce the iridescent, metallic effects seen in certain species"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "They help the octopus detect the colour vision of nearby predators"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen bilgiye göre doğru seçenek 'They control how much pigment is exposed, changing the skin's appearance' ifadesidir. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-rc-ref-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (REFERENCE/ILLUSTRATION)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "An octopus can transform the colour, pattern, and even texture of its skin within a fraction of a second, a feat made possible by thousands of tiny pigment-filled sacs called chromatophores embedded beneath its surface. Each chromatophore is surrounded by tiny muscles that, when contracted, stretch the sac and expose more pigment, and when relaxed, allow it to shrink out of view. Beneath these lie additional layers that reflect light and produce iridescent or metallic effects, adding further depth to the disguise. Remarkably, octopuses appear to achieve this without relying primarily on colour vision, since many species are thought to be colour-blind; instead, they may sense light patterns directly through photoreceptors in their skin. The entire system operates like a living projector screen, instantly displaying whatever pattern best conceals the animal against its surroundings. This extraordinary camouflage not only helps octopuses avoid predators but also allows them to ambush prey without being detected, making their skin one of the most sophisticated visual systems in the animal kingdom.\n\n30. The author's reference to 'a living projector screen' serves to illustrate ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "how slowly octopus skin changes compared to other camouflage animals"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "why octopuses are unable to see colour"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "how instantly and vividly the skin can display a concealing pattern"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "why chromatophores are located beneath the iridescent layers"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "how predators are able to detect octopuses despite their camouflage"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Yazarın 'a living projector screen' benzetmesi, parçadaki ilgili mekanizmayı somutlaştırmak için kullanılmıştır; doğru açıklama budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-rc-purpose-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (MAIN PURPOSE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "An octopus can transform the colour, pattern, and even texture of its skin within a fraction of a second, a feat made possible by thousands of tiny pigment-filled sacs called chromatophores embedded beneath its surface. Each chromatophore is surrounded by tiny muscles that, when contracted, stretch the sac and expose more pigment, and when relaxed, allow it to shrink out of view. Beneath these lie additional layers that reflect light and produce iridescent or metallic effects, adding further depth to the disguise. Remarkably, octopuses appear to achieve this without relying primarily on colour vision, since many species are thought to be colour-blind; instead, they may sense light patterns directly through photoreceptors in their skin. The entire system operates like a living projector screen, instantly displaying whatever pattern best conceals the animal against its surroundings. This extraordinary camouflage not only helps octopuses avoid predators but also allows them to ambush prey without being detected, making their skin one of the most sophisticated visual systems in the animal kingdom.\n\n31. The main purpose of this passage is to ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "criticize research that assumes octopuses are colour-blind"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "argue that octopus camouflage is less effective than previously believed"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "explain the biological mechanism behind the octopus's rapid skin camouflage"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "compare chromatophores in octopuses with similar structures in squid"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "describe how predators overcome the octopus's camouflage abilities"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçanın geneli, belirtilen olguyu açıklamaya odaklanmaktadır; bu nedenle doğru seçenek parçanın ana amacını en iyi yansıtan ifadedir. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc25-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (SUBORDINATE CLAUSE - MIXED CONNECTORS)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "----, researchers were finally able to determine the true cause of the coral die-off.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "As the reef had been studied for over a decade"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Despite limited funding for the initial survey"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "After analysing samples collected from twelve separate sites"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Even though the equipment was outdated"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Since public interest in the reef had declined"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "'After analysing samples...' bir eylemin sonucunu doğrudan açıkladığından C doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc26-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (REASON CLAUSE - BLANK AT END)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Some drivers rely heavily on speed to save time; yet obeying traffic signals consistently proves far safer ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "if traffic police are visibly present"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "when roads are recently repaved"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "since most accidents result from congestion rather than speed"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "because it significantly reduces the risk of collisions"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "even though it may lengthen the total travel time"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "'because it significantly reduces the risk of collisions' doğrudan gerekçeyi verdiğinden D doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc27-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (VARIED CONNECTOR - BLANK AT END)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The Great Barrier Reef stretches across roughly 2,300 kilometres, ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "even if satellite mapping has only recently confirmed its full extent"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "for it hosts an extraordinary diversity of marine species"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "yet it remains visible from space as a distinct feature of the coastline"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "as it was formed over millions of years"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "whereas smaller reefs nearby have suffered greater damage"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "'yet' beklenmedik ama doğrulanan bir gerçeği (uzaydan görünürlük) sunduğundan C doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc28-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (CONDITION/TIME CLAUSE - BLANK AT START)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "----, hospitals across the country have adopted electronic record-keeping systems.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Given that paper records had repeatedly led to costly errors"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "As long as internet connectivity remains reliable"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Until every hospital receives equal government funding"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Whether doctors are comfortable with new technology or not"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Though the transition required significant staff retraining"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "'Given that' hastanelerin gerçek bir gerekçeye dayanarak harekete geçtiğini ifade ettiğinden C doğru tamamlamadır."}], "4": [{"id": "ydtozg5-rc-detail-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (DETAIL/RESULT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Desert ants living in the featureless salt pans of North Africa face a daily challenge: after wandering far from their nest in search of food, often along a winding, indirect path, they must find their way straight back to a nest entrance no wider than a few millimetres, all without landmarks to guide them. Researchers discovered that these ants solve the problem through a process called path integration, continuously calculating their position relative to the nest by combining information about the direction they have travelled, tracked using polarised light patterns in the sky, with an internal estimate of distance covered, based on the number of steps taken. This constant recalculation functions much like an onboard odometer that updates itself with every stride, allowing the ant to compute a direct route home regardless of how convoluted its outward journey was. When scientists altered the ants' leg length, artificially lengthening their strides, the ants overshot the nest by a predictable distance, confirming that step counting plays a central role in this remarkable navigational system.\n\n29. According to the passage, what happened when researchers artificially lengthened the ants' legs?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The ants abandoned path integration in favour of landmarks"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The ants became unable to detect polarised light in the sky"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "The ants stopped foraging away from the nest entirely"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "The ants overshot the nest by a predictable distance"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The ants returned to the nest earlier than usual"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen bilgiye göre doğru seçenek 'The ants overshot the nest by a predictable distance' ifadesidir. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-rc-ref-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (REFERENCE/ILLUSTRATION)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Desert ants living in the featureless salt pans of North Africa face a daily challenge: after wandering far from their nest in search of food, often along a winding, indirect path, they must find their way straight back to a nest entrance no wider than a few millimetres, all without landmarks to guide them. Researchers discovered that these ants solve the problem through a process called path integration, continuously calculating their position relative to the nest by combining information about the direction they have travelled, tracked using polarised light patterns in the sky, with an internal estimate of distance covered, based on the number of steps taken. This constant recalculation functions much like an onboard odometer that updates itself with every stride, allowing the ant to compute a direct route home regardless of how convoluted its outward journey was. When scientists altered the ants' leg length, artificially lengthening their strides, the ants overshot the nest by a predictable distance, confirming that step counting plays a central role in this remarkable navigational system.\n\n30. The author's reference to 'an onboard odometer' serves to illustrate ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "how polarised light differs from ordinary sunlight"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "why ants with longer legs forage more efficiently"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "how ants use landmarks to find their way back to the nest"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "how the ants' continuous step-counting allows them to track distance travelled"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "why desert ants prefer flat, featureless terrain"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Yazarın 'an onboard odometer' benzetmesi, parçadaki ilgili mekanizmayı somutlaştırmak için kullanılmıştır; doğru açıklama budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-rc-purpose-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (MAIN PURPOSE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Desert ants living in the featureless salt pans of North Africa face a daily challenge: after wandering far from their nest in search of food, often along a winding, indirect path, they must find their way straight back to a nest entrance no wider than a few millimetres, all without landmarks to guide them. Researchers discovered that these ants solve the problem through a process called path integration, continuously calculating their position relative to the nest by combining information about the direction they have travelled, tracked using polarised light patterns in the sky, with an internal estimate of distance covered, based on the number of steps taken. This constant recalculation functions much like an onboard odometer that updates itself with every stride, allowing the ant to compute a direct route home regardless of how convoluted its outward journey was. When scientists altered the ants' leg length, artificially lengthening their strides, the ants overshot the nest by a predictable distance, confirming that step counting plays a central role in this remarkable navigational system.\n\n31. The main purpose of this passage is to ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "describe the physical characteristics of North African salt pans"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "compare the leg length of different ant species"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "criticize the experimental methods used to study ant navigation"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "explain how desert ants use path integration to navigate without landmarks"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "argue that desert ants are less efficient navigators than other insects"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçanın geneli, belirtilen olguyu açıklamaya odaklanmaktadır; bu nedenle doğru seçenek parçanın ana amacını en iyi yansıtan ifadedir. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc25-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (SUBORDINATE CLAUSE - MIXED CONNECTORS)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "----, the museum's rarest manuscript remained legible after nearly eight centuries.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "As it was displayed under bright lighting for years"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Despite its exposure to humidity during transport"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "While scholars debated its exact origin"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Because it was stored in a climate-controlled vault"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Since visitors were allowed to touch its pages"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "'Because it was stored in a climate-controlled vault' okunabilirliğin nedenini doğrudan açıkladığından D doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc26-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (REASON CLAUSE - BLANK AT END)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "People often assume that working longer hours guarantees success; in fact, working with clear priorities is far more effective ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "even though it requires more discipline to plan tasks carefully"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "if employees are properly compensated"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "when deadlines are extended"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "since long hours are common across most industries"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "because managers rarely question overtime requests"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "'even though it requires more discipline to plan tasks carefully' önceliklendirmenin bedelini kabul ederek yine de daha etkili olduğunu vurguladığından E doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc27-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (VARIED CONNECTOR - BLANK AT END)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The printing of the first encyclopaedia required contributions from hundreds of scholars, ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "even if many of them never met one another in person"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "for it aimed to gather all human knowledge into a single collection"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "yet later editions were compiled by far smaller teams"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "as it spread new ideas across the whole of Europe"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "whereas modern encyclopaedias are compiled almost entirely online"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "'as' bir sonucu/amacı doğrudan açıkladığından D doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc28-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (CONDITION/TIME CLAUSE - BLANK AT START)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "----, several universities have introduced mandatory courses on digital literacy.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "As long as enrollment numbers continue to grow"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Whether students find the courses engaging or not"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Though some faculty members questioned their necessity"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Given that many graduates struggled with basic online research skills"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Until a standardised national curriculum is agreed upon"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "'Given that' üniversitelerin gerçek bir gerekçeye dayanarak harekete geçtiğini ifade ettiğinden D doğru tamamlamadır."}], "5": [{"id": "ydtozg5-rc-detail-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (DETAIL/RESULT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "When beavers fell trees and pile branches across a stream, they are not merely building a home; they are reshaping the entire landscape around them. The resulting dam slows the water's flow, causing it to spread outward and form a pond that floods the surrounding land. This flooding kills some trees but creates open wetland habitat that supports an entirely different community of plants, insects, amphibians, and birds than existed before. Sediment and organic material that would otherwise wash downstream instead settle in the pond, gradually enriching the soil and raising the water table across a wide area. Because a single dam can influence conditions for dozens of other species, ecologists describe the beaver as a kind of unpaid landscape architect, redesigning entire watersheds through the simple act of gathering wood. When beaver populations decline in a region, wetlands frequently dry up and biodiversity drops accordingly, underscoring just how dependent many ecosystems have become on this single species' engineering behaviour.\n\n29. According to the passage, what happens to sediment and organic material when a beaver dam is built?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "It is consumed directly by the beavers as food"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "It prevents new plant species from establishing in the area"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "It causes the water table in the region to drop"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "It washes downstream more quickly than before"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "It settles in the pond, enriching the surrounding soil"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen bilgiye göre doğru seçenek 'It settles in the pond, enriching the surrounding soil' ifadesidir. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-rc-ref-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (REFERENCE/ILLUSTRATION)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "When beavers fell trees and pile branches across a stream, they are not merely building a home; they are reshaping the entire landscape around them. The resulting dam slows the water's flow, causing it to spread outward and form a pond that floods the surrounding land. This flooding kills some trees but creates open wetland habitat that supports an entirely different community of plants, insects, amphibians, and birds than existed before. Sediment and organic material that would otherwise wash downstream instead settle in the pond, gradually enriching the soil and raising the water table across a wide area. Because a single dam can influence conditions for dozens of other species, ecologists describe the beaver as a kind of unpaid landscape architect, redesigning entire watersheds through the simple act of gathering wood. When beaver populations decline in a region, wetlands frequently dry up and biodiversity drops accordingly, underscoring just how dependent many ecosystems have become on this single species' engineering behaviour.\n\n30. The author's reference to 'an unpaid landscape architect' serves to illustrate ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "why wetlands support fewer species than dry forests"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "how sediment builds up naturally without animal activity"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "how beavers are hunted for their engineering skills"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "why beaver populations have declined in many regions"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "how a single species' behaviour can reshape an entire ecosystem"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Yazarın 'an unpaid landscape architect' benzetmesi, parçadaki ilgili mekanizmayı somutlaştırmak için kullanılmıştır; doğru açıklama budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-rc-purpose-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (MAIN PURPOSE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "When beavers fell trees and pile branches across a stream, they are not merely building a home; they are reshaping the entire landscape around them. The resulting dam slows the water's flow, causing it to spread outward and form a pond that floods the surrounding land. This flooding kills some trees but creates open wetland habitat that supports an entirely different community of plants, insects, amphibians, and birds than existed before. Sediment and organic material that would otherwise wash downstream instead settle in the pond, gradually enriching the soil and raising the water table across a wide area. Because a single dam can influence conditions for dozens of other species, ecologists describe the beaver as a kind of unpaid landscape architect, redesigning entire watersheds through the simple act of gathering wood. When beaver populations decline in a region, wetlands frequently dry up and biodiversity drops accordingly, underscoring just how dependent many ecosystems have become on this single species' engineering behaviour.\n\n31. The main purpose of this passage is to ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "compare beaver dams with man-made flood control structures"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "describe the physical process by which beavers construct dams"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "argue that wetland ecosystems can survive without beavers"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "criticize beavers for destroying trees and natural habitats"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "explain how beaver dam-building reshapes ecosystems and supports biodiversity"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçanın geneli, belirtilen olguyu açıklamaya odaklanmaktadır; bu nedenle doğru seçenek parçanın ana amacını en iyi yansıtan ifadedir. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc25-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (SUBORDINATE CLAUSE - MIXED CONNECTORS)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "----, the region's beekeepers reported one of their most successful harvests in years.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Although a late frost damaged early blossoms"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "As several new farms were established nearby"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "While honey prices remained relatively low"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Even though fewer bees were kept than before"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Since the summer brought unusually favourable weather"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "'Since the summer brought unusually favourable weather' başarılı hasadın nedenini doğrudan açıkladığından E doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc26-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (REASON CLAUSE - BLANK AT END)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Many assume that expensive equipment guarantees better results; however, skilled technique matters far more in most fields ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "if the equipment is regularly maintained"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "because mastery allows even basic tools to produce excellent outcomes"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "when budgets are limited for new purchases"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "since manufacturers frequently release updated models"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "even though professionals often prefer premium brands"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "'because mastery allows even basic tools to produce excellent outcomes' doğrudan gerekçeyi verdiğinden B doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc27-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (VARIED CONNECTOR - BLANK AT END)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The construction of the Panama Canal took over a decade to complete, ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "even if disease and difficult terrain slowed progress considerably"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "for it dramatically shortened the sea route between two oceans"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "yet it remains one of the most heavily used waterways in the world"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "as thousands of workers were required at its peak"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "whereas the Suez Canal had been completed decades earlier"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "'whereas' iki inşaat projesi arasındaki zamansal karşılaştırmayı ifade ettiğinden E doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc28-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (CONDITION/TIME CLAUSE - BLANK AT START)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "----, wildlife authorities have restricted access to several previously popular hiking trails.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "As long as funding for park maintenance remains available"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Whether hikers agree with the decision or not"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Though local businesses rely heavily on tourist traffic"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Until alternative trails are constructed nearby"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Given that increased foot traffic had begun damaging fragile plant life"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "'Given that' yetkililerin gerçek bir gerekçeye dayanarak harekete geçtiğini ifade ettiğinden E doğru tamamlamadır."}], "6": [{"id": "ydtozg5-rc-detail-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (DETAIL/RESULT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Beneath a forest floor lies a vast web of thread-like fungal filaments, known as mycelium, that connect the roots of different trees, sometimes across considerable distances and even between different species. Through this network, trees can exchange not only water and nutrients such as nitrogen and phosphorus but also chemical signals that appear to warn neighbouring trees of insect attacks or drought stress. Older, well-established trees, sometimes called hub trees, tend to be connected to an especially large number of smaller seedlings, funnelling extra carbon to young trees struggling to receive enough sunlight beneath a dense canopy. Because of the sheer scale and interconnectedness of this system, researchers have nicknamed it the 'wood wide web', drawing a deliberate comparison to the internet's ability to link countless distant points into a single communicating system. While the fungi benefit from sugars produced by the trees through photosynthesis, the arrangement is now understood to be far more cooperative and complex than a simple one-way exchange.\n\n29. According to the passage, what role do 'hub trees' play in the fungal network?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "They funnel extra carbon to smaller seedlings struggling for sunlight"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "They absorb nitrogen and phosphorus exclusively for their own use"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "They warn fungi of insect attacks occurring elsewhere in the forest"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "They compete with seedlings for space within the fungal network"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "They prevent fungal filaments from connecting different tree species"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen bilgiye göre doğru seçenek 'They funnel extra carbon to smaller seedlings struggling for sunlight' ifadesidir. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-rc-ref-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (REFERENCE/ILLUSTRATION)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Beneath a forest floor lies a vast web of thread-like fungal filaments, known as mycelium, that connect the roots of different trees, sometimes across considerable distances and even between different species. Through this network, trees can exchange not only water and nutrients such as nitrogen and phosphorus but also chemical signals that appear to warn neighbouring trees of insect attacks or drought stress. Older, well-established trees, sometimes called hub trees, tend to be connected to an especially large number of smaller seedlings, funnelling extra carbon to young trees struggling to receive enough sunlight beneath a dense canopy. Because of the sheer scale and interconnectedness of this system, researchers have nicknamed it the 'wood wide web', drawing a deliberate comparison to the internet's ability to link countless distant points into a single communicating system. While the fungi benefit from sugars produced by the trees through photosynthesis, the arrangement is now understood to be far more cooperative and complex than a simple one-way exchange.\n\n30. The author's reference to 'the wood wide web' serves to illustrate ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "the scale and interconnectedness of the underground fungal network"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "why hub trees receive less sunlight than seedlings"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "how the internet has changed forest research methods"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "why some tree species cannot connect to the fungal network"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "how fungi compete with trees for nutrients"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Yazarın 'the 'wood wide web'' benzetmesi, parçadaki ilgili mekanizmayı somutlaştırmak için kullanılmıştır; doğru açıklama budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-rc-purpose-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (MAIN PURPOSE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Beneath a forest floor lies a vast web of thread-like fungal filaments, known as mycelium, that connect the roots of different trees, sometimes across considerable distances and even between different species. Through this network, trees can exchange not only water and nutrients such as nitrogen and phosphorus but also chemical signals that appear to warn neighbouring trees of insect attacks or drought stress. Older, well-established trees, sometimes called hub trees, tend to be connected to an especially large number of smaller seedlings, funnelling extra carbon to young trees struggling to receive enough sunlight beneath a dense canopy. Because of the sheer scale and interconnectedness of this system, researchers have nicknamed it the 'wood wide web', drawing a deliberate comparison to the internet's ability to link countless distant points into a single communicating system. While the fungi benefit from sugars produced by the trees through photosynthesis, the arrangement is now understood to be far more cooperative and complex than a simple one-way exchange.\n\n31. The main purpose of this passage is to ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "explain how an underground fungal network allows trees to exchange resources and signals"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "compare fungal networks in forests with those in grasslands"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "describe how hub trees are identified by researchers"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "criticize the term 'wood wide web' as a misleading comparison"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "argue that fungi ultimately harm the trees they connect to"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçanın geneli, belirtilen olguyu açıklamaya odaklanmaktadır; bu nedenle doğru seçenek parçanın ana amacını en iyi yansıtan ifadedir. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc25-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (SUBORDINATE CLAUSE - MIXED CONNECTORS)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "----, the elderly violinist continued to perform in concert halls well into her nineties.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Despite suffering a serious injury to her hand"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "As she had studied music since early childhood"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "While younger musicians dominated the concert scene"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Even though she rarely rehearsed before a show"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Since her recordings had sold poorly for decades"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "'Despite suffering a serious injury' ile 'performans vermeye devam etmesi' arasında gerçek bir zıtlık kurulduğundan A doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc26-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (REASON CLAUSE - BLANK AT END)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "People tend to trust confident speakers more readily; nonetheless, well-researched arguments carry far greater weight in the long run ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "if the audience is already familiar with the topic"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "when speeches are delivered without preparation"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "since confidence can sometimes mask a lack of knowledge"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "because accuracy ultimately withstands closer scrutiny"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "even though audiences rarely fact-check claims immediately"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "'because accuracy ultimately withstands closer scrutiny' doğrudan gerekçeyi verdiğinden D doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc27-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (VARIED CONNECTOR - BLANK AT END)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The first transatlantic telegraph cable functioned for only a few weeks before failing, ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "even if engineers had tested it extensively beforehand"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "for it proved that instant communication across oceans was possible"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "yet a more durable cable was successfully laid several years later"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "as its signal weakened rapidly across such a great distance"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "whereas telephone cables would later prove far more reliable"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "'even if' önceden yapılan testlere rağmen ortaya çıkan başarısızlığı ifade ettiğinden A doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc28-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (CONDITION/TIME CLAUSE - BLANK AT START)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "----, several manufacturers have begun labelling products with detailed environmental impact scores.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "As long as consumers continue to demand transparency"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Given that regulators had received growing pressure from environmental groups"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Whether the labels influence purchasing decisions or not"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Though the labelling process adds to production costs"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Until an international labelling standard is agreed upon"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "'As long as' üreticilerin devam eden bir koşula bağlı olarak hareket ettiğini ifade ettiğinden A doğru tamamlamadır."}], "7": [{"id": "ydtozg5-rc-detail-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (DETAIL/RESULT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Elephants are known for their loud trumpeting calls, but much of their communication actually travels in a form humans cannot hear at all: low-frequency vibrations that pass through the ground itself. When an elephant stamps its feet or produces a deep rumble, the resulting seismic waves can travel through soil for several kilometres, far beyond the range of the animal's airborne calls. Other elephants detect these signals through sensitive receptors in their feet and trunks, which pick up the faint tremors and relay them to the brain, allowing the animal to sense danger, locate distant herd members, or receive warnings about approaching predators. Researchers have compared this system to an underground telegraph, silently carrying urgent messages across distances where sound through the air would fade away entirely. Interestingly, elephants have been observed freezing in place and leaning forward on their front feet when detecting a distant seismic signal, a posture that appears to improve their ability to sense the vibrations more clearly.\n\n29. According to the passage, why do elephants sometimes freeze and lean forward on their front feet?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "To produce louder airborne trumpeting calls"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "To improve their ability to detect distant seismic vibrations"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "To warn nearby predators of their presence"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "To communicate with herd members through visual signals"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "To rest their legs after walking long distances"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen bilgiye göre doğru seçenek 'To improve their ability to detect distant seismic vibrations' ifadesidir. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-rc-ref-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (REFERENCE/ILLUSTRATION)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Elephants are known for their loud trumpeting calls, but much of their communication actually travels in a form humans cannot hear at all: low-frequency vibrations that pass through the ground itself. When an elephant stamps its feet or produces a deep rumble, the resulting seismic waves can travel through soil for several kilometres, far beyond the range of the animal's airborne calls. Other elephants detect these signals through sensitive receptors in their feet and trunks, which pick up the faint tremors and relay them to the brain, allowing the animal to sense danger, locate distant herd members, or receive warnings about approaching predators. Researchers have compared this system to an underground telegraph, silently carrying urgent messages across distances where sound through the air would fade away entirely. Interestingly, elephants have been observed freezing in place and leaning forward on their front feet when detecting a distant seismic signal, a posture that appears to improve their ability to sense the vibrations more clearly.\n\n30. The author's reference to 'an underground telegraph' serves to illustrate ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "how elephants use trumpeting calls to communicate over short distances"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "how seismic signals can silently carry information across long distances"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "why elephants have poor hearing compared to other animals"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "how researchers first discovered elephant communication"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "why predators avoid approaching elephant herds"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Yazarın 'an underground telegraph' benzetmesi, parçadaki ilgili mekanizmayı somutlaştırmak için kullanılmıştır; doğru açıklama budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-rc-purpose-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (MAIN PURPOSE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Elephants are known for their loud trumpeting calls, but much of their communication actually travels in a form humans cannot hear at all: low-frequency vibrations that pass through the ground itself. When an elephant stamps its feet or produces a deep rumble, the resulting seismic waves can travel through soil for several kilometres, far beyond the range of the animal's airborne calls. Other elephants detect these signals through sensitive receptors in their feet and trunks, which pick up the faint tremors and relay them to the brain, allowing the animal to sense danger, locate distant herd members, or receive warnings about approaching predators. Researchers have compared this system to an underground telegraph, silently carrying urgent messages across distances where sound through the air would fade away entirely. Interestingly, elephants have been observed freezing in place and leaning forward on their front feet when detecting a distant seismic signal, a posture that appears to improve their ability to sense the vibrations more clearly.\n\n31. The main purpose of this passage is to ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "compare elephant communication with that of other large mammals"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "explain how elephants use ground vibrations to communicate over long distances"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "argue that airborne trumpeting calls are more important than seismic signals"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "describe the anatomy of an elephant's foot in detail"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "criticize research methods used to study elephant behaviour"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçanın geneli, belirtilen olguyu açıklamaya odaklanmaktadır; bu nedenle doğru seçenek parçanın ana amacını en iyi yansıtan ifadedir. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc25-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (SUBORDINATE CLAUSE - MIXED CONNECTORS)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "----, the coastal town rebuilt its harbour within a single year.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "As the harbour had never been damaged before"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Despite losing nearly all of its fishing fleet in the storm"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "While neighbouring towns postponed their own repairs"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Since local fishermen preferred the old harbour design"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Even though funding arrived well ahead of schedule"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "'Despite losing nearly all of its fishing fleet' ile 'bir yılda yeniden inşa' arasında gerçek bir zıtlık kurulduğundan B doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc26-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (REASON CLAUSE - BLANK AT END)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Many gardeners water their plants daily out of habit; yet checking the soil's moisture first produces far healthier results ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "if the garden receives direct sunlight"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "when rainfall has been unusually heavy"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "since overwatering can damage roots just as much as drought"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "because most plants prefer a fixed watering schedule"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "even though it takes slightly more time each morning"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "'since overwatering can damage roots just as much as drought' doğrudan gerekçeyi verdiğinden C doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc27-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (VARIED CONNECTOR - BLANK AT END)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The ancient library of Alexandria is believed to have held hundreds of thousands of scrolls, ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "even if its exact size remains a matter of historical debate"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "for it attracted scholars from across the ancient world"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "yet almost nothing of its original collection survives today"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "as it was funded directly by the ruling dynasty"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "whereas smaller regional libraries were far less influential"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "'for' kütüphanenin etkisinin nedenini sunduğundan B doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc28-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (CONDITION/TIME CLAUSE - BLANK AT START)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "----, city planners have redesigned several intersections to reduce accidents involving cyclists.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "As long as cycling remains a popular mode of transport"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Whether cyclists follow traffic rules consistently or not"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Given that data had shown a sharp rise in cycling-related injuries"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Though the redesign required closing streets temporarily"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Until every intersection in the city has been reviewed"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "'Given that' şehir planlamacılarının gerçek bir gerekçeye dayanarak harekete geçtiğini ifade ettiğinden C doğru tamamlamadır."}], "8": [{"id": "ydtozg5-rc-detail-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (DETAIL/RESULT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "When a forager honeybee discovers a rich source of nectar, it returns to the hive and performs an intricate movement known as the waggle dance to share this discovery with its nestmates. The bee walks in a straight line while vigorously shaking its abdomen, then loops back to repeat the pattern, all within the darkness of the hive. The angle of the straight-line portion relative to vertical indicates the direction of the food source relative to the sun, while the duration of the waggling portion conveys the distance that must be travelled. Other bees follow closely behind the dancer, sensing the vibrations and orientation with remarkable precision before flying directly to the indicated location. Scientists have described the dance as a kind of living GPS coordinate, encoding both direction and distance in a form that other bees can decode purely through touch and movement in total darkness. This system allows a colony to rapidly direct large numbers of foragers to the most productive flower patches nearby.\n\n29. According to the passage, what does the duration of the waggling portion of the dance convey?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The overall size of the bee colony"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The exact species of flower that was discovered"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "The distance that must be travelled to reach the food source"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "The direction of the food source relative to the sun"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The number of other bees currently foraging nearby"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen bilgiye göre doğru seçenek 'The distance that must be travelled to reach the food source' ifadesidir. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-rc-ref-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (REFERENCE/ILLUSTRATION)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "When a forager honeybee discovers a rich source of nectar, it returns to the hive and performs an intricate movement known as the waggle dance to share this discovery with its nestmates. The bee walks in a straight line while vigorously shaking its abdomen, then loops back to repeat the pattern, all within the darkness of the hive. The angle of the straight-line portion relative to vertical indicates the direction of the food source relative to the sun, while the duration of the waggling portion conveys the distance that must be travelled. Other bees follow closely behind the dancer, sensing the vibrations and orientation with remarkable precision before flying directly to the indicated location. Scientists have described the dance as a kind of living GPS coordinate, encoding both direction and distance in a form that other bees can decode purely through touch and movement in total darkness. This system allows a colony to rapidly direct large numbers of foragers to the most productive flower patches nearby.\n\n30. The author's reference to 'a living GPS coordinate' serves to illustrate ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "why some bees fail to follow the dancer's movements"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "how bees rely on scent rather than movement to communicate"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "how the dance encodes both direction and distance for other bees to decode"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "why bees perform the dance only during daylight hours"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "how the dance differs between bee species"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Yazarın 'a living GPS coordinate' benzetmesi, parçadaki ilgili mekanizmayı somutlaştırmak için kullanılmıştır; doğru açıklama budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-rc-purpose-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (MAIN PURPOSE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "When a forager honeybee discovers a rich source of nectar, it returns to the hive and performs an intricate movement known as the waggle dance to share this discovery with its nestmates. The bee walks in a straight line while vigorously shaking its abdomen, then loops back to repeat the pattern, all within the darkness of the hive. The angle of the straight-line portion relative to vertical indicates the direction of the food source relative to the sun, while the duration of the waggling portion conveys the distance that must be travelled. Other bees follow closely behind the dancer, sensing the vibrations and orientation with remarkable precision before flying directly to the indicated location. Scientists have described the dance as a kind of living GPS coordinate, encoding both direction and distance in a form that other bees can decode purely through touch and movement in total darkness. This system allows a colony to rapidly direct large numbers of foragers to the most productive flower patches nearby.\n\n31. The main purpose of this passage is to ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "argue that honeybees rely primarily on scent to locate food"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "criticize the accuracy of the waggle dance as a communication method"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "explain how the waggle dance allows honeybees to share information about food sources"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "compare the waggle dance with the mating rituals of other insects"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "describe the internal anatomy of a honeybee's abdomen"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçanın geneli, belirtilen olguyu açıklamaya odaklanmaktadır; bu nedenle doğru seçenek parçanın ana amacını en iyi yansıtan ifadedir. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc25-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (SUBORDINATE CLAUSE - MIXED CONNECTORS)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "----, engineers were able to identify the exact source of the bridge's structural weakness.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "As the bridge had recently been repainted"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Despite the limited time available for inspection"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "By conducting a series of detailed stress tests"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Even though traffic had to be rerouted"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Since the bridge was built over a century ago"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "'By conducting a series of detailed stress tests' bir eylemin sonucunu doğrudan açıkladığından C doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc26-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (REASON CLAUSE - BLANK AT END)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Some students memorise information the night before an exam; however, reviewing material consistently throughout the term proves far more effective ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "if the exam covers a wide range of topics"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "when teachers provide detailed study guides"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "since last-minute cramming rarely covers everything"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "even though students often underestimate how much time it requires"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "because it allows knowledge to move into long-term memory"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "'because it allows knowledge to move into long-term memory' doğrudan gerekçeyi verdiğinden E doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc27-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (VARIED CONNECTOR - BLANK AT END)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The Wright brothers' first powered flight lasted only twelve seconds, ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "even if the aircraft nearly failed to leave the ground"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "for it required years of careful experimentation beforehand"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "yet it marked the beginning of the entire aviation industry"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "as it covered a distance of just over thirty-six metres"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "whereas later flights that same day lasted considerably longer"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "'yet' kısa süreye rağmen büyük tarihsel önemi vurguladığından C doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc28-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (CONDITION/TIME CLAUSE - BLANK AT START)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "----, several publishers have started releasing audiobooks alongside every new print title.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "As long as digital sales continue to outpace print sales"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Whether readers prefer listening over reading or not"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Though producing audiobooks requires additional studio time"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Given that demand for audio content had grown substantially"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Until every backlist title has been converted to audio"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "'Given that' yayıncıların gerçek bir gerekçeye dayanarak harekete geçtiğini ifade ettiğinden D doğru tamamlamadır."}], "9": [{"id": "ydtozg5-rc-detail-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (DETAIL/RESULT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Certain plants, such as the prayer plant and various species of clover, fold or lower their leaves each evening and reopen them at dawn, a daily movement known as nyctinasty. Unlike the slower growth-based movements that plants make toward sunlight, nyctinastic movements occur rapidly, driven by changes in water pressure within specialised swollen cells called pulvini located at the base of each leaf. As daylight fades, ions shift out of the cells on one side of the pulvinus, causing water to follow and the cells to lose rigidity, which allows the leaf to droop or fold. Researchers believe this nightly folding may reduce water loss, deter nocturnal insects, or protect the leaf's photosynthetic surface from cold, moisture-laden air. Because the rhythm continues even when plants are kept in constant darkness for several days, scientists describe it as an internal alarm clock rather than a simple reaction to fading light, since the plant appears to anticipate the coming night rather than merely responding to it.\n\n29. According to the passage, what causes the leaf to droop or fold during nyctinastic movement?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Cold air directly damages the leaf's outer surface"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The plant's roots absorb less water after sunset"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "The leaf grows more slowly during the night than during the day"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Ions shift within the pulvinus, causing a loss of water pressure"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Nocturnal insects physically press the leaf downward"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen bilgiye göre doğru seçenek 'Ions shift within the pulvinus, causing a loss of water pressure' ifadesidir. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-rc-ref-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (REFERENCE/ILLUSTRATION)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Certain plants, such as the prayer plant and various species of clover, fold or lower their leaves each evening and reopen them at dawn, a daily movement known as nyctinasty. Unlike the slower growth-based movements that plants make toward sunlight, nyctinastic movements occur rapidly, driven by changes in water pressure within specialised swollen cells called pulvini located at the base of each leaf. As daylight fades, ions shift out of the cells on one side of the pulvinus, causing water to follow and the cells to lose rigidity, which allows the leaf to droop or fold. Researchers believe this nightly folding may reduce water loss, deter nocturnal insects, or protect the leaf's photosynthetic surface from cold, moisture-laden air. Because the rhythm continues even when plants are kept in constant darkness for several days, scientists describe it as an internal alarm clock rather than a simple reaction to fading light, since the plant appears to anticipate the coming night rather than merely responding to it.\n\n30. The author's reference to 'an internal alarm clock' serves to illustrate ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "how nocturnal insects are deterred by folded leaves"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "why some plants fold their leaves faster than others"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "how nyctinasty is simply a direct reaction to fading sunlight"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "how the plant appears to anticipate night rather than merely respond to it"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "why pulvini are located at the base of each leaf"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Yazarın 'an internal alarm clock' benzetmesi, parçadaki ilgili mekanizmayı somutlaştırmak için kullanılmıştır; doğru açıklama budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-rc-purpose-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (MAIN PURPOSE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Certain plants, such as the prayer plant and various species of clover, fold or lower their leaves each evening and reopen them at dawn, a daily movement known as nyctinasty. Unlike the slower growth-based movements that plants make toward sunlight, nyctinastic movements occur rapidly, driven by changes in water pressure within specialised swollen cells called pulvini located at the base of each leaf. As daylight fades, ions shift out of the cells on one side of the pulvinus, causing water to follow and the cells to lose rigidity, which allows the leaf to droop or fold. Researchers believe this nightly folding may reduce water loss, deter nocturnal insects, or protect the leaf's photosynthetic surface from cold, moisture-laden air. Because the rhythm continues even when plants are kept in constant darkness for several days, scientists describe it as an internal alarm clock rather than a simple reaction to fading light, since the plant appears to anticipate the coming night rather than merely responding to it.\n\n31. The main purpose of this passage is to ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "compare nyctinasty with growth-based movements toward sunlight"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "describe how pulvini are structurally different from ordinary plant cells"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "criticize experiments that kept plants in constant darkness"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "explain the mechanism and possible functions behind nyctinastic leaf movement"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "argue that nyctinasty serves no meaningful biological function"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçanın geneli, belirtilen olguyu açıklamaya odaklanmaktadır; bu nedenle doğru seçenek parçanın ana amacını en iyi yansıtan ifadedir. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc25-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (SUBORDINATE CLAUSE - MIXED CONNECTORS)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "----, the ancient irrigation channels still function effectively today.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "As the surrounding farmland has since been abandoned"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Despite centuries of erosion and shifting soil"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "While modern engineers criticised their original design"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Because they were built using a remarkably durable stone"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Since rainfall in the region has increased recently"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "'Because they were built using a remarkably durable stone' etkinliğin nedenini doğrudan açıkladığından D doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc26-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (REASON CLAUSE - BLANK AT END)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Many assume that raising prices always increases profit; in reality, maintaining customer loyalty matters just as much ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "if competitors lower their own prices"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "because loyal customers generate steady, long-term revenue"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "when new products are introduced each season"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "since most customers rarely compare prices carefully"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "even though loyalty programmes can be costly to run"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "'because loyal customers generate steady, long-term revenue' doğrudan gerekçeyi verdiğinden B doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc27-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (VARIED CONNECTOR - BLANK AT END)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The construction of medieval cathedrals often spanned several generations, ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "even if the original architects rarely lived to see them finished"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "for they were built to inspire awe and demonstrate devotion"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "yet many still stand largely intact after hundreds of years"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "as each stage required specialised craftsmen and materials"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "whereas modern buildings are typically completed within a few years"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "'as' inşa sürecinin uzunluğunun nedenini/gerekçesini sunduğundan D doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc28-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (CONDITION/TIME CLAUSE - BLANK AT START)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "----, several coastal towns have invested in new flood barriers along their waterfronts.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "As long as insurance costs for waterfront properties remain high"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Whether residents are willing to pay higher local taxes or not"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Though construction has disrupted local businesses temporarily"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Until every barrier design has been independently tested"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Given that sea levels in the area had risen measurably over the past decade"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "'Given that' kıyı kasabalarının gerçek bir gerekçeye dayanarak harekete geçtiğini ifade ettiğinden E doğru tamamlamadır."}], "10": [{"id": "ydtozg5-rc-detail-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (DETAIL/RESULT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Bats and dolphins evolved echolocation independently, separated by millions of years and entirely different environments, yet both rely on the same basic principle: emitting sound and interpreting the returning echoes to build a picture of their surroundings. Bats typically produce ultrasonic calls through their mouth or nose, adjusting the frequency and rate of pulses depending on whether they are searching for prey or closing in on a target insect. Dolphins, by contrast, generate clicks using specialised tissues near their blowhole and focus the resulting sound waves through a fatty organ in their forehead called the melon, which acts much like a lens for sound. Despite these anatomical differences, both animals process returning echoes with extraordinary precision, distinguishing between objects only centimetres apart. Scientists studying this phenomenon have noted that evolution arrived at strikingly similar acoustic solutions in air and water, a case of convergent evolution producing what researchers sometimes call nature's parallel sonar systems in two entirely unrelated animal groups.\n\n29. According to the passage, what role does the melon play in dolphin echolocation?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "It allows dolphins to hear echoes returning from prey"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "It regulates the dolphin's buoyancy while diving"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "It stores air used to generate additional sound pulses"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "It produces the ultrasonic clicks emitted by the dolphin"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "It focuses the sound waves produced near the blowhole"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen bilgiye göre doğru seçenek 'It focuses the sound waves produced near the blowhole' ifadesidir. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-rc-ref-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (REFERENCE/ILLUSTRATION)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Bats and dolphins evolved echolocation independently, separated by millions of years and entirely different environments, yet both rely on the same basic principle: emitting sound and interpreting the returning echoes to build a picture of their surroundings. Bats typically produce ultrasonic calls through their mouth or nose, adjusting the frequency and rate of pulses depending on whether they are searching for prey or closing in on a target insect. Dolphins, by contrast, generate clicks using specialised tissues near their blowhole and focus the resulting sound waves through a fatty organ in their forehead called the melon, which acts much like a lens for sound. Despite these anatomical differences, both animals process returning echoes with extraordinary precision, distinguishing between objects only centimetres apart. Scientists studying this phenomenon have noted that evolution arrived at strikingly similar acoustic solutions in air and water, a case of convergent evolution producing what researchers sometimes call nature's parallel sonar systems in two entirely unrelated animal groups.\n\n30. The author's reference to 'a lens for sound' serves to illustrate ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "why bats and dolphins cannot both use echolocation effectively"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "how bats produce ultrasonic calls through their nose"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "why dolphins rely more on vision than on sound"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "how convergent evolution differs from independent evolution"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "how the melon focuses sound waves in a way comparable to how a lens focuses light"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Yazarın 'a lens for sound' benzetmesi, parçadaki ilgili mekanizmayı somutlaştırmak için kullanılmıştır; doğru açıklama budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-rc-purpose-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (MAIN PURPOSE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Bats and dolphins evolved echolocation independently, separated by millions of years and entirely different environments, yet both rely on the same basic principle: emitting sound and interpreting the returning echoes to build a picture of their surroundings. Bats typically produce ultrasonic calls through their mouth or nose, adjusting the frequency and rate of pulses depending on whether they are searching for prey or closing in on a target insect. Dolphins, by contrast, generate clicks using specialised tissues near their blowhole and focus the resulting sound waves through a fatty organ in their forehead called the melon, which acts much like a lens for sound. Despite these anatomical differences, both animals process returning echoes with extraordinary precision, distinguishing between objects only centimetres apart. Scientists studying this phenomenon have noted that evolution arrived at strikingly similar acoustic solutions in air and water, a case of convergent evolution producing what researchers sometimes call nature's parallel sonar systems in two entirely unrelated animal groups.\n\n31. The main purpose of this passage is to ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "describe the diet of bats and dolphins in their natural habitats"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "criticize research that overlooks differences between bats and dolphins"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "explain why echolocation is rare among mammals"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "argue that dolphin echolocation is more advanced than that of bats"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "compare how bats and dolphins independently evolved similar echolocation systems"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçanın geneli, belirtilen olguyu açıklamaya odaklanmaktadır; bu nedenle doğru seçenek parçanın ana amacını en iyi yansıtan ifadedir. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc25-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (SUBORDINATE CLAUSE - MIXED CONNECTORS)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "----, the small publishing house managed to release three award-winning novels in a single year.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Although its staff consisted of only a handful of editors"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "As larger publishers dominated the bestseller lists"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "While its offices remained in a modest downtown building"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Even though its marketing budget had been cut"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Since it had recently signed several promising new authors"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "'Since it had recently signed several promising new authors' başarının nedenini doğrudan açıkladığından E doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc26-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (REASON CLAUSE - BLANK AT END)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "People often believe that more meetings improve teamwork; however, clear written communication achieves far better results ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "if meetings are scheduled at convenient times"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "when teams are distributed across different time zones"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "since meetings can easily run over their allotted time"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "even though writing clearly takes more initial effort"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "because it gives every team member a precise, lasting reference"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "'because it gives every team member a precise, lasting reference' doğrudan gerekçeyi verdiğinden E doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc27-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (VARIED CONNECTOR - BLANK AT END)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The invention of refrigeration transformed how food was stored and transported, ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "even if early refrigeration units were bulky and unreliable"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "for it allowed perishable goods to travel far greater distances"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "yet many households did not adopt it until decades later"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "as it relied on chemical processes not yet fully understood at the time"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "whereas earlier methods depended entirely on ice harvested from lakes"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "'whereas' modern yöntemin öncesindeki uygulamayla karşılaştırmasını sunduğundan E doğru tamamlamadır."}, {"id": "ydtozg5-sc28-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SENTENCE COMPLETION (CONDITION/TIME CLAUSE - BLANK AT START)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "----, several airports have expanded their use of automated passport control gates.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "As long as passenger volumes continue to increase yearly"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Given that manual passport checks had caused lengthy delays during peak hours"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Whether travellers trust the new technology or not"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Though the gates require regular software updates"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Until international security standards are fully harmonised"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "'Given that' havalimanlarının gerçek bir gerekçeye dayanarak harekete geçtiğini ifade ettiğinden B doğru tamamlamadır."}]};
Object.keys(DENEME_YDT_INGILIZCE_OZEL_5).forEach(function(no) {
  if (!DENEME_SORU_BANKASI.YDT[no]) DENEME_SORU_BANKASI.YDT[no] = {};
  DENEME_SORU_BANKASI.YDT[no].ydtIngilizce = (DENEME_SORU_BANKASI.YDT[no].ydtIngilizce || []).concat(DENEME_YDT_INGILIZCE_OZEL_5[no]);
});
const DENEME_YDT_INGILIZCE_OZEL_6 = {"1": [{"id": "ydtozg6-a-reason-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (ANALOGY REASON)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The human immune system operates as a coordinated defence network, protecting the body from harmful invaders such as bacteria, viruses, and other pathogens. It consists of two main branches: an innate response that reacts immediately and non-specifically to any threat, and an adaptive response that develops targeted defences against specific pathogens it has previously encountered. White blood cells constantly patrol the bloodstream, identifying foreign particles and either destroying them directly or alerting other immune cells to respond. Some cells, known as memory cells, retain information about past infections for years, allowing the body to respond far more quickly if the same pathogen appears again. Vaccines work by training this memory system in advance, exposing it to a harmless version of a pathogen so the body can prepare its defences before a real infection occurs. Without a properly functioning immune system, even minor infections could become life-threatening.\n\n35. The passage describes the immune system as a coordinated defence network because it ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "combines multiple types of cells working together against threats"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "prevents all future infections once activated"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "stores pathogens rather than destroying them"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "eliminates every pathogen before it enters the bloodstream"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "relies solely on vaccines to function properly"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçadaki benzetme, doğru seçenekte belirtilen özelliği somutlaştırmak için kullanılmıştır. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-a-detail-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SYSTEM DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The human immune system operates as a coordinated defence network, protecting the body from harmful invaders such as bacteria, viruses, and other pathogens. It consists of two main branches: an innate response that reacts immediately and non-specifically to any threat, and an adaptive response that develops targeted defences against specific pathogens it has previously encountered. White blood cells constantly patrol the bloodstream, identifying foreign particles and either destroying them directly or alerting other immune cells to respond. Some cells, known as memory cells, retain information about past infections for years, allowing the body to respond far more quickly if the same pathogen appears again. Vaccines work by training this memory system in advance, exposing it to a harmless version of a pathogen so the body can prepare its defences before a real infection occurs. Without a properly functioning immune system, even minor infections could become life-threatening.\n\n36. According to the passage, memory cells ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "allow the body to respond more quickly to a previously encountered pathogen"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "are replaced entirely each time a new infection occurs"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "function independently of the rest of the immune system"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "prevent the innate immune response from activating"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "are only active during the initial exposure to a pathogen"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen bilgiye göre doğru seçenek budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-a-infer-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SYSTEM INFERENCE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The human immune system operates as a coordinated defence network, protecting the body from harmful invaders such as bacteria, viruses, and other pathogens. It consists of two main branches: an innate response that reacts immediately and non-specifically to any threat, and an adaptive response that develops targeted defences against specific pathogens it has previously encountered. White blood cells constantly patrol the bloodstream, identifying foreign particles and either destroying them directly or alerting other immune cells to respond. Some cells, known as memory cells, retain information about past infections for years, allowing the body to respond far more quickly if the same pathogen appears again. Vaccines work by training this memory system in advance, exposing it to a harmless version of a pathogen so the body can prepare its defences before a real infection occurs. Without a properly functioning immune system, even minor infections could become life-threatening.\n\n37. What can be inferred from the passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The adaptive immune response can improve over time through prior exposure"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The innate immune response is more effective than the adaptive response"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "White blood cells only respond to bacterial infections"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Memory cells are formed before a person is born"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Vaccines eliminate the need for any natural immune response"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçadaki bilgilerden mantıksal olarak çıkarılabilecek doğru sonuç budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-role-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SPECIFIC ROLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Moving to work in a different country involves far more than adjusting to a new job title or unfamiliar colleagues; it often means learning an entirely different set of unspoken workplace norms. In some cultures, direct disagreement with a manager during a meeting is considered a healthy sign of engagement, while in others, the same behaviour might be seen as disrespectful. Language proficiency alone rarely solves this problem, since even fluent speakers can misjudge when humour is appropriate or how formally to address senior staff. Many newcomers rely on close observation, watching how established employees interact before adjusting their own behaviour. Some companies now offer structured cultural training sessions, though such programmes vary widely in quality and rarely capture the subtle, everyday judgement calls that only come from lived experience.\n\n32. According to the passage, what is the role of language proficiency when adjusting to a foreign workplace?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "It is useful, but does not guarantee an understanding of unspoken cultural norms"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "It removes the need for observing how established employees behave"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "It discourages employees from adapting to workplace-specific customs"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "It has no real value since cultural training programmes address everything necessary"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "It fully prepares employees for every unspoken cultural norm they will encounter"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçada belirtilen role göre doğru seçenek budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-true-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (TRUE STATEMENT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Moving to work in a different country involves far more than adjusting to a new job title or unfamiliar colleagues; it often means learning an entirely different set of unspoken workplace norms. In some cultures, direct disagreement with a manager during a meeting is considered a healthy sign of engagement, while in others, the same behaviour might be seen as disrespectful. Language proficiency alone rarely solves this problem, since even fluent speakers can misjudge when humour is appropriate or how formally to address senior staff. Many newcomers rely on close observation, watching how established employees interact before adjusting their own behaviour. Some companies now offer structured cultural training sessions, though such programmes vary widely in quality and rarely capture the subtle, everyday judgement calls that only come from lived experience.\n\n33. According to the passage, which of the following is true?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Newcomers often observe established employees to understand unspoken norms"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Fluent speakers automatically know how much personal information to share"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Workplace training programmes are required by law in most countries"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Cultural training programmes always fully prepare employees for a foreign workplace"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Direct disagreement with a manager is viewed identically across all cultures"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçayla örtüşen tek doğru ifade budur; diğerleri parçayla çelişmekte veya parçada yer almamaktadır. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-attitude-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (AUTHOR'S ATTITUDE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Moving to work in a different country involves far more than adjusting to a new job title or unfamiliar colleagues; it often means learning an entirely different set of unspoken workplace norms. In some cultures, direct disagreement with a manager during a meeting is considered a healthy sign of engagement, while in others, the same behaviour might be seen as disrespectful. Language proficiency alone rarely solves this problem, since even fluent speakers can misjudge when humour is appropriate or how formally to address senior staff. Many newcomers rely on close observation, watching how established employees interact before adjusting their own behaviour. Some companies now offer structured cultural training sessions, though such programmes vary widely in quality and rarely capture the subtle, everyday judgement calls that only come from lived experience.\n\n34. What is the author's attitude towards cultural training programmes offered by companies?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Critical"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Dismissive"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Indifferent"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Neutral"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Optimistic"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçanın genel tonu ve kullanılan ifadeler, yazarın 'Critical' bir tutum sergilediğini göstermektedir. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-inferref-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (INFERENCE FROM REFERENCE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Contemporary productivity culture often promises that with the right app or morning routine, individuals can gain complete control over their time and, by extension, their happiness. Yet this promise frequently backfires, leaving people more anxious than before, since unpredictable interruptions and other people's demands inevitably intrude on even the most carefully planned day. The philosopher Marcus Aurelius observed centuries ago that true peace comes not from controlling every external circumstance, an impossible task, but from mastering one's own response to circumstances beyond one's control. Modern psychology has arrived at a strikingly similar conclusion: research on resilience shows that individuals who focus on their own reactions report significantly lower stress levels over time. Perhaps genuine productivity begins not with a better planner, but with a more flexible relationship to disruption itself.\n\n38. What can be inferred from the author's reference to Marcus Aurelius's view on control?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Genuine peace may depend more on one's response to events than on controlling them"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Ancient philosophy has little relevance to modern psychological research"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Aurelius believed external circumstances could always be fully controlled"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Productivity culture and Stoic philosophy share identical goals"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Modern productivity tools have made his philosophy entirely obsolete"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Yazarın atıfta bulunduğu görüşten çıkarılabilecek en tutarlı sonuç budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-stated-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (STATED FACT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Contemporary productivity culture often promises that with the right app or morning routine, individuals can gain complete control over their time and, by extension, their happiness. Yet this promise frequently backfires, leaving people more anxious than before, since unpredictable interruptions and other people's demands inevitably intrude on even the most carefully planned day. The philosopher Marcus Aurelius observed centuries ago that true peace comes not from controlling every external circumstance, an impossible task, but from mastering one's own response to circumstances beyond one's control. Modern psychology has arrived at a strikingly similar conclusion: research on resilience shows that individuals who focus on their own reactions report significantly lower stress levels over time. Perhaps genuine productivity begins not with a better planner, but with a more flexible relationship to disruption itself.\n\n39. It is stated in the passage that ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "research on resilience links lower stress to focusing on one's own reactions"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Marcus Aurelius rejected the idea that circumstances could disrupt daily plans"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "productivity culture places equal emphasis on tasks completed and flexibility"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "modern psychology contradicts the conclusions reached by ancient philosophy"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "productivity apps have eliminated most sources of daily stress"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçada doğrudan ifade edilen bilgiye uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-title-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (BEST TITLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Contemporary productivity culture often promises that with the right app or morning routine, individuals can gain complete control over their time and, by extension, their happiness. Yet this promise frequently backfires, leaving people more anxious than before, since unpredictable interruptions and other people's demands inevitably intrude on even the most carefully planned day. The philosopher Marcus Aurelius observed centuries ago that true peace comes not from controlling every external circumstance, an impossible task, but from mastering one's own response to circumstances beyond one's control. Modern psychology has arrived at a strikingly similar conclusion: research on resilience shows that individuals who focus on their own reactions report significantly lower stress levels over time. Perhaps genuine productivity begins not with a better planner, but with a more flexible relationship to disruption itself.\n\n40. Which of the following could be the best title for the passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Rethinking Productivity Through an Ancient Lens"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The Psychological Effects of Daily Scheduling"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Marcus Aurelius and the Decline of Modern Planning"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "The History of Stoic Philosophy in Ancient Rome"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Why Productivity Apps Have Failed Modern Society"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçanın tamamını en kapsamlı ve dengeli şekilde özetleyen başlık budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-detail-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SKILL-BENEFIT DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Learning to play a musical instrument requires far more than memorising finger positions; it demands the coordination of multiple cognitive systems working together in real time. A student must simultaneously read musical notation, translate it into precise movement, listen critically to the resulting sound, and adjust technique instantly if something sounds wrong. This constant coordination appears to strengthen general cognitive flexibility, the ability to shift smoothly between different types of mental tasks. Brain imaging studies have found that musicians, particularly those who began training in childhood, often show structural differences in regions associated with auditory processing, fine motor control, and memory. Music training also cultivates patience and the ability to tolerate repeated failure while gradually improving.\n\n41. According to the passage, learning a musical instrument helps individuals ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "develop general cognitive flexibility through coordinating multiple mental processes"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "become professional musicians regardless of natural ability"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "rely primarily on memorising finger positions alone"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "eliminate the need for critical listening while performing"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "avoid the need for structured, disciplined practice"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen faydaya uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-pointed-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (POINTED-OUT DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Learning to play a musical instrument requires far more than memorising finger positions; it demands the coordination of multiple cognitive systems working together in real time. A student must simultaneously read musical notation, translate it into precise movement, listen critically to the resulting sound, and adjust technique instantly if something sounds wrong. This constant coordination appears to strengthen general cognitive flexibility, the ability to shift smoothly between different types of mental tasks. Brain imaging studies have found that musicians, particularly those who began training in childhood, often show structural differences in regions associated with auditory processing, fine motor control, and memory. Music training also cultivates patience and the ability to tolerate repeated failure while gradually improving.\n\n42. It is pointed out in the passage that brain imaging studies of musicians ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "have revealed structural differences in regions related to processing, motor control, and memory"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "prove that musical training guarantees professional success"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "apply only to musicians who began training as adults"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "contradict findings related to cognitive flexibility"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "show no measurable differences compared to non-musicians"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçada özellikle vurgulanan noktaya uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-purpose-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (AUTHOR'S PRIMARY PURPOSE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Learning to play a musical instrument requires far more than memorising finger positions; it demands the coordination of multiple cognitive systems working together in real time. A student must simultaneously read musical notation, translate it into precise movement, listen critically to the resulting sound, and adjust technique instantly if something sounds wrong. This constant coordination appears to strengthen general cognitive flexibility, the ability to shift smoothly between different types of mental tasks. Brain imaging studies have found that musicians, particularly those who began training in childhood, often show structural differences in regions associated with auditory processing, fine motor control, and memory. Music training also cultivates patience and the ability to tolerate repeated failure while gradually improving.\n\n43. What is the author's primary purpose in this passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "To explain how learning an instrument can strengthen broader cognitive abilities"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "To criticise music education programmes for focusing on performance alone"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "To describe the history of music education across different cultures"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "To convince readers that musicians have superior intelligence to non-musicians"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "To argue that every child should be required to learn a musical instrument"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçanın bütünü, belirtilen faydayı açıklamaya odaklandığından yazarın asıl amacı budur. Cevap: A."}], "2": [{"id": "ydtozg6-a-reason-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (ANALOGY REASON)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A traffic light system operates much like a silent officer stationed at every major intersection, directing the flow of vehicles and pedestrians without ever raising a hand or a whistle. Sensors embedded in the road, or in more modern systems, cameras mounted above intersections, detect the presence and volume of approaching traffic, allowing the system to adjust signal timing dynamically rather than following a fixed schedule. During periods of heavy congestion, the lights extend green phases for the busiest lanes, while during quiet hours, they may switch more quickly to reduce unnecessary waiting. Pedestrian crossing signals are often synchronised with vehicle signals to prevent conflicts. In some cities, traffic lights communicate with one another along a single road, creating a coordinated 'green wave' that allows a driver travelling at a steady speed to pass through several intersections without stopping.\n\n35. The passage describes a traffic light system as a silent officer because it ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "eliminates the need for pedestrian crossing signals"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "directs the movement of vehicles and pedestrians without direct human intervention"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "punishes drivers who violate traffic rules"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "operates only during periods of heavy congestion"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "replaces the judgement of urban planners entirely"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçadaki benzetme, doğru seçenekte belirtilen özelliği somutlaştırmak için kullanılmıştır. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-a-detail-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SYSTEM DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A traffic light system operates much like a silent officer stationed at every major intersection, directing the flow of vehicles and pedestrians without ever raising a hand or a whistle. Sensors embedded in the road, or in more modern systems, cameras mounted above intersections, detect the presence and volume of approaching traffic, allowing the system to adjust signal timing dynamically rather than following a fixed schedule. During periods of heavy congestion, the lights extend green phases for the busiest lanes, while during quiet hours, they may switch more quickly to reduce unnecessary waiting. Pedestrian crossing signals are often synchronised with vehicle signals to prevent conflicts. In some cities, traffic lights communicate with one another along a single road, creating a coordinated 'green wave' that allows a driver travelling at a steady speed to pass through several intersections without stopping.\n\n36. According to the passage, a 'green wave' allows drivers to ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "avoid paying tolls at multiple intersections"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "pass through several intersections without stopping"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "communicate directly with pedestrian signals"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "bypass sensors embedded in the road"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "receive real-time alerts about accidents ahead"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen bilgiye göre doğru seçenek budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-a-infer-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SYSTEM INFERENCE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A traffic light system operates much like a silent officer stationed at every major intersection, directing the flow of vehicles and pedestrians without ever raising a hand or a whistle. Sensors embedded in the road, or in more modern systems, cameras mounted above intersections, detect the presence and volume of approaching traffic, allowing the system to adjust signal timing dynamically rather than following a fixed schedule. During periods of heavy congestion, the lights extend green phases for the busiest lanes, while during quiet hours, they may switch more quickly to reduce unnecessary waiting. Pedestrian crossing signals are often synchronised with vehicle signals to prevent conflicts. In some cities, traffic lights communicate with one another along a single road, creating a coordinated 'green wave' that allows a driver travelling at a steady speed to pass through several intersections without stopping.\n\n37. What can be inferred from the passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Traffic lights operate on a completely fixed schedule regardless of conditions"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Modern traffic systems can adapt their behaviour based on real-time traffic conditions"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Pedestrian and vehicle signals always operate independently of each other"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Urban intersections are safer without any traffic light systems"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Sensors are no longer necessary in modern traffic light systems"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçadaki bilgilerden mantıksal olarak çıkarılabilecek doğru sonuç budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-role-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SPECIFIC ROLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Bargaining in an open-air market abroad often requires skills that have little to do with spoken language. A firm handshake, a slow head shake, or simply holding up fingers to indicate a price can carry more weight than any sentence a visitor might struggle to construct. Experienced travellers learn to read a seller's posture and tone just as carefully as any spoken offer. Yet gestures are not universal: a nod that means agreement in one country may indicate the opposite elsewhere, and pointing directly at a person is considered rude in several cultures. Guidebooks increasingly include sections on local gesture etiquette, though such advice can only cover the most common situations, leaving room for misunderstanding.\n\n32. According to the passage, what is the role of gestures when bargaining in a foreign market?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "They eliminate any need to observe how locals interact"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "They can convey meaning, but their interpretation varies across cultures"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "They are universally understood in exactly the same way everywhere"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "They are less reliable than spoken language in every situation"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "They are only useful when combined with a formal guidebook"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçada belirtilen role göre doğru seçenek budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-true-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (TRUE STATEMENT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Bargaining in an open-air market abroad often requires skills that have little to do with spoken language. A firm handshake, a slow head shake, or simply holding up fingers to indicate a price can carry more weight than any sentence a visitor might struggle to construct. Experienced travellers learn to read a seller's posture and tone just as carefully as any spoken offer. Yet gestures are not universal: a nod that means agreement in one country may indicate the opposite elsewhere, and pointing directly at a person is considered rude in several cultures. Guidebooks increasingly include sections on local gesture etiquette, though such advice can only cover the most common situations, leaving room for misunderstanding.\n\n33. According to the passage, which of the following is true?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Guidebooks can fully prepare travellers for every gesture-related situation"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Pointing directly at someone is considered rude in some cultures"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Experienced travellers avoid observing sellers' posture and tone"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Gesture-based communication is only useful in open-air markets"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "A nod means agreement in every culture without exception"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçayla örtüşen tek doğru ifade budur; diğerleri parçayla çelişmekte veya parçada yer almamaktadır. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-attitude-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (AUTHOR'S ATTITUDE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Bargaining in an open-air market abroad often requires skills that have little to do with spoken language. A firm handshake, a slow head shake, or simply holding up fingers to indicate a price can carry more weight than any sentence a visitor might struggle to construct. Experienced travellers learn to read a seller's posture and tone just as carefully as any spoken offer. Yet gestures are not universal: a nod that means agreement in one country may indicate the opposite elsewhere, and pointing directly at a person is considered rude in several cultures. Guidebooks increasingly include sections on local gesture etiquette, though such advice can only cover the most common situations, leaving room for misunderstanding.\n\n34. What is the author's attitude towards guidebooks and travel apps covering gesture etiquette?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Indifferent"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Neutral"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Optimistic"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Critical"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Dismissive"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçanın genel tonu ve kullanılan ifadeler, yazarın 'Neutral' bir tutum sergilediğini göstermektedir. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-inferref-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (INFERENCE FROM REFERENCE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Habit-tracking apps have become enormously popular, promising users that consistent daily actions, recorded through streaks, will eventually reshape their character. This idea is not new. Aristotle argued that virtue is not innate but cultivated through repeated action, suggesting that people become courageous by performing courageous acts. Where Aristotle emphasised internal transformation, many modern apps focus almost exclusively on external metrics, such as an unbroken streak, sometimes causing users to feel that a single missed day undoes months of progress. Behavioural scientists note that this all-or-nothing mindset can discourage long-term habit formation, since a single lapse often leads users to abandon the habit entirely rather than simply resuming the next day.\n\n38. What can be inferred from the author's reference to Aristotle's view on virtue?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Aristotle believed virtue could be measured only through digital tracking"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Genuine character change may depend more on repeated action than on unbroken streaks"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Modern habit-tracking apps perfectly reflect Aristotle's original philosophy"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Aristotle rejected the idea that repetition could shape a person's character"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Ancient philosophy has no practical application to modern habit formation"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Yazarın atıfta bulunduğu görüşten çıkarılabilecek en tutarlı sonuç budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-stated-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (STATED FACT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Habit-tracking apps have become enormously popular, promising users that consistent daily actions, recorded through streaks, will eventually reshape their character. This idea is not new. Aristotle argued that virtue is not innate but cultivated through repeated action, suggesting that people become courageous by performing courageous acts. Where Aristotle emphasised internal transformation, many modern apps focus almost exclusively on external metrics, such as an unbroken streak, sometimes causing users to feel that a single missed day undoes months of progress. Behavioural scientists note that this all-or-nothing mindset can discourage long-term habit formation, since a single lapse often leads users to abandon the habit entirely rather than simply resuming the next day.\n\n39. It is stated in the passage that ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Aristotle believed courage exists independently of any repeated action"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "streak-based app design can discourage long-term habit formation"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "behavioural scientists fully endorse the all-or-nothing mindset"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "habit-tracking apps focus primarily on internal character transformation"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "a single missed day has no psychological effect on app users"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçada doğrudan ifade edilen bilgiye uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-title-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (BEST TITLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Habit-tracking apps have become enormously popular, promising users that consistent daily actions, recorded through streaks, will eventually reshape their character. This idea is not new. Aristotle argued that virtue is not innate but cultivated through repeated action, suggesting that people become courageous by performing courageous acts. Where Aristotle emphasised internal transformation, many modern apps focus almost exclusively on external metrics, such as an unbroken streak, sometimes causing users to feel that a single missed day undoes months of progress. Behavioural scientists note that this all-or-nothing mindset can discourage long-term habit formation, since a single lapse often leads users to abandon the habit entirely rather than simply resuming the next day.\n\n40. Which of the following could be the best title for the passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Aristotle's Complete Theory of Human Virtue"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "What Ancient Philosophy Reveals About Modern Habit Apps"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Why Behavioural Science Rejects All Habit Formation"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "The History of Streak-Based Mobile Applications"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The Rise and Fall of Habit-Tracking Technology"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçanın tamamını en kapsamlı ve dengeli şekilde özetleyen başlık budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-detail-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SKILL-BENEFIT DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Strategy-based games typically require players to plan several moves in advance, anticipate an opponent's responses, and adjust their approach when circumstances change. Unlike games that rely purely on chance, these activities reward careful analysis over impulsive decisions. Researchers studying regular players have observed improvements in working memory and in pattern recognition, the ability to notice recurring structures within complex information. Players also develop a habit of considering multiple possible outcomes before committing to a decision. Researchers note that benefits appear strongest not from occasional casual play but from sustained engagement that gradually increases in complexity.\n\n41. According to the passage, playing strategy-based games helps individuals ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "rely primarily on chance rather than careful planning"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "improve working memory and pattern recognition through sustained practice"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "avoid the need to consider multiple possible outcomes"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "develop skills that apply only within the context of the game itself"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "reduce their overall capacity for long-term thinking"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen faydaya uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-pointed-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (POINTED-OUT DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Strategy-based games typically require players to plan several moves in advance, anticipate an opponent's responses, and adjust their approach when circumstances change. Unlike games that rely purely on chance, these activities reward careful analysis over impulsive decisions. Researchers studying regular players have observed improvements in working memory and in pattern recognition, the ability to notice recurring structures within complex information. Players also develop a habit of considering multiple possible outcomes before committing to a decision. Researchers note that benefits appear strongest not from occasional casual play but from sustained engagement that gradually increases in complexity.\n\n42. It is pointed out in the passage that the cognitive benefits of strategy games ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "are identical regardless of how frequently a person plays"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "appear strongest through sustained engagement with increasing complexity"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "apply only to games played on a physical board"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "have not been observed in any cognitive research"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "appear strongest through occasional, casual play"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçada özellikle vurgulanan noktaya uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-purpose-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (AUTHOR'S PRIMARY PURPOSE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Strategy-based games typically require players to plan several moves in advance, anticipate an opponent's responses, and adjust their approach when circumstances change. Unlike games that rely purely on chance, these activities reward careful analysis over impulsive decisions. Researchers studying regular players have observed improvements in working memory and in pattern recognition, the ability to notice recurring structures within complex information. Players also develop a habit of considering multiple possible outcomes before committing to a decision. Researchers note that benefits appear strongest not from occasional casual play but from sustained engagement that gradually increases in complexity.\n\n43. What is the author's primary purpose in this passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "To argue that strategy games should replace traditional education"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "To explain how strategy games can strengthen problem-solving and planning skills"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "To criticise casual gamers for lacking strategic ability"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "To describe the history of board games across different cultures"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "To convince readers that all games improve cognitive function equally"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçanın bütünü, belirtilen faydayı açıklamaya odaklandığından yazarın asıl amacı budur. Cevap: B."}], "3": [{"id": "ydtozg6-a-reason-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (ANALOGY REASON)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A modern water treatment plant transforms untreated river or reservoir water into water safe enough to drink, guiding it through a carefully controlled journey of several distinct stages. In the first stage, large debris such as leaves and sediment are removed through screening and settling tanks. The water then passes through a coagulation process, where chemicals cause fine particles to clump together into larger clusters that settle out more easily. Following this, filtration through layers of sand and gravel removes remaining impurities, while a disinfection stage, typically using chlorine or ultraviolet light, eliminates harmful bacteria and viruses. Because each stage targets a different type of contaminant, skipping even one step can allow certain pollutants to pass through undetected. Water quality is tested repeatedly throughout the process.\n\n35. The passage describes water treatment as a purification journey because it ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "eliminates the need for any water quality testing"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "occurs instantly without any distinct stages"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "involves the water passing through a sequence of separate treatment stages"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "relies entirely on chemical disinfection alone"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "is completed before the water reaches the reservoir"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçadaki benzetme, doğru seçenekte belirtilen özelliği somutlaştırmak için kullanılmıştır. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-a-detail-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SYSTEM DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A modern water treatment plant transforms untreated river or reservoir water into water safe enough to drink, guiding it through a carefully controlled journey of several distinct stages. In the first stage, large debris such as leaves and sediment are removed through screening and settling tanks. The water then passes through a coagulation process, where chemicals cause fine particles to clump together into larger clusters that settle out more easily. Following this, filtration through layers of sand and gravel removes remaining impurities, while a disinfection stage, typically using chlorine or ultraviolet light, eliminates harmful bacteria and viruses. Because each stage targets a different type of contaminant, skipping even one step can allow certain pollutants to pass through undetected. Water quality is tested repeatedly throughout the process.\n\n36. According to the passage, the coagulation process ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "tests the water for safety before distribution"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "removes large debris such as leaves and sediment"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "causes fine particles to clump together for easier removal"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "eliminates bacteria and viruses from the water"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "adjusts the water's mineral balance"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen bilgiye göre doğru seçenek budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-a-infer-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SYSTEM INFERENCE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A modern water treatment plant transforms untreated river or reservoir water into water safe enough to drink, guiding it through a carefully controlled journey of several distinct stages. In the first stage, large debris such as leaves and sediment are removed through screening and settling tanks. The water then passes through a coagulation process, where chemicals cause fine particles to clump together into larger clusters that settle out more easily. Following this, filtration through layers of sand and gravel removes remaining impurities, while a disinfection stage, typically using chlorine or ultraviolet light, eliminates harmful bacteria and viruses. Because each stage targets a different type of contaminant, skipping even one step can allow certain pollutants to pass through undetected. Water quality is tested repeatedly throughout the process.\n\n37. What can be inferred from the passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Mineral balance adjustment is the most critical stage of treatment"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "All water treatment plants use the exact same number of stages"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Skipping a treatment stage could allow certain contaminants to remain in the water"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Chemical disinfection is unnecessary if filtration is thorough enough"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Water quality testing occurs only after treatment is fully complete"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçadaki bilgilerden mantıksal olarak çıkarılabilecek doğru sonuç budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-role-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SPECIFIC ROLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "In many Western business settings, a pause in conversation is often interpreted as awkward, prompting someone to quickly fill the gap with words. In several East Asian cultures, however, silence during a discussion can signal thoughtful consideration, and interrupting too soon may be seen as impatient. Visitors unfamiliar with this difference sometimes misread a silent pause as rejection of their proposal, when their counterpart may simply be reflecting carefully. Business consultants often advise clients to resist the instinct to speak again immediately after making a point. Many professionals who work internationally report that they begin to appreciate the value of unhurried pauses, finding that decisions made after longer reflection tend to be more carefully considered.\n\n32. According to the passage, what is the role of silence in some East Asian business settings?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "It is used only when a discussion has failed"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "It always signals rejection of a proposal"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "It can indicate thoughtful consideration rather than discomfort"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "It is considered rude regardless of context"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "It replaces the need for spoken language entirely"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçada belirtilen role göre doğru seçenek budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-true-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (TRUE STATEMENT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "In many Western business settings, a pause in conversation is often interpreted as awkward, prompting someone to quickly fill the gap with words. In several East Asian cultures, however, silence during a discussion can signal thoughtful consideration, and interrupting too soon may be seen as impatient. Visitors unfamiliar with this difference sometimes misread a silent pause as rejection of their proposal, when their counterpart may simply be reflecting carefully. Business consultants often advise clients to resist the instinct to speak again immediately after making a point. Many professionals who work internationally report that they begin to appreciate the value of unhurried pauses, finding that decisions made after longer reflection tend to be more carefully considered.\n\n33. According to the passage, which of the following is true?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Visitors never misinterpret silence when working internationally"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Business consultants always advise clients to fill pauses with more words"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Some professionals come to appreciate the value of pauses over time"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Silence is interpreted identically in Western and East Asian cultures"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Interrupting quickly is considered polite in East Asian business settings"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçayla örtüşen tek doğru ifade budur; diğerleri parçayla çelişmekte veya parçada yer almamaktadır. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-attitude-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (AUTHOR'S ATTITUDE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "In many Western business settings, a pause in conversation is often interpreted as awkward, prompting someone to quickly fill the gap with words. In several East Asian cultures, however, silence during a discussion can signal thoughtful consideration, and interrupting too soon may be seen as impatient. Visitors unfamiliar with this difference sometimes misread a silent pause as rejection of their proposal, when their counterpart may simply be reflecting carefully. Business consultants often advise clients to resist the instinct to speak again immediately after making a point. Many professionals who work internationally report that they begin to appreciate the value of unhurried pauses, finding that decisions made after longer reflection tend to be more carefully considered.\n\n34. What is the author's attitude towards understanding a culture's relationship with silence?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Indifferent"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Neutral"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Optimistic"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Critical"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Dismissive"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçanın genel tonu ve kullanılan ifadeler, yazarın 'Optimistic' bir tutum sergilediğini göstermektedir. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-inferref-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (INFERENCE FROM REFERENCE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Search engines now provide answers to almost any question within a fraction of a second. Yet some educators worry that this instant access may be quietly undermining the value of asking better questions. Socrates taught almost entirely through questioning, believing that genuine understanding emerges not from being handed a fact but from being guided through questions that expose gaps in one's own reasoning. A student who simply searches for an answer often stops at the first satisfactory result, never encountering the productive confusion that leads to deeper insight. Some teachers have responded by deliberately designing assignments that cannot be solved through a single search query, requiring students to synthesise and compare multiple conflicting sources.\n\n38. What can be inferred from the author's reference to Socrates's method of questioning?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Ancient teaching methods cannot be applied to modern classrooms"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Socrates believed instant answers were more valuable than questions"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Genuine understanding may depend more on the quality of questions asked than on quick answers"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Search engines have made questioning entirely unnecessary"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Socrates rejected any form of structured teaching"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Yazarın atıfta bulunduğu görüşten çıkarılabilecek en tutarlı sonuç budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-stated-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (STATED FACT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Search engines now provide answers to almost any question within a fraction of a second. Yet some educators worry that this instant access may be quietly undermining the value of asking better questions. Socrates taught almost entirely through questioning, believing that genuine understanding emerges not from being handed a fact but from being guided through questions that expose gaps in one's own reasoning. A student who simply searches for an answer often stops at the first satisfactory result, never encountering the productive confusion that leads to deeper insight. Some teachers have responded by deliberately designing assignments that cannot be solved through a single search query, requiring students to synthesise and compare multiple conflicting sources.\n\n39. It is stated in the passage that ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "search engines have completely replaced traditional teaching methods"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "all teachers now design assignments that reject the use of search engines"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "some educators create assignments that cannot be solved through a single search"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Socrates believed facts were more valuable than questions"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "students never encounter confusion when they use search engines"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçada doğrudan ifade edilen bilgiye uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-title-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (BEST TITLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Search engines now provide answers to almost any question within a fraction of a second. Yet some educators worry that this instant access may be quietly undermining the value of asking better questions. Socrates taught almost entirely through questioning, believing that genuine understanding emerges not from being handed a fact but from being guided through questions that expose gaps in one's own reasoning. A student who simply searches for an answer often stops at the first satisfactory result, never encountering the productive confusion that leads to deeper insight. Some teachers have responded by deliberately designing assignments that cannot be solved through a single search query, requiring students to synthesise and compare multiple conflicting sources.\n\n40. Which of the following could be the best title for the passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The Complete History of the Socratic Method"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Why Search Engines Should Be Banned From Classrooms"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Teaching the Art of Questioning in a Search-Engine Age"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "How Modern Technology Has Replaced Ancient Philosophy"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The Decline of Curiosity Among Modern Students"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçanın tamamını en kapsamlı ve dengeli şekilde özetleyen başlık budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-detail-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SKILL-BENEFIT DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Acquiring a second language requires the brain to manage two linguistic systems simultaneously, constantly suppressing one language while actively using another. This ongoing mental effort appears to strengthen executive function, which includes filtering out irrelevant information and switching flexibly between tasks. Researchers comparing bilingual and monolingual individuals have found that bilinguals often perform better on tasks measuring mental flexibility, even when the tasks have nothing directly to do with language. Some studies suggest lifelong bilingualism may be associated with a delayed onset of certain age-related cognitive declines, though researchers caution that other lifestyle factors likely contribute as well.\n\n41. According to the passage, learning a second language helps individuals ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "eliminate cultural differences in how concepts are structured"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "avoid the need to suppress their native language entirely"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "strengthen executive function skills such as filtering information and switching tasks"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "guarantee a delayed onset of all forms of cognitive decline"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "rely on a single linguistic system rather than managing multiple ones"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen faydaya uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-pointed-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (POINTED-OUT DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Acquiring a second language requires the brain to manage two linguistic systems simultaneously, constantly suppressing one language while actively using another. This ongoing mental effort appears to strengthen executive function, which includes filtering out irrelevant information and switching flexibly between tasks. Researchers comparing bilingual and monolingual individuals have found that bilinguals often perform better on tasks measuring mental flexibility, even when the tasks have nothing directly to do with language. Some studies suggest lifelong bilingualism may be associated with a delayed onset of certain age-related cognitive declines, though researchers caution that other lifestyle factors likely contribute as well.\n\n42. It is pointed out in the passage that researchers studying bilingualism and cognitive decline ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "reject the idea that bilingualism affects executive function"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "have found no connection whatsoever between the two"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "caution that other lifestyle factors likely also play a role"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "believe bilingualism is the sole cause of delayed cognitive decline"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "have concluded that monolinguals experience no cognitive decline"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçada özellikle vurgulanan noktaya uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-purpose-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (AUTHOR'S PRIMARY PURPOSE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Acquiring a second language requires the brain to manage two linguistic systems simultaneously, constantly suppressing one language while actively using another. This ongoing mental effort appears to strengthen executive function, which includes filtering out irrelevant information and switching flexibly between tasks. Researchers comparing bilingual and monolingual individuals have found that bilinguals often perform better on tasks measuring mental flexibility, even when the tasks have nothing directly to do with language. Some studies suggest lifelong bilingualism may be associated with a delayed onset of certain age-related cognitive declines, though researchers caution that other lifestyle factors likely contribute as well.\n\n43. What is the author's primary purpose in this passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "To convince readers that bilingualism guarantees a longer lifespan"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "To argue that monolingual individuals face significant cognitive disadvantages"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "To explain how learning a second language can enhance cognitive flexibility"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "To criticise language education programmes for starting too late"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "To describe the grammatical structures of specific world languages"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçanın bütünü, belirtilen faydayı açıklamaya odaklandığından yazarın asıl amacı budur. Cevap: C."}], "4": [{"id": "ydtozg6-a-reason-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (ANALOGY REASON)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Airport security screening functions as a layered filter, designed so that even if one method fails to detect a threat, another is likely to catch it. Passengers first pass through a walk-through metal detector or full-body scanner, which reveals concealed metallic or unusual objects. Carry-on bags travel separately through an X-ray machine, where trained officers examine the internal contents on a screen. Random additional checks, including explosive trace detection swabs, are applied to a percentage of passengers and bags regardless of how routine they appear, preventing the process from becoming entirely predictable. Behavioural detection officers, trained to notice unusual signs of nervousness, add a further human layer that machines alone cannot replicate. Because no single method catches every possible threat, aviation security relies on the combined effect of these overlapping checks.\n\n35. The passage describes airport security screening as a layered filter because it ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "eliminates the need for human officers entirely"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "focuses exclusively on scanning carry-on baggage"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "relies on a single highly advanced machine to detect all threats"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "combines several different detection methods so that no single failure goes unnoticed"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "applies the same checks to every passenger without variation"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçadaki benzetme, doğru seçenekte belirtilen özelliği somutlaştırmak için kullanılmıştır. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-a-detail-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SYSTEM DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Airport security screening functions as a layered filter, designed so that even if one method fails to detect a threat, another is likely to catch it. Passengers first pass through a walk-through metal detector or full-body scanner, which reveals concealed metallic or unusual objects. Carry-on bags travel separately through an X-ray machine, where trained officers examine the internal contents on a screen. Random additional checks, including explosive trace detection swabs, are applied to a percentage of passengers and bags regardless of how routine they appear, preventing the process from becoming entirely predictable. Behavioural detection officers, trained to notice unusual signs of nervousness, add a further human layer that machines alone cannot replicate. Because no single method catches every possible threat, aviation security relies on the combined effect of these overlapping checks.\n\n36. According to the passage, random additional checks are applied ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "only when a metal detector produces an alert"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "after a passenger has already boarded the aircraft"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "only to passengers who appear nervous or evasive"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "to a percentage of passengers and bags regardless of how routine they seem"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "exclusively to carry-on baggage rather than passengers"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen bilgiye göre doğru seçenek budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-a-infer-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SYSTEM INFERENCE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Airport security screening functions as a layered filter, designed so that even if one method fails to detect a threat, another is likely to catch it. Passengers first pass through a walk-through metal detector or full-body scanner, which reveals concealed metallic or unusual objects. Carry-on bags travel separately through an X-ray machine, where trained officers examine the internal contents on a screen. Random additional checks, including explosive trace detection swabs, are applied to a percentage of passengers and bags regardless of how routine they appear, preventing the process from becoming entirely predictable. Behavioural detection officers, trained to notice unusual signs of nervousness, add a further human layer that machines alone cannot replicate. Because no single method catches every possible threat, aviation security relies on the combined effect of these overlapping checks.\n\n37. What can be inferred from the passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Full-body scanners have made X-ray machines unnecessary"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Machines alone are considered sufficient for detecting all security threats"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Behavioural detection is more reliable than X-ray screening"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Combining different detection methods increases the likelihood of catching a threat"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Random checks are applied only when suspicious behaviour is observed"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçadaki bilgilerden mantıksal olarak çıkarılabilecek doğru sonuç budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-role-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SPECIFIC ROLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Selecting a gift while travelling abroad can be surprisingly complicated, since customs surrounding what is appropriate to give differ considerably from one culture to another. In some countries, giving a clock as a gift is considered deeply unlucky, while in others, presenting a gift wrapped in white paper may unintentionally evoke funeral traditions. The number of items given can also carry unexpected significance, and even the act of opening a gift can vary, with some cultures expecting the recipient to open it immediately and others considering this presumptuous. Travellers who fail to research such customs risk causing unintended offence despite their good intentions, which is why many businesspeople consult local colleagues before selecting a gift.\n\n32. According to the passage, what is the role of local colleagues or guides when selecting a gift abroad?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "They replace the need to understand any local traditions"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "They are consulted only after a gift has already been given"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "They eliminate all cultural differences surrounding gift-giving"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "They help travellers avoid unintentionally causing offence through unfamiliar customs"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "They are only necessary when giving gifts in groups of four"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçada belirtilen role göre doğru seçenek budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-true-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (TRUE STATEMENT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Selecting a gift while travelling abroad can be surprisingly complicated, since customs surrounding what is appropriate to give differ considerably from one culture to another. In some countries, giving a clock as a gift is considered deeply unlucky, while in others, presenting a gift wrapped in white paper may unintentionally evoke funeral traditions. The number of items given can also carry unexpected significance, and even the act of opening a gift can vary, with some cultures expecting the recipient to open it immediately and others considering this presumptuous. Travellers who fail to research such customs risk causing unintended offence despite their good intentions, which is why many businesspeople consult local colleagues before selecting a gift.\n\n33. According to the passage, which of the following is true?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Good intentions always prevent any risk of causing offence"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "A clock is considered a lucky gift in every culture"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "All cultures expect gifts to be opened immediately in front of the giver"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "The number of items in a gift can carry cultural significance"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "White wrapping paper is universally considered a neutral choice"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçayla örtüşen tek doğru ifade budur; diğerleri parçayla çelişmekte veya parçada yer almamaktadır. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-attitude-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (AUTHOR'S ATTITUDE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Selecting a gift while travelling abroad can be surprisingly complicated, since customs surrounding what is appropriate to give differ considerably from one culture to another. In some countries, giving a clock as a gift is considered deeply unlucky, while in others, presenting a gift wrapped in white paper may unintentionally evoke funeral traditions. The number of items given can also carry unexpected significance, and even the act of opening a gift can vary, with some cultures expecting the recipient to open it immediately and others considering this presumptuous. Travellers who fail to research such customs risk causing unintended offence despite their good intentions, which is why many businesspeople consult local colleagues before selecting a gift.\n\n34. What is the author's attitude towards travellers who fail to research gift-giving customs?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Indifferent"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Neutral"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Optimistic"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Critical"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Dismissive"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçanın genel tonu ve kullanılan ifadeler, yazarın 'Critical' bir tutum sergilediğini göstermektedir. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-inferref-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (INFERENCE FROM REFERENCE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Digital note-taking apps now allow users to store nearly unlimited information, searchable instantly, freeing people from memorising details themselves. Yet this convenience may come with a cost. The Roman orator Cicero relied on a memory technique known as the method of loci, mentally placing pieces of information within an imagined physical space so that recalling a speech simply meant walking through that space mentally. Modern cognitive research has confirmed that actively organising and retrieving information strengthens memory far more effectively than passively storing it externally. Studies comparing students who take handwritten notes with those who type suggest that the physical, effortful process of organising information by hand often produces stronger long-term recall.\n\n38. What can be inferred from the author's reference to Cicero's method of loci?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Digital note-taking apps use the exact same technique as Cicero's method"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Roman orators never relied on any form of memory technique"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Cicero believed memory could not be improved through practice"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Actively organising information may strengthen memory more than simply storing it externally"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Ancient memory techniques have been proven entirely ineffective"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Yazarın atıfta bulunduğu görüşten çıkarılabilecek en tutarlı sonuç budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-stated-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (STATED FACT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Digital note-taking apps now allow users to store nearly unlimited information, searchable instantly, freeing people from memorising details themselves. Yet this convenience may come with a cost. The Roman orator Cicero relied on a memory technique known as the method of loci, mentally placing pieces of information within an imagined physical space so that recalling a speech simply meant walking through that space mentally. Modern cognitive research has confirmed that actively organising and retrieving information strengthens memory far more effectively than passively storing it externally. Studies comparing students who take handwritten notes with those who type suggest that the physical, effortful process of organising information by hand often produces stronger long-term recall.\n\n39. It is stated in the passage that ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Cicero's method of loci is no longer relevant to any modern research"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "storing information externally always strengthens memory over time"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "typed notes always produce stronger long-term recall than handwritten ones"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "handwritten note-taking is associated with stronger long-term recall in some studies"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "digital apps have completely replaced the need for human memory"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçada doğrudan ifade edilen bilgiye uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-title-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (BEST TITLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Digital note-taking apps now allow users to store nearly unlimited information, searchable instantly, freeing people from memorising details themselves. Yet this convenience may come with a cost. The Roman orator Cicero relied on a memory technique known as the method of loci, mentally placing pieces of information within an imagined physical space so that recalling a speech simply meant walking through that space mentally. Modern cognitive research has confirmed that actively organising and retrieving information strengthens memory far more effectively than passively storing it externally. Studies comparing students who take handwritten notes with those who type suggest that the physical, effortful process of organising information by hand often produces stronger long-term recall.\n\n40. Which of the following could be the best title for the passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "How Smartphones Have Replaced Human Memory Entirely"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The Complete Biography of Cicero the Orator"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Why Digital Note-Taking Apps Should Be Abandoned"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "What Ancient Memory Techniques Reveal About Modern Learning"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The Decline of Handwriting in Modern Classrooms"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçanın tamamını en kapsamlı ve dengeli şekilde özetleyen başlık budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-detail-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SKILL-BENEFIT DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Participating in team sports requires far more than physical skill; it also demands coordination with teammates, quick communication under pressure, and the ability to manage frustration when a play does not go as planned. Young athletes must trust a teammate's judgement, accept criticism from a coach, and balance individual ambition with shared goals. Researchers have found that regular participation in structured team sports is associated with improvements in cooperation, emotional regulation, and resilience following setbacks. Coaches who emphasise effort and teamwork over winning alone appear to produce even stronger effects on these social and emotional outcomes.\n\n41. According to the passage, participating in team sports helps individuals ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "eliminate the need for constructive criticism from coaches"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "rely solely on physical skill rather than communication"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "avoid the need to manage frustration during a game"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "develop social and emotional competencies such as cooperation and resilience"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "focus exclusively on individual achievement over teamwork"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen faydaya uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-pointed-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (POINTED-OUT DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Participating in team sports requires far more than physical skill; it also demands coordination with teammates, quick communication under pressure, and the ability to manage frustration when a play does not go as planned. Young athletes must trust a teammate's judgement, accept criticism from a coach, and balance individual ambition with shared goals. Researchers have found that regular participation in structured team sports is associated with improvements in cooperation, emotional regulation, and resilience following setbacks. Coaches who emphasise effort and teamwork over winning alone appear to produce even stronger effects on these social and emotional outcomes.\n\n42. It is pointed out in the passage that coaches who emphasise effort and teamwork over winning ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "are less effective than coaches who focus purely on individual sports"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "have no measurable impact on youth development"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "produce weaker social and emotional outcomes than competition-focused coaches"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "appear to produce stronger effects on social and emotional development"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "discourage children from participating in team sports altogether"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçada özellikle vurgulanan noktaya uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-purpose-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (AUTHOR'S PRIMARY PURPOSE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Participating in team sports requires far more than physical skill; it also demands coordination with teammates, quick communication under pressure, and the ability to manage frustration when a play does not go as planned. Young athletes must trust a teammate's judgement, accept criticism from a coach, and balance individual ambition with shared goals. Researchers have found that regular participation in structured team sports is associated with improvements in cooperation, emotional regulation, and resilience following setbacks. Coaches who emphasise effort and teamwork over winning alone appear to produce even stronger effects on these social and emotional outcomes.\n\n43. What is the author's primary purpose in this passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "To describe the physical health benefits of regular exercise"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "To convince readers that team sports should replace academic subjects"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "To argue that individual sports offer no meaningful developmental benefits"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "To explain how team sports contribute to children's social and emotional development"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "To criticise coaches who prioritise winning above all else"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçanın bütünü, belirtilen faydayı açıklamaya odaklandığından yazarın asıl amacı budur. Cevap: D."}], "5": [{"id": "ydtozg6-a-reason-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (ANALOGY REASON)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A networked smoke detector system functions as an early alarm web spread throughout a building, designed to catch the earliest possible signs of fire. Each individual detector uses either a photoelectric sensor, which responds quickly to smouldering fires that produce visible smoke, or an ionisation sensor, which reacts rapidly to fast, flaming fires. When one detector senses smoke, it can transmit a signal to every other unit in the building, triggering alarms throughout the structure rather than only in the room where the fire began. Some advanced systems also send automatic alerts directly to a monitoring centre or local fire department. Regular testing and battery replacement remain essential, since even a fully networked system fails if individual units are not maintained.\n\n35. The passage describes a networked smoke detector system as an early alarm web because it ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "eliminates the need for regular testing or maintenance"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "only alerts a local fire department, not building occupants"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "responds exclusively to fast, flaming fires"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "relies on a single detector to protect the entire building"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "connects individual detectors so that an alarm in one area alerts the whole building"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçadaki benzetme, doğru seçenekte belirtilen özelliği somutlaştırmak için kullanılmıştır. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-a-detail-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SYSTEM DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A networked smoke detector system functions as an early alarm web spread throughout a building, designed to catch the earliest possible signs of fire. Each individual detector uses either a photoelectric sensor, which responds quickly to smouldering fires that produce visible smoke, or an ionisation sensor, which reacts rapidly to fast, flaming fires. When one detector senses smoke, it can transmit a signal to every other unit in the building, triggering alarms throughout the structure rather than only in the room where the fire began. Some advanced systems also send automatic alerts directly to a monitoring centre or local fire department. Regular testing and battery replacement remain essential, since even a fully networked system fails if individual units are not maintained.\n\n36. According to the passage, a photoelectric sensor ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "requires no maintenance once installed"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "is used only in buildings without ionisation sensors"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "reacts more quickly to fast, flaming fires than an ionisation sensor"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "sends alerts directly to a monitoring centre without triggering local alarms"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "responds well to smouldering fires that produce visible smoke"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen bilgiye göre doğru seçenek budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-a-infer-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SYSTEM INFERENCE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A networked smoke detector system functions as an early alarm web spread throughout a building, designed to catch the earliest possible signs of fire. Each individual detector uses either a photoelectric sensor, which responds quickly to smouldering fires that produce visible smoke, or an ionisation sensor, which reacts rapidly to fast, flaming fires. When one detector senses smoke, it can transmit a signal to every other unit in the building, triggering alarms throughout the structure rather than only in the room where the fire began. Some advanced systems also send automatic alerts directly to a monitoring centre or local fire department. Regular testing and battery replacement remain essential, since even a fully networked system fails if individual units are not maintained.\n\n37. What can be inferred from the passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Ionisation sensors are being phased out in favour of photoelectric sensors"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Automatic alerts to fire departments have made human evacuation unnecessary"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Smoke detectors are only effective in buildings with a monitoring centre"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "A networked system will always function correctly regardless of maintenance"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Individual detector maintenance remains important even in a fully networked system"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçadaki bilgilerden mantıksal olarak çıkarılabilecek doğru sonuç budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-role-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SPECIFIC ROLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Sharing a meal in an unfamiliar country often involves navigating customs that go well beyond simply choosing what to eat. In some cultures, refusing a second helping is considered polite, while in others, an empty plate is interpreted as a sign that more food is needed. Eating with the correct hand also matters in certain regions. Visitors unaware of such expectations sometimes cause quiet offence without realising it, since hosts are often too polite to correct a guest directly. Many experienced travellers make a habit of learning a handful of key phrases and observing how local diners behave before joining a shared meal, treating each meal as an opportunity to learn rather than merely an occasion to eat.\n\n32. According to the passage, what is the role of observation before joining a shared meal abroad?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "It guarantees that hosts will always correct a guest's mistakes"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "It is unnecessary if a traveller already knows the local language"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "It only matters when dietary restrictions are involved"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "It eliminates the need to learn any local phrases"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "It helps travellers avoid unintentionally offending their hosts"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçada belirtilen role göre doğru seçenek budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-true-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (TRUE STATEMENT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Sharing a meal in an unfamiliar country often involves navigating customs that go well beyond simply choosing what to eat. In some cultures, refusing a second helping is considered polite, while in others, an empty plate is interpreted as a sign that more food is needed. Eating with the correct hand also matters in certain regions. Visitors unaware of such expectations sometimes cause quiet offence without realising it, since hosts are often too polite to correct a guest directly. Many experienced travellers make a habit of learning a handful of key phrases and observing how local diners behave before joining a shared meal, treating each meal as an opportunity to learn rather than merely an occasion to eat.\n\n33. According to the passage, which of the following is true?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Language barriers have no effect on expressing dietary restrictions"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Using the left hand for eating is acceptable in every region"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "An empty plate is interpreted identically across all cultures"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Refusing a second helping is always considered impolite"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Hosts are sometimes too polite to correct a guest's mistake directly"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçayla örtüşen tek doğru ifade budur; diğerleri parçayla çelişmekte veya parçada yer almamaktadır. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-attitude-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (AUTHOR'S ATTITUDE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Sharing a meal in an unfamiliar country often involves navigating customs that go well beyond simply choosing what to eat. In some cultures, refusing a second helping is considered polite, while in others, an empty plate is interpreted as a sign that more food is needed. Eating with the correct hand also matters in certain regions. Visitors unaware of such expectations sometimes cause quiet offence without realising it, since hosts are often too polite to correct a guest directly. Many experienced travellers make a habit of learning a handful of key phrases and observing how local diners behave before joining a shared meal, treating each meal as an opportunity to learn rather than merely an occasion to eat.\n\n34. What is the author's attitude towards travellers who observe local dining customs before eating?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Critical"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Dismissive"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Indifferent"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Neutral"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Optimistic"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçanın genel tonu ve kullanılan ifadeler, yazarın 'Optimistic' bir tutum sergilediğini göstermektedir. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-inferref-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (INFERENCE FROM REFERENCE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Streaming platforms now offer viewers access to thousands of films, a scale of choice previous generations could scarcely have imagined. Rather than producing satisfaction, many users report spending more time scrolling than watching, a pattern linked to what is sometimes called the paradox of choice: beyond a certain point, additional options can produce anxiety rather than greater freedom. When faced with an overwhelming array of options, individuals often struggle to commit, fearing a better choice exists just beyond the next scroll. Some platforms have introduced curated recommendation lists designed to reduce this decision fatigue. Viewers who use such curated features often report higher satisfaction, even though the underlying catalogue remains the same.\n\n38. What can be inferred from the author's reference to the paradox of choice?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Streaming platforms have eliminated all forms of decision fatigue"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Curated recommendation features always reduce the total number of available options"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Viewers prefer scrolling through options rather than watching content"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "More available options always lead to greater satisfaction"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Beyond a certain point, additional choices may create anxiety rather than freedom"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Yazarın atıfta bulunduğu görüşten çıkarılabilecek en tutarlı sonuç budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-stated-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (STATED FACT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Streaming platforms now offer viewers access to thousands of films, a scale of choice previous generations could scarcely have imagined. Rather than producing satisfaction, many users report spending more time scrolling than watching, a pattern linked to what is sometimes called the paradox of choice: beyond a certain point, additional options can produce anxiety rather than greater freedom. When faced with an overwhelming array of options, individuals often struggle to commit, fearing a better choice exists just beyond the next scroll. Some platforms have introduced curated recommendation lists designed to reduce this decision fatigue. Viewers who use such curated features often report higher satisfaction, even though the underlying catalogue remains the same.\n\n39. It is stated in the passage that ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "the total catalogue of content changes whenever a recommendation feature is used"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "decision fatigue only affects users of streaming platforms, not other choices"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "additional viewing options always reduce the time spent scrolling"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "surprise me features have completely replaced curated recommendation lists"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "users who rely on curated features often report higher satisfaction"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçada doğrudan ifade edilen bilgiye uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-title-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (BEST TITLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Streaming platforms now offer viewers access to thousands of films, a scale of choice previous generations could scarcely have imagined. Rather than producing satisfaction, many users report spending more time scrolling than watching, a pattern linked to what is sometimes called the paradox of choice: beyond a certain point, additional options can produce anxiety rather than greater freedom. When faced with an overwhelming array of options, individuals often struggle to commit, fearing a better choice exists just beyond the next scroll. Some platforms have introduced curated recommendation lists designed to reduce this decision fatigue. Viewers who use such curated features often report higher satisfaction, even though the underlying catalogue remains the same.\n\n40. Which of the following could be the best title for the passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Why Curated Recommendations Should Be Banned"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The Decline of Traditional Television Viewing Habits"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "How Streaming Platforms Have Reduced Viewer Satisfaction Permanently"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "The Complete History of Streaming Technology"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Too Many Choices: Rethinking Decision-Making on Streaming Platforms"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçanın tamamını en kapsamlı ve dengeli şekilde özetleyen başlık budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-detail-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SKILL-BENEFIT DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Preparing a meal from scratch, particularly one involving multiple dishes that must be ready at the same time, requires a surprising degree of planning and sequencing. A cook must estimate how long each component will take and adjust on the fly when one step takes longer than expected, all while managing several simultaneous processes. Educators who incorporate cooking into classroom activities report that children develop measurable improvements in sequential thinking and in patience, since many techniques cannot be rushed. Because mistakes in cooking are usually immediately visible, children also receive rapid, tangible feedback that helps them learn from errors more quickly.\n\n41. According to the passage, cooking helps individuals develop ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "a reliance on rushing through techniques to save time"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "a complete avoidance of adapting recipes to personal taste"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "an inability to recognise mistakes during the cooking process"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "an aversion to following any structured instructions"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "sequential thinking and patience through planning and timing multiple tasks"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen faydaya uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-pointed-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (POINTED-OUT DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Preparing a meal from scratch, particularly one involving multiple dishes that must be ready at the same time, requires a surprising degree of planning and sequencing. A cook must estimate how long each component will take and adjust on the fly when one step takes longer than expected, all while managing several simultaneous processes. Educators who incorporate cooking into classroom activities report that children develop measurable improvements in sequential thinking and in patience, since many techniques cannot be rushed. Because mistakes in cooking are usually immediately visible, children also receive rapid, tangible feedback that helps them learn from errors more quickly.\n\n42. It is pointed out in the passage that mistakes made while cooking ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "have no educational value in a classroom setting"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "can only be corrected by an experienced adult"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "are more difficult to identify than mistakes in other subjects"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "are rarely noticed until long after the meal is finished"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "provide rapid, tangible feedback that helps children learn quickly"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçada özellikle vurgulanan noktaya uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-purpose-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (AUTHOR'S PRIMARY PURPOSE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Preparing a meal from scratch, particularly one involving multiple dishes that must be ready at the same time, requires a surprising degree of planning and sequencing. A cook must estimate how long each component will take and adjust on the fly when one step takes longer than expected, all while managing several simultaneous processes. Educators who incorporate cooking into classroom activities report that children develop measurable improvements in sequential thinking and in patience, since many techniques cannot be rushed. Because mistakes in cooking are usually immediately visible, children also receive rapid, tangible feedback that helps them learn from errors more quickly.\n\n43. What is the author's primary purpose in this passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "To criticise recipes for being too rigid and inflexible"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "To describe the history of cooking education in schools"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "To convince readers that professional chefs make the best teachers"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "To argue that cooking should replace traditional maths instruction"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "To explain how cooking can help develop planning, patience, and adaptability"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçanın bütünü, belirtilen faydayı açıklamaya odaklandığından yazarın asıl amacı budur. Cevap: E."}], "6": [{"id": "ydtozg6-a-reason-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (ANALOGY REASON)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Modern bank fraud detection systems act as a vigilant pattern watcher, continuously analysing millions of transactions to identify behaviour that deviates from a customer's typical spending habits. Rather than relying on fixed rules alone, many systems use machine learning models trained on historical data to recognise subtle combinations of factors, such as unusual transaction location or an atypical spending amount occurring within a short period. When a transaction appears suspicious, the system may automatically place a temporary hold on the account or send an immediate alert to the customer. Because fraud tactics constantly evolve, these systems are regularly retrained using newly identified fraud cases. However, this constant vigilance occasionally produces false positives, where a legitimate transaction is mistakenly flagged.\n\n35. The passage describes fraud detection systems as a vigilant pattern watcher because they ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "continuously analyse transactions for behaviour that deviates from a customer's typical habits"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "eliminate all false positives through machine learning"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "require manual review of every single transaction"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "only detect fraud after a customer reports it"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "apply the exact same fixed rules to every transaction without exception"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçadaki benzetme, doğru seçenekte belirtilen özelliği somutlaştırmak için kullanılmıştır. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-a-detail-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SYSTEM DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Modern bank fraud detection systems act as a vigilant pattern watcher, continuously analysing millions of transactions to identify behaviour that deviates from a customer's typical spending habits. Rather than relying on fixed rules alone, many systems use machine learning models trained on historical data to recognise subtle combinations of factors, such as unusual transaction location or an atypical spending amount occurring within a short period. When a transaction appears suspicious, the system may automatically place a temporary hold on the account or send an immediate alert to the customer. Because fraud tactics constantly evolve, these systems are regularly retrained using newly identified fraud cases. However, this constant vigilance occasionally produces false positives, where a legitimate transaction is mistakenly flagged.\n\n36. According to the passage, false positives occur when ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "a legitimate transaction is flagged because it does not match usual spending patterns"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "fraud detection systems fail to update their models"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "a customer reports a transaction as fraudulent by mistake"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "machine learning models are trained on outdated data"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "a customer's account is permanently closed due to suspected fraud"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen bilgiye göre doğru seçenek budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-a-infer-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SYSTEM INFERENCE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Modern bank fraud detection systems act as a vigilant pattern watcher, continuously analysing millions of transactions to identify behaviour that deviates from a customer's typical spending habits. Rather than relying on fixed rules alone, many systems use machine learning models trained on historical data to recognise subtle combinations of factors, such as unusual transaction location or an atypical spending amount occurring within a short period. When a transaction appears suspicious, the system may automatically place a temporary hold on the account or send an immediate alert to the customer. Because fraud tactics constantly evolve, these systems are regularly retrained using newly identified fraud cases. However, this constant vigilance occasionally produces false positives, where a legitimate transaction is mistakenly flagged.\n\n37. What can be inferred from the passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Fraud detection systems must continually adapt as fraud tactics change"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Fixed rules alone are sufficient for detecting all types of fraud"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Customers are never contacted when a transaction is flagged"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Fraud detection systems require no updates once they are trained"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Legitimate transactions are never mistakenly flagged as suspicious"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçadaki bilgilerden mantıksal olarak çıkarılabilecek doğru sonuç budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-role-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SPECIFIC ROLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Riding public transportation in an unfamiliar city often reveals a set of unspoken rules that locals follow without conscious thought. In some cities, standing on a particular side of an escalator is expected, while in others no such convention exists at all. Conversations at a normal volume may be acceptable on trains in some countries, yet considered disruptive in others. Giving up a seat for elderly or pregnant passengers is expected almost everywhere, though the manner of offering it can vary. Tourists who observe fellow passengers before acting tend to avoid drawing unwanted attention. Over time, most visitors adapt quickly, since public transportation etiquette tends to be learned rapidly through simple observation.\n\n32. According to the passage, what is the role of observation for tourists using public transportation abroad?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "It helps tourists avoid drawing unwanted attention through unfamiliar behaviour"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "It guarantees that locals will always explain the rules directly"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "It only applies to escalator etiquette"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "It removes the need to adapt to local customs over time"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "It prevents any need to give up a seat for other passengers"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçada belirtilen role göre doğru seçenek budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-true-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (TRUE STATEMENT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Riding public transportation in an unfamiliar city often reveals a set of unspoken rules that locals follow without conscious thought. In some cities, standing on a particular side of an escalator is expected, while in others no such convention exists at all. Conversations at a normal volume may be acceptable on trains in some countries, yet considered disruptive in others. Giving up a seat for elderly or pregnant passengers is expected almost everywhere, though the manner of offering it can vary. Tourists who observe fellow passengers before acting tend to avoid drawing unwanted attention. Over time, most visitors adapt quickly, since public transportation etiquette tends to be learned rapidly through simple observation.\n\n33. According to the passage, which of the following is true?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Giving up a seat for elderly passengers is expected in most places"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Tourists rarely adapt to public transportation norms over time"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Public transportation etiquette is always formally written down"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Escalator etiquette is identical in every city"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Speaking at a normal volume is considered acceptable on every train system"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçayla örtüşen tek doğru ifade budur; diğerleri parçayla çelişmekte veya parçada yer almamaktadır. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-attitude-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (AUTHOR'S ATTITUDE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Riding public transportation in an unfamiliar city often reveals a set of unspoken rules that locals follow without conscious thought. In some cities, standing on a particular side of an escalator is expected, while in others no such convention exists at all. Conversations at a normal volume may be acceptable on trains in some countries, yet considered disruptive in others. Giving up a seat for elderly or pregnant passengers is expected almost everywhere, though the manner of offering it can vary. Tourists who observe fellow passengers before acting tend to avoid drawing unwanted attention. Over time, most visitors adapt quickly, since public transportation etiquette tends to be learned rapidly through simple observation.\n\n34. What is the author's attitude towards tourists adapting to public transportation etiquette?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Optimistic"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Critical"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Dismissive"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Indifferent"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Neutral"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçanın genel tonu ve kullanılan ifadeler, yazarın 'Optimistic' bir tutum sergilediğini göstermektedir. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-inferref-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (INFERENCE FROM REFERENCE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "For much of the twentieth century, city planners designed neighbourhoods around the assumption that residents would travel primarily by car, spacing homes and shops far apart. The urban thinker Jane Jacobs challenged this approach, arguing that vibrant, safe neighbourhoods depend on a mix of residential and commercial spaces placed close together, encouraging pedestrian activity that naturally deters crime. Her ideas were initially dismissed by many professional planners. Decades later, urban researchers studying walkable neighbourhoods have found considerable support for her observations, noting that mixed-use areas tend to report stronger social ties and lower rates of certain crimes than car-dependent suburbs. Many cities are now revisiting zoning regulations once considered settled.\n\n38. What can be inferred from the author's reference to Jane Jacobs's view on urban design?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Mixing residential and commercial spaces may foster safer, more connected neighbourhoods"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Professional planners immediately adopted her ideas without resistance"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Modern research has disproven Jacobs's original observations entirely"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Walkable neighbourhoods have no measurable effect on community ties"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Jacobs believed cars should be completely banned from all cities"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Yazarın atıfta bulunduğu görüşten çıkarılabilecek en tutarlı sonuç budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-stated-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (STATED FACT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "For much of the twentieth century, city planners designed neighbourhoods around the assumption that residents would travel primarily by car, spacing homes and shops far apart. The urban thinker Jane Jacobs challenged this approach, arguing that vibrant, safe neighbourhoods depend on a mix of residential and commercial spaces placed close together, encouraging pedestrian activity that naturally deters crime. Her ideas were initially dismissed by many professional planners. Decades later, urban researchers studying walkable neighbourhoods have found considerable support for her observations, noting that mixed-use areas tend to report stronger social ties and lower rates of certain crimes than car-dependent suburbs. Many cities are now revisiting zoning regulations once considered settled.\n\n39. It is stated in the passage that ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "some cities are revisiting zoning regulations to allow mixed land use again"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "modern urban researchers have found no support for Jacobs's observations"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "wide roads were designed specifically to increase pedestrian activity"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Jacobs's ideas were immediately embraced by professional city planners"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "car-dependent suburbs report stronger social ties than walkable neighbourhoods"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçada doğrudan ifade edilen bilgiye uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-title-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (BEST TITLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "For much of the twentieth century, city planners designed neighbourhoods around the assumption that residents would travel primarily by car, spacing homes and shops far apart. The urban thinker Jane Jacobs challenged this approach, arguing that vibrant, safe neighbourhoods depend on a mix of residential and commercial spaces placed close together, encouraging pedestrian activity that naturally deters crime. Her ideas were initially dismissed by many professional planners. Decades later, urban researchers studying walkable neighbourhoods have found considerable support for her observations, noting that mixed-use areas tend to report stronger social ties and lower rates of certain crimes than car-dependent suburbs. Many cities are now revisiting zoning regulations once considered settled.\n\n40. Which of the following could be the best title for the passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Rethinking City Design Through Walkable Neighbourhoods"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Why Cars Should Be Removed From Every City"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "The History of Zoning Regulations in Modern Cities"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "How Suburbs Became Safer Than Urban Centres"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The Complete Biography of Jane Jacobs"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçanın tamamını en kapsamlı ve dengeli şekilde özetleyen başlık budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-detail-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SKILL-BENEFIT DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Participating in competitive debate requires students to research a topic thoroughly, construct a logically coherent argument, and anticipate the strongest objections an opponent might raise, often preparing to argue a position they may not personally hold. This forces students to genuinely understand the strongest version of an opposing argument, a skill that transfers to more balanced thinking elsewhere. Teachers who coach debate teams observe that students improve in identifying weak reasoning, whether in an opponent's argument or in their own. Because debate rounds are judged on the clarity and structure of an argument rather than on which side seems more likeable, students learn to separate the strength of logic from personal feelings.\n\n41. According to the passage, participating in debate helps individuals develop ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "skills in identifying weak reasoning and constructing coherent arguments"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "a preference for arguing only positions they personally believe in"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "confidence in public speaking without any improvement in reasoning skills"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "an inability to separate logic from personal feelings"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "the ability to dismiss opposing arguments without fully understanding them"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen faydaya uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-pointed-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (POINTED-OUT DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Participating in competitive debate requires students to research a topic thoroughly, construct a logically coherent argument, and anticipate the strongest objections an opponent might raise, often preparing to argue a position they may not personally hold. This forces students to genuinely understand the strongest version of an opposing argument, a skill that transfers to more balanced thinking elsewhere. Teachers who coach debate teams observe that students improve in identifying weak reasoning, whether in an opponent's argument or in their own. Because debate rounds are judged on the clarity and structure of an argument rather than on which side seems more likeable, students learn to separate the strength of logic from personal feelings.\n\n42. It is pointed out in the passage that debate rounds are typically judged on ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "the clarity and structure of an argument rather than personal likeability"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "the number of sources a student cites during the round"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "how confidently a student speaks regardless of argument quality"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "whether the student's personal beliefs align with their assigned position"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "which side appears more likeable to the audience"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçada özellikle vurgulanan noktaya uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-purpose-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (AUTHOR'S PRIMARY PURPOSE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Participating in competitive debate requires students to research a topic thoroughly, construct a logically coherent argument, and anticipate the strongest objections an opponent might raise, often preparing to argue a position they may not personally hold. This forces students to genuinely understand the strongest version of an opposing argument, a skill that transfers to more balanced thinking elsewhere. Teachers who coach debate teams observe that students improve in identifying weak reasoning, whether in an opponent's argument or in their own. Because debate rounds are judged on the clarity and structure of an argument rather than on which side seems more likeable, students learn to separate the strength of logic from personal feelings.\n\n43. What is the author's primary purpose in this passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "To explain how debate practice can strengthen critical thinking and reasoning skills"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "To criticise students who struggle with public speaking"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "To describe the history of competitive debate as an activity"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "To convince readers that debate judges are biased toward eloquent speakers"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "To argue that debate should be a mandatory subject in every school"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçanın bütünü, belirtilen faydayı açıklamaya odaklandığından yazarın asıl amacı budur. Cevap: A."}], "7": [{"id": "ydtozg6-a-reason-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (ANALOGY REASON)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "During an outbreak of a contagious disease, quarantine measures act as a protective buffer, separating individuals who may have been exposed to a pathogen from the wider, unexposed population. Unlike isolation, which applies to individuals already confirmed to be infected, quarantine applies to those who have had contact with an infected person but show no symptoms yet, since many diseases can spread before symptoms appear. By restricting the movement of potentially exposed individuals for a period matching the disease's incubation window, health authorities aim to interrupt chains of transmission. Modern quarantine guidelines are calculated using detailed data on how long a specific pathogen typically takes to produce symptoms, though prolonged quarantine can create economic hardship.\n\n35. The passage describes quarantine as a protective buffer because it ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "applies exclusively to individuals who are already confirmed to be infected"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "separates potentially exposed individuals from the wider population before symptoms appear"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "eliminates the need for any isolation measures"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "is based on a fixed period regardless of the disease involved"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "removes all economic hardship associated with disease outbreaks"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçadaki benzetme, doğru seçenekte belirtilen özelliği somutlaştırmak için kullanılmıştır. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-a-detail-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SYSTEM DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "During an outbreak of a contagious disease, quarantine measures act as a protective buffer, separating individuals who may have been exposed to a pathogen from the wider, unexposed population. Unlike isolation, which applies to individuals already confirmed to be infected, quarantine applies to those who have had contact with an infected person but show no symptoms yet, since many diseases can spread before symptoms appear. By restricting the movement of potentially exposed individuals for a period matching the disease's incubation window, health authorities aim to interrupt chains of transmission. Modern quarantine guidelines are calculated using detailed data on how long a specific pathogen typically takes to produce symptoms, though prolonged quarantine can create economic hardship.\n\n36. According to the passage, modern quarantine periods are determined by ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "public opinion regarding the severity of the outbreak"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "detailed data on a pathogen's typical incubation period"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "the economic impact of restricting movement"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "the number of confirmed infections in a given region"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "a fixed number of days applied to every disease equally"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen bilgiye göre doğru seçenek budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-a-infer-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SYSTEM INFERENCE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "During an outbreak of a contagious disease, quarantine measures act as a protective buffer, separating individuals who may have been exposed to a pathogen from the wider, unexposed population. Unlike isolation, which applies to individuals already confirmed to be infected, quarantine applies to those who have had contact with an infected person but show no symptoms yet, since many diseases can spread before symptoms appear. By restricting the movement of potentially exposed individuals for a period matching the disease's incubation window, health authorities aim to interrupt chains of transmission. Modern quarantine guidelines are calculated using detailed data on how long a specific pathogen typically takes to produce symptoms, though prolonged quarantine can create economic hardship.\n\n37. What can be inferred from the passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Quarantine and isolation refer to the exact same public health measure"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Diseases can potentially spread before an infected person shows symptoms"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Quarantine periods have remained unchanged throughout history"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Quarantine measures never have negative social or economic effects"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Isolation is applied to individuals who show no symptoms at all"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçadaki bilgilerden mantıksal olarak çıkarılabilecek doğru sonuç budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-role-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SPECIFIC ROLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Striking up a casual conversation with a stranger can mean very different things depending on where in the world it takes place. In some cultures, commenting on the weather or a shared wait in line is a friendly, expected way to pass the time, while in others, unsolicited conversation may be viewed as intrusive. Questions that seem harmless in one context, such as asking about someone's salary, can be considered deeply personal elsewhere. Business travellers must judge how much small talk should precede a professional discussion, since diving straight into business matters may seem abrupt in cultures that value relationship-building first. Because these expectations are rarely written down, newcomers often learn them only through trial and error.\n\n32. According to the passage, what is the role of small talk before a professional discussion in some cultures?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "It is universally seen as an unnecessary delay"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "It can be an expected step in relationship-building before business begins"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "It always frustrates business travellers regardless of the culture"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "It replaces the need for any formal business discussion"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "It is only appropriate when discussing personal topics"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçada belirtilen role göre doğru seçenek budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-true-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (TRUE STATEMENT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Striking up a casual conversation with a stranger can mean very different things depending on where in the world it takes place. In some cultures, commenting on the weather or a shared wait in line is a friendly, expected way to pass the time, while in others, unsolicited conversation may be viewed as intrusive. Questions that seem harmless in one context, such as asking about someone's salary, can be considered deeply personal elsewhere. Business travellers must judge how much small talk should precede a professional discussion, since diving straight into business matters may seem abrupt in cultures that value relationship-building first. Because these expectations are rarely written down, newcomers often learn them only through trial and error.\n\n33. According to the passage, which of the following is true?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Questions about salary are considered appropriate small talk everywhere"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Some cultures may view unsolicited conversation with a stranger as intrusive"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Business travellers never need to adjust their approach to small talk"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Small talk conventions are always clearly written down for newcomers"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Diving straight into business is welcomed in every culture"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçayla örtüşen tek doğru ifade budur; diğerleri parçayla çelişmekte veya parçada yer almamaktadır. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-attitude-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (AUTHOR'S ATTITUDE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Striking up a casual conversation with a stranger can mean very different things depending on where in the world it takes place. In some cultures, commenting on the weather or a shared wait in line is a friendly, expected way to pass the time, while in others, unsolicited conversation may be viewed as intrusive. Questions that seem harmless in one context, such as asking about someone's salary, can be considered deeply personal elsewhere. Business travellers must judge how much small talk should precede a professional discussion, since diving straight into business matters may seem abrupt in cultures that value relationship-building first. Because these expectations are rarely written down, newcomers often learn them only through trial and error.\n\n34. What is the author's attitude towards newcomers learning small talk conventions through trial and error?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Indifferent"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Neutral"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Optimistic"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Critical"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Dismissive"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçanın genel tonu ve kullanılan ifadeler, yazarın 'Neutral' bir tutum sergilediğini göstermektedir. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-inferref-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (INFERENCE FROM REFERENCE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Classical economic theory, shaped by the ideas of Adam Smith, long assumed that individuals act as broadly rational agents, weighing costs and benefits carefully. This formed the foundation of Smith's notion that self-interested choices, guided as if by an invisible hand, tend to produce beneficial outcomes for society. Modern behavioural economics has repeatedly demonstrated that real financial decisions frequently deviate from strict rationality, influenced by cognitive biases such as a strong aversion to loss. Retailers have taken note, structuring pricing displays to exploit these predictable patterns. Rather than fully discrediting classical theory, behavioural economists generally argue that their findings refine it.\n\n38. What can be inferred from the author's reference to Adam Smith's invisible hand?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Smith's theory has been completely abandoned by modern economists"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Classical economic assumptions may need refinement in light of predictable human biases"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Behavioural economics rejects the existence of any rational decision-making"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Smith believed individuals never act in their own self-interest"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Modern retailers have eliminated all forms of cognitive bias"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Yazarın atıfta bulunduğu görüşten çıkarılabilecek en tutarlı sonuç budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-stated-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (STATED FACT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Classical economic theory, shaped by the ideas of Adam Smith, long assumed that individuals act as broadly rational agents, weighing costs and benefits carefully. This formed the foundation of Smith's notion that self-interested choices, guided as if by an invisible hand, tend to produce beneficial outcomes for society. Modern behavioural economics has repeatedly demonstrated that real financial decisions frequently deviate from strict rationality, influenced by cognitive biases such as a strong aversion to loss. Retailers have taken note, structuring pricing displays to exploit these predictable patterns. Rather than fully discrediting classical theory, behavioural economists generally argue that their findings refine it.\n\n39. It is stated in the passage that ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "behavioural economists aim to completely discredit classical economic theory"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "retailers structure pricing displays to exploit predictable irrational patterns"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "loss aversion has been proven to have no effect on financial decisions"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Adam Smith's theory accounted fully for cognitive biases"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "markets function best when psychology is entirely ignored"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçada doğrudan ifade edilen bilgiye uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-title-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (BEST TITLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Classical economic theory, shaped by the ideas of Adam Smith, long assumed that individuals act as broadly rational agents, weighing costs and benefits carefully. This formed the foundation of Smith's notion that self-interested choices, guided as if by an invisible hand, tend to produce beneficial outcomes for society. Modern behavioural economics has repeatedly demonstrated that real financial decisions frequently deviate from strict rationality, influenced by cognitive biases such as a strong aversion to loss. Retailers have taken note, structuring pricing displays to exploit these predictable patterns. Rather than fully discrediting classical theory, behavioural economists generally argue that their findings refine it.\n\n40. Which of the following could be the best title for the passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The Complete Life and Work of Adam Smith"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "How Behavioural Economics Refines Classical Economic Theory"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Why Classical Economics Should Be Entirely Rejected"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "The History of Retail Pricing Strategies"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "How Modern Markets Have Eliminated Human Bias"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçanın tamamını en kapsamlı ve dengeli şekilde özetleyen başlık budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-detail-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SKILL-BENEFIT DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Chess requires players to consider not only their immediate next move but also several moves that might follow, weighing long-term consequences against short-term appeal. Beginners often focus narrowly on capturing pieces immediately available, while experienced players learn to sacrifice short-term material advantage for stronger long-term positioning. Educational researchers who have introduced chess into school curricula report improvements in students' ability to plan ahead and consider multiple consequences before acting. Because chess provides immediate, visible feedback, students also learn to analyse their own mistakes systematically rather than attributing losses purely to bad luck.\n\n41. According to the passage, playing chess helps individuals develop ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "a tendency to focus exclusively on capturing pieces immediately available"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "the ability to plan ahead and weigh long-term consequences against short-term gains"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "a reliance on luck rather than systematic analysis of mistakes"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "an avoidance of sacrificing any material advantage under any circumstance"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "skills that have no connection to other academic subjects"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen faydaya uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-pointed-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (POINTED-OUT DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Chess requires players to consider not only their immediate next move but also several moves that might follow, weighing long-term consequences against short-term appeal. Beginners often focus narrowly on capturing pieces immediately available, while experienced players learn to sacrifice short-term material advantage for stronger long-term positioning. Educational researchers who have introduced chess into school curricula report improvements in students' ability to plan ahead and consider multiple consequences before acting. Because chess provides immediate, visible feedback, students also learn to analyse their own mistakes systematically rather than attributing losses purely to bad luck.\n\n42. It is pointed out in the passage that chess provides students with ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "no meaningful feedback about the quality of their decisions"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "immediate, visible feedback that helps them analyse mistakes systematically"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "a tendency to attribute losses purely to bad luck"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "skills that apply only within the context of the game itself"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "an incentive to avoid taking any risks whatsoever"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçada özellikle vurgulanan noktaya uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-purpose-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (AUTHOR'S PRIMARY PURPOSE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Chess requires players to consider not only their immediate next move but also several moves that might follow, weighing long-term consequences against short-term appeal. Beginners often focus narrowly on capturing pieces immediately available, while experienced players learn to sacrifice short-term material advantage for stronger long-term positioning. Educational researchers who have introduced chess into school curricula report improvements in students' ability to plan ahead and consider multiple consequences before acting. Because chess provides immediate, visible feedback, students also learn to analyse their own mistakes systematically rather than attributing losses purely to bad luck.\n\n43. What is the author's primary purpose in this passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "To argue that chess should replace mathematics instruction in schools"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "To explain how playing chess can develop strategic thinking and resilience"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "To criticise beginners for focusing too heavily on capturing pieces"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "To describe the history of chess as a competitive sport"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "To convince readers that chess players are more intelligent than non-players"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçanın bütünü, belirtilen faydayı açıklamaya odaklandığından yazarın asıl amacı budur. Cevap: B."}], "8": [{"id": "ydtozg6-a-reason-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (ANALOGY REASON)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A circuit breaker functions as a protective interruption within an electrical system, designed to automatically stop the flow of electricity the moment it detects a dangerous surge or overload. Inside the device, a metal strip bends when it becomes too hot due to excess current, physically separating the circuit before wiring can overheat. Unlike a fuse, which must be physically replaced after it activates, most modern circuit breakers can simply be switched back on once the underlying problem has been resolved. Larger buildings often contain a hierarchy of circuit breakers, with a main breaker protecting the entire system and smaller breakers dedicated to individual rooms, allowing a fault in one area to be isolated without cutting power to the whole building.\n\n35. The passage describes a circuit breaker as a protective interruption because it ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "increases the amount of current flowing through a circuit"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "permanently disconnects a building from its electrical supply"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "automatically stops the flow of electricity when it detects a dangerous surge"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "must be physically replaced every time it activates"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "only protects the main electrical system, not individual rooms"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçadaki benzetme, doğru seçenekte belirtilen özelliği somutlaştırmak için kullanılmıştır. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-a-detail-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SYSTEM DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A circuit breaker functions as a protective interruption within an electrical system, designed to automatically stop the flow of electricity the moment it detects a dangerous surge or overload. Inside the device, a metal strip bends when it becomes too hot due to excess current, physically separating the circuit before wiring can overheat. Unlike a fuse, which must be physically replaced after it activates, most modern circuit breakers can simply be switched back on once the underlying problem has been resolved. Larger buildings often contain a hierarchy of circuit breakers, with a main breaker protecting the entire system and smaller breakers dedicated to individual rooms, allowing a fault in one area to be isolated without cutting power to the whole building.\n\n36. According to the passage, a key difference between a circuit breaker and a fuse is that ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "a fuse detects electrical surges more accurately than a breaker"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "a fuse can be switched back on after activating, while a breaker cannot"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "a circuit breaker can typically be reset, while a fuse must be replaced"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "a fuse responds more quickly than a circuit breaker"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "a circuit breaker cannot protect individual rooms within a building"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen bilgiye göre doğru seçenek budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-a-infer-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SYSTEM INFERENCE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A circuit breaker functions as a protective interruption within an electrical system, designed to automatically stop the flow of electricity the moment it detects a dangerous surge or overload. Inside the device, a metal strip bends when it becomes too hot due to excess current, physically separating the circuit before wiring can overheat. Unlike a fuse, which must be physically replaced after it activates, most modern circuit breakers can simply be switched back on once the underlying problem has been resolved. Larger buildings often contain a hierarchy of circuit breakers, with a main breaker protecting the entire system and smaller breakers dedicated to individual rooms, allowing a fault in one area to be isolated without cutting power to the whole building.\n\n37. What can be inferred from the passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Circuit breakers respond too slowly to prevent most electrical fires"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "A building's electrical system can be organised so that isolated faults do not affect the whole system"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Fuses are considered more advanced than modern circuit breakers"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Circuit breakers eliminate the possibility of any electrical fire occurring"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "A fault in one room's circuit will always cut power to the entire building"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçadaki bilgilerden mantıksal olarak çıkarılabilecek doğru sonuç budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-role-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SPECIFIC ROLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The physical distance people maintain during a conversation varies considerably across cultures, often without either party realising it. In some regions, standing close during a discussion is entirely normal, while in others such proximity would feel uncomfortable. These differences frequently lead to an unconscious dance during cross-cultural encounters, where one person steps closer while the other steps back, sometimes repeating the pattern without either understanding why. Researchers note that misjudging personal space can unintentionally signal aggression or excessive familiarity. Training programmes for diplomats increasingly include guidance on regional norms, though such guidance offers only general tendencies rather than precise rules.\n\n32. According to the passage, what is the role of training programmes addressing personal space norms?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "They guarantee that misunderstandings will never occur"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "They eliminate all individual variation in personal space preferences"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "They provide general guidance, though not precise, universal rules"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "They are only useful for diplomats, not businesspeople"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "They replace the need for any cross-cultural awareness"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçada belirtilen role göre doğru seçenek budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-true-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (TRUE STATEMENT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The physical distance people maintain during a conversation varies considerably across cultures, often without either party realising it. In some regions, standing close during a discussion is entirely normal, while in others such proximity would feel uncomfortable. These differences frequently lead to an unconscious dance during cross-cultural encounters, where one person steps closer while the other steps back, sometimes repeating the pattern without either understanding why. Researchers note that misjudging personal space can unintentionally signal aggression or excessive familiarity. Training programmes for diplomats increasingly include guidance on regional norms, though such guidance offers only general tendencies rather than precise rules.\n\n33. According to the passage, which of the following is true?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Individual preferences never vary within a single culture"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Personal space preferences are identical for every individual within a culture"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Misjudging personal space can unintentionally signal unintended attitudes"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Standing close during conversation is considered normal in every region"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Diplomats no longer require training on personal space norms"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçayla örtüşen tek doğru ifade budur; diğerleri parçayla çelişmekte veya parçada yer almamaktadır. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-attitude-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (AUTHOR'S ATTITUDE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The physical distance people maintain during a conversation varies considerably across cultures, often without either party realising it. In some regions, standing close during a discussion is entirely normal, while in others such proximity would feel uncomfortable. These differences frequently lead to an unconscious dance during cross-cultural encounters, where one person steps closer while the other steps back, sometimes repeating the pattern without either understanding why. Researchers note that misjudging personal space can unintentionally signal aggression or excessive familiarity. Training programmes for diplomats increasingly include guidance on regional norms, though such guidance offers only general tendencies rather than precise rules.\n\n34. What is the author's attitude towards training programmes that address personal space norms?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Dismissive"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Indifferent"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Neutral"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Optimistic"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Critical"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçanın genel tonu ve kullanılan ifadeler, yazarın 'Neutral' bir tutum sergilediğini göstermektedir. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-inferref-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (INFERENCE FROM REFERENCE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The modern minimalism movement, which encourages owning fewer possessions and prioritising experiences, is often presented as a distinctly contemporary reaction to consumer culture. Yet its core ideas closely echo those of Henry David Thoreau, who withdrew to a simple cabin near Walden Pond to test whether a life stripped of unnecessary possessions might reveal what he considered genuinely essential. Thoreau argued that many people unknowingly spend their working lives labouring to acquire possessions that provide little lasting satisfaction. Where Thoreau's experiment was a personal exercise, today's minimalism movement has become a highly visible social phenomenon, complete with bestselling books and dedicated online communities.\n\n38. What can be inferred from the author's reference to Thoreau's experiment at Walden Pond?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Thoreau's experiment was conducted as a highly public social movement"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Thoreau believed material possessions were entirely without value"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "The core ideas behind modern minimalism have historical precedent"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Thoreau's ideas have no meaningful connection to modern minimalism"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Modern minimalism was directly created as a continuation of Thoreau's writings"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Yazarın atıfta bulunduğu görüşten çıkarılabilecek en tutarlı sonuç budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-stated-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (STATED FACT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The modern minimalism movement, which encourages owning fewer possessions and prioritising experiences, is often presented as a distinctly contemporary reaction to consumer culture. Yet its core ideas closely echo those of Henry David Thoreau, who withdrew to a simple cabin near Walden Pond to test whether a life stripped of unnecessary possessions might reveal what he considered genuinely essential. Thoreau argued that many people unknowingly spend their working lives labouring to acquire possessions that provide little lasting satisfaction. Where Thoreau's experiment was a personal exercise, today's minimalism movement has become a highly visible social phenomenon, complete with bestselling books and dedicated online communities.\n\n39. It is stated in the passage that ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Thoreau's ideas have been proven scientifically incorrect"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Thoreau's experiment was a highly visible, public social movement"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "modern minimalism has become a highly visible phenomenon with books and online communities"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Thoreau believed possessions always improve long-term satisfaction"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "contemporary minimalists reject the idea of decluttering entirely"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçada doğrudan ifade edilen bilgiye uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-title-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (BEST TITLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The modern minimalism movement, which encourages owning fewer possessions and prioritising experiences, is often presented as a distinctly contemporary reaction to consumer culture. Yet its core ideas closely echo those of Henry David Thoreau, who withdrew to a simple cabin near Walden Pond to test whether a life stripped of unnecessary possessions might reveal what he considered genuinely essential. Thoreau argued that many people unknowingly spend their working lives labouring to acquire possessions that provide little lasting satisfaction. Where Thoreau's experiment was a personal exercise, today's minimalism movement has become a highly visible social phenomenon, complete with bestselling books and dedicated online communities.\n\n40. Which of the following could be the best title for the passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "How Decluttering Became a Bestselling Book Genre"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The Complete Biography of Henry David Thoreau"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Modern Minimalism and Its Roots in Thoreau's Philosophy"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Why Consumer Culture Should Be Completely Abandoned"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The History of Walden Pond as a Tourist Destination"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçanın tamamını en kapsamlı ve dengeli şekilde özetleyen başlık budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-detail-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SKILL-BENEFIT DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Writing fiction requires an author to imagine, in considerable detail, how a character unlike themselves might think and react to a given situation, often setting aside their own assumptions. To create a believable character, a writer must consider that character's background and motivations consistently, a process resembling the effort of genuinely trying to understand another person's perspective in real life. Researchers studying creative writing programmes have found that students who regularly practise writing unfamiliar perspectives show measurable improvements on tests assessing empathy. This effect appears strongest when writers are encouraged to write about characters from unfamiliar backgrounds rather than ones resembling their own life experience.\n\n41. According to the passage, creative writing helps individuals develop ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "a reduced ability to understand other people's perspectives"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "a tendency to write only characters similar to themselves"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "empathy and perspective-taking through imagining unfamiliar characters' experiences"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "an aversion to considering a character's background or motivations"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "skills that apply only to professional authors"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen faydaya uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-pointed-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (POINTED-OUT DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Writing fiction requires an author to imagine, in considerable detail, how a character unlike themselves might think and react to a given situation, often setting aside their own assumptions. To create a believable character, a writer must consider that character's background and motivations consistently, a process resembling the effort of genuinely trying to understand another person's perspective in real life. Researchers studying creative writing programmes have found that students who regularly practise writing unfamiliar perspectives show measurable improvements on tests assessing empathy. This effect appears strongest when writers are encouraged to write about characters from unfamiliar backgrounds rather than ones resembling their own life experience.\n\n42. It is pointed out in the passage that the empathy-building effect of creative writing ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "is unrelated to a writer's ability to imagine another's perspective"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "is strongest when writers focus only on characters similar to themselves"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "appears strongest when writers write about unfamiliar backgrounds or circumstances"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "has not been measured through any research studies"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "applies exclusively to professional novelists"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçada özellikle vurgulanan noktaya uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-purpose-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (AUTHOR'S PRIMARY PURPOSE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Writing fiction requires an author to imagine, in considerable detail, how a character unlike themselves might think and react to a given situation, often setting aside their own assumptions. To create a believable character, a writer must consider that character's background and motivations consistently, a process resembling the effort of genuinely trying to understand another person's perspective in real life. Researchers studying creative writing programmes have found that students who regularly practise writing unfamiliar perspectives show measurable improvements on tests assessing empathy. This effect appears strongest when writers are encouraged to write about characters from unfamiliar backgrounds rather than ones resembling their own life experience.\n\n43. What is the author's primary purpose in this passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "To convince readers that empathy cannot be taught or developed"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "To argue that all students should become professional writers"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "To explain how creative writing practice can help build empathy and perspective-taking"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "To criticise writers who create characters unlike themselves"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "To describe the history of fiction as a literary genre"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçanın bütünü, belirtilen faydayı açıklamaya odaklandığından yazarın asıl amacı budur. Cevap: C."}], "9": [{"id": "ydtozg6-a-reason-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (ANALOGY REASON)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Modern grammar-checking software acts much like a careful second reader, scanning written text for errors that even attentive human writers frequently overlook. Using algorithms trained on vast collections of written language, these tools compare a sentence's structure against common grammatical patterns, flagging issues such as subject-verb disagreement or inconsistent verb tense. More advanced systems analyse tone and clarity, suggesting alternative phrasing. However, because language is highly context-dependent, these tools occasionally misinterpret intentional stylistic choices as genuine errors. For this reason, most writing professionals treat such software as a helpful first pass rather than a final authority. As natural language processing improves, these tools are expected to grow more accurate.\n\n35. The passage describes grammar-checking software as a careful second reader because it ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "rewrites entire documents without input from the original writer"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "only works on text written by professional writers"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "replaces the need for any human review of written text"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "scans text for errors that even attentive writers often miss"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "always distinguishes correctly between errors and stylistic choices"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçadaki benzetme, doğru seçenekte belirtilen özelliği somutlaştırmak için kullanılmıştır. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-a-detail-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SYSTEM DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Modern grammar-checking software acts much like a careful second reader, scanning written text for errors that even attentive human writers frequently overlook. Using algorithms trained on vast collections of written language, these tools compare a sentence's structure against common grammatical patterns, flagging issues such as subject-verb disagreement or inconsistent verb tense. More advanced systems analyse tone and clarity, suggesting alternative phrasing. However, because language is highly context-dependent, these tools occasionally misinterpret intentional stylistic choices as genuine errors. For this reason, most writing professionals treat such software as a helpful first pass rather than a final authority. As natural language processing improves, these tools are expected to grow more accurate.\n\n36. According to the passage, why do most writing professionals treat grammar-checking software as a first pass rather than a final authority?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Because it requires an internet connection to function"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Because it only works with a limited number of languages"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Because the software cannot detect subject-verb disagreement"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Because it occasionally misinterprets intentional stylistic choices as errors"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Because it is too slow to be useful for lengthy documents"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen bilgiye göre doğru seçenek budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-a-infer-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SYSTEM INFERENCE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Modern grammar-checking software acts much like a careful second reader, scanning written text for errors that even attentive human writers frequently overlook. Using algorithms trained on vast collections of written language, these tools compare a sentence's structure against common grammatical patterns, flagging issues such as subject-verb disagreement or inconsistent verb tense. More advanced systems analyse tone and clarity, suggesting alternative phrasing. However, because language is highly context-dependent, these tools occasionally misinterpret intentional stylistic choices as genuine errors. For this reason, most writing professionals treat such software as a helpful first pass rather than a final authority. As natural language processing improves, these tools are expected to grow more accurate.\n\n37. What can be inferred from the passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "All stylistic sentence fragments are flagged correctly as intentional"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Grammar-checking software cannot analyse tone or clarity at all"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Professional writers no longer rely on grammar-checking tools"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Grammar-checking software is expected to become more accurate over time"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Human writers no longer need to review their own work"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçadaki bilgilerden mantıksal olarak çıkarılabilecek doğru sonuç budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-role-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SPECIFIC ROLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The meaning of being 'on time' shifts considerably depending on where a person happens to be working. In some cultures, arriving even a few minutes late to a meeting can be seen as a sign of disrespect, prompting apologies for minor delays. In others, a stated meeting time functions more as a general guideline, and arriving twenty minutes after the scheduled start may draw little comment. These differing expectations can create friction when professionals from different backgrounds collaborate. International management guides increasingly caution readers against assuming that their own culture's approach to time represents any kind of universal standard. Experienced global professionals tend to observe local patterns during their first few interactions.\n\n32. According to the passage, what is the role of observing local patterns for professionals working internationally?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "It replaces the need for international management guides"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "It is only useful during the first meeting with new colleagues"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "It guarantees punctuality norms will be identical across all cultures"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "It allows professionals to calibrate their expectations rather than assume their own norms apply"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "It eliminates any friction between professionals from different backgrounds"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçada belirtilen role göre doğru seçenek budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-true-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (TRUE STATEMENT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The meaning of being 'on time' shifts considerably depending on where a person happens to be working. In some cultures, arriving even a few minutes late to a meeting can be seen as a sign of disrespect, prompting apologies for minor delays. In others, a stated meeting time functions more as a general guideline, and arriving twenty minutes after the scheduled start may draw little comment. These differing expectations can create friction when professionals from different backgrounds collaborate. International management guides increasingly caution readers against assuming that their own culture's approach to time represents any kind of universal standard. Experienced global professionals tend to observe local patterns during their first few interactions.\n\n33. According to the passage, which of the following is true?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Friction between professionals from different cultures never occurs regarding time"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Rigid punctuality is considered polite by every culture without exception"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Arriving late is interpreted identically across every culture"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "A stated meeting time can function as a rough guideline in some cultures"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "International management guides recommend applying one's own culture's norms universally"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçayla örtüşen tek doğru ifade budur; diğerleri parçayla çelişmekte veya parçada yer almamaktadır. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-attitude-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (AUTHOR'S ATTITUDE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The meaning of being 'on time' shifts considerably depending on where a person happens to be working. In some cultures, arriving even a few minutes late to a meeting can be seen as a sign of disrespect, prompting apologies for minor delays. In others, a stated meeting time functions more as a general guideline, and arriving twenty minutes after the scheduled start may draw little comment. These differing expectations can create friction when professionals from different backgrounds collaborate. International management guides increasingly caution readers against assuming that their own culture's approach to time represents any kind of universal standard. Experienced global professionals tend to observe local patterns during their first few interactions.\n\n34. What is the author's attitude towards assuming one's own culture's approach to time is a universal standard?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Indifferent"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Neutral"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Optimistic"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Critical"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Dismissive"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçanın genel tonu ve kullanılan ifadeler, yazarın 'Critical' bir tutum sergilediğini göstermektedir. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-inferref-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (INFERENCE FROM REFERENCE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Many people now routinely check their phones while watching television or glancing at notifications mid-conversation, a pattern researchers describe as continuous partial attention, a state in which a person constantly monitors multiple streams of information without fully engaging with any single one. Unlike simple multitasking, which involves switching between two focused tasks, this pattern keeps a person in a near-permanent state of alertness. Neuroscientists have found that it can leave individuals feeling simultaneously busy and unproductive. Some researchers argue that this constant partial engagement gradually reduces a person's tolerance for sustained attention. Several workplaces have begun experimenting with designated notification-free periods.\n\n38. What can be inferred from the author's reference to continuous partial attention?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Neuroscientists have found no negative effects associated with this pattern"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Workplaces have abandoned all efforts to address this behaviour"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "This pattern only affects people who use social media excessively"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Constantly monitoring multiple information streams may reduce one's capacity for deep focus"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Continuous partial attention is identical to simple multitasking"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Yazarın atıfta bulunduğu görüşten çıkarılabilecek en tutarlı sonuç budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-stated-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (STATED FACT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Many people now routinely check their phones while watching television or glancing at notifications mid-conversation, a pattern researchers describe as continuous partial attention, a state in which a person constantly monitors multiple streams of information without fully engaging with any single one. Unlike simple multitasking, which involves switching between two focused tasks, this pattern keeps a person in a near-permanent state of alertness. Neuroscientists have found that it can leave individuals feeling simultaneously busy and unproductive. Some researchers argue that this constant partial engagement gradually reduces a person's tolerance for sustained attention. Several workplaces have begun experimenting with designated notification-free periods.\n\n39. It is stated in the passage that ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "continuous partial attention requires less mental energy than focused work"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "this behaviour has no connection to a person's tolerance for deep reading"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "continuous partial attention involves switching briefly between two focused tasks"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "some workplaces have introduced notification-free periods to restore sustained focus"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "neuroscientists have proven this pattern improves productivity overall"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçada doğrudan ifade edilen bilgiye uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-title-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (BEST TITLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Many people now routinely check their phones while watching television or glancing at notifications mid-conversation, a pattern researchers describe as continuous partial attention, a state in which a person constantly monitors multiple streams of information without fully engaging with any single one. Unlike simple multitasking, which involves switching between two focused tasks, this pattern keeps a person in a near-permanent state of alertness. Neuroscientists have found that it can leave individuals feeling simultaneously busy and unproductive. Some researchers argue that this constant partial engagement gradually reduces a person's tolerance for sustained attention. Several workplaces have begun experimenting with designated notification-free periods.\n\n40. Which of the following could be the best title for the passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "How Smartphones Have Improved Workplace Productivity"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The Decline of Reading Habits in Modern Society"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "The Complete History of Multitasking Research"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Continuous Partial Attention and the Cost of Constant Connectivity"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Why Notifications Should Be Banned From All Workplaces"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçanın tamamını en kapsamlı ve dengeli şekilde özetleyen başlık budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-detail-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SKILL-BENEFIT DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Regular volunteering, particularly in roles that bring individuals into direct contact with people facing different circumstances, often produces a shift in how volunteers understand the challenges within their own community. Volunteers who work directly within these contexts frequently report a deeper, more concrete understanding of specific barriers that are not always obvious from outside the situation. Researchers studying long-term volunteers have found that this sustained exposure is associated with increased civic engagement more broadly, including higher rates of voting. The depth of this effect depends heavily on the nature of the volunteering itself, since brief, one-time events tend to produce far weaker and less lasting shifts in awareness.\n\n41. According to the passage, volunteering helps individuals develop ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "an understanding limited exclusively to the specific cause supported"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "a preference for brief, one-time volunteering events"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "a purely abstract understanding of community issues"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "a deeper, concrete understanding of barriers faced by others through direct contact"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "a decreased interest in civic engagement over time"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen faydaya uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-pointed-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (POINTED-OUT DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Regular volunteering, particularly in roles that bring individuals into direct contact with people facing different circumstances, often produces a shift in how volunteers understand the challenges within their own community. Volunteers who work directly within these contexts frequently report a deeper, more concrete understanding of specific barriers that are not always obvious from outside the situation. Researchers studying long-term volunteers have found that this sustained exposure is associated with increased civic engagement more broadly, including higher rates of voting. The depth of this effect depends heavily on the nature of the volunteering itself, since brief, one-time events tend to produce far weaker and less lasting shifts in awareness.\n\n42. It is pointed out in the passage that the depth of volunteering's effect on awareness ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "is strongest during brief, one-time volunteering events"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "cannot be measured through any research methods"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "is identical regardless of how long a person volunteers"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "depends heavily on whether the volunteering is sustained or brief"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "has no connection to the type of volunteering performed"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçada özellikle vurgulanan noktaya uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-purpose-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (AUTHOR'S PRIMARY PURPOSE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Regular volunteering, particularly in roles that bring individuals into direct contact with people facing different circumstances, often produces a shift in how volunteers understand the challenges within their own community. Volunteers who work directly within these contexts frequently report a deeper, more concrete understanding of specific barriers that are not always obvious from outside the situation. Researchers studying long-term volunteers have found that this sustained exposure is associated with increased civic engagement more broadly, including higher rates of voting. The depth of this effect depends heavily on the nature of the volunteering itself, since brief, one-time events tend to produce far weaker and less lasting shifts in awareness.\n\n43. What is the author's primary purpose in this passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "To describe the history of volunteering as a civic institution"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "To convince readers that voting rates depend solely on volunteering"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "To argue that volunteering should be mandatory for all citizens"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "To explain how sustained volunteering can deepen civic awareness and engagement"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "To criticise short-term volunteering events as entirely worthless"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçanın bütünü, belirtilen faydayı açıklamaya odaklandığından yazarın asıl amacı budur. Cevap: D."}], "10": [{"id": "ydtozg6-a-reason-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (ANALOGY REASON)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Noise-cancelling headphones function as an acoustic shield, using built-in microphones to detect incoming ambient sound and then generating an inverse sound wave that cancels it out before it reaches the listener's ear. This technology, known as active noise cancellation, is particularly effective against low, consistent sounds such as the hum of an aircraft engine, since these steady frequencies are easier to predict and counteract. Sudden or highly variable sounds are considerably harder to cancel because the system has less time to generate an accurate opposing wave. Many headphones combine active cancellation with passive noise blocking, where the physical cushioning of the ear cups blocks sound mechanically, providing a second layer of defence.\n\n35. The passage describes noise-cancelling headphones as an acoustic shield because they ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "rely exclusively on physical cushioning to block sound"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "function equally well against every type of sound, regardless of frequency"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "require no power source to operate"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "amplify all incoming sound before it reaches the listener's ear"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "generate an inverse sound wave that cancels out incoming ambient noise"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçadaki benzetme, doğru seçenekte belirtilen özelliği somutlaştırmak için kullanılmıştır. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-a-detail-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SYSTEM DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Noise-cancelling headphones function as an acoustic shield, using built-in microphones to detect incoming ambient sound and then generating an inverse sound wave that cancels it out before it reaches the listener's ear. This technology, known as active noise cancellation, is particularly effective against low, consistent sounds such as the hum of an aircraft engine, since these steady frequencies are easier to predict and counteract. Sudden or highly variable sounds are considerably harder to cancel because the system has less time to generate an accurate opposing wave. Many headphones combine active cancellation with passive noise blocking, where the physical cushioning of the ear cups blocks sound mechanically, providing a second layer of defence.\n\n36. According to the passage, active noise cancellation is particularly effective against ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "all sounds regardless of frequency or consistency"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "only sounds produced within the headphones themselves"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "sounds that occur exclusively at high frequencies"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "sudden, sharp sounds such as a car horn"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "low, consistent sounds such as an aircraft engine's hum"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen bilgiye göre doğru seçenek budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-a-infer-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SYSTEM INFERENCE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Noise-cancelling headphones function as an acoustic shield, using built-in microphones to detect incoming ambient sound and then generating an inverse sound wave that cancels it out before it reaches the listener's ear. This technology, known as active noise cancellation, is particularly effective against low, consistent sounds such as the hum of an aircraft engine, since these steady frequencies are easier to predict and counteract. Sudden or highly variable sounds are considerably harder to cancel because the system has less time to generate an accurate opposing wave. Many headphones combine active cancellation with passive noise blocking, where the physical cushioning of the ear cups blocks sound mechanically, providing a second layer of defence.\n\n37. What can be inferred from the passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Active noise cancellation requires no additional power compared to passive listening"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Sharp, sudden sounds are easier for active cancellation to predict than steady sounds"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Passive noise blocking is unnecessary if active cancellation is present"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Active noise cancellation is more effective against unpredictable sounds than steady ones"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Combining active and passive noise reduction can address a wider range of sounds"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçadaki bilgilerden mantıksal olarak çıkarılabilecek doğru sonuç budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-role-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SPECIFIC ROLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The pace and tone of business negotiations differ substantially depending on the cultural context in which they take place. In some regions, negotiators expect to reach an agreement relatively quickly, while in others, an agreement reached too rapidly may raise suspicion. Raising one's voice during a heated negotiation is interpreted as passionate engagement in certain cultures, while elsewhere it might be seen as a serious breach of professional conduct. Silence following an offer can also carry different meanings. Negotiators who fail to account for these differences risk misreading their counterpart's intentions entirely. Seasoned international negotiators often spend considerable time researching a counterpart's cultural background before a meeting even begins.\n\n32. According to the passage, what is the role of researching a counterpart's cultural background before a negotiation?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "It guarantees that an agreement will be reached quickly"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "It eliminates the need to consider the pace of negotiation"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "It is unnecessary once a negotiator has experience in one culture"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "It is considered less important than understanding financial details"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "It helps prevent negotiators from misreading their counterpart's true intentions"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçada belirtilen role göre doğru seçenek budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-true-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (TRUE STATEMENT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The pace and tone of business negotiations differ substantially depending on the cultural context in which they take place. In some regions, negotiators expect to reach an agreement relatively quickly, while in others, an agreement reached too rapidly may raise suspicion. Raising one's voice during a heated negotiation is interpreted as passionate engagement in certain cultures, while elsewhere it might be seen as a serious breach of professional conduct. Silence following an offer can also carry different meanings. Negotiators who fail to account for these differences risk misreading their counterpart's intentions entirely. Seasoned international negotiators often spend considerable time researching a counterpart's cultural background before a meeting even begins.\n\n33. According to the passage, which of the following is true?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Seasoned negotiators consider cultural research less important than financial details"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Negotiation pace has no effect on how intentions are perceived"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Raising one's voice is interpreted identically across all negotiation contexts"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Reaching an agreement quickly is always viewed positively in every culture"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Silence after an offer can carry different meanings depending on context"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçayla örtüşen tek doğru ifade budur; diğerleri parçayla çelişmekte veya parçada yer almamaktadır. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-b-attitude-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (AUTHOR'S ATTITUDE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The pace and tone of business negotiations differ substantially depending on the cultural context in which they take place. In some regions, negotiators expect to reach an agreement relatively quickly, while in others, an agreement reached too rapidly may raise suspicion. Raising one's voice during a heated negotiation is interpreted as passionate engagement in certain cultures, while elsewhere it might be seen as a serious breach of professional conduct. Silence following an offer can also carry different meanings. Negotiators who fail to account for these differences risk misreading their counterpart's intentions entirely. Seasoned international negotiators often spend considerable time researching a counterpart's cultural background before a meeting even begins.\n\n34. What is the author's attitude towards seasoned negotiators who research a counterpart's cultural background?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Critical"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Dismissive"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Indifferent"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Neutral"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Optimistic"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçanın genel tonu ve kullanılan ifadeler, yazarın 'Optimistic' bir tutum sergilediğini göstermektedir. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-inferref-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (INFERENCE FROM REFERENCE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Video games are often designed around a deliberately calibrated balance between challenge and skill, gradually increasing difficulty as a player improves. This design closely mirrors the psychological concept of flow, a state in which a person becomes fully absorbed in an activity, losing track of time because the task's demands align with their current abilities. Researchers have found that flow can occur across a wide range of activities, from playing an instrument to rock climbing, yet modern game designers have become the most systematic engineers of the experience. Critics note, however, that this same engineered engagement can be used to encourage excessive play, blurring the line between a genuinely enjoyable activity and a deliberately addictive one.\n\n38. What can be inferred from the author's reference to the psychological concept of flow?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Game designers invented the concept of flow specifically for entertainment purposes"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Flow always leads to excessive or addictive behaviour"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Musical instruments and rock climbing cannot produce a state of flow"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Flow can only be experienced while playing video games"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The sense of full absorption in an activity depends on a balance between challenge and skill"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Yazarın atıfta bulunduğu görüşten çıkarılabilecek en tutarlı sonuç budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-stated-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (STATED FACT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Video games are often designed around a deliberately calibrated balance between challenge and skill, gradually increasing difficulty as a player improves. This design closely mirrors the psychological concept of flow, a state in which a person becomes fully absorbed in an activity, losing track of time because the task's demands align with their current abilities. Researchers have found that flow can occur across a wide range of activities, from playing an instrument to rock climbing, yet modern game designers have become the most systematic engineers of the experience. Critics note, however, that this same engineered engagement can be used to encourage excessive play, blurring the line between a genuinely enjoyable activity and a deliberately addictive one.\n\n39. It is stated in the passage that ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "game designers were the first researchers to study the concept of flow"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "flow always results in a deliberately addictive experience"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "difficulty settings have no effect on a player's sense of engagement"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "flow requires a task to be either extremely easy or extremely difficult"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "flow can occur across a wide range of activities beyond video games"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçada doğrudan ifade edilen bilgiye uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-c-title-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (BEST TITLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Video games are often designed around a deliberately calibrated balance between challenge and skill, gradually increasing difficulty as a player improves. This design closely mirrors the psychological concept of flow, a state in which a person becomes fully absorbed in an activity, losing track of time because the task's demands align with their current abilities. Researchers have found that flow can occur across a wide range of activities, from playing an instrument to rock climbing, yet modern game designers have become the most systematic engineers of the experience. Critics note, however, that this same engineered engagement can be used to encourage excessive play, blurring the line between a genuinely enjoyable activity and a deliberately addictive one.\n\n40. Which of the following could be the best title for the passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Why Video Games Should Be Considered Harmful"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The Psychology of Rock Climbing and Musical Performance"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "How Difficulty Settings Have Replaced Traditional Game Design"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "The Complete History of Video Game Design"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Flow, Challenge, and the Engineering of Engagement in Modern Games"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçanın tamamını en kapsamlı ve dengeli şekilde özetleyen başlık budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-detail-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (SKILL-BENEFIT DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Writing computer code requires breaking a complex problem down into a precise sequence of smaller, unambiguous instructions that a machine can execute exactly as written. Beginners frequently discover that a program fails not because their overall idea was wrong, but because a single instruction was slightly imprecise, a discovery that gradually teaches rigorous, step-by-step reasoning. Educators who teach programming to young students report that this process strengthens broader logical reasoning skills, including the ability to identify exactly where a chain of reasoning breaks down. Because coding provides nearly instant feedback, students learn to test hypotheses quickly and revise their thinking based on concrete results rather than assumptions.\n\n41. According to the passage, learning to code helps individuals develop ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "a tolerance for ambiguity in following instructions"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "skills that apply exclusively within computer science classrooms"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "an aversion to testing hypotheses or revising their thinking"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "a reliance on implicit understanding rather than precise instructions"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "rigorous, step-by-step logical reasoning through precise problem breakdown"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçada açıkça belirtilen faydaya uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-pointed-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (POINTED-OUT DETAIL)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Writing computer code requires breaking a complex problem down into a precise sequence of smaller, unambiguous instructions that a machine can execute exactly as written. Beginners frequently discover that a program fails not because their overall idea was wrong, but because a single instruction was slightly imprecise, a discovery that gradually teaches rigorous, step-by-step reasoning. Educators who teach programming to young students report that this process strengthens broader logical reasoning skills, including the ability to identify exactly where a chain of reasoning breaks down. Because coding provides nearly instant feedback, students learn to test hypotheses quickly and revise their thinking based on concrete results rather than assumptions.\n\n42. It is pointed out in the passage that coding provides students with ----.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "a habit of relying on assumptions rather than concrete results"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "skills that cannot transfer beyond computer science"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "an incentive to avoid identifying where reasoning breaks down"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "no meaningful feedback about whether their reasoning is correct"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "nearly instant feedback that encourages testing and revising ideas"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçada özellikle vurgulanan noktaya uyan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg6-d-purpose-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "READING COMPREHENSION (AUTHOR'S PRIMARY PURPOSE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Writing computer code requires breaking a complex problem down into a precise sequence of smaller, unambiguous instructions that a machine can execute exactly as written. Beginners frequently discover that a program fails not because their overall idea was wrong, but because a single instruction was slightly imprecise, a discovery that gradually teaches rigorous, step-by-step reasoning. Educators who teach programming to young students report that this process strengthens broader logical reasoning skills, including the ability to identify exactly where a chain of reasoning breaks down. Because coding provides nearly instant feedback, students learn to test hypotheses quickly and revise their thinking based on concrete results rather than assumptions.\n\n43. What is the author's primary purpose in this passage?", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "To criticise beginners for making imprecise programming errors"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "To describe the history of computer programming languages"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "To convince readers that only children can learn to code effectively"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "To argue that coding should replace all other school subjects"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "To explain how learning to code can strengthen logical reasoning skills"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçanın bütünü, belirtilen faydayı açıklamaya odaklandığından yazarın asıl amacı budur. Cevap: E."}]};
Object.keys(DENEME_YDT_INGILIZCE_OZEL_6).forEach(function(no) {
  if (!DENEME_SORU_BANKASI.YDT[no]) DENEME_SORU_BANKASI.YDT[no] = {};
  DENEME_SORU_BANKASI.YDT[no].ydtIngilizce = (DENEME_SORU_BANKASI.YDT[no].ydtIngilizce || []).concat(DENEME_YDT_INGILIZCE_OZEL_6[no]);
});
const DENEME_YDT_INGILIZCE_OZEL_7 = {"1": [{"id": "ydtozg7-d44-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (HISTORY/TRIVIA)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Leo:\n– Did you know the Antikythera mechanism is considered the world's first analogue computer?\n\nNora:\n– Yes, it was used to predict astronomical positions, right?\n\nLeo:\n– Exactly. It could even track the cycles of the ancient Olympic Games.\n\nNora:\n– ----\n\nLeo:\n– That's right. Its complexity wasn't matched by any device for over a thousand years.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "This explains why the mechanism is seen as centuries ahead of its time."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Was it discovered by fishermen off the coast of Greece?"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "But do we know exactly who built it?"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Then it must have needed frequent repairs to stay accurate."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Is it currently kept in a museum in Athens?"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Leo'nun 'That's right, karmaşıklığı bin yıl boyunca eşleşmedi' cevabı, Nora'nın mekanizmanın çağının çok ötesinde olduğunu belirten yorumunu doğrular. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d45-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (RESEARCH GUESS)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Priya:\n– Have you heard what recent research found about using screens right before bed?\n\nSam:\n– ----\n\nPriya:\n– Well, no. The study actually found that it wasn't the light itself but the content people watched that most affected sleep quality.\n\nSam:\n– That's surprising. I always assumed the blue light was the main culprit.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Wasn't it that the blue light from screens directly disrupts melatonin production?"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "I have no idea, I never really followed that kind of research."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Studies like that change every year anyway, so who can really trust them?"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "I bet it showed that screens make people fall asleep faster, not slower."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Didn't it prove that reading a physical book is always better than any screen?"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Sam'in 'mavi ışığın doğrudan sorumlu olduğu' varsayımı, Priya'nın bunu düzelttiği cevapla ('aslında mavi ışık değil, içerik') tutarlıdır. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d46-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (NAMED PHENOMENON)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Ana:\n– Sometimes I get this strange feeling that I've already experienced something before, even though I know I haven't.\n\nLeo:\n– ----\n\nAna:\n– Interesting, I never realised there was an actual name for that feeling.\n\nLeo:\n– Yes, some researchers think it happens when your brain processes a moment twice in quick succession.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "That's a well-known experience in psychology called déjà vu."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "You've probably just forgotten a similar dream you once had."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "That usually happens when people are extremely tired or stressed."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "I get that a lot too, especially in unfamiliar places."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Doctors say that's mostly linked to poor sleep quality."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Leo'nun ilk cevabı fenomeni isimlendirmeli ki Ana 'gerçek bir isim olduğunu bilmiyordum' diyebilsin; bu, 'déjà vu' cevabıyla tutarlıdır. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d47-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (SCIENTIFIC AGREEMENT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Derin:\n– Did you know petting a dog can actually lower our stress hormone levels?\n\nIlker:\n– Really? I thought it was just because they're so friendly and fun to be around.\n\nDerin:\n– ----\n\nIlker:\n– The one linked to stress? Wow, no wonder I feel so relaxed after playing with my dog!", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Sure, gentle interaction with dogs has been shown to reduce cortisol levels."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Right, but their energy mostly just distracts us from our worries."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Indeed, I believe dogs can sense our exact emotions instantly."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "It is mainly their loyalty that makes us feel emotionally secure."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "People with low energy levels should probably get a dog."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Derin'in 'cortisol' hormonunu belirtmesi, Ilker'in 'strese bağlı olan' tepkisiyle tutarlıdır. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d48-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (TRAVEL ADVICE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Derya:\n– Hey, I know you've been to Rome before. I'm finally going next month. Any tips?\n\nOnur:\n– ----\n\nDerya:\n– Oh, that's a really good point. I'll definitely plan around that.\n\nOnur:\n– Also, you might want to book tickets for the Colosseum online in advance to skip the long queues.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Many museums and churches are closed on certain days, so check schedules ahead."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Keep in mind that tipping isn't really expected in most restaurants there."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Make sure you try the gelato from small shops rather than tourist spots."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "You should visit Trastevere; it's a lively neighbourhood with great food."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "It's generally safe, but watch your belongings around busy tourist sites."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Onur'un boşluktaki önerisi, Derya'nın 'ona göre plan yapacağım' tepkisine uygun olarak zamanlama/program konulu bir tavsiye olmalıdır. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p49-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (CAUSE-PURPOSE STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Audio recorded in noisy outdoor environments is frequently corrupted by wind interference, so sound engineers apply specialized filtering software to clean the recordings without losing subtle vocal nuances.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "As wind interference frequently corrupts audio recorded outdoors, sound engineers apply specialized filtering software so they can clean the recordings while preserving subtle vocal nuances."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Outdoor audio recordings are barely affected by wind interference, so engineers rarely need specialized filtering software to preserve vocal nuances."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Sound engineers cannot preserve subtle vocal nuances in outdoor recordings because wind interference makes them impossible to clean without specialized software."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "To prevent wind interference from affecting outdoor recordings, engineers tend to avoid specialized filtering software and rely on re-recording instead."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Outdoor recordings give clear audio without being affected by wind; therefore, engineers rarely feel the need to use specialized filtering software."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki anlamı (neden-sonuç ve amaç ilişkisini) hiçbir bilgi eklemeden ya da çıkarmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p50-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (PHENOMENON DESCRIPTION)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "There is a mysterious lake in Bolivia that turns bright red during certain months, a phenomenon that puzzles scientists and tourists alike, often attributed to microorganisms in the water.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "A lake in Bolivia turns bright red during certain months, puzzling both scientists and tourists, a phenomenon commonly attributed to microorganisms present in the water."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "A lake in Bolivia turns bright red every single day of the year, which scientists find far less puzzling than tourists do, and is attributed to microorganisms."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "There is a strange lake in Bolivia that scientists and tourists dismiss entirely, since its colour change is not actually caused by microorganisms."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "A lake in Bolivia occasionally appears reddish, a detail that scientists find puzzling but tourists rarely notice, often attributed to changing weather patterns."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "There is a lake in Bolivia whose red colour has never been fully explained by scientists, despite being commonly linked to microorganisms in the water."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki tüm unsurları (fenomen, kimleri etkilediği ve verilen açıklama) hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p51-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (DOUBLE-NEGATIVE MEDICAL STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Progeria, a rare genetic disorder causing accelerated ageing in children, cannot be cured, nor can the underlying gene mutation be corrected.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The rare genetic disorder progeria, which causes accelerated ageing in children, remains incurable, and the gene mutation responsible for it cannot be corrected either."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Progeria, a common genetic disorder causing accelerated ageing in adults, cannot be cured, though the underlying gene mutation can sometimes be corrected."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Progeria, a rare genetic disorder causing accelerated ageing in children, can now be cured, but the underlying gene mutation cannot yet be corrected."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Progeria is a rare genetic disorder that slows down ageing in children, and it has no cure, nor can the gene mutation be corrected."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Progeria, a rare genetic disorder causing accelerated ageing in children, has no cure, but researchers have already corrected the underlying gene mutation."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki çift olumsuzluk yapısını (tedavisi yok, ne de X geri alınabilir) hiçbir bilgi eklemeden ya da değiştirmeden koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p52-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (EXCLUSIVE MATERIAL PROPERTY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Magnetic putty contains tiny iron particles that make it respond only to strong magnets, not to ordinary metal objects.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Because it contains tiny iron particles, magnetic putty responds only to strong magnets rather than to ordinary metal objects."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Magnetic putty is coated with iron particles, which allows it to respond to ordinary metal objects and not to strong magnets."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "The iron particles in magnetic putty ensure that it easily sticks to any metal object placed near it."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Thanks to the particles around it, magnetic putty always responds to strong magnets together while avoiding ordinary metal objects."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "What makes magnetic putty special is the iron content that causes it to react to any nearby object equally."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki 'yalnızca X ile, Y ile değil' dışlayıcı özelliği hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p53-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (NOT MERELY X BUT Y STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Art education should not be a mere training in technical skill but a means of nurturing personal expression and creative thinking.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Art education should be a way of nurturing personal expression and creative thinking rather than a tool for technical skill training alone."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Technical skill training is a fundamental step in order to truly nurture personal expression through art education."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Art education can test students' technical ability instead of helping them nurture personal expression and creative thinking."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Art education can help students develop personal expression, but the necessity of technical skill training should also be reconsidered."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Art education should not only be based on nurturing personal expression but also be supported by extensive technical skill training."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki 'yalnızca X değil, Y' karşıtlık yapısını hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: A."}], "2": [{"id": "ydtozg7-d44-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (HISTORY/TRIVIA)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Mark:\n– Did you know the Dead Sea Scrolls include the oldest known copies of parts of the Hebrew Bible?\n\nElla:\n– Yes, they were found hidden in caves, weren't they?\n\nMark:\n– Right, a shepherd stumbled upon the first scrolls completely by accident.\n\nElla:\n– ----\n\nMark:\n– Exactly. Scholars still debate exactly who hid them there and why.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Then the caves must have been carefully mapped out beforehand."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "That must be one of the biggest mysteries in biblical archaeology."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Were the scrolls written entirely in Latin?"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "So the scrolls were immediately translated after being found?"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Is the shepherd's identity known today?"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Mark'ın 'Exactly, kimin ve neden sakladığı hâlâ tartışılıyor' cevabı, Ella'nın 'gizem' vurgusunu doğrular. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d45-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (RESEARCH GUESS)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Leo:\n– Have you heard about the recent study on chewing gum while studying?\n\nMia:\n– ----\n\nLeo:\n– Well, no, actually the researchers found it only helped with simple, repetitive tasks, not complex problem-solving.\n\nMia:\n– Interesting, I thought it would help across the board.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I never really pay attention to that kind of research anyway."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Wasn't it that chewing gum improves focus on any kind of task?"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "All these studies contradict each other eventually, don't they?"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "I bet it showed gum has no effect on concentration whatsoever."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Didn't it find that chewing gum mainly reduces stress, not focus?"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Mia'nın 'her tür görevde işe yaradığı' varsayımı, Leo'nun düzeltmesiyle ('yalnızca basit görevlerde') tutarlıdır. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d46-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (NAMED PHENOMENON)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Marco:\n– It's so frustrating when I know a word perfectly well, but I just can't recall it in the moment.\n\nSofia:\n– ----\n\nMarco:\n– Interesting, I didn't know psychologists had actually studied that specific feeling.\n\nSofia:\n– Right, and they've found it happens more often as people get older.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "You probably just need to get more sleep at night."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "That's a well-documented experience known as the tip-of-the-tongue phenomenon."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "That usually only happens with words in a foreign language."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "I think that's simply a sign of a poor vocabulary overall."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "It's mostly caused by trying to multitask while speaking."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Sofia'nın fenomeni isimlendirmesi ('tip-of-the-tongue'), Marco'nun 'psikologların incelediğini bilmiyordum' tepkisiyle tutarlıdır. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d47-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (SCIENTIFIC AGREEMENT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Yara:\n– Did you know spending time near horses can actually sync your heart rate with theirs?\n\nTarek:\n– Really? I always assumed it was just because they're such calm animals.\n\nYara:\n– ----\n\nTarek:\n– The one connected to bonding? Wow, that explains why I feel so at ease around horses!", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "In fact, the connection between humans and horses affects our behaviour deeply."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Right, but physical closeness alone can trigger the release of oxytocin."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Indeed, I believe horses can somehow read human emotions directly."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Sure, it is their large size that naturally makes people feel calmer."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "People with irregular heart rates should probably avoid horses."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Yara'nın 'oxytocin' hormonunu belirtmesi, Tarek'in 'bağlanmayla ilişkili' tepkisiyle tutarlıdır. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d48-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (TRAVEL ADVICE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Fusun:\n– Hey, I know you've been to Kyoto before. I'm finally going next month. Any tips?\n\nKenji:\n– ----\n\nFusun:\n– Oh, that's a really good point. I'll keep that in mind so I don't offend anyone.\n\nKenji:\n– Also, you might want to visit Fushimi Inari early in the morning to avoid the crowds.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Many temples close quite early, so plan your visits accordingly."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Keep in mind that it's considered polite to remove your shoes before entering certain buildings."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Make sure you try the street food near Nishiki Market."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "You should visit Arashiyama; the bamboo grove is stunning."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "It's a safe city, but always watch your bags in crowded stations."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Kenji'nin boşluktaki önerisi, Fusun'un 'kimseyi gücendirmemek için aklımda tutacağım' tepkisine uygun olarak görgü kuralı konulu olmalıdır. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p49-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (CAUSE-PURPOSE STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Fresh produce shipped over long distances often loses a portion of its vitamin content due to prolonged exposure to light and heat, so distributors use refrigerated transport to slow this degradation without sacrificing shelf life.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Shipped produce retains its vitamin content perfectly without refrigeration; therefore, distributors rarely feel the need to use refrigerated transport."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Because prolonged exposure to light and heat often causes fresh produce to lose some vitamin content during long shipments, distributors use refrigerated transport so they can slow this loss while maintaining shelf life."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Fresh produce transported long distances rarely loses any vitamin content, so distributors seldom need refrigerated transport to protect shelf life."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Distributors cannot maintain shelf life in shipped produce because light and heat exposure makes it impossible to slow vitamin loss without refrigeration."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "To prevent vitamin loss during shipping, distributors tend to avoid refrigerated transport and instead ship produce as quickly as possible."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki anlamı (neden-sonuç ve amaç ilişkisini) hiçbir bilgi eklemeden ya da çıkarmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p50-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (PHENOMENON DESCRIPTION)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "There is a curious cave in Slovenia where a strange humming sound can be heard deep underground, a phenomenon that intrigues geologists and explorers alike, often explained as air moving through narrow rock passages.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "There is a cave in Slovenia whose humming sound has never been fully explained by geologists, despite being commonly linked to air moving through rock passages."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "A cave in Slovenia produces a strange humming sound deep underground, intriguing both geologists and explorers, a phenomenon commonly explained as air moving through narrow rock passages."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "A cave in Slovenia produces a loud humming sound only at the entrance, which intrigues explorers far more than geologists, and is explained by air movement."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "There is a curious cave in Slovenia that geologists and explorers dismiss entirely, since the humming sound is not actually related to air movement."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "A cave in Slovenia occasionally produces a faint sound, a detail that intrigues geologists but rarely interests explorers, often explained as underground water flow."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki tüm unsurları (fenomen, kimleri etkilediği ve verilen açıklama) hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p51-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (DOUBLE-NEGATIVE MEDICAL STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Huntington's disease, an inherited neurological disorder causing gradual loss of motor control, has no cure, nor can the damage to brain cells be undone.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Huntington's disease, an inherited neurological disorder causing gradual loss of motor control, has no cure, but researchers have already undone the damage to brain cells."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Huntington's disease, an inherited neurological disorder that gradually reduces motor control, remains incurable, and the damage caused to brain cells cannot be undone either."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Huntington's disease, a common neurological disorder causing sudden loss of motor control, has no cure, though the damage to brain cells can sometimes be undone."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Huntington's disease, an inherited neurological disorder causing gradual loss of motor control, can now be cured, but the damage to brain cells cannot yet be undone."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Huntington's disease is an inherited neurological disorder that improves motor control gradually, and it has no cure, nor can brain cell damage be undone."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki çift olumsuzluk yapısını (tedavisi yok, ne de X geri alınabilir) hiçbir bilgi eklemeden ya da değiştirmeden koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p52-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (EXCLUSIVE MATERIAL PROPERTY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Ferrofluid contains suspended magnetic nanoparticles that make it form spikes only in the presence of a magnetic field, not under normal conditions.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "What makes ferrofluid special is the nanoparticle content that causes it to remain completely still near any magnetic field."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Because it contains suspended magnetic nanoparticles, ferrofluid forms spikes only when a magnetic field is present, not under normal conditions."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Ferrofluid is coated with magnetic nanoparticles, which allows it to form spikes under normal conditions and not in a magnetic field."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "The magnetic nanoparticles in ferrofluid ensure that it easily forms spikes regardless of whether a magnetic field is present."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Thanks to the nanoparticles around it, ferrofluid always forms spikes together while avoiding magnetic fields entirely."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki 'yalnızca X ile, Y ile değil' dışlayıcı özelliği hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p53-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (NOT MERELY X BUT Y STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Physical education should not be a mere test of athletic performance but a means of promoting lifelong habits of health and wellbeing.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Physical education should not only be based on promoting healthy habits but also be supported by rigorous testing of athletic performance."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Physical education should be a way of promoting lifelong habits of health and wellbeing rather than a tool for testing athletic performance alone."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Testing athletic performance is a fundamental step in order to truly promote lifelong habits of health through physical education."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Physical education can test students' athletic performance instead of helping them build lifelong habits of health and wellbeing."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Physical education can help students build healthy habits, but the necessity of testing athletic performance should also be reconsidered."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki 'yalnızca X değil, Y' karşıtlık yapısını hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: B."}], "3": [{"id": "ydtozg7-d44-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (HISTORY/TRIVIA)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Sara:\n– Did you know the Terracotta Army was built to guard the tomb of China's first emperor?\n\nTom:\n– Yes, and each soldier apparently has a unique face?\n\nSara:\n– Exactly, there are thought to be over 8,000 figures in total.\n\nTom:\n– ----\n\nSara:\n– That's right. It took decades of labour from thousands of workers to build it all.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Then archaeologists must have finished excavating the entire site by now."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Was it discovered during a construction project?"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "That must have required an enormous amount of time and resources."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "So the emperor personally supervised the entire construction?"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Are the figures made from the same clay used in modern pottery?"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Sara'nın 'onlarca yıl süren emek' açıklaması, Tom'un 'muazzam zaman ve kaynak' yorumunu doğrular. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d45-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (RESEARCH GUESS)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Owen:\n– Did you catch the new research on standing desks?\n\nTara:\n– ----\n\nOwen:\n– Well, no, it actually found no significant difference in productivity, only in reported comfort levels.\n\nTara:\n– Huh, I assumed standing would make people noticeably more productive.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I haven't really followed any of that research closely."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Studies about office furniture change their conclusions constantly anyway."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Wasn't it that standing desks significantly boost overall productivity?"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "I bet it showed standing desks actually decrease productivity considerably."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Didn't it prove that sitting is now considered completely harmless?"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Tara'nın 'verimliliği belirgin şekilde artırdığı' varsayımı, Owen'ın düzeltmesiyle ('anlamlı fark yok, sadece konfor') tutarlıdır. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d46-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (NAMED PHENOMENON)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Derya:\n– Have you noticed that whenever someone near me yawns, I almost immediately yawn too?\n\nUmut:\n– ----\n\nDerya:\n– Interesting, I always thought that was just a random coincidence.\n\nUmut:\n– Not at all, some researchers even link it to empathy and social bonding.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "That's probably just because you're not getting enough sleep lately."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "I think that only happens between people who know each other well."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "That's an actual phenomenon researchers call contagious yawning."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "It's mostly linked to boredom rather than anything social."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "That usually only occurs late at night, not during the day."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Umut'un fenomeni isimlendirmesi ('contagious yawning'), Derya'nın 'rastlantı sanıyordum' tepkisiyle tutarlıdır. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d47-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (SCIENTIFIC AGREEMENT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Nils:\n– Did you know the smell after rain can actually improve our mood?\n\nGreta:\n– Really? I always thought it was just a pleasant, familiar smell.\n\nNils:\n– ----\n\nGreta:\n– The compound released from soil? Wow, that explains why I feel so refreshed during a rainstorm!", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "In fact, the connection between humans and nature runs quite deep."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Right, but the sound of rainfall alone is what calms most people."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Indeed, I believe a compound called petrichor is partly responsible for that effect."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Sure, it is simply the drop in temperature that lifts people's spirits."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "People who dislike rain should probably spend more time outdoors."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Nils'in 'petrichor' bileşiğini belirtmesi, Greta'nın 'topraktan salınan bileşik' tepkisiyle tutarlıdır. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d48-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (TRAVEL ADVICE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Elif:\n– Hey, I know you've been to Marrakech before. I'm finally going next month. Any tips?\n\nHamid:\n– ----\n\nElif:\n– Oh, that's a really good point. I'll make sure to seek those out.\n\nHamid:\n– Also, you might want to visit the souks in the late afternoon when it's a bit cooler.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Many shops close during the midday heat, so plan accordingly."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Keep in mind that bargaining is expected in most of the markets there."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Make sure you try the street food stalls in Jemaa el-Fnaa square at night."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "You should visit the Majorelle Garden; it's a peaceful escape from the busy streets."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "It's a lively city, but always agree on taxi fares before getting in."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Hamid'in boşluktaki önerisi, Elif'in 'onları arayacağım' tepkisine uygun olarak yemek bulma konulu olmalıdır. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p49-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (CAUSE-PURPOSE STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Signals transmitted through fiber-optic cables can weaken over very long distances, so network engineers install signal boosters at regular intervals to maintain data quality without introducing noticeable delays.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "To prevent signal weakening over long distances, engineers tend to avoid installing signal boosters and instead use shorter cable runs only."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Fiber-optic cables carry signals over long distances without any weakening; therefore, engineers rarely feel the need to install signal boosters."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Because signals transmitted through fiber-optic cables can weaken over long distances, network engineers install signal boosters at regular intervals so they can maintain data quality without causing noticeable delays."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Signals transmitted through fiber-optic cables barely weaken over long distances, so engineers rarely need to install signal boosters to maintain data quality."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Network engineers cannot maintain data quality over long fiber-optic cables because signal weakening makes it impossible to avoid noticeable delays without boosters."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki anlamı (neden-sonuç ve amaç ilişkisini) hiçbir bilgi eklemeden ya da çıkarmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p50-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (PHENOMENON DESCRIPTION)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "There is a puzzling forest in Poland where the pine trees grow with a distinctive curved bend near their base, a phenomenon that baffles botanists and visitors alike, often explained as a deliberate technique used decades ago.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "A forest in Poland occasionally has curved trees, a detail that baffles botanists but rarely interests visitors, often explained as a natural genetic mutation."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "There is a forest in Poland whose curved trees have never been fully explained by botanists, despite being commonly linked to a deliberate technique used decades ago."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "A forest in Poland has pine trees that grow with a distinctive curved bend near their base, baffling both botanists and visitors, a phenomenon commonly explained as a deliberate technique used decades ago."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "A forest in Poland has pine trees that grow with a curved bend at their very top, which baffles visitors far more than botanists, and is explained as a deliberate technique."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "There is a puzzling forest in Poland that botanists and visitors dismiss entirely, since the curved trees are not actually the result of any deliberate technique."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki tüm unsurları (fenomen, kimleri etkilediği ve verilen açıklama) hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p51-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (DOUBLE-NEGATIVE MEDICAL STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Cystic fibrosis, a genetic disorder affecting the lungs and digestive system, has no complete cure, nor can the underlying genetic defect be fully repaired.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Cystic fibrosis is a genetic disorder that improves lung and digestive function over time, and it has no complete cure, nor can the genetic defect be repaired."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Cystic fibrosis, a genetic disorder affecting the lungs and digestive system, has no complete cure, but researchers have already fully repaired the underlying genetic defect."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Cystic fibrosis, a genetic disorder that affects the lungs and digestive system, remains without a complete cure, and the underlying genetic defect cannot be fully repaired either."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Cystic fibrosis, a rare disorder affecting only the digestive system, has no complete cure, though the underlying genetic defect can sometimes be fully repaired."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Cystic fibrosis, a genetic disorder affecting the lungs and digestive system, can now be completely cured, but the underlying genetic defect cannot yet be fully repaired."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki çift olumsuzluk yapısını (tedavisi yok, ne de X geri alınabilir) hiçbir bilgi eklemeden ya da değiştirmeden koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p52-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (EXCLUSIVE MATERIAL PROPERTY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Hydrophobic sand contains a special silicone coating that makes the grains repel water only when submerged, not when exposed to humid air alone.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Thanks to the coating around it, hydrophobic sand grains always repel water together while avoiding submersion entirely."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "What makes hydrophobic sand special is the silicone coating that causes it to absorb moisture from humid air only."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Because it contains a special silicone coating, hydrophobic sand's grains repel water only when submerged, not simply when exposed to humid air."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Hydrophobic sand is coated with silicone, which allows the grains to absorb water only when submerged and not when exposed to humid air."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The silicone coating on hydrophobic sand ensures that its grains easily absorb water under any humid condition."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki 'yalnızca X ile, Y ile değil' dışlayıcı özelliği hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p53-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (NOT MERELY X BUT Y STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Language learning should not be a mere memorisation of grammar rules but a means of connecting with different cultures and ways of thinking.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Language learning can help students connect with other cultures, but the necessity of memorising grammar rules should also be reconsidered."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Language learning should not only be based on connecting with different cultures but also be supported by extensive grammar memorisation."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Language learning should be a way of connecting with different cultures and ways of thinking rather than a tool for memorising grammar rules alone."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Memorising grammar rules is a fundamental step in order to truly connect with different cultures through language learning."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Language learning can test students' grammar knowledge instead of helping them connect with different cultures and ways of thinking."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki 'yalnızca X değil, Y' karşıtlık yapısını hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: C."}], "4": [{"id": "ydtozg7-d44-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (HISTORY/TRIVIA)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Ben:\n– Did you know the Voynich manuscript is written in a script no one has ever deciphered?\n\nAmy:\n– Really? Not even the world's best codebreakers have cracked it?\n\nBen:\n– Nope, some even worked on it during World War Two without success.\n\nAmy:\n– ----\n\nBen:\n– Precisely. Some researchers even wonder if it might just be an elaborate hoax.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Then it must contain some kind of hidden treasure map."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Was it written by a famous scientist of the time?"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "But surely modern computers have solved it by now?"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "I suppose that raises doubts about whether it even has real meaning at all."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Is the manuscript kept in a well-guarded vault today?"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Ben'in 'belki de aldatmaca olduğu' yorumu, Amy'nin 'gerçek anlamı olup olmadığına dair şüphe' ifadesini doğrular. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d45-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (RESEARCH GUESS)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Fiona:\n– Have you seen the new study on houseplants and indoor air quality?\n\nGreg:\n– ----\n\nFiona:\n– Well, no, it actually found that you'd need dozens of plants in a single room to make any real difference.\n\nGreg:\n– Oh, that's less impressive than I expected.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I don't really keep up with that kind of research, honestly."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "These studies always seem to change their minds every year."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "I bet it showed plants have zero effect on air quality at all."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Wasn't it that just a couple of houseplants can purify a whole room?"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Didn't it find that plants mainly help by reducing noise levels?"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Greg'in 'birkaç bitkinin bir odayı arındırabileceği' varsayımı, Fiona'nın düzeltmesiyle ('düzinelerce bitki gerekir') tutarlıdır. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d46-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (NAMED PHENOMENON)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Halil:\n– Have you noticed how the years seem to pass by so much faster now than when we were kids?\n\nZeynep:\n– ----\n\nHalil:\n– Interesting, I always assumed that was just my imagination.\n\nZeynep:\n– Not at all, some psychologists link it to how each year represents a smaller fraction of your total life.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "That's mostly because adults have far fewer holidays than children."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "I think that only happens to people with very busy schedules."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "It's probably just because you're paying less attention nowadays."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "That's a recognised effect that researchers sometimes call time compression."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "It's mainly caused by a decline in memory as people get older."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Zeynep'in fenomeni isimlendirmesi ('time compression'), Halil'in 'hayal gücüm sanıyordum' tepkisiyle tutarlıdır. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d47-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (SCIENTIFIC AGREEMENT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Omar:\n– Did you know sunlight exposure can actually boost our mood significantly?\n\nLayla:\n– Really? I always thought it was just because sunny days feel more cheerful.\n\nOmar:\n– ----\n\nLayla:\n– The one linked to feeling good? Wow, that explains why I feel happier on bright days!", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "In fact, the connection between weather and mood affects everyone differently."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Right, but warmer temperatures alone are what improve people's mood."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Indeed, I believe sunlight mainly helps by improving our sleep schedule."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Sure, sunlight exposure triggers the release of serotonin in the brain."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "People who dislike sunny weather should probably wear sunglasses more often."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Omar'ın 'serotonin' hormonunu belirtmesi, Layla'nın 'iyi hissetmeyle ilişkili' tepkisiyle tutarlıdır. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d48-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (TRAVEL ADVICE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Nadia:\n– Hey, I know you've been to Reykjavik before. I'm finally going next month. Any tips?\n\nBjorn:\n– ----\n\nNadia:\n– Oh, that's a really good point. I'll definitely make time for that.\n\nBjorn:\n– Also, you might want to pack layers, since the weather changes quickly there.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Many restaurants there are quite expensive, so budget accordingly."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Keep in mind that tap water is perfectly safe and tastes great there."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Make sure you try the local hot dogs from a well-known street stand."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "You should visit the Blue Lagoon; it's worth setting aside a full afternoon for."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "It's a small city, but renting a car makes exploring much easier."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Bjorn'un boşluktaki önerisi, Nadia'nın 'buna zaman ayıracağım' tepkisine uygun olarak zaman gerektiren bir gezi yeri konulu olmalıdır. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p49-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (CAUSE-PURPOSE STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Old photographs stored in humid conditions often develop mould damage over time, so archivists use climate-controlled storage rooms to slow this deterioration without altering the images' original colours.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Archivists cannot preserve the original colours of old photographs because humidity makes mould damage impossible to slow without climate control."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "To prevent mould damage in humid conditions, archivists tend to avoid climate-controlled storage rooms and instead rely on regular cleaning."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Old photographs stored in humid conditions keep their original colours without any mould damage; therefore, archivists rarely feel the need for climate-controlled storage."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Because old photographs stored in humid conditions often develop mould damage over time, archivists use climate-controlled storage rooms so they can slow this deterioration without altering the images' original colours."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Old photographs stored in humid conditions rarely develop mould damage, so archivists seldom need climate-controlled storage rooms to protect their colours."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki anlamı (neden-sonuç ve amaç ilişkisini) hiçbir bilgi eklemeden ya da çıkarmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p50-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (PHENOMENON DESCRIPTION)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "There is a remarkable spring in Turkey where the water changes temperature dramatically within a short distance, a phenomenon that fascinates hydrologists and tourists alike, often explained as the mixing of separate underground water sources.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "There is a remarkable spring in Turkey that hydrologists and tourists dismiss entirely, since the temperature change is not actually caused by mixing water sources."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "A spring in Turkey occasionally shows a slight temperature change, a detail that fascinates hydrologists but rarely interests tourists, often explained as seasonal rainfall."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "There is a spring in Turkey whose temperature change has never been fully explained by hydrologists, despite being commonly linked to the mixing of underground water sources."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "A spring in Turkey has water that changes temperature dramatically within a short distance, fascinating both hydrologists and tourists, a phenomenon commonly explained as the mixing of separate underground water sources."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "A spring in Turkey has water that changes colour dramatically within a short distance, which fascinates tourists far more than hydrologists, and is explained as mixing water sources."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki tüm unsurları (fenomen, kimleri etkilediği ve verilen açıklama) hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p51-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (DOUBLE-NEGATIVE MEDICAL STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, a progressive disease affecting nerve cells that control muscle movement, has no cure, nor can the loss of motor neurons be reversed.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, a progressive disease affecting nerve cells that control muscle movement, can now be cured, but the loss of motor neurons cannot yet be reversed."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis is a progressive disease that gradually restores muscle movement, and it has no cure, nor can motor neuron loss be reversed."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, a progressive disease affecting nerve cells that control muscle movement, has no cure, but researchers have already reversed the loss of motor neurons."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, a progressive disease affecting the nerve cells that control muscle movement, remains incurable, and the loss of motor neurons cannot be reversed either."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Amyotrophic lateral sclerosis, a rare disease affecting only muscle tissue directly, has no cure, though the loss of motor neurons can sometimes be reversed."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki çift olumsuzluk yapısını (tedavisi yok, ne de X geri alınabilir) hiçbir bilgi eklemeden ya da değiştirmeden koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p52-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (EXCLUSIVE MATERIAL PROPERTY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Self-healing rubber contains microcapsules of sealant that release their contents only when the material is cut, not under normal wear.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The microcapsules in self-healing rubber ensure that sealant is constantly released regardless of whether the material is cut."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Thanks to the capsules around it, self-healing rubber always releases sealant together while avoiding any actual cuts."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "What makes self-healing rubber special is the microcapsule content that causes it to release sealant only under normal wear."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Because it contains microcapsules of sealant, self-healing rubber releases their contents only when the material is cut, not under normal wear."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Self-healing rubber is coated with sealant microcapsules, which release their contents under normal wear and not when cut."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki 'yalnızca X ile, Y ile değil' dışlayıcı özelliği hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p53-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (NOT MERELY X BUT Y STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Scientific research should not be a mere pursuit of publishable results but a means of genuinely advancing human understanding.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Scientific research can test how publishable a result is instead of helping to genuinely advance human understanding."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Scientific research can help advance human understanding, but the necessity of pursuing publishable results should also be reconsidered."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Scientific research should not only be based on advancing human understanding but also be supported by a strong pursuit of publishable results."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Scientific research should be a way of genuinely advancing human understanding rather than a tool for pursuing publishable results alone."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Pursuing publishable results is a fundamental step in order to truly advance human understanding through scientific research."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki 'yalnızca X değil, Y' karşıtlık yapısını hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: D."}], "5": [{"id": "ydtozg7-d44-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (HISTORY/TRIVIA)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Claire:\n– Did you know the Bayeux Tapestry is actually an embroidery, not a woven tapestry?\n\nNick:\n– Interesting, and it tells the story of the Norman conquest, right?\n\nClaire:\n– Yes, it stretches over seventy metres long.\n\nNick:\n– ----\n\nClaire:\n– Exactly, historians still marvel at how it survived nearly intact for centuries.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Then it must have been created using a mechanical loom."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Was it commissioned by King Harold himself?"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "So each scene was embroidered by a single artist alone?"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "But how many battles does it actually depict?"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "That's remarkable that something so fragile has lasted this long."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Claire'in 'yüzyıllarca neredeyse bozulmadan kalması' açıklaması, Nick'in 'kırılgan bir şeyin bu kadar dayanması' yorumunu doğrular. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d45-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (RESEARCH GUESS)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Nadia:\n– Did you hear about the study on background noise and creativity?\n\nRavi:\n– ----\n\nNadia:\n– Well, no, actually it found that moderate noise helped creative tasks, but loud noise hurt concentration overall.\n\nRavi:\n– That's more nuanced than I would have guessed.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I never really pay much attention to studies like that."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Research on noise levels seems to change its conclusions constantly."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "I bet it showed that any noise at all reduces creativity significantly."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Wasn't it that complete silence is always best for creative thinking?"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Didn't it prove that louder background noise always boosts creativity?"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Ravi'nin 'daha yüksek gürültünün her zaman yaratıcılığı artırdığı' varsayımı, Nadia'nın düzeltmesiyle ('orta düzey gürültü yardımcı, yüksek gürültü zararlı') tutarlıdır. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d46-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (NAMED PHENOMENON)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Petra:\n– Sometimes a song gets stuck in my head for hours, even if I don't even like it that much.\n\nAdam:\n– ----\n\nPetra:\n– Interesting, I didn't realise researchers had actually studied that.\n\nAdam:\n– Yes, and simple, repetitive melodies seem to trigger it more often than complex ones.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "That usually only happens with songs you've heard very recently."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "I think that's mostly a sign of a strong musical memory."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "That's probably linked to how often the radio plays that song."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "It's mainly caused by listening to music through headphones too often."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "That's an actual phenomenon researchers refer to as an earworm."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Adam'ın fenomeni isimlendirmesi ('earworm'), Petra'nın 'araştırıldığını bilmiyordum' tepkisiyle tutarlıdır. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d47-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (SCIENTIFIC AGREEMENT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Rina:\n– Did you know laughing with friends can actually reduce physical pain?\n\nDev:\n– Really? I always thought it was just a nice distraction from discomfort.\n\nRina:\n– ----\n\nDev:\n– The one linked to natural pain relief? Wow, that explains why I feel better after a good laugh!", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "In fact, the connection between humor and health runs quite deep."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Right, but spending time with friends alone is what relieves the pain."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Indeed, I believe laughter mainly works by distracting the brain completely."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Sure, it is simply the deep breathing during laughter that helps."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "People with chronic pain should try laughter, since it releases endorphins."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Rina'nın 'endorphin' hormonunu belirtmesi, Dev'in 'doğal ağrı kesici' tepkisiyle tutarlıdır. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d48-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (TRAVEL ADVICE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Serkan:\n– Hey, I know you've been to Bangkok before. I'm finally going next month. Any tips?\n\nAnong:\n– ----\n\nSerkan:\n– Oh, that's a really good point. I'll be extra careful, then.\n\nAnong:\n– Also, you might want to negotiate the price before getting into a tuk-tuk.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Many temples require covered shoulders and knees, so dress modestly."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Keep in mind that spicy food there can be much hotter than you expect."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Make sure you try the floating markets early in the morning."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "You should visit Chatuchak Market; it's massive and has everything."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "It's a busy city, so always keep an eye on your belongings in crowded areas."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Anong'un boşluktaki önerisi, Serkan'ın 'daha dikkatli olacağım' tepkisine uygun olarak güvenlik konulu olmalıdır. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p49-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (CAUSE-PURPOSE STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Crops grown in nutrient-poor soil frequently produce lower yields, so farmers apply targeted fertilisers to boost production without depleting the soil's remaining nutrients.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Crops grown in nutrient-poor soil are barely affected in terms of yield, so farmers rarely need targeted fertilisers to boost production."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Farmers cannot boost production in nutrient-poor soil because low nutrient levels make it impossible to avoid depleting the soil further with fertilisers."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "To prevent low yields in nutrient-poor soil, farmers tend to avoid targeted fertilisers and instead rotate crops more frequently."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Crops grown in nutrient-poor soil produce high yields without any fertiliser; therefore, farmers rarely feel the need to apply targeted fertilisers."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Because crops grown in nutrient-poor soil frequently produce lower yields, farmers apply targeted fertilisers so they can boost production without depleting the soil's remaining nutrients."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki anlamı (neden-sonuç ve amaç ilişkisini) hiçbir bilgi eklemeden ya da çıkarmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p50-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (PHENOMENON DESCRIPTION)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "There is an unusual beach in New Zealand where large, perfectly round boulders lie scattered across the sand, a phenomenon that intrigues geologists and photographers alike, often explained as the slow hardening of mineral deposits over millions of years.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "A beach in New Zealand has small, oddly shaped boulders scattered near the water, which intrigues photographers far more than geologists, and is explained as mineral hardening."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "There is an unusual beach in New Zealand that geologists and photographers dismiss entirely, since the round boulders are not actually the result of mineral hardening."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "A beach in New Zealand occasionally has round boulders, a detail that intrigues geologists but rarely interests photographers, often explained as volcanic activity."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "There is a beach in New Zealand whose round boulders have never been fully explained by geologists, despite being commonly linked to the slow hardening of mineral deposits."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "A beach in New Zealand has large, perfectly round boulders scattered across the sand, intriguing both geologists and photographers, a phenomenon commonly explained as the slow hardening of mineral deposits over millions of years."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki tüm unsurları (fenomen, kimleri etkilediği ve verilen açıklama) hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p51-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (DOUBLE-NEGATIVE MEDICAL STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Type 1 diabetes, an autoimmune condition in which the body attacks insulin-producing cells, has no cure, nor can the destroyed cells be regenerated naturally.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Type 1 diabetes, a common condition unrelated to the immune system, has no cure, though the destroyed cells can sometimes be naturally regenerated."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Type 1 diabetes, an autoimmune condition in which the body attacks insulin-producing cells, can now be cured, but the destroyed cells cannot yet be naturally regenerated."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Type 1 diabetes is an autoimmune condition that gradually restores insulin-producing cells, and it has no cure, nor can the cells be regenerated."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Type 1 diabetes, an autoimmune condition in which the body attacks insulin-producing cells, has no cure, but researchers have already regenerated the destroyed cells naturally."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Type 1 diabetes, an autoimmune condition in which the body attacks its own insulin-producing cells, remains incurable, and the destroyed cells cannot be naturally regenerated either."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki çift olumsuzluk yapısını (tedavisi yok, ne de X geri alınabilir) hiçbir bilgi eklemeden ya da değiştirmeden koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p52-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (EXCLUSIVE MATERIAL PROPERTY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Non-Newtonian fluid such as oobleck contains suspended starch particles that make it behave like a solid only under sudden pressure, not when handled gently.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Oobleck is coated with starch particles, which make it behave like a solid when handled gently and not under sudden pressure."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The starch particles in oobleck ensure that it behaves like a solid regardless of how much pressure is applied."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Thanks to the particles around it, oobleck always behaves like a solid together while avoiding sudden pressure entirely."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "What makes oobleck special is the starch content that causes it to behave like a liquid only under sudden pressure."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Because it contains suspended starch particles, a non-Newtonian fluid like oobleck behaves like a solid only under sudden pressure, not when handled gently."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki 'yalnızca X ile, Y ile değil' dışlayıcı özelliği hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p53-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (NOT MERELY X BUT Y STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Financial literacy education should not be a mere lesson in calculating interest rates but a means of building confidence in lifelong money management.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Calculating interest rates is a fundamental step in order to truly build confidence in money management through financial literacy education."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Financial literacy education can test students' ability to calculate interest instead of helping them build confidence in money management."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Financial literacy education can help build confidence in money management, but the necessity of calculating interest rates should also be reconsidered."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Financial literacy education should not only be based on building confidence in money management but also be supported by extensive interest rate calculation."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Financial literacy education should be a way of building confidence in lifelong money management rather than a tool for calculating interest rates alone."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki 'yalnızca X değil, Y' karşıtlık yapısını hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: E."}], "6": [{"id": "ydtozg7-d44-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (HISTORY/TRIVIA)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Owen:\n– Did you know the Nazca Lines can only be fully seen from the air?\n\nPriya:\n– Yes, and they were made over a thousand years ago?\n\nOwen:\n– Exactly, and no one is entirely sure why the ancient Nazca people created them.\n\nPriya:\n– ----\n\nOwen:\n– That's right. Some believe they had religious purposes, while others link them to astronomy.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "So there are several competing theories about their original purpose?"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Then they must have been drawn using aerial photography."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Was the site excavated recently by archaeologists?"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Are the lines made from a type of coloured stone?"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Then tourists must be allowed to walk freely across them."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Owen'ın 'kimisi dini amaç, kimisi astronomi' açıklaması, Priya'nın 'rakip teoriler' yorumunu doğrular. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d45-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (RESEARCH GUESS)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Jonas:\n– Have you seen the recent research on cold showers?\n\nElena:\n– ----\n\nJonas:\n– Well, no, it actually found the alertness boost was short-lived, lasting less than an hour.\n\nElena:\n– That's a lot less than I expected.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Wasn't it that cold showers provide a long-lasting boost in alertness?"}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "I honestly haven't looked into that kind of research at all."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "These wellness studies seem to contradict each other every few months."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "I bet it showed cold showers have absolutely no effect on alertness."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Didn't it find that cold showers mainly improve skin health instead?"}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Elena'nın 'kalıcı bir uyanıklık artışı sağladığı' varsayımı, Jonas'ın düzeltmesiyle ('etki bir saatten az sürdü') tutarlıdır. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d46-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (NAMED PHENOMENON)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Kaan:\n– Loud, sudden noises always make me jump, even when I'm expecting something might happen.\n\nNihan:\n– ----\n\nKaan:\n– Interesting, I always assumed that reaction was just nervousness.\n\nNihan:\n– Not exactly, it's actually an automatic reflex built into the nervous system.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "That's a built-in response researchers call the startle reflex."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "That usually only happens to people who are naturally anxious."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "It's mostly a habit that people can train themselves out of easily."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "I think that only occurs when someone is completely unprepared."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "It's probably linked to poor hearing rather than the nervous system."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Nihan'ın fenomeni isimlendirmesi ('startle reflex'), Kaan'ın 'sinirlilik sanıyordum' tepkisiyle tutarlıdır. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d47-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (SCIENTIFIC AGREEMENT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Petra:\n– Did you know a long hug can actually make us feel less anxious?\n\nIker:\n– Really? I always thought it was just a comforting gesture.\n\nPetra:\n– ----\n\nIker:\n– The one released through touch? Wow, that explains why hugging my sister always calms me down!", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Sure, sustained physical contact triggers the release of oxytocin in the brain."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Right, but only hugs from close family members have any real effect."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Indeed, I believe hugging mainly works by improving posture temporarily."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "It is mainly the warmth of another person's body that reduces anxiety."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "People who dislike physical contact should probably avoid hugging altogether."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Petra'nın 'oxytocin' hormonunu belirtmesi, Iker'in 'dokunma yoluyla salınan' tepkisiyle tutarlıdır. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d48-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (TRAVEL ADVICE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Zeynep:\n– Hey, I know you've been to Cape Town before. I'm finally going next month. Any tips?\n\nThabo:\n– ----\n\nZeynep:\n– Oh, that's a really good point. I'll definitely check the forecast before planning.\n\nThabo:\n– Also, you might want to book a Table Mountain cable car ticket online in advance.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The weather there can change quickly, so check conditions before hiking."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Keep in mind that tipping around ten to fifteen percent is customary there."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Make sure you try the local seafood near the waterfront."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "You should visit Boulders Beach; the penguins are a must-see."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "It's generally safe in tourist areas, but avoid walking alone at night."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Thabo'nun boşluktaki önerisi, Zeynep'in 'hava durumunu kontrol edeceğim' tepkisine uygun olarak hava koşulları konulu olmalıdır. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p49-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (CAUSE-PURPOSE STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Voice recordings made in echo-heavy rooms often sound distorted, so audio technicians apply digital correction tools to clarify the sound without removing the recording's natural warmth.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Because voice recordings made in echo-heavy rooms often sound distorted, audio technicians apply digital correction tools so they can clarify the sound without removing the recording's natural warmth."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Voice recordings made in echo-heavy rooms are barely distorted, so technicians rarely need digital correction tools to clarify the sound."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Audio technicians cannot preserve a recording's natural warmth in echo-heavy rooms because distortion makes it impossible to clarify the sound without removing that warmth."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "To prevent distortion in echo-heavy rooms, technicians tend to avoid digital correction tools and instead re-record in a different location."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Voice recordings made in echo-heavy rooms sound perfectly clear without any distortion; therefore, technicians rarely feel the need for digital correction tools."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki anlamı (neden-sonuç ve amaç ilişkisini) hiçbir bilgi eklemeden ya da çıkarmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p50-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (PHENOMENON DESCRIPTION)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "There is a mysterious lake in Canada that appears to change colour throughout the summer, a phenomenon that fascinates chemists and travellers alike, often explained as mineral deposits evaporating at different rates.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "A lake in Canada appears to change colour throughout the summer, fascinating both chemists and travellers, a phenomenon commonly explained as mineral deposits evaporating at different rates."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "A lake in Canada appears to change colour only once a year, which fascinates travellers far more than chemists, and is explained by evaporating minerals."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "There is a mysterious lake in Canada that chemists and travellers dismiss entirely, since the colour change is not actually caused by evaporating minerals."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "A lake in Canada occasionally shifts in colour, a detail that fascinates chemists but rarely interests travellers, often explained as algae growth."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "There is a lake in Canada whose colour change has never been fully explained by chemists, despite being commonly linked to mineral deposits evaporating at different rates."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki tüm unsurları (fenomen, kimleri etkilediği ve verilen açıklama) hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p51-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (DOUBLE-NEGATIVE MEDICAL STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Duchenne muscular dystrophy, a genetic disorder causing progressive muscle weakness, has no cure, nor can the damaged muscle tissue be fully restored.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Duchenne muscular dystrophy, a genetic disorder that causes progressive muscle weakness, remains incurable, and the damaged muscle tissue cannot be fully restored either."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Duchenne muscular dystrophy, a rare disorder causing sudden muscle weakness, has no cure, though the damaged muscle tissue can sometimes be fully restored."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Duchenne muscular dystrophy, a genetic disorder causing progressive muscle weakness, can now be cured, but the damaged muscle tissue cannot yet be fully restored."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Duchenne muscular dystrophy is a genetic disorder that gradually strengthens muscle tissue, and it has no cure, nor can the tissue be restored."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Duchenne muscular dystrophy, a genetic disorder causing progressive muscle weakness, has no cure, but researchers have already fully restored the damaged muscle tissue."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki çift olumsuzluk yapısını (tedavisi yok, ne de X geri alınabilir) hiçbir bilgi eklemeden ya da değiştirmeden koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p52-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (EXCLUSIVE MATERIAL PROPERTY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Gecko adhesive tape contains millions of microscopic hair-like structures that allow it to stick firmly only to smooth, clean surfaces, not to rough or dusty ones.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Because it contains millions of microscopic hair-like structures, gecko adhesive tape sticks firmly only to smooth, clean surfaces, not to rough or dusty ones."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Gecko adhesive tape is coated with microscopic structures, which allow it to stick firmly to rough, dusty surfaces and not to smooth ones."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "The microscopic structures on gecko adhesive tape ensure that it easily sticks to any surface regardless of texture or cleanliness."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Thanks to the structures around it, gecko adhesive tape always sticks firmly together while avoiding smooth surfaces entirely."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "What makes gecko adhesive tape special is the microscopic structures that cause it to stick only to rough surfaces."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki 'yalnızca X ile, Y ile değil' dışlayıcı özelliği hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p53-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (NOT MERELY X BUT Y STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Civic education should not be a mere recitation of laws and institutions but a means of preparing students to participate actively in their communities.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Civic education should be a way of preparing students to participate actively in their communities rather than a tool for reciting laws and institutions alone."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Reciting laws and institutions is a fundamental step in order to truly prepare students for active participation through civic education."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Civic education can test students' knowledge of laws instead of helping them participate actively in their communities."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Civic education can help prepare students for active participation, but the necessity of reciting laws and institutions should also be reconsidered."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Civic education should not only be based on preparing students for active participation but also be supported by extensive recitation of laws."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki 'yalnızca X değil, Y' karşıtlık yapısını hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: A."}], "7": [{"id": "ydtozg7-d44-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (HISTORY/TRIVIA)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Derek:\n– Did you know some of Stonehenge's stones were transported from over 200 kilometres away?\n\nLiz:\n– Really? How did they move something so heavy that far?\n\nDerek:\n– That's actually still debated among archaeologists.\n\nLiz:\n– ----\n\nDerek:\n– Exactly. It shows just how determined and organised the builders must have been.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Then the stones were probably quarried locally after all."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "That level of effort suggests it held huge significance for its builders."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Was Stonehenge originally built as a simple farming tool?"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "So modern engineers have finally recreated the exact method?"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Are the stones arranged in a random, unplanned pattern?"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Derek'in 'inşacıların ne kadar kararlı ve organize olduğu' yorumu, Liz'in 'büyük önem taşıdığı' ifadesini doğrular. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d45-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (RESEARCH GUESS)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Carmen:\n– Did you read about the new study on gratitude journaling?\n\nPeter:\n– ----\n\nCarmen:\n– Well, no, it actually found the effect was strongest only when people wrote entries by hand, not on a phone or computer.\n\nPeter:\n– That's an interesting detail I hadn't considered.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I don't really follow psychology research like that."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Wasn't it that gratitude journaling boosts happiness regardless of the method used?"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "These happiness studies seem to change their findings every year anyway."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "I bet it showed gratitude journaling has no measurable effect on mood."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Didn't it prove that only professional therapists can guide effective journaling?"}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Peter'ın 'yöntemden bağımsız olarak işe yaradığı' varsayımı, Carmen'in düzeltmesiyle ('sadece elle yazıldığında en güçlü') tutarlıdır. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d46-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (NAMED PHENOMENON)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Ferit:\n– It's strange how a group of smart individuals can sometimes make a really poor decision together.\n\nAylin:\n– ----\n\nFerit:\n– Interesting, I never thought there was a specific term for that.\n\nAylin:\n– Yes, and it often happens when people avoid disagreeing to preserve group harmony.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "That's usually just a matter of bad luck rather than anything systematic."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "That's a well-studied phenomenon in psychology known as groupthink."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "It mostly happens in groups that don't know each other well."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "I think that only occurs in very large organisations, not small groups."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "That's mainly caused by a lack of intelligence among group members."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Aylin'in fenomeni isimlendirmesi ('groupthink'), Ferit'in 'özel bir terim olduğunu düşünmemiştim' tepkisiyle tutarlıdır. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d47-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (SCIENTIFIC AGREEMENT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Farah:\n– Did you know being surrounded by the colour blue can actually make people feel calmer?\n\nTomas:\n– Really? I always thought that was just a personal preference.\n\nFarah:\n– ----\n\nTomas:\n– The one linked to lowering heart rate? Wow, that explains why I feel relaxed near the ocean!", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "In fact, colour preferences vary enormously between different cultures."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Right, exposure to the colour blue has been shown to slightly lower heart rate."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Indeed, I believe blue mainly works by reminding people of the sky."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Sure, it is simply association with vacations that creates that feeling."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "People who dislike the colour blue should probably avoid the beach."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Farah'ın 'kalp atış hızını düşürme' etkisini belirtmesi, Tomas'ın 'kalp hızını düşürmeyle ilişkili' tepkisiyle tutarlıdır. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d48-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (TRAVEL ADVICE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Mateus:\n– Hey, I know you've been to Lisbon before. I'm finally going next month. Any tips?\n\nInes:\n– ----\n\nMateus:\n– Oh, that's a really good point. I'll bring the right footwear then.\n\nInes:\n– Also, you might want to take the historic tram 28 for a scenic ride through the old town.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Many museums offer free entry on the first Sunday of the month."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Keep in mind that the streets are quite hilly and often cobblestoned."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Make sure you try the pastel de nata from a well-known local bakery."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "You should visit Belem Tower; it's right by the river."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "It's a walkable city, but public transport passes can save you money."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Ines'in boşluktaki önerisi, Mateus'un 'doğru ayakkabıyı getireceğim' tepkisine uygun olarak zemin/yürüyüş konulu olmalıdır. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p49-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (CAUSE-PURPOSE STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Bridges built in earthquake-prone regions can suffer structural stress during tremors, so engineers install flexible joints to absorb the movement without compromising the bridge's overall stability.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Bridges built in earthquake-prone regions remain completely stable during tremors without any stress; therefore, engineers rarely feel the need for flexible joints."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Because bridges built in earthquake-prone regions can suffer structural stress during tremors, engineers install flexible joints so they can absorb the movement without compromising the bridge's overall stability."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Bridges built in earthquake-prone regions barely suffer structural stress during tremors, so engineers rarely need flexible joints to maintain stability."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Engineers cannot maintain a bridge's stability in earthquake-prone regions because structural stress makes it impossible to absorb movement without flexible joints."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "To prevent structural stress during tremors, engineers tend to avoid flexible joints and instead reinforce the entire bridge structure only."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki anlamı (neden-sonuç ve amaç ilişkisini) hiçbir bilgi eklemeden ya da çıkarmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p50-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (PHENOMENON DESCRIPTION)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "There is a striking canyon in the United States where the rock layers display vivid, alternating bands of colour, a phenomenon that captivates geologists and hikers alike, often explained as the gradual deposit of different mineral sediments over time.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "There is a canyon in the United States whose colourful rock bands have never been fully explained by geologists, despite being commonly linked to gradual mineral sediment deposits."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "A canyon in the United States displays vivid, alternating bands of colour in its rock layers, captivating both geologists and hikers, a phenomenon commonly explained as the gradual deposit of different mineral sediments over time."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "A canyon in the United States displays faint, single-toned rock layers, which captivates hikers far more than geologists, and is explained as mineral sediment deposits."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "There is a striking canyon in the United States that geologists and hikers dismiss entirely, since the colourful bands are not actually caused by mineral sediments."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "A canyon in the United States occasionally shows colourful rock bands, a detail that captivates geologists but rarely interests hikers, often explained as recent erosion."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki tüm unsurları (fenomen, kimleri etkilediği ve verilen açıklama) hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p51-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (DOUBLE-NEGATIVE MEDICAL STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Multiple sclerosis, a chronic disease in which the immune system damages nerve fibres, has no cure, nor can the damaged nerve coating be fully rebuilt.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Multiple sclerosis, a chronic disease in which the immune system damages nerve fibres, has no cure, but researchers have already fully rebuilt the damaged nerve coating."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Multiple sclerosis, a chronic disease in which the immune system damages nerve fibres, remains incurable, and the damaged nerve coating cannot be fully rebuilt either."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Multiple sclerosis, a rare disease unrelated to the immune system, has no cure, though the damaged nerve coating can sometimes be fully rebuilt."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Multiple sclerosis, a chronic disease in which the immune system damages nerve fibres, can now be cured, but the damaged nerve coating cannot yet be fully rebuilt."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Multiple sclerosis is a chronic disease that gradually repairs nerve fibres, and it has no cure, nor can the nerve coating be rebuilt."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki çift olumsuzluk yapısını (tedavisi yok, ne de X geri alınabilir) hiçbir bilgi eklemeden ya da değiştirmeden koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p52-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (EXCLUSIVE MATERIAL PROPERTY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Shape-memory alloy contains a special crystal structure that allows it to return to its original form only when heated above a certain temperature, not at room temperature.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "What makes shape-memory alloy special is the crystal structure that causes it to remain deformed even after heating."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Because it contains a special crystal structure, shape-memory alloy returns to its original form only when heated above a certain temperature, not at room temperature."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Shape-memory alloy is made with a special crystal structure, which allows it to return to its original form at room temperature and not when heated."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "The crystal structure in shape-memory alloy ensures that it returns to its original form regardless of temperature."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Thanks to the structure within it, shape-memory alloy always returns to its original form together while avoiding heat entirely."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki 'yalnızca X ile, Y ile değil' dışlayıcı özelliği hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p53-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (NOT MERELY X BUT Y STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The study of literature should not be a mere analysis of plot and structure but a means of deepening our understanding of the human experience.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The study of literature should not only be based on understanding human experience but also be supported by rigorous plot and structure analysis."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The study of literature should be a way of deepening our understanding of the human experience rather than a tool for analysing plot and structure alone."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Analysing plot and structure is a fundamental step in order to truly deepen our understanding of the human experience."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "The study of literature can test students' ability to analyse plot instead of helping them understand the human experience."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The study of literature can help deepen understanding of human experience, but the necessity of analysing plot and structure should also be reconsidered."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki 'yalnızca X değil, Y' karşıtlık yapısını hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: B."}], "8": [{"id": "ydtozg7-d44-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (HISTORY/TRIVIA)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Rosa:\n– Did you know the Library of Alexandria once held hundreds of thousands of scrolls?\n\nFelix:\n– Yes, and scholars came from all over the ancient world to study there?\n\nRosa:\n– Exactly, but sadly most of its collection was eventually lost.\n\nFelix:\n– ----\n\nRosa:\n– That's right. Historians still debate exactly how and when it disappeared.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Then a full replica of the library must exist somewhere today."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Was the library rebuilt shortly after it was destroyed?"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "It's a shame we may never know the full story behind its loss."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "So none of its scrolls survived in any form whatsoever?"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Were the scrolls stored in a fireproof section of the building?"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Rosa'nın 'nasıl ve ne zaman kaybolduğunun hâlâ tartışıldığı' cevabı, Felix'in 'tüm hikâyeyi asla bilemeyebiliriz' yorumunu doğrular. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d45-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (RESEARCH GUESS)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Yusuf:\n– Have you seen the research on nature walks and stress levels?\n\nDana:\n– ----\n\nYusuf:\n– Well, no, it actually found that even viewing pictures of nature had a similar, smaller effect on stress reduction.\n\nDana:\n– That's surprising that images alone had any effect at all.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I haven't really kept up with that particular area of research."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Studies about stress and nature seem to shift every couple of years."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Wasn't it that only physically walking in nature reduces stress at all?"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "I bet it showed nature walks have no real effect on stress levels."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Didn't it find that stress reduction depends entirely on walking speed?"}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Dana'nın 'sadece fiziksel yürüyüşün işe yaradığı' varsayımı, Yusuf'un düzeltmesiyle ('doğa görselleri bile etkili') tutarlıdır. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d46-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (NAMED PHENOMENON)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Deniz:\n– It's odd how I can remember exactly where I was during a few major world events, but barely recall what I did last Tuesday.\n\nMelis:\n– ----\n\nDeniz:\n– Interesting, I always thought that was just my own memory being selective.\n\nMelis:\n– Not really, researchers have found that emotionally intense events are stored differently than ordinary ones.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "That's probably just because you have a naturally weak memory overall."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "I think that only happens to people who watch a lot of news."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "That's an actual phenomenon researchers call a flashbulb memory."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "It's mostly caused by discussing those events frequently with others."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "That usually only applies to memories from very early childhood."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Melis'in fenomeni isimlendirmesi ('flashbulb memory'), Deniz'in 'seçici bellek sanıyordum' tepkisiyle tutarlıdır. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d47-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (SCIENTIFIC AGREEMENT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Nadia:\n– Did you know regular running can actually improve our mood over time?\n\nAlex:\n– Really? I always thought it was just the sense of achievement afterward.\n\nNadia:\n– ----\n\nAlex:\n– The one linked to feeling rewarded? Wow, that explains the so-called runner's high!", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "In fact, the connection between exercise and mood affects everyone differently."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Right, but only competitive runners experience any real mood benefit."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Indeed, I believe running triggers the release of dopamine in the brain."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Sure, it is simply the fresh air outdoors that improves people's mood."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "People who dislike running should probably try walking instead."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Nadia'nın 'dopamine' hormonunu belirtmesi, Alex'in 'ödül hissiyle ilişkili' tepkisiyle tutarlıdır. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d48-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (TRAVEL ADVICE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Katarina:\n– Hey, I know you've been to Prague before. I'm finally going next month. Any tips?\n\nMilan:\n– ----\n\nKatarina:\n– Oh, that's a really good point. I'll be sure to look for those.\n\nMilan:\n– Also, you might want to cross Charles Bridge early in the morning to avoid the crowds.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Many attractions get very crowded in the summer months."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Keep in mind that trams are a fast and reliable way to get around."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Make sure you try the local trdelnik pastries from small street vendors."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "You should visit Prague Castle; it's one of the largest castle complexes in the world."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "It's a safe city, but watch out for pickpockets in busy tourist areas."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Milan'ın boşluktaki önerisi, Katarina'nın 'onları arayacağım' tepkisine uygun olarak yemek bulma konulu olmalıdır. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p49-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (CAUSE-PURPOSE STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Wireless networks in crowded buildings often suffer from signal interference, so IT teams install additional access points to maintain connection speed without overloading any single router.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "To prevent signal interference in crowded buildings, IT teams tend to avoid installing additional access points and instead limit the number of users."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Wireless networks in crowded buildings maintain full connection speed without any interference; therefore, IT teams rarely feel the need for additional access points."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Because wireless networks in crowded buildings often suffer from signal interference, IT teams install additional access points so they can maintain connection speed without overloading any single router."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Wireless networks in crowded buildings are barely affected by signal interference, so IT teams rarely need additional access points to maintain connection speed."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "IT teams cannot maintain connection speed in crowded buildings because signal interference makes it impossible to avoid overloading a single router without additional access points."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki anlamı (neden-sonuç ve amaç ilişkisini) hiçbir bilgi eklemeden ya da çıkarmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p50-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (PHENOMENON DESCRIPTION)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "There is a curious desert in Africa where the sand appears to sing or hum when disturbed, a phenomenon that fascinates physicists and travellers alike, often explained as vibrations caused by grains sliding over one another.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "A desert in Africa occasionally makes a faint sound, a detail that fascinates physicists but rarely interests travellers, often explained as strong desert winds."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "There is a desert in Africa whose humming sand has never been fully explained by physicists, despite being commonly linked to vibrations from sliding grains."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "A desert in Africa produces a singing or humming sound when its sand is disturbed, fascinating both physicists and travellers, a phenomenon commonly explained as vibrations caused by grains sliding over one another."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "A desert in Africa produces a loud humming sound constantly, even without any disturbance, which fascinates travellers far more than physicists, and is explained as sliding grains."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "There is a curious desert in Africa that physicists and travellers dismiss entirely, since the humming sound is not actually caused by sliding sand grains."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki tüm unsurları (fenomen, kimleri etkilediği ve verilen açıklama) hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p51-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (DOUBLE-NEGATIVE MEDICAL STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Alzheimer's disease, a progressive brain disorder affecting memory and cognition, has no cure, nor can the loss of brain cells be reversed.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Alzheimer's disease is a progressive brain disorder that gradually restores memory and cognition, and it has no cure, nor can brain cell loss be reversed."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Alzheimer's disease, a progressive brain disorder affecting memory and cognition, has no cure, but researchers have already reversed the loss of brain cells."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Alzheimer's disease, a progressive brain disorder that affects memory and cognition, remains incurable, and the loss of brain cells cannot be reversed either."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Alzheimer's disease, a rare disorder affecting only physical coordination, has no cure, though the loss of brain cells can sometimes be reversed."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Alzheimer's disease, a progressive brain disorder affecting memory and cognition, can now be cured, but the loss of brain cells cannot yet be reversed."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki çift olumsuzluk yapısını (tedavisi yok, ne de X geri alınabilir) hiçbir bilgi eklemeden ya da değiştirmeden koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p52-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (EXCLUSIVE MATERIAL PROPERTY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Anti-fog coating contains a hydrophilic layer that allows moisture to spread evenly only across the coated surface, not to form separate droplets.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Thanks to the layer within it, anti-fog coating always spreads moisture evenly together while avoiding the coated surface entirely."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "What makes anti-fog coating special is the hydrophilic layer that causes moisture to evaporate immediately upon contact."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Because it contains a hydrophilic layer, anti-fog coating allows moisture to spread evenly only across the coated surface, not to form separate droplets."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Anti-fog coating is made with a hydrophilic layer, which allows moisture to form separate droplets and not spread evenly."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The hydrophilic layer in anti-fog coating ensures that moisture forms droplets regardless of how the surface is coated."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki 'yalnızca X ile, Y ile değil' dışlayıcı özelliği hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p53-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (NOT MERELY X BUT Y STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Environmental education should not be a mere list of facts about pollution but a means of inspiring genuine responsibility toward the planet.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Environmental education can help inspire responsibility toward the planet, but the necessity of listing pollution facts should also be reconsidered."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Environmental education should not only be based on inspiring responsibility toward the planet but also be supported by an extensive list of pollution facts."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Environmental education should be a way of inspiring genuine responsibility toward the planet rather than a tool for listing facts about pollution alone."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Listing facts about pollution is a fundamental step in order to truly inspire responsibility toward the planet through environmental education."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Environmental education can test students' knowledge of pollution facts instead of helping them develop genuine responsibility toward the planet."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki 'yalnızca X değil, Y' karşıtlık yapısını hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: C."}], "9": [{"id": "ydtozg7-d44-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (HISTORY/TRIVIA)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Hana:\n– Did you know the Lascaux cave paintings are around 17,000 years old?\n\nJosh:\n– Wow, and they were only discovered by accident, weren't they?\n\nHana:\n– Yes, a group of teenagers stumbled upon them while looking for their dog.\n\nJosh:\n– ----\n\nHana:\n– Exactly, and now visitors can only see a replica to protect the originals.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Then the paintings must have been made using modern pigments."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Was the site immediately opened to the public afterward?"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "So the cave has remained completely untouched since its discovery?"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "I imagine the paintings needed careful protection once people started visiting."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Are the teenagers who found it still alive today?"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Hana'nın 'ziyaretçilerin yalnızca kopyasını görebildiği' açıklaması, Josh'un 'dikkatli koruma gerekliydi' yorumunu doğrular. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d45-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (RESEARCH GUESS)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Marcus:\n– Did you catch the new study on blue light glasses?\n\nSelin:\n– ----\n\nMarcus:\n– Well, no, it actually found no significant difference in eye strain between people who wore them and those who didn't.\n\nSelin:\n– That's not what the advertisements claim at all.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I don't usually pay attention to studies about eyewear."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Research on screen-related products changes constantly anyway."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "I bet it showed blue light glasses worsen eye strain over time."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Wasn't it that blue light glasses significantly reduce digital eye strain?"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Didn't it prove that eye strain is caused mainly by poor lighting?"}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Selin'in 'gözlüklerin dijital göz yorgunluğunu önemli ölçüde azalttığı' varsayımı, Marcus'un düzeltmesiyle ('anlamlı fark bulunamadı') tutarlıdır. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d46-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (NAMED PHENOMENON)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Bora:\n– It's funny how the first price I see for something always affects how good or bad the next price seems, even if it's unrelated.\n\nSila:\n– ----\n\nBora:\n– Interesting, I always thought that was just me being bad at judging value.\n\nSila:\n– Not at all, it's actually a well-known bias in how people make decisions.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "That usually only happens to people who shop impulsively."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "I think that only applies to expensive purchases, not small ones."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "It's mostly linked to how much money a person actually has."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "That's a recognised effect that researchers call anchoring bias."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "That's probably caused by comparing too many products at once."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Sila'nın fenomeni isimlendirmesi ('anchoring bias'), Bora'nın 'değer yargılamada kötüyüm sanıyordum' tepkisiyle tutarlıdır. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d47-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (SCIENTIFIC AGREEMENT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Ravi:\n– Did you know simply being near water can actually make people feel calmer?\n\nSanne:\n– Really? I always thought that was just the peaceful scenery.\n\nRavi:\n– ----\n\nSanne:\n– The state linked to lower stress? Wow, that explains why I always relax near the lake!", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "In fact, the connection between nature and wellbeing runs quite deep."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Right, but only the sound of waves is what actually relaxes people."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Indeed, I believe water mainly helps by cooling down the body."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Sure, proximity to water can shift the brain into a relaxed state researchers call blue mind."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "People who dislike swimming should probably avoid lakes altogether."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Ravi'nin 'blue mind' durumunu belirtmesi, Sanne'nin 'düşük stresle ilişkili durum' tepkisiyle tutarlıdır. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d48-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (TRAVEL ADVICE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Hana:\n– Hey, I know you've been to Seoul before. I'm finally going next month. Any tips?\n\nJinho:\n– ----\n\nHana:\n– Oh, that's a really good point. I'll definitely set aside a whole day for that.\n\nJinho:\n– Also, you might want to try the subway; it's fast and covers almost the entire city.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Many restaurants there stay open surprisingly late at night."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Keep in mind that tipping isn't customary and can even be seen as odd."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Make sure you try the street food in Myeongdong at night."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "You should visit Bukchon Hanok Village; it takes time to explore properly."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "It's a safe city, but crowded subway stations can be overwhelming at rush hour."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Jinho'nun boşluktaki önerisi, Hana'nın 'buna bütün bir gün ayıracağım' tepkisine uygun olarak zaman gerektiren bir yer konulu olmalıdır. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p49-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (CAUSE-PURPOSE STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Museum artefacts displayed under bright lighting can fade over time, so curators use filtered lighting systems to preserve visibility without accelerating the artefacts' deterioration.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Curators cannot preserve artefact visibility under bright lighting because fading makes it impossible to slow deterioration without filtered lighting."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "To prevent artefact fading under bright lighting, curators tend to avoid filtered lighting systems and instead display artefacts in complete darkness."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Museum artefacts displayed under bright lighting keep their visibility without any fading; therefore, curators rarely feel the need for filtered lighting systems."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Because museum artefacts displayed under bright lighting can fade over time, curators use filtered lighting systems so they can preserve visibility without accelerating the artefacts' deterioration."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Museum artefacts displayed under bright lighting barely fade over time, so curators rarely need filtered lighting systems to preserve visibility."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki anlamı (neden-sonuç ve amaç ilişkisini) hiçbir bilgi eklemeden ya da çıkarmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p50-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (PHENOMENON DESCRIPTION)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "There is a fascinating reef off the coast of Australia where certain corals emit a faint natural glow at night, a phenomenon that intrigues marine biologists and divers alike, often explained as a chemical reaction within the coral's own tissue.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "There is a fascinating reef off the coast of Australia that marine biologists and divers dismiss entirely, since the glow is not actually caused by any chemical reaction."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "A reef off the coast of Australia occasionally shows a faint glow, a detail that intrigues marine biologists but rarely interests divers, often explained as reflected moonlight."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "There is a reef off the coast of Australia whose glowing corals have never been fully explained by marine biologists, despite being commonly linked to a chemical reaction within the tissue."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "A reef off the coast of Australia has corals that emit a faint natural glow at night, intriguing both marine biologists and divers, a phenomenon commonly explained as a chemical reaction within the coral's own tissue."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "A reef off the coast of Australia has corals that glow brightly during the daytime, which intrigues divers far more than marine biologists, and is explained by a chemical reaction."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki tüm unsurları (fenomen, kimleri etkilediği ve verilen açıklama) hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p51-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (DOUBLE-NEGATIVE MEDICAL STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Sickle cell disease, an inherited blood disorder causing red blood cells to become misshapen, has no widely available cure, nor can the abnormal haemoglobin be corrected in existing cells.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Sickle cell disease, an inherited blood disorder causing red blood cells to become misshapen, now has a widely available cure, but the abnormal haemoglobin cannot yet be corrected."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Sickle cell disease is an inherited blood disorder that gradually restores normal red blood cell shape, and it has no widely available cure, nor can haemoglobin be corrected."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Sickle cell disease, an inherited blood disorder causing red blood cells to become misshapen, has no widely available cure, but researchers have already corrected the abnormal haemoglobin in existing cells."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Sickle cell disease, an inherited blood disorder that causes red blood cells to become misshapen, has no widely available cure, and the abnormal haemoglobin in existing cells cannot be corrected either."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Sickle cell disease, a common blood disorder unrelated to genetics, has no widely available cure, though the abnormal haemoglobin can sometimes be corrected."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki çift olumsuzluk yapısını (tedavisi yok, ne de X geri alınabilir) hiçbir bilgi eklemeden ya da değiştirmeden koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p52-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (EXCLUSIVE MATERIAL PROPERTY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Superhydrophobic fabric contains a nanostructured surface that makes water form beads only on the treated side, not on the untreated interior.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The nanostructured surface on superhydrophobic fabric ensures that water forms beads regardless of which side it touches."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Thanks to the structure within it, superhydrophobic fabric always forms beads together while avoiding the treated side entirely."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "What makes superhydrophobic fabric special is the nanostructured surface that causes water to soak in immediately on contact."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Because it contains a nanostructured surface, superhydrophobic fabric causes water to form beads only on the treated side, not on the untreated interior."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Superhydrophobic fabric is made with a nanostructured surface, which causes water to form beads on the untreated interior and not on the treated side."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki 'yalnızca X ile, Y ile değil' dışlayıcı özelliği hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p53-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (NOT MERELY X BUT Y STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The study of philosophy should not be a mere memorisation of famous arguments but a means of developing one's own capacity for careful, independent reasoning.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The study of philosophy can test students' memory of famous arguments instead of helping them develop independent reasoning."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The study of philosophy can help develop independent reasoning, but the necessity of memorising famous arguments should also be reconsidered."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "The study of philosophy should not only be based on developing independent reasoning but also be supported by extensive memorisation of famous arguments."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "The study of philosophy should be a way of developing one's own capacity for careful, independent reasoning rather than a tool for memorising famous arguments alone."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Memorising famous arguments is a fundamental step in order to truly develop independent reasoning through the study of philosophy."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki 'yalnızca X değil, Y' karşıtlık yapısını hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: D."}], "10": [{"id": "ydtozg7-d44-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (HISTORY/TRIVIA)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Grant:\n– Did you know the Sutton Hoo ship burial contained treasures fit for a king, yet no body was ever found?\n\nWendy:\n– That's strange. How can they be sure it belonged to a king at all?\n\nGrant:\n– The wealth and quality of the objects buried with it are the main clues.\n\nWendy:\n– ----\n\nGrant:\n– Exactly. The acidic soil likely dissolved any human remains over the centuries.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Then the ship itself must have been buried empty on purpose."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Was the site excavated using modern ground-penetrating radar?"}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "So archaeologists simply guessed the identity based on nearby villages?"}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Are similar ship burials common throughout northern Europe?"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "I suppose the soil conditions might explain why no remains survived."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Grant'in 'asitli toprağın kalıntıları eritmiş olabileceği' açıklaması, Wendy'nin 'toprak koşulları açıklayabilir' yorumunu doğrular. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d45-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (RESEARCH GUESS)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Isabel:\n– Have you heard about the recent research on multitasking?\n\nThéo:\n– ----\n\nIsabel:\n– Well, no, it actually found that even brief interruptions could double the time needed to complete a task accurately.\n\nThéo:\n– That's a much bigger effect than I would have guessed.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I don't really follow that sort of workplace research closely."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "These productivity studies seem to disagree with each other constantly."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "I bet it showed multitasking has barely any effect on accuracy at all."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Wasn't it that multitasking only slightly increases the risk of small errors?"}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Didn't it find that even short interruptions barely affect task completion time?"}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Théo'nun 'kısa kesintilerin tamamlanma süresini pek etkilemediği' varsayımı, Isabel'in düzeltmesiyle ('süreyi iki katına çıkarabildiği') tutarlıdır. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d46-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (NAMED PHENOMENON)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Elif:\n– Have you noticed how once you believe something, you start noticing evidence that supports it everywhere?\n\nKerem:\n– ----\n\nElif:\n– Interesting, I always assumed that was just paying closer attention.\n\nKerem:\n– Not exactly, it's a well-documented tendency that affects almost everyone.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "That usually only happens with topics people care deeply about."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "I think that's mostly linked to how much free time someone has."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "It's probably caused by spending too much time on social media."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "That's mainly a sign of someone being unusually stubborn."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "That's a recognised pattern researchers refer to as confirmation bias."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Kerem'in fenomeni isimlendirmesi ('confirmation bias'), Elif'in 'sadece dikkat etmek sanıyordum' tepkisiyle tutarlıdır. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d47-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (SCIENTIFIC AGREEMENT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Lian:\n– Did you know slow, deep breathing can actually calm down our whole body?\n\nMarco:\n– Really? I always thought it was just a mental trick to feel calmer.\n\nLian:\n– ----\n\nMarco:\n– The nerve linked to relaxation? Wow, that explains why deep breathing always settles my nerves!", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "In fact, the connection between breathing and mood affects everyone differently."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Right, but only breathing through the nose has any real calming effect."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Indeed, I believe deep breathing mainly works by distracting the mind."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Sure, it is simply the pause in activity that makes people feel calmer."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "People under stress should try it, since it stimulates the vagus nerve directly."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Lian'ın 'vagus siniri' bilgisini vermesi, Marco'nun 'rahatlamayla ilişkili sinir' tepkisiyle tutarlıdır. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-d48-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "DIALOGUE COMPLETION (TRAVEL ADVICE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Camila:\n– Hey, I know you've been to Buenos Aires before. I'm finally going next month. Any tips?\n\nDiego:\n– ----\n\nCamila:\n– Oh, that's a really good point. I'll keep my things close, then.\n\nDiego:\n– Also, you might want to watch a tango show in the San Telmo neighbourhood.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Many shops close for a long break in the middle of the afternoon."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Keep in mind that dinner is usually eaten much later than in other countries."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Make sure you try the steak; it's considered some of the best in the world."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "You should visit La Boca; the colourful buildings are very photogenic."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "It's generally safe, but stay alert in crowded areas and on public transport."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Diego'nun boşluktaki önerisi, Camila'nın 'eşyalarımı yakın tutacağım' tepkisine uygun olarak güvenlik konulu olmalıdır. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p49-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (CAUSE-PURPOSE STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Recorded interviews conducted in windy outdoor settings often contain unwanted background noise, so podcast editors apply noise-reduction software to clarify speech without distorting the speaker's natural tone.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Recorded interviews conducted in windy outdoor settings rarely contain background noise, so editors seldom need noise-reduction software to clarify speech."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Podcast editors cannot preserve a speaker's natural tone in windy outdoor interviews because background noise makes it impossible to clarify speech without distortion."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "To prevent background noise in windy outdoor interviews, editors tend to avoid noise-reduction software and instead re-record indoors only."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Recorded interviews conducted in windy outdoor settings contain perfectly clear speech without any background noise; therefore, editors rarely feel the need for noise-reduction software."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Because recorded interviews conducted in windy outdoor settings often contain unwanted background noise, podcast editors apply noise-reduction software so they can clarify speech without distorting the speaker's natural tone."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki anlamı (neden-sonuç ve amaç ilişkisini) hiçbir bilgi eklemeden ya da çıkarmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p50-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (PHENOMENON DESCRIPTION)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "There is a peculiar valley in Iceland where the ground occasionally emits a low rumbling sound, a phenomenon that puzzles geologists and residents alike, often explained as shifting gas pockets deep beneath the surface.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "A valley in Iceland constantly emits a loud rumbling sound, which puzzles residents far more than geologists, and is explained by shifting gas pockets."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "There is a peculiar valley in Iceland that geologists and residents dismiss entirely, since the rumbling sound is not actually caused by shifting gas pockets."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "A valley in Iceland occasionally emits a faint sound, a detail that puzzles geologists but rarely interests residents, often explained as underground water flow."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "There is a valley in Iceland whose rumbling sound has never been fully explained by geologists, despite being commonly linked to shifting gas pockets deep beneath the surface."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "A valley in Iceland occasionally emits a low rumbling sound from the ground, puzzling both geologists and residents, a phenomenon commonly explained as shifting gas pockets deep beneath the surface."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki tüm unsurları (fenomen, kimleri etkilediği ve verilen açıklama) hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p51-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (DOUBLE-NEGATIVE MEDICAL STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Parkinson's disease, a progressive nervous system disorder affecting movement, has no cure, nor can the loss of dopamine-producing brain cells be undone.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Parkinson's disease, a rare disorder unrelated to the nervous system, has no cure, though the loss of dopamine-producing brain cells can sometimes be undone."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Parkinson's disease, a progressive nervous system disorder affecting movement, can now be cured, but the loss of dopamine-producing brain cells cannot yet be undone."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Parkinson's disease is a progressive nervous system disorder that gradually restores movement, and it has no cure, nor can the loss of dopamine-producing cells be undone."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Parkinson's disease, a progressive nervous system disorder affecting movement, has no cure, but researchers have already undone the loss of dopamine-producing brain cells."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Parkinson's disease, a progressive nervous system disorder that affects movement, remains incurable, and the loss of dopamine-producing brain cells cannot be undone either."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki çift olumsuzluk yapısını (tedavisi yok, ne de X geri alınabilir) hiçbir bilgi eklemeden ya da değiştirmeden koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p52-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (EXCLUSIVE MATERIAL PROPERTY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Thermochromic ink contains temperature-sensitive dye molecules that change colour only within a specific temperature range, not outside of it.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Thermochromic ink is made with temperature-sensitive dye molecules, which change colour outside a specific range and not within it."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The dye molecules in thermochromic ink ensure that it changes colour regardless of the surrounding temperature."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Thanks to the molecules within it, thermochromic ink always changes colour together while avoiding a specific temperature range entirely."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "What makes thermochromic ink special is the dye content that causes it to remain a single colour at all temperatures."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Because it contains temperature-sensitive dye molecules, thermochromic ink changes colour only within a specific temperature range, not outside of it."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki 'yalnızca X ile, Y ile değil' dışlayıcı özelliği hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg7-p53-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAPHRASE (NOT MERELY X BUT Y STRUCTURE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Music education should not be a mere drill in reading notation but a means of cultivating genuine emotional expression through sound.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Drilling notation reading is a fundamental step in order to truly cultivate emotional expression through music education."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Music education can test students' ability to read notation instead of helping them cultivate genuine emotional expression."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Music education can help cultivate emotional expression through sound, but the necessity of drilling notation reading should also be reconsidered."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Music education should not only be based on cultivating emotional expression but also be supported by extensive notation drilling."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Music education should be a way of cultivating genuine emotional expression through sound rather than a tool for drilling notation reading alone."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Verilen cümledeki 'yalnızca X değil, Y' karşıtlık yapısını hiçbir değişiklik yapmadan koruyan tek parafraz budur. Cevap: E."}]};
Object.keys(DENEME_YDT_INGILIZCE_OZEL_7).forEach(function(no) {
  if (!DENEME_SORU_BANKASI.YDT[no]) DENEME_SORU_BANKASI.YDT[no] = {};
  DENEME_SORU_BANKASI.YDT[no].ydtIngilizce = (DENEME_SORU_BANKASI.YDT[no].ydtIngilizce || []).concat(DENEME_YDT_INGILIZCE_OZEL_7[no]);
});
const DENEME_YDT_INGILIZCE_OZEL_8 = {"1": [{"id": "ydtozg8-s54-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (CALMING/SUPPORTIVE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A close friend of yours says she feels too nervous before her upcoming driving test, but you know she has practised extensively and is a careful driver. So, you try to calm her down in a supportive way by saying: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Everyone gets a bit nervous before a driving test, but you've practised so much that I'm confident you'll pass."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "If you keep worrying like this, the examiner will definitely notice and fail you."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Don't stress too much; even if you fail, you can just retake it as many times as you want."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Honestly, I'm a little surprised you're this nervous, since you never seem fully confident behind the wheel."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Relax, driving tests aren't really that important in the end anyway."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Sınava iyi hazırlanmış bir arkadaşı desteklerken, endişenin normal olduğunu kabul edip hazırlığına dayanarak güven veren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s55-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (EXPLAINING RESPONSIBILITY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Your younger sister wants to get a pet rabbit, thinking it will just be about cuddling and playing. However, she does not realise how much daily care it requires. To explain to her that a rabbit is not only a cuddly companion, you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "A rabbit is a living creature that depends on you for proper food, a clean home, and regular health checks, not just cuddles."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Different rabbit breeds have very different temperaments and activity levels."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Many rabbits enjoy having toys to chew on to keep their teeth healthy."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Rabbits can live for several years if they are given a proper diet."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Having a rabbit means daily care is required, but don't worry, I'll take care of everything for you."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Sorumluluğun eğlenceden ibaret olmadığını vurgulayan, hayvanın temel ihtiyaçlarını öne çıkaran ifade doğrudur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s56-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (PRACTICAL TRAVEL WARNING)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "One of your foreign friends tells you he wants to visit Petra in Jordan, and so he will go during the summer holiday. Since you know the site involves a lot of walking with very little shade, you want to warn him, so you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "You should bring plenty of water and start early in the morning before it gets too hot to walk comfortably."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "It would be a good idea to book your flights a few months in advance to get a better price."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "I wish you had told me earlier that you wanted to go; I visited last year and could have given you tips sooner."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "If I were you, I'd also visit Wadi Rum, since it's not far from Petra."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "If possible, consider going in spring, when the wildflowers are in bloom across the desert."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Gölgesiz ve çok yürüyüş gerektiren bir yer için sıcak havaya karşı somut bir önlem öneren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s57-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (APOLOGY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "You are attending a friend's dinner party. While reaching across the table for the salt, you accidentally knock over a glass of red wine onto the white tablecloth. Highly embarrassed, you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I'm so sorry! That was clumsy of me. Let me help clean this up right away."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "This tablecloth looks quite expensive. I'm sure it can be washed easily."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "You should really keep glasses further from the edge of the table."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "I guess if the table had been a bit more stable, this wouldn't have happened."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "I'm not sure how that happened, but I think the glass was placed too close to the edge."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Kazara oluşan bir kazadan sonra samimi özür dileyip yardım teklif eden ifade doğrudur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s58-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (SERIOUS PROFESSIONAL CONCERN)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "You have been skipping your prescribed physical therapy exercises, but you feel embarrassed about how slowly your recovery is going. At your routine follow-up appointment, your physiotherapist reviews your progress, and the results show your mobility has barely improved. She is concerned about your health and says in a serious manner: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I understand these exercises can feel discouraging, but skipping them is exactly why your recovery has stalled. Let's find an approach you can stick to."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "I'm glad you're managing without the exercises, but you might consider doing them once you feel ready."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "I'm not surprised by these results; this is exactly what happens when my advice is ignored."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Maybe we should just forget the exercises and try a completely different treatment instead."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The results are clear. Skipping these exercises is causing permanent damage to your joints."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Ciddi bir sağlık uyarısı yaparken hem sorunu açıklayan hem de yapıcı bir çözüm öneren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g59-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (PSYCHOLOGY CONCEPT)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The placebo effect describes a phenomenon in which a person experiences a real improvement in symptoms after receiving a treatment that has no actual therapeutic value. First documented systematically in medical trials during the twentieth century, the effect helps explain why patients sometimes feel better after taking a sugar pill they believe to be real medicine. The placebo effect occurs when a person's expectation of improvement genuinely influences how their brain and body respond. ---- In such cases, doctors have found that a patient's belief and expectation can measurably affect real physiological processes, not just their perception of pain.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "This expectation can trigger the release of the body's own natural painkillers, known as endorphins."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Such expectations are considered irrelevant to genuine medical outcomes."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Sugar pills are typically manufactured using inactive ingredients such as lactose."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "This means real medicine is rarely more effective than a placebo in any condition."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Clinical trials are usually conducted over a period of several months."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve bir sonraki cümleye mantıksal olarak bağlanan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g60-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (HISTORICAL ROLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Town criers in medieval and early modern Europe were not important just for shouting announcements in the town square. ---- By memorising royal proclamations, local bylaws, and important news, they served as one of the only reliable sources of public information in an age when most people could not read. Their loud, formal announcements also drew crowds, making them both messengers and a form of public entertainment. Over time, the criers' role declined as printed newspapers gradually became the primary means of sharing news across communities.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "These officials played a key role in spreading news, announcing decrees, and keeping communities informed before printed media existed."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Their loud voices were considered a divine gift, often linked to supernatural beings from ancient folklore."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "They therefore held significant political power, often influencing the decisions of kings and nobles directly."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "The primary duty of these officials was to compose new laws that were meant to please and flatter the ruling monarch."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Many of them were also skilled craftspeople who would trade goods and tools between neighbouring towns."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve mesleğin gerçek işlevini doğru şekilde tanımlayan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g61-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (RESTORATION PROJECT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The restoration of a centuries-old Renaissance masterpiece in 2015 was the most extensive conservation project the painting had ever undergone, addressing decades of accumulated grime, cracked varnish, and minor paint loss. It involved carefully cleaning the surface, stabilising flaking pigment, and retouching damaged areas using historically accurate materials. ---- When completed, the restoration not only revived the painting's original vibrant colours but also reinforced its structural stability, ensuring that it remains safe to display and study for future generations.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The project also incorporated advanced imaging technology to study the layers of paint hidden beneath the visible surface."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The painting had suffered damage from decades of exposure to smoke, humidity, and poor lighting conditions."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "The artist behind the painting remains one of the most celebrated figures in art history."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "There was a chance that removing the old varnish might damage the fragile paint layers underneath."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Despite its age and previous restoration attempts, the painting continues to be one of the museum's most visited works."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve süreç anlatımıyla sonuç cümlesi arasında doğru köprüyü kuran tek seçenek budur. Cevap: A."}], "2": [{"id": "ydtozg8-s54-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (CALMING/SUPPORTIVE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A close friend of yours says he feels overwhelmed before his first public speech at a conference, but you know he has rehearsed the presentation many times. So, you try to calm him down in a supportive way by saying: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I doubt anyone will actually pay attention to what you say, so don't overthink it."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "It's natural to feel nervous before speaking in public, but you've rehearsed so thoroughly that you'll do great."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "If your voice shakes up there, people might assume you don't know your subject well."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Try not to worry; even a poor presentation won't really affect your career much."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Public speaking anxiety usually only affects people who haven't prepared properly at all."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Prova yapmış bir arkadaşı desteklerken, endişenin doğal olduğunu kabul edip hazırlığına dayanarak güven veren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s55-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (EXPLAINING RESPONSIBILITY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Your little brother wants to start growing vegetables in the garden, thinking it will just be about picking fresh tomatoes to eat. However, he does not realise how much regular effort it requires. To explain to him that gardening is not only about harvesting, you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Different vegetables need to be planted at different times of the year."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "A garden depends on you for regular watering, weeding, and protection from pests, not just picking the harvest."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Many gardeners enjoy the fresh smell of soil after it rains."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Vegetables grown at home often taste better than store-bought ones."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Gardening does require regular effort, but don't worry, I'll handle all of that for you."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Bahçenin sürekli emek gerektirdiğini, sadece hasat toplamaktan ibaret olmadığını vurgulayan ifade doğrudur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s56-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (PRACTICAL TRAVEL WARNING)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "One of your foreign friends tells you she wants to visit Venice, and so she will go during the winter holiday. Since you know the city occasionally floods during that season, you want to warn her, so you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "You should try to visit early in the morning to avoid the tourist crowds near St Mark's Square."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "It would be a good idea to check the tide forecasts and pack waterproof boots, since flooding can happen in winter."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "I wish you had told me earlier that you wanted to go; I went in autumn, and we could have planned it together."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "If I were you, I'd also visit nearby Verona, since it's an easy day trip from Venice."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "If possible, consider going in late spring, when the weather is milder and drier."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Kışın sel riskine karşı somut bir önlem (gelgit tahmini, su geçirmez bot) öneren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s57-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (APOLOGY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "You are helping a friend move into a new apartment. While carrying a box down the stairs, you accidentally drop it, and a few fragile items inside break. Highly embarrassed, you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I'm not sure what happened, but I think the box wasn't packed very well."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "I'm terribly sorry! That was careless of me. Let me help replace whatever broke."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Those items look old anyway. I'm sure it's not a big loss."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "You should really label boxes as fragile more clearly next time."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "I guess if the stairs had better lighting, this wouldn't have happened."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Kazara oluşan bir kazadan sonra samimi özür dileyip telafi teklif eden ifade doğrudur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s58-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (SERIOUS PROFESSIONAL CONCERN)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "You have been avoiding your dentist's recommended treatment for a cavity, but you are anxious about the procedure. At your routine check-up, your dentist takes new X-rays, and the results show the decay has spread further into the tooth. He is concerned about your health and says in a serious manner: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I'm glad you're managing without the treatment, but you should consider it eventually."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "I understand the procedure feels intimidating, but avoiding it is exactly why the decay has spread. Let's talk through what to expect so it feels less overwhelming."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "I'm not surprised by these results; this is exactly what happens when patients ignore my advice."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Maybe we should just forget the treatment and monitor the tooth for now."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The results are clear. Avoiding this treatment is causing irreversible damage to the tooth."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Ciddi bir sağlık uyarısı yaparken hem sorunu açıklayan hem de yapıcı bir çözüm öneren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g59-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (PSYCHOLOGY CONCEPT)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The spotlight effect describes people's tendency to overestimate how much others notice their appearance, mistakes, or behaviour in social situations. First studied extensively by social psychologists in the late twentieth century, the concept explains why a person might feel intensely embarrassed about a small stain on their shirt, assuming everyone around them has noticed it. The spotlight effect occurs because people are naturally focused on their own experience and mistakenly assume others are paying just as much attention to them. ---- Once this bias is recognised, many people find they can worry considerably less about minor social mistakes.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Clothing choices are often influenced by current fashion trends."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "In reality, most people are too preoccupied with their own concerns to notice these small details at all."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "This means that other people are usually watching a person's every move closely."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Social psychology emerged as a distinct field of study in the twentieth century."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "As a result, embarrassment in social situations has been completely eliminated by modern research."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve bir sonraki cümleye mantıksal olarak bağlanan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g60-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (HISTORICAL ROLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Scribes in ancient Egypt were not important just for the sake of copying religious texts by hand. ---- By recording tax records, legal contracts, and government correspondence, they helped keep the machinery of the state running smoothly across a vast kingdom. Their specialised training also elevated their social status, making them both administrators and respected members of society. Over time, the scribes' exclusive role declined as literacy gradually spread to a wider portion of the population.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Their writing ability was considered a divine gift, often linked to supernatural beings from ancient mythology."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "These officials played a key role in maintaining official records, drafting contracts, and supporting the administration of the kingdom."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "They therefore held significant political power, often making final decisions on behalf of the pharaoh."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "The primary duty of these officials was to compose religious hymns intended to please the gods and pharaoh alike."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Many of them were also skilled farmers who would trade crops and livestock between villages."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve mesleğin gerçek işlevini doğru şekilde tanımlayan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g61-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (RESTORATION PROJECT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The renovation of a two-thousand-year-old Roman aqueduct in 2018 was the most ambitious engineering project undertaken on the structure since its original construction, addressing serious cracks and erosion along several arched sections. It involved reinforcing the stone foundations, repairing damaged arches, and installing modern drainage to redirect rainwater away from vulnerable areas. ---- When completed, the renovation not only preserved the aqueduct's ancient appearance but also allowed engineers to study its original construction techniques in greater detail, ensuring that it remains a valuable historical site for future generations.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The project also incorporated new lighting systems to make the site accessible for evening tours."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The aqueduct had suffered structural damage from centuries of earthquakes, weathering, and nearby construction work."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Roman engineers were renowned for their innovative use of arches in large-scale construction projects."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "There was a chance that reinforcing the old stonework might alter the aqueduct's original historical appearance."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Despite its age and the damage it had suffered, the aqueduct had continued to attract thousands of visitors annually."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve süreç anlatımıyla sonuç cümlesi arasında doğru köprüyü kuran tek seçenek budur. Cevap: B."}], "3": [{"id": "ydtozg8-s54-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (CALMING/SUPPORTIVE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A close friend of yours says she feels anxious about her upcoming job interview, but you know she has researched the company thoroughly and prepared strong answers. So, you try to calm her down in a supportive way by saying: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "If they don't hire you, it probably just means the job wasn't a good fit anyway."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "I wouldn't worry about it too much; most interviewers barely listen to the answers."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "It's completely normal to feel anxious, but you've prepared so well that I'm sure you'll impress them."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "I have to admit, I'm a bit worried too, since interviews can go wrong so easily."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Just try not to think about it at all until the day of the interview."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "İyi hazırlanmış bir arkadaşı desteklerken, endişenin normal olduğunu kabul edip hazırlığına dayanarak güven veren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s55-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (EXPLAINING RESPONSIBILITY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Your cousin wants to get his driving licence, thinking it will just be about the freedom to go wherever he wants. However, he does not realise how much responsibility it requires. To explain to him that driving is not only about freedom, you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Different cars have very different fuel efficiency and maintenance needs."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Many new drivers enjoy taking long road trips during the summer."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Driving means you are responsible for your own safety and the safety of everyone else on the road, not just your own convenience."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "A driving licence needs to be renewed every few years in most countries."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Driving does come with responsibility, but don't worry, I'll always be there to help you park."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Sürücülüğün sadece özgürlük değil, herkesin güvenliğine dair sorumluluk gerektirdiğini vurgulayan ifade doğrudur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s56-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (PRACTICAL TRAVEL WARNING)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "One of your foreign friends tells you he wants to visit Kyoto, and so he will go during the cherry blossom season. Since you know that particular period gets extremely crowded, you want to warn him, so you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "You should try to visit the temples early in the morning before the tour groups arrive."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "It would be a good idea to book accommodation well in advance, since hotels fill up quickly."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "I wish you had told me earlier that you wanted to go; I went during that exact week last year and could have shared some tips."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "If I were you, I'd also visit Nara, since the deer park there is unforgettable."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "If possible, consider going in autumn instead, when the crowds are noticeably smaller."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "'Daha önce söyleseydin' ifadesi, aynı dönemde gitmiş olma deneyimini paylaşan doğal bir tepkidir. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s57-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (APOLOGY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "You are giving a presentation at work. While gesturing enthusiastically, you accidentally knock your coffee cup onto your laptop keyboard. Highly embarrassed, you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I'm not sure how that happened, but I think the cup was placed too close to the keyboard."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "These things happen to everyone sometimes, so I wouldn't worry about it too much."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "I'm so sorry, everyone! That was clumsy of me. Let me quickly clean this up and continue."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "You should really keep drinks away from laptops during presentations."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "I guess if the desk had been a bit larger, this wouldn't have happened."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Kazara oluşan bir kazadan sonra samimi özür dileyip durumu hızlıca toparlayan ifade doğrudur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s58-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (SERIOUS PROFESSIONAL CONCERN)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "You have been refusing to wear the orthotic insoles your podiatrist prescribed, but you find them uncomfortable. At your routine follow-up, he examines your feet, and the results show your foot alignment has worsened. He is concerned about your health and says in a serious manner: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I'm glad you're managing without the insoles, but you might consider using them eventually."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Maybe we should just forget the insoles and try a different kind of shoe instead."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "I understand they feel uncomfortable at first, but avoiding them is exactly why your alignment has worsened. Let's find a pair that fits you better."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "I'm not surprised by these results; this is exactly what happens when patients ignore my advice."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The results are clear. Not using the insoles is causing irreversible damage to your joints."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Ciddi bir sağlık uyarısı yaparken hem sorunu açıklayan hem de yapıcı bir çözüm öneren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g59-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (PSYCHOLOGY CONCEPT)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The Dunning-Kruger effect describes a pattern in which people with limited knowledge or skill in a particular area tend to overestimate their own competence. First identified by two American psychologists in the late 1990s, the effect explains why a beginner might feel more confident about a task than someone with genuine, extensive experience. The effect occurs because a certain level of skill is required not only to perform a task well but also to accurately judge one's own performance. ---- As people gain more experience, they typically become more aware of how much they still have to learn, which paradoxically lowers their confidence before it eventually rises again.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "As a result, formal education has become entirely unnecessary for developing real expertise."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Confidence levels can be measured through standardised psychological questionnaires."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Without that foundational knowledge, a novice simply lacks the ability to recognise their own mistakes."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "This means that experts are usually far less accurate than beginners in judging their own abilities."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The effect was named after the two psychologists who first identified it."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve bir sonraki cümleye mantıksal olarak bağlanan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g60-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (HISTORICAL ROLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Guild masters in medieval European towns were not important just for overseeing the daily work of their workshop. ---- By setting quality standards, training apprentices, and regulating prices, they helped maintain trust between craftspeople and the wider community. Their respected position also gave them influence in local town councils, making them both skilled tradespeople and community leaders. Over time, the guilds' tight control declined as industrial production gradually replaced small, independent workshops.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Their craftsmanship was considered a divine gift, often linked to supernatural beings from local folklore."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "They therefore held significant religious power, often influencing the appointment of local priests."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "These officials played a key role in setting professional standards, training new workers, and regulating local trade."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "The primary duty of these officials was to compose trade agreements intended to please foreign merchants."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Many of them were also skilled musicians who would perform at festivals throughout the year."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve mesleğin gerçek işlevini doğru şekilde tanımlayan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g61-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (RESTORATION PROJECT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The restoration of a nineteenth-century sailing ship in 2019 was the largest preservation project the vessel had undergone since being permanently docked as a museum exhibit, addressing rotting timber and corroded metal fittings throughout the hull. It involved replacing damaged wooden planks, treating the remaining timber against further decay, and restoring the ship's original rigging using traditional techniques. ---- When completed, the restoration not only preserved the ship's historical authenticity but also made it safe for the public to board and explore, ensuring that it remains an educational attraction for future generations.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The project also incorporated modern fire suppression systems to protect the vessel from potential hazards."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The ship had suffered gradual damage from decades of exposure to saltwater, weather, and pests."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "The vessel is widely regarded as one of the finest surviving examples of nineteenth-century shipbuilding."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "There was a chance that replacing too much original timber might compromise the ship's historical authenticity."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Despite the extensive damage it had suffered, the ship had remained a popular attraction throughout the restoration."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve süreç anlatımıyla sonuç cümlesi arasında doğru köprüyü kuran tek seçenek budur. Cevap: C."}], "4": [{"id": "ydtozg8-s54-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (CALMING/SUPPORTIVE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A close friend of yours says he feels shaky before his first solo violin performance, but you know he has practised the piece hundreds of times. So, you try to calm him down in a supportive way by saying: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I'm sure the audience won't notice even if you make a few mistakes here and there."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "If you mess up, just remember it's only one performance out of many in your career."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Honestly, a lot of musicians never fully get over stage fright, so don't expect it to go away."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Feeling shaky before a solo is completely normal, but you've practised so much that you'll play beautifully."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Try to think of something else entirely so you forget about the performance until it starts."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Çok prova yapmış bir arkadaşı desteklerken, endişenin normal olduğunu kabul edip hazırlığına dayanarak güven veren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s55-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (EXPLAINING RESPONSIBILITY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Your niece wants to adopt a parrot, thinking it will just be about teaching it fun phrases to say. However, she does not realise how much long-term commitment it requires. To explain to her that a parrot is not only an entertaining pet, you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Different parrot species can live for several decades if properly cared for."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Many parrots enjoy having a variety of toys to keep them mentally stimulated."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Parrots are known for being able to mimic a wide range of sounds."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "A parrot is a living being that depends on you for social interaction, proper diet, and a safe environment for its entire life, not just entertainment."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "A parrot does need long-term care, but don't worry, we can figure it out together as we go."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Papağanın sadece eğlence değil, yaşam boyu ihtiyaçları olan canlı bir varlık olduğunu vurgulayan ifade doğrudur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s56-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (PRACTICAL TRAVEL WARNING)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "One of your foreign friends tells you she wants to visit Cappadocia, and so she will go during the summer holiday. Since you know the region is famous for both hot air balloons and hiking valleys, you want to suggest more, so you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "You should try to book the balloon ride as early as possible, since flights fill up fast."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "It would be a good idea to wear comfortable shoes, as the valleys involve a lot of walking."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "I wish you had told me earlier that you wanted to go; I went two summers ago and loved it."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "If I were you, I'd also stay in one of the cave hotels, since it's a unique experience unique to the region."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "If possible, consider going in spring or autumn, when the temperatures are more comfortable."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Ek bir öneri sunma bağlamında, bölgeye özgü benzersiz bir deneyimi (mağara oteli) öneren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s57-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (APOLOGY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "You are visiting a friend's home for the first time. While admiring a shelf of decorative plates, you accidentally bump into it, and one plate falls and cracks. Highly embarrassed, you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I'm not sure how that happened, but I think the shelf was a little unstable."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "These plates look quite old anyway; I'm sure it's not too big a loss."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "You should really keep fragile items further from the edge of the shelf."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "I'm so sorry! That was careless of me. Please let me replace it or pay for the damage."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "I guess if the shelf had been more secure, this wouldn't have happened."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Kazara oluşan bir kazadan sonra samimi özür dileyip telafi teklif eden ifade doğrudur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s58-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (SERIOUS PROFESSIONAL CONCERN)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "You have been ignoring your doctor's advice to reduce your sugar intake, but you find it difficult to change your habits. At your routine check-up, she reviews your latest blood test, and the results show your blood sugar levels have risen further. She is concerned about your health and says in a serious manner: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I'm glad you're managing without changing your diet, but you might consider it eventually."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "I'm not surprised by these results; this is exactly what happens when patients ignore my advice."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Maybe we should just forget the diet changes and try medication instead."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "I understand changing habits is hard, but avoiding it is exactly why your levels have risen. Let's work out small, manageable changes together."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The results are clear. Ignoring this advice is causing irreversible damage to your organs."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Ciddi bir sağlık uyarısı yaparken hem sorunu açıklayan hem de yapıcı bir çözüm öneren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g59-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (PSYCHOLOGY CONCEPT)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The mere exposure effect describes people's tendency to develop a preference for things simply because they are familiar with them. First demonstrated through psychological experiments in the 1960s, the effect explains why a song a person disliked at first can eventually become one of their favourites after being heard repeatedly. The effect occurs because repeated exposure to a stimulus gradually reduces the uncertainty a person feels toward it. ---- Advertisers have long taken advantage of this tendency, repeating brand names and jingles frequently in the hope that familiarity alone will build consumer preference.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The experiments were first conducted using a range of unfamiliar images and sounds."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "As a result, advertising has become completely unnecessary in modern marketing."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Musical preferences often vary considerably between different age groups."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "As uncertainty decreases, the stimulus begins to feel safer and more pleasant, even without any objective change in its quality."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "This means that people always prefer entirely new and unfamiliar experiences over familiar ones."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve bir sonraki cümleye mantıksal olarak bağlanan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g60-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (HISTORICAL ROLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Caravan traders along the Silk Road were not important just for the sake of transporting silk and spices across vast distances. ---- By carrying goods, ideas, and technologies between distant civilisations, they helped connect cultures that would otherwise have had little contact with one another. Their long journeys also exposed them to diverse languages and customs, making them both merchants and unofficial cultural intermediaries. Over time, their central role declined as sea routes gradually became a faster and more efficient means of long-distance trade.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Their navigational skill was considered a divine gift, often linked to supernatural beings from regional mythology."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Many of them were also skilled soldiers who would defend distant kingdoms during times of war."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "They therefore held significant religious power, often appointed as advisors to regional emperors."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "These traders played a key role in connecting distant civilisations, exchanging goods, ideas, and technologies along their routes."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The primary duty of these traders was to compose detailed maps intended to please wealthy sponsors back home."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve mesleğin gerçek işlevini doğru şekilde tanımlayan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g61-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (RESTORATION PROJECT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The renovation of a century-old suspension bridge in 2020 was the most extensive engineering project carried out on the structure since it first opened to traffic, addressing corroded cables and weakened support towers. It involved replacing the main suspension cables, reinforcing the towers, and upgrading the road deck to handle modern traffic loads. ---- When completed, the renovation not only restored the bridge's structural safety but also preserved its distinctive historic appearance, ensuring that it remains open to both vehicles and pedestrians for future generations.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The project also incorporated pedestrian walkways and bicycle lanes to accommodate modern commuters."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The bridge had suffered gradual deterioration from decades of heavy traffic, salt exposure, and severe weather."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "The bridge remains one of the most photographed engineering landmarks in the entire region."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "There was a chance that the aging support towers might not withstand the stress of continued heavy use."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Despite its age and the challenges of the renovation, the bridge had remained open to limited traffic throughout most of the project."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve süreç anlatımıyla sonuç cümlesi arasında doğru köprüyü kuran tek seçenek budur. Cevap: D."}], "5": [{"id": "ydtozg8-s54-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (CALMING/SUPPORTIVE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A close friend of yours says she feels tense before her final exam in mathematics, but you know she has solved countless practice problems all month. So, you try to calm her down in a supportive way by saying: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "If you don't do well, you can always retake the course again next semester."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "I wouldn't stress about it; grades in this subject rarely matter later in life."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "You should probably do one more practice problem right now to feel more prepared."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "A lot of students struggle with this exam, so don't expect too much from yourself."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "It's normal to feel tense, but you've solved so many practice problems that you're well prepared for this."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Çok çalışmış bir arkadaşı desteklerken, endişenin normal olduğunu kabul edip hazırlığına dayanarak güven veren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s55-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (EXPLAINING RESPONSIBILITY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Your younger cousin wants to join the school choir, thinking it will just be about singing his favourite songs. However, he does not realise how much discipline it requires. To explain to him that being in a choir is not only about singing for fun, you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Different choirs perform different styles of music depending on the season."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Many choir members enjoy the friendships they build during rehearsals."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Choir performances often take place in front of large audiences at school events."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "A school choir usually rehearses several times a week before a big performance."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Being in a choir requires you to commit to regular rehearsals, follow instructions carefully, and support the group, not just sing what you enjoy."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Korodaki disiplinin sadece şarkı söylemekten ibaret olmadığını, düzenli katılım ve grup uyumu gerektirdiğini vurgulayan ifade doğrudur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s56-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (PRACTICAL TRAVEL WARNING)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "One of your foreign friends tells you he wants to visit Bangkok, and so he will go during the summer holiday. Since you know that period falls within the rainy season, you want to warn him, so you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "You should try to visit the temples early in the morning before the heat and humidity build up."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "It would be a good idea to pack a light raincoat, since sudden downpours are common."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "I wish you had told me earlier that you wanted to go; I went in December and could have given you tips sooner."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "If I were you, I'd also visit Chiang Mai, since it offers a nice contrast to the busy city."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "If possible, consider going between November and February, when the weather is drier and cooler."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Yağmur mevsimini göz önünde bulundurarak alternatif ve daha uygun bir seyahat zamanı öneren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s57-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (APOLOGY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "You are attending a colleague's farewell party. While trying to take a group photo, you accidentally step backward into a table, knocking over a cake. Highly embarrassed, you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I'm not sure how that happened, but I think the table was placed too close to where we were standing."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "These cakes are never as sturdy as they look anyway."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "You should really set up tables further from where people are taking photos."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "I guess if the venue had been bigger, this wouldn't have happened."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "I'm so sorry, everyone! That was clumsy of me. Let me help clean this up and see if we can order another cake."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Kazara oluşan bir kazadan sonra samimi özür dileyip somut bir çözüm öneren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s58-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (SERIOUS PROFESSIONAL CONCERN)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "You have been refusing to wear your prescribed back brace, but you feel self-conscious about how it looks. At your routine appointment, your doctor examines your spine, and the results show your posture has worsened significantly. He is concerned about your health and says in a serious manner: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I'm glad you're managing without the brace, but you might consider it in the future."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Maybe we should just forget the brace and hope things improve naturally."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "I'm not surprised by these results; this is exactly what happens when patients ignore my advice."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "I understand it feels uncomfortable to wear, but avoiding it is exactly why your posture has worsened."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The results are clear. Not wearing the brace is causing irreversible damage to your spine."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Sonuçların kesinliğini vurgulayan ve kalıcı hasara dikkat çeken ciddi bir uyarı ifade doğrudur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g59-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (PSYCHOLOGY CONCEPT)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A self-fulfilling prophecy describes a situation in which a person's expectation about an outcome directly influences their behaviour in ways that make that outcome more likely to occur. First explored systematically by sociologists in the mid-twentieth century, the concept explains why a student who is expected to fail might unconsciously reduce their own effort, ultimately fulfilling that very expectation. The effect occurs because expectations, whether held by oneself or communicated by others, subtly shape motivation, attention, and behaviour. ---- Teachers who are told, even falsely, that certain students are exceptionally gifted have been shown to unconsciously give those students more encouragement and attention.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "This means that expectations have no real influence on how people ultimately behave."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Sociology as a discipline developed significantly during the twentieth century."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "As a result, all academic outcomes are now considered entirely predetermined from birth."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Classroom sizes have decreased considerably in many countries in recent decades."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "This influence can happen without either the person expecting the outcome or acting on the expectation being fully aware of it."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve bir sonraki cümleye mantıksal olarak bağlanan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g60-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (HISTORICAL ROLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Lighthouse keepers stationed along dangerous coastlines were not important just for the sake of living in isolated, scenic locations. ---- By maintaining the light and monitoring the weather around the clock, they helped prevent countless ships from wrecking on hidden rocks and shallow waters. Their careful record-keeping also assisted maritime authorities in tracking shipping patterns, making them both safety guardians and informal weather observers. Over time, the keepers' hands-on role declined as automated lighthouse systems gradually replaced the need for constant human supervision.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Their dedication was considered a divine gift, often linked to supernatural beings from maritime folklore."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Many of them were also skilled fishermen who would trade their catch with passing sailors."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "They therefore held significant political power, often influencing maritime trade laws directly."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "The primary duty of these workers was to compose detailed poetry inspired by the isolation of coastal life."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "These workers played a key role in guiding ships safely, preventing shipwrecks, and monitoring coastal weather conditions."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve mesleğin gerçek işlevini doğru şekilde tanımlayan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g61-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (RESTORATION PROJECT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The restoration of a medieval cathedral in 2021 was the largest conservation project undertaken on the building in over a century, addressing water damage, crumbling stonework, and a badly deteriorated roof. It involved repairing the stone facade, replacing damaged roof timbers, and restoring the cathedral's stained-glass windows using traditional craftsmanship. ---- When completed, the restoration not only preserved the cathedral's architectural grandeur but also strengthened its structure against future weather damage, ensuring that it remains a place of worship and heritage for future generations.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The project also incorporated modern fire detection systems to help protect the building going forward."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The cathedral had suffered gradual deterioration from centuries of weather exposure and pollution."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "The cathedral remains one of the most visited religious landmarks in the entire country."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "There was a chance that the crumbling stonework might collapse before repairs could be completed."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Despite the extensive damage and years of restoration work, the cathedral had continued to hold regular services throughout the project."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve süreç anlatımıyla sonuç cümlesi arasında doğru köprüyü kuran tek seçenek budur. Cevap: E."}], "6": [{"id": "ydtozg8-s54-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (CALMING/SUPPORTIVE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A close friend of yours says he feels uneasy before his first flight as a passenger, but you know the airline has an excellent safety record. So, you try to calm him down in a supportive way by saying: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Feeling uneasy before a first flight is completely normal, and this airline has a great safety record, so you'll be fine."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "If something goes wrong, there's honestly not much anyone can do about it anyway."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "You should probably just avoid looking out the window during takeoff and landing."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "A lot of people never really get used to flying, no matter how many times they do it."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Try not to think about the flight at all until you're already at the gate."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Güvenlik geçmişi iyi bir havayoluyla uçacak bir arkadaşı desteklerken, endişenin normal olduğunu kabul edip somut bir gerekçeyle güven veren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s55-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (EXPLAINING RESPONSIBILITY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Your little sister wants to keep a goldfish, thinking it will just be about watching it swim around. However, she does not realise how much upkeep it requires. To explain to her that a goldfish is not only a decoration, you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "A goldfish is a living animal that depends on you for clean water, proper feeding, and a suitable tank, not just something to watch."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Different goldfish varieties can grow to very different sizes."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Many people find watching fish swim to be quite relaxing."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Goldfish tanks come in a wide range of shapes and sizes."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "A goldfish does need regular care, but don't worry, I'll clean the tank whenever it's needed."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Japon balığının canlı bir varlık olarak temel bakım ihtiyaçları olduğunu vurgulayan ifade doğrudur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s56-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (PRACTICAL TRAVEL WARNING)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "One of your foreign friends tells you she wants to visit Machu Picchu, and so she will go during the summer holiday. Since you know that period falls within the region's rainy season, you want to warn her, so you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "You should bring a good rain jacket and waterproof shoes, since trails can get quite slippery."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "It would be a good idea to book your entry ticket well in advance, since daily visitor numbers are limited."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "I wish you had told me earlier that you wanted to go; I went in June and could have shared some tips."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "If I were you, I'd also spend a day exploring the nearby town of Cusco before heading up."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "If possible, consider going between May and September, when the weather tends to be drier."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Yağmur mevsiminde kaygan patikalara karşı somut bir önlem (yağmurluk, su geçirmez ayakkabı) öneren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s57-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (APOLOGY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "You are touring a friend's garden. While admiring the flowers, you accidentally step on a small plant bed, crushing several seedlings. Highly embarrassed, you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I'm so sorry! That was careless of me. Let me help you replant some new seedlings."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "I'm not sure how that happened, but I think the bed was placed too close to the path."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Seedlings are pretty fragile anyway; I'm sure a few losses don't matter much."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "You should really mark the plant beds more clearly for guests."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "I guess if the path had been wider, this wouldn't have happened."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Kazara oluşan bir kazadan sonra samimi özür dileyip telafi teklif eden ifade doğrudur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s58-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (SERIOUS PROFESSIONAL CONCERN)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "You have been avoiding your recommended eye exercises for lazy eye, but you find them tedious. At your routine appointment, your ophthalmologist tests your vision, and the results show no improvement in your weaker eye. She is concerned about your health and says in a serious manner: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I understand the exercises feel tedious, but skipping them is exactly why there's been no improvement. Let's find a routine that's easier to keep up with."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "I'm glad you're managing without the exercises, but you might consider doing them eventually."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "I'm not surprised by these results; this is exactly what happens when my advice is ignored."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Maybe we should just forget the exercises and consider surgery instead."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The results are clear. Skipping these exercises is causing permanent vision loss in that eye."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Ciddi bir sağlık uyarısı yaparken hem sorunu açıklayan hem de yapıcı bir çözüm öneren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g59-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (PSYCHOLOGY CONCEPT)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Hindsight bias describes the tendency for people to believe, after an event has occurred, that they could have predicted its outcome all along. First studied extensively by psychologists in the 1970s, the concept explains why people often say 'I knew it all along' after a surprising event turns out a certain way. The bias occurs because once an outcome is known, the brain reconstructs memories of earlier uncertainty to fit the now-known result. ---- This distortion can be particularly problematic in fields such as medicine and finance, where professionals may unfairly judge earlier decisions as obviously flawed simply because the outcome is now known.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "As a result, people often underestimate how uncertain a situation genuinely seemed before the outcome was revealed."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "This means that people are generally excellent at predicting future events accurately."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Psychological research methods have become increasingly sophisticated since the 1970s."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "As a result, memory itself has been proven to be entirely unreliable in every context."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Financial markets are influenced by a wide range of unpredictable global events."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve bir sonraki cümleye mantıksal olarak bağlanan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g60-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (HISTORICAL ROLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Night watchmen patrolling the streets of pre-modern towns were not important just for calling out the hour as they walked. ---- By keeping an eye out for fires, thieves, and other disturbances, they provided one of the earliest forms of organised public safety before formal police forces existed. Their familiar presence also reassured residents, making them both protectors and a comforting nightly routine. Over time, the watchmen's informal role declined as professional police departments gradually took over the responsibility of maintaining public order.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "These officials played a key role in maintaining public safety, watching for danger, and reassuring residents through the night."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The primary duty of these officials was to compose new town regulations intended to please local merchants."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Many of them were also skilled blacksmiths who would repair tools and weapons during the day."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Their vigilance was considered a divine gift, often linked to supernatural beings from local legend."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "They therefore held significant political power, often deciding local tax rates on their own."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve mesleğin gerçek işlevini doğru şekilde tanımlayan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g61-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (RESTORATION PROJECT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The renovation of a nineteenth-century opera house in 2016 was the most comprehensive project undertaken on the building since it originally opened, addressing outdated wiring, worn seating, and a deteriorating stage floor. It involved installing modern electrical and sound systems, restoring the ornate ceiling murals, and replacing the stage floor with reinforced, fire-resistant materials. ---- When completed, the renovation not only preserved the theatre's ornate historical character but also equipped it with modern technical capabilities, ensuring that it remains a premier venue for performances for future generations.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The project also incorporated improved accessibility features, including ramps and lifts for wheelchair users."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The theatre had suffered gradual decline from decades of heavy use and outdated maintenance practices."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "The opera house remains one of the most architecturally admired performance venues in the country."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "There was a chance that restoring the murals might damage the delicate original paintwork underneath."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Despite its ageing infrastructure, the theatre had continued to host performances throughout most of its history."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve süreç anlatımıyla sonuç cümlesi arasında doğru köprüyü kuran tek seçenek budur. Cevap: A."}], "7": [{"id": "ydtozg8-s54-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (CALMING/SUPPORTIVE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A close friend of yours says she feels nervous before defending her thesis in front of the committee, but you know she has prepared thorough answers to every likely question. So, you try to calm her down in a supportive way by saying: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "If the committee asks something you don't know, just admit you have no idea and move on."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "It's natural to feel nervous before a defence, but you've prepared such thorough answers that you'll do well."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Try not to worry; most committees don't really pay close attention during the defence anyway."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Honestly, a lot of students never fully recover from a difficult thesis defence."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "You should probably prepare a few more answers right now, just to be safe."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Tez savunmasına iyi hazırlanmış bir arkadaşı desteklerken, endişenin doğal olduğunu kabul edip hazırlığına dayanarak güven veren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s55-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (EXPLAINING RESPONSIBILITY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Your neighbour's son wants to start a small business selling lemonade, thinking it will just be about earning quick money. However, he does not realise how much planning it requires. To explain to him that running a stand is not only about profit, you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Different recipes for lemonade can taste quite different depending on the ingredients."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Running a stand means you are responsible for planning, managing costs, and dealing with customers, not just collecting money."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Many kids enjoy setting up lemonade stands during the summer holidays."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Lemonade stands are often more successful in busy neighbourhoods."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Running a stand does require planning, but don't worry, I'll handle the difficult parts for you."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Küçük bir işletmenin sadece kazançtan ibaret olmadığını, planlama ve müşteri ilişkileri gerektirdiğini vurgulayan ifade doğrudur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s56-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (PRACTICAL TRAVEL WARNING)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "One of your foreign friends tells you he wants to visit Reykjavik, and so he will go during the winter holiday. Since you know daylight hours are extremely short at that time of year, you want to warn him, so you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "You should try to plan outdoor activities carefully, since it gets dark quite early in the afternoon."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "It would be a good idea to check the aurora forecast, since the long dark hours actually make it a great time to see the northern lights."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "I wish you had told me earlier that you wanted to go; I went in July and could have shared some tips."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "If I were you, I'd also visit the Blue Lagoon, since it's especially nice in cold weather."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "If possible, consider going in summer instead, when daylight lasts almost the entire day."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Kısa gün ışığını olumlu bir fırsata (kuzey ışıkları) dönüştüren somut bir öneri sunan ifade doğrudur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s57-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (APOLOGY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "You are helping out at a school science fair. While adjusting a display, you accidentally knock over a model volcano, spilling the baking-soda mixture everywhere. Highly embarrassed, you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I'm not sure how that happened, but I think the display was set up a bit too close to the edge."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "I'm terribly sorry! That was clumsy of me. Let me help clean this up and fix the display."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "These science projects are never that sturdy anyway."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "You should really secure displays more firmly at these events."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "I guess if the table had been more level, this wouldn't have happened."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Kazara oluşan bir kazadan sonra samimi özür dileyip durumu düzeltmeye çalışan ifade doğrudur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s58-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (SERIOUS PROFESSIONAL CONCERN)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "You have been refusing to use your prescribed inhaler regularly, but you worry about becoming dependent on it. At your routine check-up, your doctor tests your lung function, and the results show it has declined further. He is concerned about your health and says in a serious manner: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I'm glad you're managing without it, but you might consider using it in the future."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "I understand the worry about dependency, but avoiding the inhaler is exactly why your lung function has declined. Let's talk about how it actually works."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "I'm not surprised by these results; this is exactly what happens when patients ignore my advice."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Maybe we should just forget the inhaler and try breathing exercises instead."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The results are clear. Not using the inhaler is causing irreversible damage to your lungs."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Ciddi bir sağlık uyarısı yaparken hastanın endişesini anlayıp yapıcı bir çözüm öneren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g59-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (PSYCHOLOGY CONCEPT)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Learned helplessness describes a state in which a person or animal stops trying to change or avoid a negative situation, having learned from repeated past experience that their efforts make no difference. First identified through experiments with animals in the 1960s, the concept later helped explain certain patterns of passivity observed in humans facing prolonged difficult circumstances. The state develops when repeated attempts to escape or control a situation consistently fail to produce any change. ---- Once this belief takes hold, a person may stop attempting to improve their situation even when new opportunities for change genuinely become available.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Psychologists continue to debate the ethics of early animal research methods."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Over time, the individual begins to believe that their actions have no meaningful effect on the outcome at all."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "This means that people facing difficult circumstances always find a way to overcome them eventually."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "The original experiments were conducted using controlled laboratory conditions."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "As a result, human motivation has been shown to be entirely unrelated to past experience."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve bir sonraki cümleye mantıksal olarak bağlanan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g60-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (HISTORICAL ROLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Royal couriers serving medieval kingdoms were not important just for the sake of riding swiftly between distant castles. ---- By carrying official letters, urgent military orders, and diplomatic messages, they kept rulers informed and connected across territories that could otherwise take weeks to cross. Their reliability and speed also made them trusted figures at court, making them both messengers and valued royal servants. Over time, the couriers' essential role declined as postal systems and telegraph networks gradually offered faster, more reliable communication.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Their speed was considered a divine gift, often linked to supernatural beings from regional folklore."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "These riders played a key role in delivering urgent messages, connecting distant territories, and supporting royal administration."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Many of them were also skilled blacksmiths who would shoe horses for travelling merchants."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "They therefore held significant political power, often making final decisions on behalf of the king."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The primary duty of these riders was to compose diplomatic treaties intended to please foreign rulers."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve mesleğin gerçek işlevini doğru şekilde tanımlayan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g61-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (RESTORATION PROJECT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The restoration of a Second World War-era aircraft in 2017 was the most extensive project undertaken on the plane since it was retired from active service, addressing corroded metal panels and a non-functioning engine. It involved rebuilding the engine using original specifications, replacing corroded sections of the fuselage, and repainting the exterior in its historically accurate wartime colours. ---- When completed, the restoration not only returned the aircraft to full flying condition but also preserved its historical accuracy in remarkable detail, ensuring that it remains a working piece of aviation history for future generations.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The project also incorporated modern safety instruments discreetly hidden within the historic cockpit."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The aircraft had suffered significant deterioration after decades of storage in poor environmental conditions."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "The aircraft type is widely regarded as one of the most significant designs of the era."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "There was a chance that rebuilding the engine might not restore it to genuine working condition."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Despite years of storage and deterioration, the aircraft had remained largely intact structurally."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve süreç anlatımıyla sonuç cümlesi arasında doğru köprüyü kuran tek seçenek budur. Cevap: B."}], "8": [{"id": "ydtozg8-s54-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (CALMING/SUPPORTIVE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A close friend of yours says he feels anxious before his first day coaching a youth football team, but you know he has studied the training plan carefully. So, you try to calm him down in a supportive way by saying: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "If the kids don't listen to you, it probably just means coaching isn't for you."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "I wouldn't worry too much; young kids rarely remember their first coach anyway."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "It's completely normal to feel anxious, but you've studied the training plan so carefully that you'll do great."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Honestly, I'm a bit worried too, since coaching kids can go wrong in so many ways."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Just try not to think about it until the first practice actually starts."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Antrenman planını iyi çalışmış bir arkadaşı desteklerken, endişenin normal olduğunu kabul edip hazırlığına dayanarak güven veren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s55-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (EXPLAINING RESPONSIBILITY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Your younger brother wants to join the school debate team, thinking it will just be about arguing and winning. However, he does not realise how much preparation it requires. To explain to him that debate is not only about winning, you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Different debate formats follow very different sets of rules."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Many debate teams travel to compete in tournaments throughout the year."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Being on a debate team means you are responsible for thorough research, careful preparation, and respectful argument, not just winning."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Debate skills are considered useful for many future careers."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Debate does require preparation, but don't worry, I'll help you write your arguments every time."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Münazaranın sadece kazanmaktan ibaret olmadığını, araştırma ve hazırlık gerektirdiğini vurgulayan ifade doğrudur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s56-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (PRACTICAL TRAVEL WARNING)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "One of your foreign friends tells you she wants to visit New Orleans, and so she will go during the summer holiday. Since you know that period overlaps with hurricane season, you want to warn her, so you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "You should try to check the weather forecast regularly in the days before your trip."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "It would be a good idea to keep some flexibility in your travel plans in case of storms."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "I wish you had told me earlier that you wanted to go; I went in March and could have shared some tips."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "If I were you, I'd also plan a day trip to the nearby bayous."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "If possible, consider going in spring instead, when the weather is generally calmer."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "'Daha önce söyleseydin' ifadesi, farklı bir zamanda gitmiş olma deneyimini paylaşan doğal bir tepkidir. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s57-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (APOLOGY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "You are browsing in a small bookstore. While reaching for a book on a high shelf, you accidentally knock several books onto the floor. Highly embarrassed, you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I'm not sure how that happened, but I think the shelf was a little too crowded."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Books fall off shelves all the time; I wouldn't worry about it too much."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "I'm so sorry! That was clumsy of me. Let me pick these up and put them back properly."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "You should really organise the shelves so books don't fall so easily."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "I guess if the shelf had been lower, this wouldn't have happened."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Kazara oluşan bir kazadan sonra samimi özür dileyip durumu düzelten ifade doğrudur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s58-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (SERIOUS PROFESSIONAL CONCERN)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "You have been avoiding your recommended physiotherapy sessions after knee surgery, but you find the exercises painful. At your routine follow-up, your surgeon examines your knee, and the results show limited range of motion. He is concerned about your health and says in a serious manner: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I'm glad you're managing without the sessions, but you might consider attending eventually."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Maybe we should just forget the physiotherapy and hope the knee heals on its own."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "I understand the exercises are painful, but avoiding them is exactly why your range of motion is limited. Let's adjust the plan so it's more manageable."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "I'm not surprised by these results; this is exactly what happens when patients ignore my advice."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The results are clear. Skipping physiotherapy is causing permanent stiffness in your knee."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Ciddi bir sağlık uyarısı yaparken ağrıyı kabul edip yapıcı bir çözüm öneren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g59-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (PSYCHOLOGY CONCEPT)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The peak-end rule describes how people tend to judge an overall experience largely based on how it felt at its most intense moment and at its very end, rather than based on the total duration or sum of every moment. First demonstrated through experiments involving mildly unpleasant experiences in the 1990s, the rule helps explain why a long, mostly enjoyable holiday can be remembered negatively if it ends with a stressful, chaotic departure. The rule occurs because memory does not store experiences as a complete, moment-by-moment record. ---- Businesses in hospitality and customer service have used this insight deliberately, focusing extra effort on ensuring a strong, positive final impression.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "As a result, every single moment of an experience is now known to be remembered with equal accuracy."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Customer satisfaction surveys are commonly used across many industries."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Instead, the brain relies on a few especially memorable moments to represent the entire experience."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "This means that the length of an experience is always the most important factor in how it is remembered."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The original experiments involved participants submerging their hands in cold water."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve bir sonraki cümleye mantıksal olarak bağlanan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g60-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (HISTORICAL ROLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Apprentices working under master craftspeople in medieval towns were not important just for performing simple, repetitive tasks in the workshop. ---- By learning specialised skills over many years under close supervision, they ensured that valuable trade knowledge was passed carefully from one generation to the next. Their gradual progression through the trade also strengthened the guild system as a whole, making them both learners and future guarantors of quality craftsmanship. Over time, the apprenticeship system's dominance declined as formal schools and factories gradually offered alternative paths into skilled work.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Their dedication was considered a divine gift, often linked to supernatural beings from local mythology."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "They therefore held significant political power, often deciding prices within their trade independently."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "These workers played a key role in preserving specialised skills, ensuring that trade knowledge passed accurately between generations."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "The primary duty of these workers was to compose new trade regulations intended to please the guild masters."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Many of them were also skilled musicians who would entertain workshop owners during long working hours."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve mesleğin gerçek işlevini doğru şekilde tanımlayan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g61-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (RESTORATION PROJECT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The renovation of a centuries-old public fountain in 2019 was the most significant restoration project the monument had undergone since its original construction, addressing crumbling stonework and a failing water circulation system. It involved repairing the ornate stone carvings, installing a modern, energy-efficient pump system, and restoring the original decorative lighting. ---- When completed, the renovation not only revived the fountain's original visual splendour but also made its operation far more sustainable, ensuring that it remains a beloved public landmark for future generations.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The project also incorporated water-recycling technology to reduce the fountain's overall water consumption."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The fountain had suffered gradual deterioration from decades of pollution, weathering, and mineral buildup."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "The fountain remains one of the most iconic and frequently photographed landmarks in the city."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "There was a chance that repairing the delicate stone carvings might further damage the fragile original details."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Despite years of disrepair, the fountain had continued to operate, though only at a fraction of its original capacity."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve süreç anlatımıyla sonuç cümlesi arasında doğru köprüyü kuran tek seçenek budur. Cevap: C."}], "9": [{"id": "ydtozg8-s54-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (CALMING/SUPPORTIVE)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A close friend of yours says she feels nervous before her first cooking demonstration in front of a live audience, but you know she has practised every recipe step multiple times. So, you try to calm her down in a supportive way by saying: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I'm sure the audience won't notice even if a dish doesn't turn out quite right."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "If something goes wrong, just remember it's only one demonstration among many you'll do."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Honestly, a lot of chefs never fully get comfortable cooking in front of an audience."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Feeling nervous before a demonstration is completely normal, but you've practised every step so thoroughly that you'll do wonderfully."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Try to think about something else entirely so you forget about it until it starts."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Tüm adımları prova etmiş bir arkadaşı desteklerken, endişenin normal olduğunu kabul edip hazırlığına dayanarak güven veren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s55-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (EXPLAINING RESPONSIBILITY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Your cousin wants to adopt a horse, thinking it will just be about riding it whenever she wants. However, she does not realise how much daily responsibility it requires. To explain to her that a horse is not only a means of enjoyment, you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Different horse breeds are suited to different types of riding."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Many people find spending time with horses to be very calming."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Horses can form strong bonds with the people who care for them regularly."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "A horse is a living animal that depends on you every single day for feeding, exercise, and proper shelter, not just occasional rides."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "A horse does need daily care, but don't worry, the stable staff will take care of everything."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Atın günlük bakım gerektiren canlı bir varlık olduğunu, sadece binmek için var olmadığını vurgulayan ifade doğrudur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s56-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (PRACTICAL TRAVEL WARNING)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "One of your foreign friends tells you he wants to visit the Amazon rainforest, and so he will go during the summer holiday. Since you know the region has both a river-cruise season and a jungle-trekking season, you want to suggest more, so you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "You should try to book a guided tour, since navigating the rainforest alone can be quite dangerous."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "It would be a good idea to pack insect repellent, since mosquitoes are common throughout the year."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "I wish you had told me earlier that you wanted to go; I went last year and loved every moment of it."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "If I were you, I'd also consider a river cruise, since it offers a completely different perspective on the rainforest."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "If possible, consider going in the dry season, when trekking trails are easier to access."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Ek bir öneri sunma bağlamında, farklı bir deneyim türünü (nehir turu) öneren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s57-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (APOLOGY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "You are attending a wedding reception. While dancing enthusiastically, you accidentally bump into a waiter, causing him to spill a tray of drinks. Highly embarrassed, you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I'm not sure how that happened, but I think the dance floor was a bit too crowded."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Spills happen at every wedding; I wouldn't worry about it too much."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "You should really keep waiters away from the dance floor during the reception."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "I'm terribly sorry! That was careless of me. Let me help clean this up and get you some more drinks."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "I guess if the tray had been lighter, this wouldn't have happened."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Kazara oluşan bir kazadan sonra samimi özür dileyip telafi teklif eden ifade doğrudur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s58-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (SERIOUS PROFESSIONAL CONCERN)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "You have been ignoring your dermatologist's advice to apply sunscreen daily, but you find it inconvenient. At your routine check-up, she examines your skin, and the results show new sun damage has developed. She is concerned about your health and says in a serious manner: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I'm glad you're managing without sunscreen, but you might consider using it eventually."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "I'm not surprised by these results; this is exactly what happens when patients ignore my advice."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Maybe we should just forget the sunscreen and try a different skincare routine."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "I understand it feels inconvenient, but avoiding it is exactly why new damage has developed. Let's find a product that's easier to fit into your routine."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The results are clear. Not using sunscreen is causing irreversible damage to your skin."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Ciddi bir sağlık uyarısı yaparken pratik zorluğu kabul edip yapıcı bir çözüm öneren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g59-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (PSYCHOLOGY CONCEPT)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The spacing effect describes the finding that information is remembered more effectively when study sessions are spread out over time, rather than crammed into a single, intense session. First documented by a German psychologist in the late nineteenth century, the effect explains why reviewing material briefly over several days tends to produce stronger long-term memory than studying the same material for an equivalent total time in one sitting. The effect occurs because spaced repetition forces the brain to retrieve information after it has begun to fade slightly. ---- Modern flashcard applications now often use algorithms based on this principle, scheduling reviews at gradually increasing intervals.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The original research was conducted using lists of nonsense syllables."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "As a result, reviewing material has been proven to be entirely unnecessary for long-term memory."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Memory researchers continue to study a wide range of related cognitive phenomena."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "This retrieval effort appears to strengthen the memory more than simply reviewing information while it is still fresh."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "This means that studying intensively in a single session always produces the strongest possible memory."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve bir sonraki cümleye mantıksal olarak bağlanan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g60-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (HISTORICAL ROLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Itinerant peddlers travelling between medieval villages were not important just for the sake of selling small household goods. ---- By carrying news, gossip, and rare items between isolated communities, they served as one of the few connections that remote villages had to the wider world. Their frequent visits also gave villagers access to goods otherwise unavailable locally, making them both traders and informal messengers. Over time, the peddlers' role declined as improved roads and permanent shops gradually made regular trade routes unnecessary.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Their persuasive skill was considered a divine gift, often linked to supernatural beings from village folklore."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Many of them were also skilled healers who would treat illnesses using local herbal remedies."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "They therefore held significant political power, often influencing decisions made by village councils."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "These traders played a key role in connecting isolated villages, sharing news, and providing access to distant goods."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The primary duty of these traders was to compose detailed trade agreements intended to please wealthy landowners."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve mesleğin gerçek işlevini doğru şekilde tanımlayan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g61-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (RESTORATION PROJECT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The restoration of a set of ancient defensive city walls in 2020 was the largest heritage project the site had undergone in decades, addressing crumbling sections, unstable foundations, and extensive plant overgrowth. It involved stabilising the foundations, carefully removing invasive vegetation, and rebuilding collapsed sections using matching traditional materials. ---- When completed, the restoration not only preserved the walls' historical integrity but also made large sections safely accessible to visitors for the first time in years, ensuring that they remain an important heritage site for future generations.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The project also incorporated informational signage to help visitors understand the walls' historical significance."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The walls had suffered gradual damage from centuries of weathering, plant growth, and nearby urban development."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "The walls remain one of the best-preserved examples of ancient defensive architecture in the region."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "There was a chance that removing the extensive plant overgrowth might further destabilise already weakened sections."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Despite centuries of neglect, significant portions of the walls had remained remarkably well preserved."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve süreç anlatımıyla sonuç cümlesi arasında doğru köprüyü kuran tek seçenek budur. Cevap: D."}], "10": [{"id": "ydtozg8-s54-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (CALMING/SUPPORTIVE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A close friend of yours says he feels tense before his citizenship interview, but you know he has studied the material extensively for weeks. So, you try to calm him down in a supportive way by saying: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "If you don't pass, you can always apply again after a certain waiting period."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "I wouldn't stress about it; the interview questions are usually far too random to prepare for anyway."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "You should probably review the material one more time right before you go in."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "A lot of applicants struggle with this interview, so try not to expect too much from yourself."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "It's normal to feel tense, but you've studied so extensively that you're well prepared for this interview."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Haftalarca çalışmış bir arkadaşı desteklerken, endişenin normal olduğunu kabul edip hazırlığına dayanarak güven veren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s55-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (EXPLAINING RESPONSIBILITY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Your younger sister wants to babysit the neighbour's toddler, thinking it will just be about playing games all afternoon. However, she does not realise how much attentiveness it requires. To explain to her that babysitting is not only about playing, you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Different toddlers have very different personalities and energy levels."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Many toddlers enjoy simple games like hide and seek."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Babysitting can be a good way to earn some extra pocket money."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Toddlers usually need a nap sometime in the early afternoon."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Babysitting means you are responsible for a child's safety, meals, and wellbeing at every moment, not just entertaining them."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Çocuk bakımının sadece oyun oynamaktan ibaret olmadığını, sürekli dikkat ve sorumluluk gerektirdiğini vurgulayan ifade doğrudur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s56-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (PRACTICAL TRAVEL WARNING)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "One of your foreign friends tells you she wants to visit Santorini, and so she will go during the peak summer holiday. Since you know the island gets extremely crowded and expensive at that time, you want to warn her, so you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "You should try to book your accommodation as early as possible, since prices rise quickly."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "It would be a good idea to visit the famous sunset spots early to secure a good viewing place."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "I wish you had told me earlier that you wanted to go; I went in May and could have shared some tips."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "If I were you, I'd also visit the nearby island of Naxos, since it's much quieter."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "If possible, consider going in late spring or early autumn, when the island is less crowded and prices are lower."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Yoğunluk ve yüksek fiyatları göz önünde bulundurarak alternatif ve daha uygun bir seyahat zamanı öneren ifade doğrudur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s57-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (APOLOGY)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "You are visiting a museum with a friend. While leaning in to look closely at an exhibit, you accidentally trigger the alarm by touching the display case. Highly embarrassed, you say: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I'm not sure how that happened, but I think the case was placed a bit too close to visitors."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "These alarms go off for the smallest things anyway; I wouldn't worry about it."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "You should really place a clearer warning sign next to sensitive exhibits."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "I guess if the case had been further from the walkway, this wouldn't have happened."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "I'm so sorry! That was clumsy of me. I didn't mean to get so close to the display."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Kazara oluşan bir kazadan sonra samimi özür dileyen ifade doğrudur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-s58-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "SITUATIONAL RESPONSE (SERIOUS PROFESSIONAL CONCERN)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "You have been avoiding your prescribed blood pressure medication, but you dislike the side effects. At your routine appointment, your doctor checks your readings, and the results show your blood pressure has risen to a dangerous level. He is concerned about your health and says in a serious manner: ----", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "I'm glad you're managing without it, but you might consider taking it eventually."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Maybe we should just forget the medication and try lifestyle changes instead."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "I'm not surprised by these results; this is exactly what happens when patients ignore my advice."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "I understand the side effects are unpleasant, but avoiding the medication is exactly why your readings have risen."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The results are clear. Not taking this medication is putting you at serious risk of a heart attack or stroke."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Sonuçların kesinliğini vurgulayan ve ciddi bir sağlık riskine dikkat çeken uyarı ifade doğrudur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g59-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (PSYCHOLOGY CONCEPT)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The halo effect describes the tendency for a person's overall impression of someone in one area, such as physical appearance, to unconsciously shape their judgement of that same person's unrelated qualities, such as intelligence or kindness. First identified by an American psychologist in the early twentieth century, the effect explains why physically attractive individuals are sometimes assumed, without evidence, to be more competent or trustworthy than others. The effect occurs because the brain tends to seek consistency, assuming that a positive trait in one area likely extends to others. ---- Employers have been shown to unconsciously favour more physically attractive candidates during interviews, even when qualifications are otherwise identical.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "This means that physical appearance is always an accurate indicator of a person's true abilities."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The psychologist who identified the effect published his findings in a well-known academic journal."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "As a result, hiring decisions are now made entirely without any consideration of appearance."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Job interviews typically include several rounds before a final decision is made."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "This mental shortcut allows for faster judgements, but it often leads to inaccurate assumptions about a person's actual abilities."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve bir sonraki cümleye mantıksal olarak bağlanan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g60-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (HISTORICAL ROLE)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Court jesters employed in royal households were not important just for the sake of making rulers and their guests laugh. ---- By using humour and clever wordplay, they were sometimes able to offer honest criticism or difficult truths that no ordinary courtier would dare to voice directly to a ruler. Their close access to powerful figures also made them unusually well-informed about court affairs, making them both entertainers and occasional confidants. Over time, the jesters' role declined as changing court customs and shifting entertainment tastes gradually made the position obsolete.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The primary duty of these performers was to compose new laws intended to please visiting foreign dignitaries."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Their wit was considered a divine gift, often linked to supernatural beings from court legend."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Many of them were also skilled blacksmiths who would repair weapons for the royal guard."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "They therefore held significant military power, often commanding troops during times of conflict."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "These performers played a key role in offering honest, humour-disguised feedback that others in the court feared to give directly."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve mesleğin gerçek işlevini doğru şekilde tanımlayan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg8-g61-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (RESTORATION PROJECT)", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The renovation of a nineteenth-century railway station in 2021 was the most extensive project carried out on the building since its original construction, addressing a deteriorating roof, outdated platforms, and inaccessible entrances. It involved repairing the iconic glass-and-iron roof structure, modernising the platforms, and installing lifts and ramps throughout the station. ---- When completed, the renovation not only preserved the station's distinctive Victorian architecture but also made it fully accessible to all passengers, ensuring that it remains a vital transport hub for future generations.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The project also incorporated digital information displays throughout the station to assist passengers."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The station had suffered gradual decline from decades of heavy use and insufficient maintenance funding."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "The station remains one of the most architecturally significant railway buildings in the entire country."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "There was a chance that repairing the fragile glass-and-iron roof might prove more difficult than initially expected."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Despite its ageing infrastructure and years of disrepair, the station had continued to serve thousands of passengers daily throughout the renovation."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve süreç anlatımıyla sonuç cümlesi arasında doğru köprüyü kuran tek seçenek budur. Cevap: E."}]};
Object.keys(DENEME_YDT_INGILIZCE_OZEL_8).forEach(function(no) {
  if (!DENEME_SORU_BANKASI.YDT[no]) DENEME_SORU_BANKASI.YDT[no] = {};
  DENEME_SORU_BANKASI.YDT[no].ydtIngilizce = (DENEME_SORU_BANKASI.YDT[no].ydtIngilizce || []).concat(DENEME_YDT_INGILIZCE_OZEL_8[no]);
});
const DENEME_YDT_INGILIZCE_OZEL_9 = {"1": [{"id": "ydtozg9-g62-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (LANGUAGE FEATURES)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Icelandic is one of the most conservative languages in the world, having changed so little over the centuries that modern speakers can still read thousand-year-old sagas with relative ease. This stability is partly deliberate: rather than simply borrowing foreign words for new inventions, Icelandic committees coin new terms from native root words. For example, the word for 'computer', tölva, combines 'number' and 'prophetess'. ---- The word for 'telephone', sími, was originally an old word for 'thread' or 'wire', repurposed for the modern device. This careful linguistic engineering makes Icelandic both remarkably pure and a fascinating case study for language planners.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "This practice of repurposing old words for modern concepts extends across many areas of technology and science."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Icelandic grammar relies on a complex system of four noun cases that change word endings dramatically."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Icelandic is spoken by fewer than 400,000 people, nearly all of whom live on the island itself."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Many linguists consider Icelandic pronunciation to be among the most difficult in the Nordic language family."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The Icelandic alphabet includes several letters not found in the standard Latin alphabet, such as þ and ð."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve sonraki cümledeki örneği doğru şekilde hazırlayan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-g63-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (BIOLOGICAL ADAPTATION)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Anglerfish display one of the most unusual hunting strategies in the deep sea. Living in near-total darkness at extreme depths, they rely on a modified fin spine that dangles above their mouth, tipped with a glowing lure produced by bioluminescent bacteria. ---- Smaller fish, attracted to this glowing light, swim close enough for the anglerfish to strike with its wide, sharp-toothed jaws. Because prey is scarce at such depths, this passive hunting method allows the anglerfish to conserve significant amounts of energy compared to actively chasing food.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "This lure acts as bait, mimicking the movement of small prey to draw curious fish within striking distance."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Unlike most deep-sea fish, anglerfish are unable to survive without regular access to sunlight."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "The bioluminescent bacteria living in the lure are ultimately harmful to the anglerfish itself over time."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Anglerfish primarily feed on plant matter that drifts down from the ocean's surface."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Female anglerfish are considerably smaller than males, unlike in most other fish species."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve sonraki cümleyle mantıksal olarak örtüşen tek seçenek budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t64-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - RELATIVE CLAUSE + DOUBLE RESULT", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Unlike most planets, Venus rotates in the opposite direction to its orbit, which makes its day longer than its year and causes the sun to rise in the west.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Çoğu gezegenden farklı olarak, Venüs yörüngesine ters yönde döner; bu da gününü yılından daha uzun kılar ve güneşin batıdan doğmasına neden olur."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Venüs, pek çok gezegenin aksine, yörüngesine ters yönde döner ve bu, güneşin batıdan doğmasına neden olurken gününü yılından daha kısa kılar."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Pek çok gezegenin aksine, Venüs'ün yörüngesine ters yönde dönüşü, güneşin doğudan doğmasına neden olur ve gününü yılından daha uzun kılar."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Çoğu gezegenden farklı olarak, yörüngesine ters yönde döndüğü için Venüs'ün günü yılından daha uzundur ve ayrıca güneşin batıdan doğmasına neden olur; bu durum onu güneş sistemindeki en sıcak gezegen yapar."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Diğer çoğu gezegenin aksine, Venüs'ün yörüngesine ters yönde dönmesi, güneşin batıdan doğmasına neden olur."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki tüm bilgileri (karşılaştırma, sonuç ve ek detay) hiçbir ekleme ya da çıkarma yapmadan doğru şekilde aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t65-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - HISTORICAL ORIGIN + EPONYM", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The cardigan sweater became fashionable in Britain after James Brudenell, the seventh Earl of Cardigan, was seen wearing a knitted wool jacket during the Crimean War.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Kazak tipi hırka, Kırım Savaşı sırasında yedinci Cardigan Kontu James Brudenell'in örgü bir yün ceket giyerken görülmesinin ardından Britanya'da moda hâline geldi."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "James Brudenell, Kırım Savaşı sırasında örgü bir yün ceket giydiği için yedinci Cardigan Kontu unvanını almıştır."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Kazak tipi hırka, yedinci Cardigan Kontu James Brudenell tarafından Kırım Savaşı'ndan önce icat edilerek Britanya'da moda hâline geldi."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Kazak tipi hırka, Kırım Savaşı sırasında yedinci Cardigan Kontu James Brudenell'in örgü bir yün ceket giyerken görülmesinin ardından Britanya'da moda hâline geldi ve savaşın kazanılmasında önemli rol oynadı."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Kazak tipi hırka, Kırım Savaşı sırasında birçok İngiliz askerinin örgü yün ceketler giymesinin ardından Britanya'da moda hâline geldi."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki kişi, olay ve sonucu hiçbir ekleme, çıkarma ya da yer/tarih değişikliği yapmadan doğru şekilde aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t66-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - CHAIN OF CAUSATION", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Chronic sleep deprivation raises levels of the stress hormone cortisol, which in turn increases appetite and triggers unhealthy weight gain over time.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Kronik uyku yoksunluğu, stres hormonu kortizolün seviyesini yükseltir; bu da iştahı artırır ve zamanla sağlıksız kilo alımını tetikler."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Kronik uyku yoksunluğu, stres hormonu kortizolün seviyesini düşürür ve bu da iştahı azaltarak zamanla sağlıklı kilo kaybını tetikler."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Stres hormonu kortizol, kronik uyku yoksunluğunun seviyesini yükseltir; bu da iştahı artırır ve zamanla sağlıksız kilo alımını tetikler."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Kronik uyku yoksunluğu, stres hormonu kortizolün seviyesini yükseltir; bu da iştahı artırır, zamanla sağlıksız kilo alımını tetikler ve kalp hastalığı riskini tamamen ortadan kaldırır."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Kronik uyku yoksunluğu, iştahı doğrudan artırarak zamanla sağlıksız kilo alımını tetikler."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki nedensellik zincirini (X, Y'ye yol açar; bu da Z'yi tetikler) hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya bilgi eklemeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t67-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - EMBEDDED CLAUSE + STATISTICS + PURPOSE", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "In Finland, where research shows that excessive screen time is affecting children's concentration, schools are limiting phone use in classrooms in an effort to improve academic focus.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Araştırmaların, aşırı ekran süresinin çocukların konsantrasyonunu etkilediğini gösterdiği Finlandiya'da, okullar akademik odaklanmayı artırmak amacıyla sınıflarda telefon kullanımını sınırlandırıyor."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Finlandiya'da, okulların sınıflarda telefon kullanımını sınırlandırdığı araştırmalar sonucunda, çocukların ekran süresinin akademik odaklanmayı artırdığı ortaya çıkmıştır."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Araştırmaların, aşırı ekran süresinin çocukların konsantrasyonunu güçlendirdiğini gösterdiği Finlandiya'da, okullar sınıflarda telefon kullanımını teşvik ediyor."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Araştırmaların, aşırı ekran süresinin çocukların konsantrasyonunu etkilediğini gösterdiği Finlandiya'da, okullar akademik odaklanmayı artırmak amacıyla sınıflarda telefon kullanımını tamamen yasakladı ve bu karar tüm veliler tarafından desteklendi."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Finlandiya'da okullar, akademik odaklanmayı artırmak amacıyla sınıflarda telefon kullanımını sınırlandırıyor."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki istatistiksel veriyi, amaç ifadesini ve yapılan eylemi hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya değiştirmeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t68-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - PARTICIPLE CLAUSE + DEFINITION", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Held every two years, the Venice Biennale brings together artists from around the world to showcase contemporary works across a wide range of media.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "İki yılda bir düzenlenen Venedik Bienali, dünyanın dört bir yanından sanatçıları çağdaş eserlerini geniş bir medya yelpazesinde sergilemek üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Her yıl düzenlenen Venedik Bienali, dünyanın dört bir yanından sanatçıları çağdaş eserlerini geniş bir medya yelpazesinde sergilemek üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "İki yılda bir düzenlenen Venedik Bienali, yalnızca İtalyan sanatçıları çağdaş eserlerini geniş bir medya yelpazesinde sergilemek üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "İki yılda bir düzenlenen Venedik Bienali, dünyanın dört bir yanından sanatçıları çağdaş eserlerini geniş bir medya yelpazesinde sergilemek üzere bir araya getirir ve bu etkinlik dünyanın en çok ziyaret edilen turistik yeridir."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Dünyanın dört bir yanından sanatçılar, çağdaş eserlerini sergilemek amacıyla iki yılda bir düzenlenen Venedik Bienali'ni organize eder."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki sıklık, yer ve amaç bilgilerini hiçbir yönünü değiştirmeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t69-1", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - APPOSITIVE + REPORTED FINDING", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A new study examining the reasons for the collapse of the Maya civilization, one of the most advanced societies in Mesoamerica, has revealed that a prolonged drought contributed to the abandonment of their major cities.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Mezoamerika'nın en gelişmiş toplumlarından biri olan Maya uygarlığının çöküş nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, uzun süreli bir kuraklık büyük şehirlerinin terk edilmesinde etkili oldu."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Maya uygarlığının, büyük şehirlerini terk etmesinin ardından, Mezoamerika'nın en gelişmiş toplumlarından biri olan bu uygarlığın uzun süreli bir kuraklığa neden olduğu ortaya çıkmıştır."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Mezoamerika'nın en gelişmiş toplumlarından biri olan Maya uygarlığının çöküş nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, ani bir sel büyük şehirlerinin terk edilmesinde etkili oldu."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Mezoamerika'nın en gelişmiş toplumlarından biri olan Maya uygarlığının çöküş nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, uzun süreli bir kuraklık büyük şehirlerinin genişlemesinde etkili oldu."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Mezoamerika'nın en gelişmiş toplumlarından biri olan Maya uygarlığının çöküş nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, uzun süreli bir kuraklık büyük şehirlerinin terk edilmesinde etkili oldu ve bu uygarlığın izleri günümüzde tamamen kaybolmuştur."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki uygarlık, konum ve çöküş nedenini hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya bilgi eklemeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: A."}], "2": [{"id": "ydtozg9-g62-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (LANGUAGE FEATURES)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Welsh is known for its distinctive sound system and its long history as one of the oldest living languages in Europe. One of its most striking features is a phenomenon called consonant mutation, in which the first sound of a word changes depending on grammatical context. ---- For instance, the word for 'cat', cath, becomes gath after certain words, with the initial 'c' softening to a 'g' sound. This system, while logical to native speakers, often confuses learners accustomed to fixed word forms.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Welsh place names are often extremely long, sometimes combining several descriptive words into a single name."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "This means the beginning of a familiar word can shift entirely, even though its core meaning stays the same."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Welsh has been an official language in Wales alongside English since the early twenty-first century."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Many Welsh speakers today live in bilingual households, using both Welsh and English daily."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The Welsh alphabet does not include the letters j, k, q, v, x, or z in native vocabulary."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve sonraki cümledeki örneği doğru şekilde hazırlayan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-g63-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (BIOLOGICAL ADAPTATION)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Electric eels possess a remarkable biological adaptation that sets them apart from nearly all other freshwater fish. Along most of their body, specialised cells called electrocytes are stacked in series, functioning much like a biological battery. ---- When threatened or hunting prey, the eel can discharge these cells simultaneously, producing a shock strong enough to stun small fish or deter predators. This ability allows the eel to hunt effectively even in murky water where vision is of little use.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "These electrocytes are found exclusively in the eel's head, rather than distributed along its body."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Individually, each electrocyte produces only a tiny voltage, but together they can generate a powerful combined charge."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Electric eels rely primarily on their eyesight to locate prey in murky river water."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "The electric shock produced by these eels is rarely strong enough to affect any animal larger than an insect."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Electric eels are technically a type of catfish rather than a true eel, despite their name."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve sonraki cümleyle mantıksal olarak örtüşen tek seçenek budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t64-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - RELATIVE CLAUSE + DOUBLE RESULT", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Unlike most mammals, the platypus lays eggs instead of giving birth to live young, which places it among the rarest groups of mammals and puzzled scientists for decades.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Ornitorenk, çoğu memelinin aksine canlı yavru doğurmak yerine yumurtlar ve bu, onu memelilerin en yaygın gruplarından biri hâline getirirken bilim insanlarını onlarca yıl şaşırtmıştır."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Çoğu memeliden farklı olarak, ornitorenk canlı yavru doğurmak yerine yumurtlar; bu da onu memelilerin en nadir gruplarından biri hâline getirir ve bilim insanlarını onlarca yıl şaşırtmıştır."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Ornitorenk, diğer memelilerin aksine yumurtlar; bu onu memelilerin en nadir gruplarından biri yapar ve bilim insanlarını yüzyıllardır şaşırtmaktadır."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Çoğu memeliden farklı olarak, ornitorenk yumurtlar ve canlı yavru da doğurabilir; bu da onu memelilerin en nadir gruplarından biri hâline getirir."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Ornitorenk, memelilerin en nadir gruplarından biri olduğu için çoğu memeliden farklı olarak canlı yavru doğurmak yerine yumurtlar."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki tüm bilgileri (karşılaştırma, sonuç ve ek detay) hiçbir ekleme ya da çıkarma yapmadan doğru şekilde aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t65-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - HISTORICAL ORIGIN + EPONYM", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The sandwich became a common meal in Britain after John Montagu, the fourth Earl of Sandwich, reportedly asked for meat served between two slices of bread so he could keep playing cards.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Sandviç, Sandwich Kontu dördüncü John Montagu'nun kart oyununa devam edebilmek için etin iki dilim ekmek arasında servis edilmesini istediği iddia edildikten sonra Britanya'da yaygın bir yemek hâline geldi ve kısa sürede tüm Avrupa'da yasaklandı."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Sandviç, Sandwich Kontu dördüncü John Montagu'nun kart oyununa devam edebilmek için etin iki dilim ekmek arasında servis edilmesini istediği iddia edildikten sonra Britanya'da yaygın bir yemek hâline geldi."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Dördüncü John Montagu, sandviç adı verilen yemeği icat ettiği için Sandwich Kontu unvanını almıştır."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Sandviç, Sandwich Kontu dördüncü John Montagu'nun kart oyununu bırakmak istemesi üzerine etin tek dilim ekmekle servis edilmesini istediği iddia edildikten sonra Britanya'da yaygın bir yemek hâline geldi."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Sandviç, dördüncü John Montagu'nun kart oyununa devam edebilmesi için hizmetçilerinden birinin etin iki dilim ekmek arasında servis edilmesini önermesinin ardından Britanya'da yaygın bir yemek hâline geldi."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki kişi, olay ve sonucu hiçbir ekleme, çıkarma ya da yer/tarih değişikliği yapmadan doğru şekilde aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t66-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - CHAIN OF CAUSATION", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Prolonged dehydration increases the viscosity of the blood, which in turn forces the heart to work harder and triggers persistent fatigue.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Uzun süreli susuzluk, kanın yoğunluğunu azaltır; bu da kalbin daha az çalışmasına yol açar ve sürekli enerji artışını tetikler."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Uzun süreli susuzluk, kanın yoğunluğunu artırır; bu da kalbin daha zor çalışmasına yol açar ve sürekli yorgunluğu tetikler."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Kalbin daha zor çalışması, uzun süreli susuzluğun kanın yoğunluğunu artırmasına yol açar ve bu da sürekli yorgunluğu tetikler."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Uzun süreli susuzluk, kanın yoğunluğunu artırır; bu da kalbin daha zor çalışmasına yol açar, sürekli yorgunluğu tetikler ve böbrek fonksiyonlarını tamamen iyileştirir."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Uzun süreli susuzluk, kalbin doğrudan daha zor çalışmasına yol açarak sürekli yorgunluğu tetikler."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki nedensellik zincirini (X, Y'ye yol açar; bu da Z'yi tetikler) hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya bilgi eklemeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t67-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - EMBEDDED CLAUSE + STATISTICS + PURPOSE", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "In Japan, where official statistics show that nearly thirty percent of the population is over sixty-five, several nursing homes are adopting robotic assistants in an effort to address the shortage of caregivers.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Resmî istatistiklerin, nüfusun neredeyse yüzde otuzunun altmış beş yaş üstünde olduğunu gösterdiği Japonya'da, birkaç bakımevi bakıcı fazlasını azaltmak amacıyla robotik asistanları kaldırıyor."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Resmî istatistiklerin, nüfusun neredeyse yüzde otuzunun altmış beş yaş üstünde olduğunu gösterdiği Japonya'da, birkaç bakımevi bakıcı sıkıntısını gidermek amacıyla robotik asistanlar kullanmaya başlıyor."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Japonya'da, birkaç bakımevinin robotik asistanlar kullanmaya başlamasının ardından, nüfusun neredeyse yüzde otuzunun altmış beş yaş üstünde olduğu ortaya çıkmıştır."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Resmî istatistiklerin, nüfusun neredeyse yüzde onunun altmış beş yaş üstünde olduğunu gösterdiği Japonya'da, birkaç bakımevi bakıcı sıkıntısını gidermek amacıyla robotik asistanlar kullanmaya başlıyor."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Resmî istatistiklerin, nüfusun neredeyse yüzde otuzunun altmış beş yaş üstünde olduğunu gösterdiği Japonya'da, birkaç bakımevi bakıcı sıkıntısını gidermek amacıyla robotik asistanlar kullanmaya başlıyor ve bu robotlar insan bakıcıların yerini tamamen almıştır."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki istatistiksel veriyi, amaç ifadesini ve yapılan eylemi hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya değiştirmeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t68-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - PARTICIPLE CLAUSE + DEFINITION", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Held every year, the Cannes Film Festival brings together filmmakers from around the world to screen new films and compete for prestigious awards.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Her yıl düzenlenen Cannes Film Festivali, dünyanın dört bir yanından yönetmenleri yalnızca belgesel filmler göstermek üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Her yıl düzenlenen Cannes Film Festivali, dünyanın dört bir yanından yönetmenleri yeni filmlerini göstermek ve prestijli ödüller için yarışmak üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "İki yılda bir düzenlenen Cannes Film Festivali, dünyanın dört bir yanından yönetmenleri yeni filmlerini göstermek ve prestijli ödüller için yarışmak üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Her yıl düzenlenen Cannes Film Festivali, dünyanın dört bir yanından yönetmenleri yeni filmlerini göstermek ve prestijli ödüller için yarışmak üzere bir araya getirir ve yalnızca profesyonel eleştirmenlerin katılımına izin verir."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Dünyanın dört bir yanından yönetmenler, yeni filmlerini göstermek amacıyla her yıl düzenlenen Cannes Film Festivali'ni yönetir."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki sıklık, yer ve amaç bilgilerini hiçbir yönünü değiştirmeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t69-2", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - APPOSITIVE + REPORTED FINDING", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A new study examining the reasons for the decline of the Western Roman Empire, one of the most influential powers in ancient history, has revealed that repeated economic crises weakened its ability to defend its borders.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Antik tarihin en etkili güçlerinden biri olan Batı Roma İmparatorluğu'nun gerilemesinin ardından, tekrarlanan ekonomik krizlerin sınırlarını savunma yeteneğini güçlendirdiği ortaya çıkmıştır."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Antik tarihin en etkili güçlerinden biri olan Batı Roma İmparatorluğu'nun gerileme nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, tekrarlanan ekonomik krizler sınırlarını savunma yeteneğini zayıflattı."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Antik tarihin en etkili güçlerinden biri olan Batı Roma İmparatorluğu'nun gerileme nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, tek bir askerî yenilgi sınırlarını savunma yeteneğini zayıflattı."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Antik tarihin en etkili güçlerinden biri olan Batı Roma İmparatorluğu'nun gerileme nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, tekrarlanan ekonomik krizler sınırlarını genişletme yeteneğini zayıflattı."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Antik tarihin en etkili güçlerinden biri olan Batı Roma İmparatorluğu'nun gerileme nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, tekrarlanan ekonomik krizler sınırlarını savunma yeteneğini zayıflattı ve imparatorluk bir gecede tamamen yıkılmıştır."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki uygarlık, konum ve çöküş nedenini hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya bilgi eklemeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: B."}], "3": [{"id": "ydtozg9-g62-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (LANGUAGE FEATURES)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Georgian, spoken in the Caucasus region, is known for a strikingly complex verb system unlike that of most European languages. A single Georgian verb can encode not only the action itself but also the subject, the object, and even the manner in which the action was carried out. ---- As a result, a single word in Georgian can sometimes convey what would require an entire sentence in English. This density makes Georgian both linguistically efficient and notoriously difficult for outsiders to master.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Georgian uses its own unique alphabet, unrelated to both the Latin and Cyrillic scripts used by its neighbours."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The Georgian language has no grammatical gender, unlike many other languages in the region."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "This means a single verb form can carry information that several separate words would be needed to express elsewhere."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Georgian literature dates back over a thousand years, with some of the earliest surviving texts being religious in nature."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Many linguists classify Georgian as part of a small language family with no confirmed relatives outside the Caucasus."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve sonraki cümledeki örneği doğru şekilde hazırlayan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-g63-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (BIOLOGICAL ADAPTATION)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Chameleons are widely known for their ability to change colour, though the purpose behind this trait is often misunderstood. Rather than primarily serving as camouflage, colour change in chameleons functions mainly as a form of communication with other chameleons. ---- A male displaying bright, contrasting colours may be signalling dominance or readiness to mate, while duller tones often indicate stress or submission. Specialised cells beneath the skin, containing pigments and light-reflecting crystals, allow this rapid colour shift to occur within seconds.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Chameleons change colour exclusively to blend into their immediate surroundings and avoid predators."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Female chameleons are entirely incapable of changing their skin colour, unlike males of the species."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Bright colours often signal aggression or mating readiness, while paler shades can indicate a calmer or submissive state."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "The colour-changing ability of chameleons has no connection to their mood or social interactions."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Chameleons lose their colour-changing ability entirely once they reach full adulthood."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve sonraki cümleyle mantıksal olarak örtüşen tek seçenek budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t64-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - RELATIVE CLAUSE + DOUBLE RESULT", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Unlike most fish, certain shark species give birth to live young without developing a placenta, which allows the embryos to be nourished by unfertilised eggs and increases their chances of survival.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Çoğu balıktan farklı olarak, bazı köpekbalığı türleri plasenta geliştirmeden canlı yavru doğurur; bu da embriyoların döllenmemiş yumurtalarla beslenmesini önler ve hayatta kalma şanslarını azaltır."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Bazı köpekbalığı türleri, çoğu balığın aksine plasenta geliştirmeden canlı yavru doğurur ve bu, embriyoların yumurtalardan değil doğrudan anneden beslenmesini sağlayarak hayatta kalma şanslarını artırır."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Çoğu balıktan farklı olarak, bazı köpekbalığı türleri plasenta geliştirmeden canlı yavru doğurur; bu da embriyoların döllenmemiş yumurtalarla beslenmesini sağlar ve hayatta kalma şanslarını artırır."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Bazı köpekbalığı türleri, plasenta geliştirmeden canlı yavru doğurduğu için çoğu balıktan farklıdır ve bu türler, dünyanın en büyük balıkları arasında yer alır."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Çoğu balıktan farklı olarak, bazı köpekbalığı türleri döllenmemiş yumurtalarla beslenen embriyolar taşır ve plasenta geliştirmeden canlı yavru doğurur."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki tüm bilgileri (karşılaştırma, sonuç ve ek detay) hiçbir ekleme ya da çıkarma yapmadan doğru şekilde aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t65-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - HISTORICAL ORIGIN + EPONYM", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The term silhouette became associated with simple black outlines after Étienne de Silhouette, a French finance minister, became known for his frugal habits and inexpensive paper cutouts.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Silhouette terimi, Fransız maliye bakanı Étienne de Silhouette'in tutumlu alışkanlıkları ve pahalı kâğıt kesimleriyle tanınmasının ardından basit siyah dış hatlarla ilişkilendirilmeye başlandı."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Étienne de Silhouette, basit siyah dış hatlarla resim yapma tekniğini icat ettiği için Fransa'da maliye bakanı olarak atanmıştır."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Silhouette terimi, Fransız maliye bakanı Étienne de Silhouette'in tutumlu alışkanlıkları ve ucuz kâğıt kesimleriyle tanınmasının ardından basit siyah dış hatlarla ilişkilendirilmeye başlandı."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Silhouette terimi, Fransız maliye bakanı Étienne de Silhouette'in tutumlu alışkanlıkları ve ucuz kâğıt kesimleriyle tanınmasının ardından karmaşık ve renkli resimlerle ilişkilendirilmeye başlandı."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Silhouette terimi, Fransız bir ressamın tutumlu alışkanlıkları ve ucuz kâğıt kesimleriyle tanınmasının ardından basit siyah dış hatlarla ilişkilendirilmeye başlandı."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki kişi, olay ve sonucu hiçbir ekleme, çıkarma ya da yer/tarih değişikliği yapmadan doğru şekilde aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t66-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - CHAIN OF CAUSATION", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Exposure to screen light before bedtime suppresses the production of melatonin, which in turn disrupts the body's internal clock and triggers difficulty falling asleep.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Yatmadan önce ekran ışığına maruz kalmak melatonin üretimini artırır; bu da vücudun iç saatini düzenler ve uykuya dalmayı kolaylaştırır."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Vücudun iç saatinin bozulması, yatmadan önce ekran ışığına maruz kalmanın melatonin üretimini baskılamasına neden olur ve bu da uykuya dalmayı zorlaştırır."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Yatmadan önce ekran ışığına maruz kalmak melatonin üretimini baskılar; bu da vücudun iç saatini bozar ve uykuya dalmayı zorlaştırır."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Yatmadan önce ekran ışığına maruz kalmak melatonin üretimini baskılar; bu da vücudun iç saatini bozar, uykuya dalmayı zorlaştırır ve görme keskinliğini tamamen artırır."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Yatmadan önce ekran ışığına maruz kalmak, vücudun iç saatini doğrudan bozarak uykuya dalmayı zorlaştırır."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki nedensellik zincirini (X, Y'ye yol açar; bu da Z'yi tetikler) hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya bilgi eklemeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t67-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - EMBEDDED CLAUSE + STATISTICS + PURPOSE", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "In the Netherlands, where surveys reveal that regular cyclists have notably lower obesity rates than non-cyclists, several cities are expanding cycling infrastructure in an effort to promote public health.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Anketlerin, düzenli bisiklet kullananların bisiklet kullanmayanlara göre belirgin şekilde daha yüksek obezite oranlarına sahip olduğunu ortaya koyduğu Hollanda'da, birkaç şehir bisiklet altyapısını genişletiyor."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Hollanda'da, birkaç şehrin bisiklet altyapısını genişletmesinin ardından, düzenli bisiklet kullananların daha düşük obezite oranlarına sahip olduğu keşfedilmiştir."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Anketlerin, düzenli bisiklet kullananların bisiklet kullanmayanlara göre belirgin şekilde daha düşük obezite oranlarına sahip olduğunu ortaya koyduğu Hollanda'da, birkaç şehir halk sağlığını desteklemek amacıyla bisiklet altyapısını genişletiyor."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Anketlerin, düzenli bisiklet kullananların bisiklet kullanmayanlara göre belirgin şekilde daha düşük obezite oranlarına sahip olduğunu ortaya koyduğu Hollanda'da, birkaç şehir halk sağlığını desteklemek amacıyla bisiklet altyapısını genişletiyor ve otomobil kullanımını tamamen yasaklamıştır."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Hollanda'da birkaç şehir, halk sağlığını desteklemek amacıyla bisiklet altyapısını genişletiyor."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki istatistiksel veriyi, amaç ifadesini ve yapılan eylemi hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya değiştirmeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t68-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - PARTICIPLE CLAUSE + DEFINITION", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Held every year, the Eurovision Song Contest unites performers from dozens of countries to compete for the title of best original song.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Her yıl düzenlenen Eurovision Şarkı Yarışması, yalnızca birkaç ülkeden sanatçıları en iyi orijinal şarkı unvanı için yarışmak üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "İki yılda bir düzenlenen Eurovision Şarkı Yarışması, onlarca ülkeden sanatçıları en iyi orijinal şarkı unvanı için yarışmak üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Her yıl düzenlenen Eurovision Şarkı Yarışması, onlarca ülkeden sanatçıları en iyi orijinal şarkı unvanı için yarışmak üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Her yıl düzenlenen Eurovision Şarkı Yarışması, onlarca ülkeden sanatçıları en iyi orijinal şarkı unvanı için yarışmak üzere bir araya getirir ve kazananın büyük bir nakit ödül aldığı bilinmektedir."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Onlarca ülkeden sanatçılar, en iyi orijinal şarkı unvanı için yarışmak amacıyla her yıl düzenlenen Eurovision Şarkı Yarışması'nı düzenler."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki sıklık, yer ve amaç bilgilerini hiçbir yönünü değiştirmeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t69-3", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - APPOSITIVE + REPORTED FINDING", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A new study examining the reasons for the decline of the Indus Valley Civilization, one of the earliest urban societies in the world, has revealed that a shift in river courses disrupted agriculture across the region.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Dünyanın en eski kentsel toplumlarından biri olan İndus Vadisi Uygarlığı'nın gerilemesinin ardından, nehir yataklarındaki değişimin tarımı bozduğu keşfedilmiştir."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Dünyanın en eski kentsel toplumlarından biri olan İndus Vadisi Uygarlığı'nın gerileme nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, şiddetli bir deprem tarımı bozdu."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Dünyanın en eski kentsel toplumlarından biri olan İndus Vadisi Uygarlığı'nın gerileme nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, nehir yataklarındaki bir değişim bölgedeki tarımı bozdu."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Dünyanın en eski kentsel toplumlarından biri olan İndus Vadisi Uygarlığı'nın gerileme nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, nehir yataklarındaki bir değişim bölgedeki ticareti geliştirdi."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Dünyanın en eski kentsel toplumlarından biri olan İndus Vadisi Uygarlığı'nın gerileme nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, nehir yataklarındaki bir değişim bölgedeki tarımı bozdu ve bu uygarlığın tüm yazılı kayıtları günümüze ulaşmıştır."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki uygarlık, konum ve çöküş nedenini hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya bilgi eklemeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: C."}], "4": [{"id": "ydtozg9-g62-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (LANGUAGE FEATURES)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Korean is well known for its elaborate system of speech levels, which require speakers to adjust their grammar depending on the social status of the person they are addressing. A single verb can take several different forms depending on whether the listener is a close friend, a stranger, or an elder. ---- Choosing the wrong level can unintentionally signal rudeness or excessive formality, even if the underlying message is identical. Mastering this system remains one of the greatest challenges for learners of Korean as a second language.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Korean uses a unique alphabet called Hangul, which was deliberately designed to be easy to learn."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Korean sentence structure typically places the verb at the very end of the sentence."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Many Korean words have been borrowed from Chinese over the course of many centuries."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "This means the exact same sentence can sound polite, neutral, or overly casual depending on the verb ending chosen."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "South Korea has one of the highest literacy rates in the world, partly due to the simplicity of its writing system."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve sonraki cümledeki örneği doğru şekilde hazırlayan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-g63-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (BIOLOGICAL ADAPTATION)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Arctic ground squirrels undergo one of the most extreme forms of hibernation known among mammals. During the long winter months, their body temperature can drop below freezing, a state that would be lethal for most other warm-blooded animals. ---- Their blood continues to flow, though at a dramatically reduced rate, preventing the formation of damaging ice crystals within their cells. This remarkable physiological adaptation allows the squirrels to survive months of extreme cold with minimal energy expenditure.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Despite this extreme cold, the squirrels remain fully active throughout the winter, foraging as usual."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Arctic ground squirrels are unable to survive temperatures below freezing under any circumstances."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "This hibernation strategy is unique to Arctic ground squirrels and has not been observed in any other species."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Remarkably, their bodily fluids avoid freezing solid, allowing vital organs to continue functioning at a minimal level."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Arctic ground squirrels wake up every few hours throughout the winter to search for stored food."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve sonraki cümleyle mantıksal olarak örtüşen tek seçenek budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t64-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - RELATIVE CLAUSE + DOUBLE RESULT", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Unlike most plants, certain bamboo species flower only once every several decades, which causes entire forests to bloom simultaneously and then die shortly afterward.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Çoğu bitkiden farklı olarak, bazı bambu türleri her birkaç on yılda yalnızca bir kez çiçek açar; ancak bu, ormanların yalnızca kısmen çiçeklenmesine neden olur."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Bazı bambu türleri, çoğu bitkinin aksine her birkaç on yılda bir kez çiçek açar ve bu durum, çiçeklenmeden hemen önce tüm ormanların kurumasına neden olur."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Çoğu bitkiden farklı olarak, bazı bambu türlerinin her yıl düzenli olarak çiçek açması, tüm ormanların aynı anda çiçeklenip kısa süre sonra ölmesine neden olur."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Çoğu bitkiden farklı olarak, bazı bambu türleri yalnızca her birkaç on yılda bir çiçek açar; bu da tüm ormanların aynı anda çiçeklenmesine ve kısa süre sonra ölmesine neden olur."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Bazı bambu türleri her birkaç on yılda bir çiçek açar ve bu, çoğu bitkiden farklı olarak ormanların büyümesini hızlandırır."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki tüm bilgileri (karşılaştırma, sonuç ve ek detay) hiçbir ekleme ya da çıkarma yapmadan doğru şekilde aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t65-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - HISTORICAL ORIGIN + EPONYM", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The guillotine became closely associated with the French Revolution after Joseph-Ignace Guillotin, a physician, proposed it as a more humane method of execution.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Giyotin, hekim Joseph-Ignace Guillotin'in bunu daha insancıl bir idam yöntemi olarak önermesinin ardından Fransız Devrimi'yle yakından ilişkilendirildi ve kısa sürede tüm dünyada yasaklandı."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Joseph-Ignace Guillotin, giyotini icat ettiği için Fransız Devrimi'nin liderlerinden biri olmuştur."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Giyotin, hekim Joseph-Ignace Guillotin'in bunu daha acımasız bir idam yöntemi olarak önermesinin ardından Fransız Devrimi'yle yakından ilişkilendirildi."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Giyotin, hekim Joseph-Ignace Guillotin'in bunu daha insancıl bir idam yöntemi olarak önermesinin ardından Fransız Devrimi'yle yakından ilişkilendirildi."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Giyotin, Fransız Devrimi sırasında bir grup mühendisin daha insancıl bir idam yöntemi geliştirmesinin ardından hekim Joseph-Ignace Guillotin'in adıyla anılmaya başlandı."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki kişi, olay ve sonucu hiçbir ekleme, çıkarma ya da yer/tarih değişikliği yapmadan doğru şekilde aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t66-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - CHAIN OF CAUSATION", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Excessive sodium intake causes the body to retain water, which in turn raises blood pressure and places additional strain on the kidneys.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Aşırı sodyum alımı, vücudun su tutmasına neden olur; bu da kan basıncını yükseltir ve böbrekler üzerinde ek yük oluşturur, ancak bu durum tamamen zararsızdır."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Böbrekler üzerindeki ek yük, aşırı sodyum alımının vücudun su tutmasına neden olmasına yol açar ve bu da kan basıncını yükseltir."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Aşırı sodyum alımı, vücudun su kaybetmesine neden olur; bu da kan basıncını düşürür ve böbrekler üzerindeki yükü azaltır."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Aşırı sodyum alımı, vücudun su tutmasına neden olur; bu da kan basıncını yükseltir ve böbrekler üzerinde ek yük oluşturur."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Aşırı sodyum alımı, kan basıncını doğrudan yükselterek böbrekler üzerinde ek yük oluşturur."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki nedensellik zincirini (X, Y'ye yol açar; bu da Z'yi tetikler) hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya bilgi eklemeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t67-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - EMBEDDED CLAUSE + STATISTICS + PURPOSE", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "In Norway, where government data shows that more than half of new car sales are now electric, authorities continue to offer generous tax incentives in an effort to reduce carbon emissions.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Hükûmet verilerinin, yeni araba satışlarının yarısından azının artık elektrikli olduğunu gösterdiği Norveç'te, yetkililer karbon emisyonlarını azaltmak amacıyla cömert vergi teşvikleri sunmaya devam ediyor."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Norveç'te, yetkililerin cömert vergi teşvikleri sunmasının ardından, yeni araba satışlarının yarısından fazlasının elektrikli olduğu keşfedilmiştir."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Hükûmet verilerinin, yeni araba satışlarının yarısından fazlasının artık elektrikli olduğunu gösterdiği Norveç'te, yetkililer karbon emisyonlarını artırmak amacıyla cömert vergi teşvikleri sunmaya devam ediyor."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Hükûmet verilerinin, yeni araba satışlarının yarısından fazlasının artık elektrikli olduğunu gösterdiği Norveç'te, yetkililer karbon emisyonlarını azaltmak amacıyla cömert vergi teşvikleri sunmaya devam ediyor."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Norveç'te yetkililer, karbon emisyonlarını azaltmak amacıyla cömert vergi teşvikleri sunmaya devam ediyor."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki istatistiksel veriyi, amaç ifadesini ve yapılan eylemi hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya değiştirmeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t68-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - PARTICIPLE CLAUSE + DEFINITION", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Held every year before Lent, the Rio Carnival brings together performers and spectators from around the world to celebrate through music, dance, and elaborate costumes.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Paskalya'dan önce her yıl düzenlenen Rio Karnavalı, dünyanın dört bir yanından sanatçıları ve seyircileri müzik, dans ve ayrıntılı kostümlerle kutlama yapmak üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Büyük Perhiz'den sonra her yıl düzenlenen Rio Karnavalı, dünyanın dört bir yanından sanatçıları ve seyircileri müzik, dans ve ayrıntılı kostümlerle kutlama yapmak üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Büyük Perhiz'den önce her yıl düzenlenen Rio Karnavalı, yalnızca Brezilyalı sanatçıları müzik, dans ve ayrıntılı kostümlerle kutlama yapmak üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Büyük Perhiz'den önce her yıl düzenlenen Rio Karnavalı, dünyanın dört bir yanından sanatçıları ve seyircileri müzik, dans ve ayrıntılı kostümlerle kutlama yapmak üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Dünyanın dört bir yanından sanatçılar ve seyirciler, müzik ve dansla kutlama yapmak amacıyla Büyük Perhiz'den önce düzenlenen Rio Karnavalı'nı organize eder."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki sıklık, yer ve amaç bilgilerini hiçbir yönünü değiştirmeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t69-4", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - APPOSITIVE + REPORTED FINDING", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A new study examining the reasons for the collapse of the society on Easter Island, one of the most isolated inhabited places on Earth, has revealed that extensive deforestation severely damaged the island's ecosystem.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Dünyadaki en izole yerleşim yerlerinden biri olan Paskalya Adası'ndaki toplumun çöküşünün ardından, yoğun ormansızlaşmanın adanın ekosistemine hiçbir zarar vermediği ortaya çıkmıştır."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Dünyadaki en izole yerleşim yerlerinden biri olan Paskalya Adası'ndaki toplumun çöküş nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, ani bir volkanik patlama adanın ekosistemine ciddi zarar verdi."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Dünyadaki en izole yerleşim yerlerinden biri olan Paskalya Adası'ndaki toplumun çöküş nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, yoğun ormansızlaşma adanın nüfusunu artırdı."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Dünyadaki en izole yerleşim yerlerinden biri olan Paskalya Adası'ndaki toplumun çöküş nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, yoğun ormansızlaşma adanın ekosistemine ciddi zarar verdi."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Dünyadaki en izole yerleşim yerlerinden biri olan Paskalya Adası'ndaki toplumun çöküş nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, yoğun ormansızlaşma adanın ekosistemine ciddi zarar verdi ve ada günümüzde tamamen ıssızdır."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki uygarlık, konum ve çöküş nedenini hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya bilgi eklemeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: D."}], "5": [{"id": "ydtozg9-g62-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (LANGUAGE FEATURES)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Xhosa, spoken primarily in South Africa, is famous for incorporating click consonants into its everyday vocabulary, a feature shared by only a small number of the world's languages. These clicks are produced by drawing air inward rather than pushing it outward, as with ordinary consonants. ---- The word for 'Xhosa' itself begins with one such click, represented in writing by the letter x. Producing these sounds accurately typically requires years of practice for non-native speakers.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Xhosa belongs to the Bantu language family, which includes hundreds of related languages across the continent."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Many Xhosa speakers are also fluent in English or Afrikaans due to South Africa's colonial history."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Xhosa grammar relies heavily on a system of noun classes that affect verb agreement throughout a sentence."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "The Xhosa people have a rich oral tradition of storytelling passed down through many generations."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "There are several distinct types of clicks in Xhosa, each represented by a different letter or letter combination."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve sonraki cümledeki örneği doğru şekilde hazırlayan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-g63-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (BIOLOGICAL ADAPTATION)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Camels are often mistakenly believed to store water directly within their humps. In reality, the humps are composed almost entirely of fatty tissue, which the camel can metabolise for energy during long periods without food. ---- When this fat is broken down, it produces water as a byproduct, which helps explain the misconception. Camels conserve actual water through other adaptations, such as producing highly concentrated urine and minimising sweat loss.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "The camel's hump grows progressively larger with age, regardless of the animal's diet or activity level."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Camels are entirely unable to survive more than a few days without direct access to food or water."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "A camel's hump can shrink and lean to one side when its fat reserves become significantly depleted."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Scientists have found no biological connection between a camel's fat reserves and its ability to survive drought."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Although this fat is not water itself, breaking it down chemically does release a small amount of water."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve sonraki cümleyle mantıksal olarak örtüşen tek seçenek budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t64-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - RELATIVE CLAUSE + DOUBLE RESULT", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Unlike most amphibians, the axolotl retains its larval features throughout its life, which allows it to remain permanently aquatic and gives it a remarkable capacity to regenerate lost limbs.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Çoğu amfibiden farklı olarak, aksolot larva özelliklerini yaşamı boyunca kaybeder; bu da onu kalıcı olarak karasal hâle getirir ve kayıp uzuvlarını yenileme yeteneğini azaltır."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Aksolot, çoğu amfibinin aksine larva özelliklerini erişkinlikte de korur, ancak bu özellik onu sudan tamamen bağımsız hâle getirir."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Çoğu amfibiden farklı olarak, aksolotun larva özelliklerini koruması, onu kısa ömürlü kılar ve uzuvlarını yenileme kapasitesini ortadan kaldırır."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Aksolot, çoğu amfibinin aksine larva özelliklerini yaşamı boyunca korur ve bu da yalnızca kalıcı olarak sucul kalmasını sağlar."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Çoğu amfibiden farklı olarak, aksolot larva özelliklerini yaşamı boyunca korur; bu da onu kalıcı olarak sucul hâle getirir ve kayıp uzuvlarını yenileme konusunda dikkat çekici bir yetenek kazandırır."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki tüm bilgileri (karşılaştırma, sonuç ve ek detay) hiçbir ekleme ya da çıkarma yapmadan doğru şekilde aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t65-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - HISTORICAL ORIGIN + EPONYM", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The word boycott entered everyday English after Charles Boycott, a land agent in Ireland, was shunned by his local community following a dispute over rent.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Boycott kelimesi, İrlanda'da bir toprak yöneticisi olan Charles Boycott'un kira anlaşmazlığının ardından yerel halk tarafından dışlanmasının ardından günlük İngilizceye girmiş ve kısa sürede unutulmuştur."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Charles Boycott, İrlanda'da yerel halkı bir kira anlaşmazlığı nedeniyle dışladığı için 'boycott' kelimesiyle anılmaya başlanmıştır."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Boycott kelimesi, İrlanda'da bir toprak yöneticisi olan Charles Boycott'un bir kira anlaşmazlığının ardından yerel halk tarafından desteklenmesinin ardından günlük İngilizceye girmiştir."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Boycott kelimesi, İngiltere'de bir toprak yöneticisi olan Charles Boycott'un bir kira anlaşmazlığının ardından yerel halk tarafından dışlanmasının ardından günlük İngilizceye girmiştir."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Boycott kelimesi, İrlanda'da bir toprak yöneticisi olan Charles Boycott'un bir kira anlaşmazlığının ardından yerel halk tarafından dışlanmasının ardından günlük İngilizceye girmiştir."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki kişi, olay ve sonucu hiçbir ekleme, çıkarma ya da yer/tarih değişikliği yapmadan doğru şekilde aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t66-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - CHAIN OF CAUSATION", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Chronic stress elevates cortisol levels over time, which in turn weakens the immune system and increases susceptibility to infections.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Kronik stres, zamanla kortizol seviyesini düşürür; bu da bağışıklık sistemini güçlendirir ve enfeksiyonlara karşı direnci artırır."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Bağışıklık sisteminin zayıflaması, kronik stresin zamanla kortizol seviyesini yükseltmesine neden olur ve bu da enfeksiyon riskini artırır."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Kronik stres, zamanla kortizol seviyesini yükseltir; bu da bağışıklık sistemini güçlendirir ve enfeksiyonlara karşı direnci artırır."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Kronik stres, zamanla kortizol seviyesini yükseltir; bu da bağışıklık sistemini zayıflatır, enfeksiyon riskini artırır ve kalp sağlığını tamamen iyileştirir."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Kronik stres, zamanla kortizol seviyesini yükseltir; bu da bağışıklık sistemini zayıflatır ve enfeksiyonlara karşı duyarlılığı artırır."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki nedensellik zincirini (X, Y'ye yol açar; bu da Z'yi tetikler) hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya bilgi eklemeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t67-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - EMBEDDED CLAUSE + STATISTICS + PURPOSE", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "In South Korea, where demographic data shows that the birth rate has fallen to one of the lowest levels in the world, the government is expanding childcare subsidies in an effort to encourage larger families.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Demografik verilerin, doğum oranının dünyadaki en yüksek seviyelerden birine yükseldiğini gösterdiği Güney Kore'de, hükûmet daha büyük aileleri teşvik etmek amacıyla çocuk bakım sübvansiyonlarını genişletiyor."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Güney Kore'de, hükûmetin çocuk bakım sübvansiyonlarını genişletmesinin ardından, doğum oranının dünyadaki en düşük seviyelerden birine düştüğü ortaya çıkmıştır."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Demografik verilerin, doğum oranının dünyadaki en düşük seviyelerden birine düştüğünü gösterdiği Güney Kore'de, hükûmet daha küçük aileleri teşvik etmek amacıyla çocuk bakım sübvansiyonlarını azaltıyor."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Demografik verilerin, doğum oranının dünyadaki en düşük seviyelerden birine düştüğünü gösterdiği Güney Kore'de, hükûmet daha büyük aileleri teşvik etmek amacıyla çocuk bakım sübvansiyonlarını genişletiyor ve bu politika doğum oranını tamamen ikiye katlamıştır."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Demografik verilerin, doğum oranının dünyadaki en düşük seviyelerden birine düştüğünü gösterdiği Güney Kore'de, hükûmet daha büyük aileleri teşvik etmek amacıyla çocuk bakım sübvansiyonlarını genişletiyor."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki istatistiksel veriyi, amaç ifadesini ve yapılan eylemi hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya değiştirmeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t68-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - PARTICIPLE CLAUSE + DEFINITION", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Held every year in London, the Chelsea Flower Show brings together horticulturalists and garden designers to showcase innovative garden displays.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Her yıl Paris'te düzenlenen Chelsea Çiçek Gösterisi, bahçıvanları ve bahçe tasarımcılarını yenilikçi bahçe sergileri sunmak üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "İki yılda bir Londra'da düzenlenen Chelsea Çiçek Gösterisi, bahçıvanları ve bahçe tasarımcılarını yenilikçi bahçe sergileri sunmak üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Her yıl Londra'da düzenlenen Chelsea Çiçek Gösterisi, yalnızca profesyonel bahçıvanları yenilikçi bahçe sergileri sunmak üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Her yıl Londra'da düzenlenen Chelsea Çiçek Gösterisi, bahçıvanları ve bahçe tasarımcılarını yenilikçi bahçe sergileri sunmak üzere bir araya getirir ve etkinliğin geliri tamamen hayır kurumlarına bağışlanır."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Her yıl Londra'da düzenlenen Chelsea Çiçek Gösterisi, bahçıvanları ve bahçe tasarımcılarını yenilikçi bahçe sergileri sunmak üzere bir araya getirir."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki sıklık, yer ve amaç bilgilerini hiçbir yönünü değiştirmeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t69-5", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - APPOSITIVE + REPORTED FINDING", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A new study examining the reasons for the decline of the Khmer Empire, one of the most powerful civilizations in Southeast Asia, has revealed that alternating periods of severe drought and flooding damaged its vital water infrastructure.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Güneydoğu Asya'nın en güçlü uygarlıklarından biri olan Kmer İmparatorluğu'nun gerilemesinin ardından, şiddetli kuraklık ve sel dönemlerinin dönüşümlü olarak yaşanmasına neden olan su altyapısı hasarı ortaya çıkmıştır."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Güneydoğu Asya'nın en güçlü uygarlıklarından biri olan Kmer İmparatorluğu'nun gerileme nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, sürekli barış dönemleri hayati su altyapısına zarar verdi."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Güneydoğu Asya'nın en güçlü uygarlıklarından biri olan Kmer İmparatorluğu'nun gerileme nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, şiddetli kuraklık ve sel dönemlerinin dönüşümlü olarak yaşanması hayati su altyapısını güçlendirdi."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Güneydoğu Asya'nın en güçlü uygarlıklarından biri olan Kmer İmparatorluğu'nun gerileme nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, şiddetli kuraklık ve sel dönemlerinin dönüşümlü olarak yaşanması hayati su altyapısına zarar verdi ve bu altyapı hiçbir zaman yeniden inşa edilmedi."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Güneydoğu Asya'nın en güçlü uygarlıklarından biri olan Kmer İmparatorluğu'nun gerileme nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, şiddetli kuraklık ve sel dönemlerinin dönüşümlü olarak yaşanması hayati su altyapısına zarar verdi."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki uygarlık, konum ve çöküş nedenini hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya bilgi eklemeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: E."}], "6": [{"id": "ydtozg9-g62-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (LANGUAGE FEATURES)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Navajo, spoken by the Navajo Nation in the southwestern United States, organises meaning primarily around verbs rather than nouns, unlike English, which relies heavily on nouns to convey information. A single Navajo verb can incorporate details about who is acting, what is being acted upon, and even the shape or texture of an object involved. ---- This verb-centred structure was famously exploited during the Second World War, when Navajo speakers developed an unbreakable military code based on their language. Its complexity, so difficult for outsiders to grasp, ultimately proved to be a strategic advantage.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "This means a single verb can express nuances that would require several separate words or sentences in English."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The Navajo Nation is the largest federally recognised Native American tribe in the United States."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Navajo has no native written form and was historically transmitted entirely through oral tradition."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Many Navajo words have been adapted into English, particularly place names found in the southwestern states."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Navajo distinguishes between several different types of past tense, depending on how recently an event occurred."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve sonraki cümledeki örneği doğru şekilde hazırlayan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-g63-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (BIOLOGICAL ADAPTATION)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Arctic terns undertake the longest migration of any known animal, travelling from their breeding grounds in the Arctic to feeding areas near Antarctica each year. ---- By following this route, the birds experience two summers annually, taking advantage of abundant daylight and food availability at both poles. Over the course of its lifetime, a single Arctic tern may fly a distance roughly equivalent to travelling to the moon and partway back.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "This round trip can cover well over seventy thousand kilometres, making it the longest migratory journey recorded in the animal kingdom."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Unlike most migratory birds, Arctic terns remain in a single location year-round rather than travelling long distances."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Arctic terns primarily migrate to escape predators rather than to follow favourable feeding conditions."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "The migration route of the Arctic tern has remained completely unknown to scientists until very recently."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Arctic terns typically travel alone during migration, avoiding contact with other members of their species."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve sonraki cümleyle mantıksal olarak örtüşen tek seçenek budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t64-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - RELATIVE CLAUSE + DOUBLE RESULT", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Unlike most animals, the so-called immortal jellyfish can revert to an earlier stage of its life cycle when threatened, which allows it to avoid death and effectively start its life over again.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Çoğu hayvandan farklı olarak, sözde ölümsüz denizanası tehdit altında kaldığında yaşam döngüsünün daha erken bir evresine dönebilir; bu da ölümden kaçınmasını ve yaşamına yeniden başlamasını etkili biçimde sağlar."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Sözde ölümsüz denizanası, çoğu hayvanın aksine tehdit altında kaldığında yaşam döngüsünün daha ileri bir evresine geçer ve bu, ölümden kaçınmasını engeller."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Çoğu hayvandan farklı olarak, sözde ölümsüz denizanasının yaşam döngüsü tek bir evreden oluşur; bu da onun tehdit altında ölmesini engeller."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Sözde ölümsüz denizanası, tehdit altında kaldığında yaşam döngüsünün daha erken bir evresine dönebilir ve bu yetenek onu okyanuslardaki en büyük denizanası türü yapar."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Çoğu hayvandan farklı olarak, sözde ölümsüz denizanası yalnızca üreme dönemlerinde yaşam döngüsünün erken bir evresine döner; bu da ölümden kaçınmasını sağlar."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki tüm bilgileri (karşılaştırma, sonuç ve ek detay) hiçbir ekleme ya da çıkarma yapmadan doğru şekilde aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t65-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - HISTORICAL ORIGIN + EPONYM", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The word nicotine came into common use after Jean Nicot, a French diplomat, introduced tobacco plants to the French court in the sixteenth century.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Nicotine kelimesi, Fransız diplomat Jean Nicot'un on altıncı yüzyılda tütün bitkilerini Fransız sarayına tanıtmasının ardından yaygın olarak kullanılmaya başlanmıştır."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Jean Nicot, on altıncı yüzyılda tütün bitkilerini Fransız sarayına tanıttığı için Fransa'da diplomat olarak atanmıştır."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Nicotine kelimesi, Fransız diplomat Jean Nicot'un on dokuzuncu yüzyılda tütün bitkilerini Fransız sarayına tanıtmasının ardından yaygın olarak kullanılmaya başlanmıştır."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Nicotine kelimesi, Fransız diplomat Jean Nicot'un on altıncı yüzyılda tütün bitkilerini İngiliz sarayına tanıtmasının ardından yaygın olarak kullanılmaya başlanmıştır."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Nicotine kelimesi, Fransız diplomat Jean Nicot'un on altıncı yüzyılda tütün bitkilerini Fransız sarayına tanıtmasının ardından yaygın olarak kullanılmaya başlanmış ve tütün o dönemde şifalı bir bitki olarak kabul edilmiştir."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki kişi, olay ve sonucu hiçbir ekleme, çıkarma ya da yer/tarih değişikliği yapmadan doğru şekilde aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t66-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - CHAIN OF CAUSATION", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Overuse of antibiotics disrupts the natural balance of gut bacteria, which in turn causes digestive problems and increases the risk of nutrient deficiencies.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Antibiyotiklerin aşırı kullanımı, bağırsak bakterilerinin doğal dengesini bozar; bu da sindirim sorunlarına yol açar ve besin eksikliği riskini artırır."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Antibiyotiklerin aşırı kullanımı, bağırsak bakterilerinin doğal dengesini güçlendirir; bu da sindirimi iyileştirir ve besin eksikliği riskini azaltır."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Sindirim sorunları, antibiyotiklerin aşırı kullanımının bağırsak bakterilerinin dengesini bozmasına neden olur ve bu da besin eksikliği riskini artırır."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Antibiyotiklerin aşırı kullanımı, bağırsak bakterilerinin doğal dengesini bozar; bu da sindirim sorunlarına yol açar, besin eksikliği riskini artırır ve bağışıklık sistemini tamamen güçlendirir."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Antibiyotiklerin aşırı kullanımı, sindirim sorunlarına doğrudan yol açarak besin eksikliği riskini artırır."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki nedensellik zincirini (X, Y'ye yol açar; bu da Z'yi tetikler) hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya bilgi eklemeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t67-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - EMBEDDED CLAUSE + STATISTICS + PURPOSE", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "In Sweden, where workplace studies indicate that long working hours are contributing to rising burnout rates, several companies are trialling a four-day workweek in an effort to improve employee wellbeing.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "İşyeri çalışmalarının, uzun çalışma saatlerinin artan tükenmişlik oranlarına katkıda bulunduğunu gösterdiği İsveç'te, birkaç şirket çalışan refahını artırmak amacıyla dört günlük çalışma haftasını deniyor."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "İsveç'te, birkaç şirketin dört günlük çalışma haftasını denemesinin ardından, uzun çalışma saatlerinin tükenmişlik oranlarını azalttığı ortaya çıkmıştır."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "İşyeri çalışmalarının, kısa çalışma saatlerinin artan tükenmişlik oranlarına katkıda bulunduğunu gösterdiği İsveç'te, birkaç şirket çalışan refahını artırmak amacıyla dört günlük çalışma haftasını deniyor."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "İşyeri çalışmalarının, uzun çalışma saatlerinin artan tükenmişlik oranlarına katkıda bulunduğunu gösterdiği İsveç'te, birkaç şirket çalışan refahını artırmak amacıyla dört günlük çalışma haftasını deniyor ve bu uygulama tüm ülkede zorunlu hâle getirilmiştir."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "İsveç'te birkaç şirket, çalışan refahını artırmak amacıyla dört günlük çalışma haftasını deniyor."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki istatistiksel veriyi, amaç ifadesini ve yapılan eylemi hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya değiştirmeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t68-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - PARTICIPLE CLAUSE + DEFINITION", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Held every August, the Edinburgh Fringe Festival unites performers from various artistic backgrounds to present shows ranging from comedy to experimental theatre.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Her Ağustos ayında düzenlenen Edinburgh Fringe Festivali, farklı sanatsal geçmişlere sahip sanatçıları komedi ile deneysel tiyatro arasında değişen gösteriler sunmak üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Her Aralık ayında düzenlenen Edinburgh Fringe Festivali, farklı sanatsal geçmişlere sahip sanatçıları komedi ile deneysel tiyatro arasında değişen gösteriler sunmak üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Her Ağustos ayında düzenlenen Edinburgh Fringe Festivali, yalnızca komedyenleri gösteriler sunmak üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Her Ağustos ayında düzenlenen Edinburgh Fringe Festivali, farklı sanatsal geçmişlere sahip sanatçıları komedi ile deneysel tiyatro arasında değişen gösteriler sunmak üzere bir araya getirir ve dünyanın en büyük sanat festivali olarak bilinir."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Farklı sanatsal geçmişlere sahip sanatçılar, gösterilerini sunmak amacıyla her Ağustos ayında düzenlenen Edinburgh Fringe Festivali'ni yönetir."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki sıklık, yer ve amaç bilgilerini hiçbir yönünü değiştirmeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: A."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t69-6", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - APPOSITIVE + REPORTED FINDING", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A new study examining the reasons for the decline of the Minoan civilization, one of the earliest advanced societies in Europe, has revealed that a massive volcanic eruption severely disrupted agriculture and trade across the region.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Avrupa'nın en erken gelişmiş toplumlarından biri olan Minos uygarlığının gerileme nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, büyük bir volkanik patlama bölgedeki tarımı ve ticareti ciddi şekilde aksattı."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Minos uygarlığının, tarımı ve ticareti geliştirmesinin ardından, Avrupa'nın en erken gelişmiş toplumlarından biri olan bu uygarlığın büyük bir volkanik patlamaya neden olduğu ortaya çıkmıştır."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Avrupa'nın en erken gelişmiş toplumlarından biri olan Minos uygarlığının gerileme nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, uzun süreli bir kuraklık bölgedeki tarımı ve ticareti ciddi şekilde aksattı."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Avrupa'nın en erken gelişmiş toplumlarından biri olan Minos uygarlığının gerileme nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, büyük bir volkanik patlama bölgedeki tarımı ve ticareti önemli ölçüde geliştirdi."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Avrupa'nın en erken gelişmiş toplumlarından biri olan Minos uygarlığının gerileme nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, büyük bir volkanik patlama bölgedeki tarımı ve ticareti ciddi şekilde aksattı ve bu uygarlığın tüm sanat eserleri günümüze kadar hiç zarar görmeden ulaştı."}], "dogru": "A", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki uygarlık, konum ve çöküş nedenini hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya bilgi eklemeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: A."}], "7": [{"id": "ydtozg9-g62-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (LANGUAGE FEATURES)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Finnish is often cited as one of the more challenging European languages for English speakers to learn, largely due to its extensive case system. Rather than relying on prepositions such as 'in', 'on', or 'from', Finnish attaches different endings directly to nouns to convey the same meaning. ---- The word talo, meaning 'house', can become talossa ('in the house') or talosta ('from the house') simply by changing its ending. With fifteen distinct cases in total, Finnish nouns can take on a remarkable number of different forms.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Finnish belongs to the Uralic language family, making it distantly related to Hungarian and Estonian."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "This system means that a single noun can appear in dozens of different forms depending on its grammatical role."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Finnish pronunciation is generally considered straightforward because words are spelled exactly as they sound."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Many Finnish compound words are formed by combining several shorter words into one long word."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Finland consistently ranks among the countries with the highest levels of English proficiency in Europe."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve sonraki cümledeki örneği doğru şekilde hazırlayan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-g63-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (BIOLOGICAL ADAPTATION)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The platypus is one of the very few mammals capable of producing venom, a trait more commonly associated with reptiles and insects. Male platypuses have a sharp spur on each hind leg connected to a venom gland, used primarily during competition with rival males. ---- Although rarely fatal to humans, a sting from this spur can cause intense, long-lasting pain that conventional painkillers often fail to relieve. Researchers continue to study this venom for potential insights into new pain-management treatments.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "This venom is used exclusively for capturing prey, rather than for any form of social or competitive behaviour."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "During the breeding season, males use this venomous spur in confrontations to establish dominance over one another."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Female platypuses also possess venomous spurs, which they use primarily to defend their young from predators."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "The venom produced by platypuses is generally considered far more dangerous to humans than most snake venom."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Platypus venom has already been fully developed into a widely available commercial pain medication."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve sonraki cümleyle mantıksal olarak örtüşen tek seçenek budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t64-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - RELATIVE CLAUSE + DOUBLE RESULT", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Unlike what many people assume, the narwhal's long spiral tusk is not a horn but an elongated tooth, which grows through the upper lip and can reach lengths of over two metres.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Pek çok insanın varsaydığının aksine, narvalın uzun spiral dişi bir boynuz değil, uzamış bir dişten ibarettir; ancak bu diş üst dudaktan değil alt çenenin içinden büyür ve iki metreyi aşan uzunluklara ulaşabilir."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Pek çok insanın varsaydığının aksine, narvalın uzun spiral dişi bir boynuz değil, uzamış bir diştir; bu diş üst dudaktan büyür ve iki metreyi aşan uzunluklara ulaşabilir."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Narvalın uzun spiral dişi, pek çok insanın varsaydığı gibi bir boynuzdur ve üst dudaktan büyüyerek iki metreyi aşan uzunluklara ulaşabilir."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Pek çok insanın varsaydığının aksine, narvalın uzun spiral dişi uzamış bir diştir; bu diş üst dudaktan büyür ve genellikle bir metreyi geçmeyen uzunluklara ulaşır."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Narvalın uzun spiral dişinin bir boynuz değil, uzamış bir diş olması, onu diğer balina türlerinden ayıran tek özelliktir ve üst dudaktan büyüyerek iki metreyi aşabilir."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki tüm bilgileri (karşılaştırma, sonuç ve ek detay) hiçbir ekleme ya da çıkarma yapmadan doğru şekilde aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t65-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - HISTORICAL ORIGIN + EPONYM", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Pizza Margherita became popular in Italy after a Neapolitan chef created the dish in honour of Queen Margherita during a royal visit to Naples.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Napoli'li bir şef, kraliçe Margherita'nın onuruna Napoli'ye yapılan bir kraliyet ziyareti sırasında pizza Margherita'yı yaratmış, ancak bu yemek İtalya'da hiçbir zaman popüler olmamıştır."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Pizza Margherita, Napoli'li bir şefin kraliçe Margherita'nın onuruna Napoli'ye yapılan bir kraliyet ziyareti sırasında bu yemeği yaratmasının ardından İtalya'da popüler hâle geldi."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Kraliçe Margherita, Napoli'ye yaptığı bir ziyaret sırasında pizza Margherita'yı bizzat yarattığı için bu yemek İtalya'da popüler hâle geldi."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Pizza Margherita, bir Roma'lı şefin kraliçe Margherita'nın onuruna Roma'ya yapılan bir kraliyet ziyareti sırasında bu yemeği yaratmasının ardından İtalya'da popüler hâle geldi."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Pizza Margherita, Napoli'li bir şefin kraliçe Margherita'nın onuruna Napoli'ye yapılan bir kraliyet ziyareti sırasında bu yemeği yaratmasının ardından tüm dünyada yasaklanmıştır."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki kişi, olay ve sonucu hiçbir ekleme, çıkarma ya da yer/tarih değişikliği yapmadan doğru şekilde aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t66-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - CHAIN OF CAUSATION", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Cigarette smoke introduces carbon monoxide into the bloodstream, which in turn reduces the oxygen available to tissues and accelerates cellular damage.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Sigara dumanı, kan dolaşımına oksijen sokar; bu da dokulara ulaşan karbon monoksit miktarını azaltır ve hücresel hasarı yavaşlatır."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Sigara dumanı, kan dolaşımına karbon monoksit sokar; bu da dokulara ulaşan oksijen miktarını azaltır ve hücresel hasarı hızlandırır."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Dokulara ulaşan oksijenin azalması, sigara dumanının kan dolaşımına karbon monoksit sokmasına neden olur ve bu da hücresel hasarı hızlandırır."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Sigara dumanı, kan dolaşımına karbon monoksit sokar; bu da dokulara ulaşan oksijen miktarını azaltır, hücresel hasarı hızlandırır ve akciğer kapasitesini tamamen iyileştirir."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Sigara dumanı, dokulara ulaşan oksijen miktarını doğrudan azaltarak hücresel hasarı hızlandırır."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki nedensellik zincirini (X, Y'ye yol açar; bu da Z'yi tetikler) hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya bilgi eklemeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t67-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - EMBEDDED CLAUSE + STATISTICS + PURPOSE", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "In Germany, where environmental reports indicate that packaging waste has increased significantly over the past decade, lawmakers are introducing a new tax on single-use plastic in an effort to reduce pollution.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Çevre raporlarının, ambalaj atığının son on yılda önemli ölçüde azaldığını gösterdiği Almanya'da, yasa koyucular kirliliği azaltmak amacıyla tek kullanımlık plastiğe yeni bir vergi getiriyor."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Çevre raporlarının, ambalaj atığının son on yılda önemli ölçüde arttığını gösterdiği Almanya'da, yasa koyucular kirliliği azaltmak amacıyla tek kullanımlık plastiğe yeni bir vergi getiriyor."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Almanya'da, yasa koyucuların tek kullanımlık plastiğe yeni bir vergi getirmesinin ardından, ambalaj atığının son on yılda önemli ölçüde arttığı ortaya çıkmıştır."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Çevre raporlarının, ambalaj atığının son on yılda önemli ölçüde arttığını gösterdiği Almanya'da, yasa koyucular kirliliği azaltmak amacıyla tek kullanımlık plastiğe yeni bir vergi getiriyor ve bu vergi tüm plastik üretimini tamamen durdurmuştur."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Almanya'da yasa koyucular, kirliliği azaltmak amacıyla tek kullanımlık plastiğe yeni bir vergi getiriyor."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki istatistiksel veriyi, amaç ifadesini ve yapılan eylemi hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya değiştirmeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t68-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - PARTICIPLE CLAUSE + DEFINITION", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Held every January in Davos, the World Economic Forum brings together political leaders and business executives to discuss pressing global economic issues.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Her Ocak ayında Cenevre'de düzenlenen Dünya Ekonomik Forumu, siyasi liderleri ve iş dünyası yöneticilerini acil küresel ekonomik meseleleri tartışmak üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Her Ocak ayında Davos'ta düzenlenen Dünya Ekonomik Forumu, siyasi liderleri ve iş dünyası yöneticilerini acil küresel ekonomik meseleleri tartışmak üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Her Temmuz ayında Davos'ta düzenlenen Dünya Ekonomik Forumu, siyasi liderleri ve iş dünyası yöneticilerini acil küresel ekonomik meseleleri tartışmak üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Her Ocak ayında Davos'ta düzenlenen Dünya Ekonomik Forumu, siyasi liderleri ve iş dünyası yöneticilerini acil küresel ekonomik meseleleri tartışmak üzere bir araya getirir ve bu toplantılarda bağlayıcı kararlar alınır."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Siyasi liderler ve iş dünyası yöneticileri, küresel ekonomik meseleleri tartışmak amacıyla her Ocak ayında Davos'ta düzenlenen Dünya Ekonomik Forumu'nu yönetir."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki sıklık, yer ve amaç bilgilerini hiçbir yönünü değiştirmeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: B."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t69-7", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - APPOSITIVE + REPORTED FINDING", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A new study examining the reasons for the collapse of the Mycenaean civilization, one of the dominant powers in the Bronze Age Aegean, has revealed that a combination of earthquakes and internal conflict weakened its major palace centres.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Tunç Çağı Ege'sindeki hâkim güçlerden biri olan Miken uygarlığının çöküşünün ardından, depremlerin ve iç çatışmaların büyük saray merkezlerini güçlendirdiği ortaya çıkmıştır."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Tunç Çağı Ege'sindeki hâkim güçlerden biri olan Miken uygarlığının çöküş nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, depremler ve iç çatışmaların bir arada yaşanması büyük saray merkezlerini zayıflattı."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Tunç Çağı Ege'sindeki hâkim güçlerden biri olan Miken uygarlığının çöküş nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, dış istilalar tek başına büyük saray merkezlerini zayıflattı."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Tunç Çağı Ege'sindeki hâkim güçlerden biri olan Miken uygarlığının çöküş nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, depremler ve iç çatışmaların bir arada yaşanması büyük saray merkezlerinin yeniden inşasını hızlandırdı."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Tunç Çağı Ege'sindeki hâkim güçlerden biri olan Miken uygarlığının çöküş nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, depremler ve iç çatışmaların bir arada yaşanması büyük saray merkezlerini zayıflattı ve bu merkezlerin tamamı günümüze kadar hasarsız ulaştı."}], "dogru": "B", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki uygarlık, konum ve çöküş nedenini hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya bilgi eklemeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: B."}], "8": [{"id": "ydtozg9-g62-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (LANGUAGE FEATURES)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Arabic vocabulary is built around a system of three-letter roots, with each root carrying a core meaning that branches out into a whole family of related words. The root k-t-b, for example, relates to the general concept of writing. ---- From this same root come kitab, meaning 'book', maktaba, meaning 'library', and kaatib, meaning 'writer'. Once learners grasp a root's core meaning, they can often guess the meaning of dozens of related words they have never encountered before.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Arabic is written from right to left, unlike most European languages, which are written left to right."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Classical Arabic differs considerably from the various spoken dialects used across the Arab world today."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "By adding different patterns of vowels and additional letters to this root, entirely new but related words can be formed."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Arabic calligraphy is considered a highly respected art form throughout much of the Islamic world."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Arabic has influenced the vocabulary of many other languages, including Spanish, Persian, and Urdu."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve sonraki cümledeki örneği doğru şekilde hazırlayan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-g63-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (BIOLOGICAL ADAPTATION)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The bombardier beetle possesses one of the most sophisticated chemical defence systems in the insect world. When threatened, it mixes two separate chemical compounds stored in internal glands, triggering a rapid reaction inside a specialised chamber. ---- The resulting mixture reaches near-boiling temperatures and is expelled explosively toward the attacker, often accompanied by an audible popping sound. This defence mechanism is effective enough to deter predators many times the beetle's own size.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "These two chemicals remain harmless and inert even after being combined within the beetle's body."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "The beetle stores only a single chemical compound, which becomes dangerous only after prolonged exposure to air."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "This reaction produces a scalding, irritating spray that the beetle can aim with surprising precision at a threat."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Bombardier beetles primarily rely on camouflage rather than any form of active chemical defence."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "The chemical reaction inside the beetle occurs slowly, taking several minutes to produce any noticeable effect."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve sonraki cümleyle mantıksal olarak örtüşen tek seçenek budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t64-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - RELATIVE CLAUSE + DOUBLE RESULT", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Unlike other cephalopods that mainly change colour, the mimic octopus can also alter the shape and movement of its body, which allows it to imitate other, more dangerous marine animals.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Diğer kafadanbacaklılardan farklı olarak, taklitçi ahtapot yalnızca rengini değiştirebilir; bu da onun daha tehlikeli deniz canlılarını taklit etmesini engeller."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Taklitçi ahtapot, çoğunlukla renk değiştiren diğer kafadanbacaklıların aksine yalnızca hareketini değiştirebilir; bu da onun daha tehlikeli deniz canlılarını taklit etmesini sağlar."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Çoğunlukla renk değiştiren diğer kafadanbacaklılardan farklı olarak, taklitçi ahtapot vücudunun şeklini ve hareketini de değiştirebilir; bu da onun daha tehlikeli diğer deniz canlılarını taklit etmesini sağlar."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Taklitçi ahtapot, diğer kafadanbacaklılardan farklı olarak vücudunun şeklini ve hareketini değiştirebilir; bu yetenek onu okyanuslardaki en zehirli deniz canlısı yapar."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Çoğunlukla renk değiştiren diğer kafadanbacaklıların aksine, taklitçi ahtapotun vücut şeklini değiştirmesi, onun avlarını daha hızlı yakalamasını sağlar."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki tüm bilgileri (karşılaştırma, sonuç ve ek detay) hiçbir ekleme ya da çıkarma yapmadan doğru şekilde aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t65-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - HISTORICAL ORIGIN + EPONYM", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The Christmas tree tradition became widespread in Britain after Prince Albert, the German-born husband of Queen Victoria, introduced the custom to the royal household.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Noel ağacı geleneği, Kraliçe Victoria'nın Almanya doğumlu eşi Prens Albert'in bu geleneği İngiliz halkına değil yalnızca kraliyet ailesine tanıtmasının ardından Britanya'da tamamen unutulmuştur."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Prens Albert, Noel ağacı geleneğini kraliyet hanesine tanıttığı için Kraliçe Victoria ile evlenmiştir."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Noel ağacı geleneği, Kraliçe Victoria'nın Almanya doğumlu eşi Prens Albert'in bu geleneği kraliyet hanesine tanıtmasının ardından Britanya'da yaygınlaştı."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Noel ağacı geleneği, Kraliçe Victoria'nın Fransa doğumlu eşi Prens Albert'in bu geleneği kraliyet hanesine tanıtmasının ardından Britanya'da yaygınlaştı."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Noel ağacı geleneği, Kraliçe Victoria'nın kendisinin bu geleneği kraliyet hanesine tanıtmasının ardından Britanya'da yaygınlaştı."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki kişi, olay ve sonucu hiçbir ekleme, çıkarma ya da yer/tarih değişikliği yapmadan doğru şekilde aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t66-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - CHAIN OF CAUSATION", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Prolonged exposure to loud noise damages the delicate hair cells of the inner ear, which in turn causes gradual hearing loss and can trigger persistent ringing in the ears.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Yüksek sese uzun süre maruz kalmak, iç kulaktaki hassas tüy hücrelerini güçlendirir; bu da işitmeyi keskinleştirir ve kulak çınlamasını tamamen ortadan kaldırır."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Kademeli işitme kaybı, yüksek sese uzun süre maruz kalmanın iç kulaktaki tüy hücrelerine zarar vermesine neden olur ve bu da kulak çınlamasını tetikleyebilir."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Yüksek sese uzun süre maruz kalmak, iç kulaktaki hassas tüy hücrelerine zarar verir; bu da kademeli işitme kaybına yol açar ve kalıcı kulak çınlamasını tetikleyebilir."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Yüksek sese uzun süre maruz kalmak, iç kulaktaki hassas tüy hücrelerine zarar verir; bu da kademeli işitme kaybına yol açar, kulak çınlamasını tetikleyebilir ve denge duyusunu tamamen iyileştirir."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Yüksek sese uzun süre maruz kalmak, kademeli işitme kaybına doğrudan yol açarak kulak çınlamasını tetikleyebilir."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki nedensellik zincirini (X, Y'ye yol açar; bu da Z'yi tetikler) hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya bilgi eklemeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t67-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - EMBEDDED CLAUSE + STATISTICS + PURPOSE", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "In New Zealand, where health surveys show that youth anxiety rates have risen sharply in recent years, the government is funding free counselling sessions in schools in an effort to support students' mental health.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Sağlık anketlerinin, gençlerdeki kaygı oranlarının son yıllarda keskin bir şekilde düştüğünü gösterdiği Yeni Zelanda'da, hükûmet okullarda ücretsiz danışmanlık seansları için fon sağlıyor."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Yeni Zelanda'da, hükûmetin okullarda ücretsiz danışmanlık seansları için fon sağlamasının ardından, gençlerdeki kaygı oranlarının keskin bir şekilde yükseldiği ortaya çıkmıştır."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Sağlık anketlerinin, gençlerdeki kaygı oranlarının son yıllarda keskin bir şekilde yükseldiğini gösterdiği Yeni Zelanda'da, hükûmet öğrencilerin ruh sağlığını desteklemek amacıyla okullarda ücretsiz danışmanlık seansları için fon sağlıyor."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Sağlık anketlerinin, gençlerdeki kaygı oranlarının son yıllarda keskin bir şekilde yükseldiğini gösterdiği Yeni Zelanda'da, hükûmet öğrencilerin ruh sağlığını desteklemek amacıyla okullarda ücretsiz danışmanlık seansları için fon sağlıyor ve kaygı sorunu tamamen ortadan kalkmıştır."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Yeni Zelanda'da hükûmet, öğrencilerin ruh sağlığını desteklemek amacıyla okullarda ücretsiz danışmanlık seansları için fon sağlıyor."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki istatistiksel veriyi, amaç ifadesini ve yapılan eylemi hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya değiştirmeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t68-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - PARTICIPLE CLAUSE + DEFINITION", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Held every year in Mecca, the Hajj pilgrimage brings together millions of Muslims from around the world to perform a series of religious rituals.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Her yıl Medine'de düzenlenen Hac ibadeti, dünyanın dört bir yanından milyonlarca Müslümanı bir dizi dini ritüeli gerçekleştirmek üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "İki yılda bir Mekke'de düzenlenen Hac ibadeti, dünyanın dört bir yanından milyonlarca Müslümanı bir dizi dini ritüeli gerçekleştirmek üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Her yıl Mekke'de düzenlenen Hac ibadeti, dünyanın dört bir yanından milyonlarca Müslümanı bir dizi dini ritüeli gerçekleştirmek üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Her yıl Mekke'de düzenlenen Hac ibadeti, dünyanın dört bir yanından milyonlarca Müslümanı bir dizi dini ritüeli gerçekleştirmek üzere bir araya getirir ve katılım için özel bir vize gerekmez."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Dünyanın dört bir yanından milyonlarca Müslüman, dini ritüelleri gerçekleştirmek amacıyla her yıl Mekke'de düzenlenen Hac ibadetini organize eder."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki sıklık, yer ve amaç bilgilerini hiçbir yönünü değiştirmeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: C."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t69-8", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - APPOSITIVE + REPORTED FINDING", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A new study examining the reasons for the abandonment of settlements by the Ancestral Puebloans, one of the most sophisticated cultures in the American Southwest, has revealed that a prolonged megadrought made large-scale farming unsustainable.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Amerikan Güneybatısı'ndaki en gelişmiş kültürlerden biri olan Ata Puebloların yerleşimlerini terk etmesinin ardından, uzun süreli bir mega kuraklığın büyük ölçekli tarımı sürdürülebilir hâle getirdiği ortaya çıkmıştır."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Amerikan Güneybatısı'ndaki en gelişmiş kültürlerden biri olan Ata Puebloların yerleşimlerini terk etme nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, ani bir sel büyük ölçekli tarımı sürdürülemez hâle getirdi."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Amerikan Güneybatısı'ndaki en gelişmiş kültürlerden biri olan Ata Puebloların yerleşimlerini terk etme nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, uzun süreli bir mega kuraklık büyük ölçekli tarımı sürdürülemez hâle getirdi."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Amerikan Güneybatısı'ndaki en gelişmiş kültürlerden biri olan Ata Puebloların yerleşimlerini terk etme nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, uzun süreli bir mega kuraklık büyük ölçekli tarımı önemli ölçüde geliştirdi."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Amerikan Güneybatısı'ndaki en gelişmiş kültürlerden biri olan Ata Puebloların yerleşimlerini terk etme nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, uzun süreli bir mega kuraklık büyük ölçekli tarımı sürdürülemez hâle getirdi ve bu kültür tüm izlerini kaybederek tarihten tamamen silindi."}], "dogru": "C", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki uygarlık, konum ve çöküş nedenini hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya bilgi eklemeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: C."}], "9": [{"id": "ydtozg9-g62-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (LANGUAGE FEATURES)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Japanese is unusual in that it regularly combines three distinct writing systems within a single sentence. Kanji, borrowed originally from Chinese characters, represents whole concepts or words, while hiragana and katakana are phonetic syllabaries used for grammatical elements and foreign loanwords respectively. ---- A single sentence might therefore include a kanji character for a noun, hiragana endings to show grammar, and katakana for a borrowed word such as 'coffee'. Balancing all three systems fluently takes most learners several years to master.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Kanji characters were originally adapted from Chinese script over a thousand years ago."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Hiragana is typically the first writing system taught to young Japanese children."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Katakana is most commonly associated with words borrowed from other languages, particularly English."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "This means that a single piece of writing often blends all three systems seamlessly, each serving a distinct grammatical purpose."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "There are thousands of kanji characters in total, though only around two thousand are used in everyday writing."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve sonraki cümledeki örneği doğru şekilde hazırlayan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-g63-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (BIOLOGICAL ADAPTATION)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Hagfish, ancient jawless fish found on the ocean floor, possess an extraordinary defence mechanism unlike that of almost any other animal. When grabbed or threatened by a predator, glands along their body release a substance that expands rapidly upon contact with seawater. ---- Within a fraction of a second, this substance can clog the gills of an attacking fish, forcing it to release the hagfish and retreat. Remarkably, the hagfish itself remains unaffected by its own slime despite being covered in it.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "This substance dissolves harmlessly in seawater without producing any noticeable physical effect."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Hagfish primarily use this substance to attract mates rather than to defend against predators."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "The slime produced by hagfish takes several hours to reach its full defensive thickness and effectiveness."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "This substance transforms into a thick, sticky slime capable of overwhelming a predator almost instantly."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Predators that encounter hagfish slime rarely experience any lasting effects and typically continue their attack unaffected."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve sonraki cümleyle mantıksal olarak örtüşen tek seçenek budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t64-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - RELATIVE CLAUSE + DOUBLE RESULT", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Unlike deciduous trees in temperate climates, the baobab tree drops its leaves during the dry season rather than in winter, which helps it conserve water and survive extended periods of drought.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Ilıman iklimlerdeki yaprak döken ağaçlardan farklı olarak, baobab ağacı yapraklarını kışın değil, kurak mevsimde döker; ancak bu durum su tasarrufunu engeller ve uzun kuraklık dönemlerinde hayatta kalmasını zorlaştırır."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Baobab ağacı, ılıman iklimlerdeki yaprak döken ağaçların aksine yapraklarını kurak mevsimde değil kış aylarında döker; bu da su tasarrufu yapmasını sağlar."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Ilıman iklimlerdeki yaprak döken ağaçlardan farklı olarak, baobab ağacının yapraklarını dökmesi yalnızca aşırı sıcaklarda gerçekleşir ve bu, onun su ihtiyacını tamamen ortadan kaldırır."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Ilıman iklimlerdeki yaprak döken ağaçlardan farklı olarak, baobab ağacı yapraklarını kışın değil kurak mevsimde döker; bu da su tasarrufu yapmasına ve uzun kuraklık dönemlerinde hayatta kalmasına yardımcı olur."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Baobab ağacı, yapraklarını kurak mevsimde döktüğü için ılıman iklimlerdeki yaprak döken ağaçlardan daha uzun yaşar."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki tüm bilgileri (karşılaştırma, sonuç ve ek detay) hiçbir ekleme ya da çıkarma yapmadan doğru şekilde aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t65-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - HISTORICAL ORIGIN + EPONYM", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The word shrapnel became a common military term after Henry Shrapnel, a British artillery officer, invented an explosive shell designed to scatter metal fragments.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Shrapnel kelimesi, İngiliz topçu subayı Henry Shrapnel'in metal parçaları etrafa saçacak şekilde tasarlanmış patlayıcı bir mermi icat etmesinin ardından yaygın bir askerî terim olmuş, ancak bu mermi hiçbir savaşta kullanılmamıştır."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Henry Shrapnel, metal parçaları etrafa saçacak şekilde tasarlanmış patlayıcı bir mermi icat ettiği için İngiliz ordusunda topçu subayı olarak göreve başlamıştır."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Shrapnel kelimesi, İngiliz topçu subayı Henry Shrapnel'in su geçirmez bir zırh tasarlamasının ardından yaygın bir askerî terim olmuştur."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Shrapnel kelimesi, İngiliz topçu subayı Henry Shrapnel'in metal parçaları etrafa saçacak şekilde tasarlanmış patlayıcı bir mermi icat etmesinin ardından yaygın bir askerî terim olmuştur."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Shrapnel kelimesi, Fransız topçu subayı Henry Shrapnel'in metal parçaları etrafa saçacak şekilde tasarlanmış patlayıcı bir mermi icat etmesinin ardından yaygın bir askerî terim olmuştur."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki kişi, olay ve sonucu hiçbir ekleme, çıkarma ya da yer/tarih değişikliği yapmadan doğru şekilde aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t66-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - CHAIN OF CAUSATION", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Regularly consuming excessive sugar causes repeated spikes in blood glucose, which in turn promotes insulin resistance and raises the risk of developing type 2 diabetes.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Düzenli olarak aşırı şeker tüketmek, kan şekerinde tekrarlayan düşüşlere neden olur; bu da insülin duyarlılığını artırır ve tip 2 diyabet riskini azaltır."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "İnsülin direncinin artması, düzenli olarak aşırı şeker tüketmenin kan şekerinde tekrarlayan yükselmelere neden olmasına yol açar ve bu da tip 2 diyabet riskini artırır."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Düzenli olarak aşırı şeker tüketmek, kan şekerinde tekrarlayan yükselmelere neden olur; bu da insülin direncini azaltır ve tip 2 diyabet riskini düşürür."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Düzenli olarak aşırı şeker tüketmek, kan şekerinde tekrarlayan yükselmelere neden olur; bu da insülin direncini artırır ve tip 2 diyabet geliştirme riskini yükseltir."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Düzenli olarak aşırı şeker tüketmek, insülin direncini doğrudan artırarak tip 2 diyabet riskini yükseltir."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki nedensellik zincirini (X, Y'ye yol açar; bu da Z'yi tetikler) hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya bilgi eklemeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t67-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - EMBEDDED CLAUSE + STATISTICS + PURPOSE", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "In Singapore, where official reports indicate that natural freshwater resources cover only a small fraction of national demand, authorities are expanding water recycling programmes in an effort to secure long-term supply.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Resmî raporların, doğal tatlı su kaynaklarının ulusal talebin büyük bir kısmını karşıladığını belirttiği Singapur'da, yetkililer uzun vadeli arzı güvence altına almak amacıyla su geri dönüşüm programlarını genişletiyor."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Singapur'da, yetkililerin su geri dönüşüm programlarını genişletmesinin ardından, doğal tatlı su kaynaklarının ulusal talebin yalnızca küçük bir kısmını karşıladığı ortaya çıkmıştır."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Resmî raporların, doğal tatlı su kaynaklarının ulusal talebin yalnızca küçük bir kısmını karşıladığını belirttiği Singapur'da, yetkililer su tüketimini artırmak amacıyla su geri dönüşüm programlarını sınırlandırıyor."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Resmî raporların, doğal tatlı su kaynaklarının ulusal talebin yalnızca küçük bir kısmını karşıladığını belirttiği Singapur'da, yetkililer uzun vadeli arzı güvence altına almak amacıyla su geri dönüşüm programlarını genişletiyor."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Singapur'da yetkililer, uzun vadeli arzı güvence altına almak amacıyla su geri dönüşüm programlarını genişletiyor."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki istatistiksel veriyi, amaç ifadesini ve yapılan eylemi hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya değiştirmeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t68-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - PARTICIPLE CLAUSE + DEFINITION", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Held every July, the Tour de France unites professional cyclists from around the world to compete across a demanding multi-stage race.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Her Temmuz ayında düzenlenen Tour de France, dünyanın dört bir yanından amatör bisikletçileri zorlu, çok etaplı bir yarışta yarışmak üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Her Mart ayında düzenlenen Tour de France, dünyanın dört bir yanından profesyonel bisikletçileri zorlu, çok etaplı bir yarışta yarışmak üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "İki yılda bir düzenlenen Tour de France, dünyanın dört bir yanından profesyonel bisikletçileri zorlu, çok etaplı bir yarışta yarışmak üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Her Temmuz ayında düzenlenen Tour de France, dünyanın dört bir yanından profesyonel bisikletçileri zorlu, çok etaplı bir yarışta yarışmak üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Dünyanın dört bir yanından profesyonel bisikletçiler, zorlu bir yarışta yarışmak amacıyla her Temmuz ayında düzenlenen Tour de France'ı organize eder."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki sıklık, yer ve amaç bilgilerini hiçbir yönünü değiştirmeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: D."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t69-9", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - APPOSITIVE + REPORTED FINDING", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A new study examining the reasons for the disappearance of the Norse colony in Greenland, one of the westernmost settlements of medieval Europe, has revealed that a shift toward a colder climate undermined their farming-based economy.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Orta Çağ Avrupası'nın en batıdaki yerleşimlerinden biri olan Grönland'daki İskandinav kolonisinin ortadan kaybolmasının ardından, daha soğuk bir iklime kaymanın tarım temelli ekonomiyi güçlendirdiği ortaya çıkmıştır."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Orta Çağ Avrupası'nın en batıdaki yerleşimlerinden biri olan Grönland'daki İskandinav kolonisinin ortadan kaybolma nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, ani bir salgın hastalık tarım temelli ekonomiyi zayıflattı."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Orta Çağ Avrupası'nın en batıdaki yerleşimlerinden biri olan Grönland'daki İskandinav kolonisinin ortadan kaybolma nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, daha soğuk bir iklime kayma tarım temelli ekonomiyi önemli ölçüde güçlendirdi."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Orta Çağ Avrupası'nın en batıdaki yerleşimlerinden biri olan Grönland'daki İskandinav kolonisinin ortadan kaybolma nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, daha soğuk bir iklime kayma tarım temelli ekonomiyi zayıflattı."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Orta Çağ Avrupası'nın en batıdaki yerleşimlerinden biri olan Grönland'daki İskandinav kolonisinin ortadan kaybolma nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, daha soğuk bir iklime kayma tarım temelli ekonomiyi zayıflattı ve bu koloniden hiçbir arkeolojik kalıntı günümüze ulaşmamıştır."}], "dogru": "D", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki uygarlık, konum ve çöküş nedenini hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya bilgi eklemeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: D."}], "10": [{"id": "ydtozg9-g62-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (LANGUAGE FEATURES)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Basque, spoken in parts of northern Spain and southwestern France, is considered a language isolate, meaning it has no known relationship to any other living language. Unlike its Indo-European neighbours, Basque did not evolve from Latin or any shared ancestor, making its origins a long-standing mystery among linguists. ---- Its grammar also follows an unusual pattern, marking whether a verb's subject is acting upon something or simply existing in a state. This combination of mystery and structural uniqueness has made Basque one of the most studied minority languages in Europe.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Basque is spoken by roughly one million people across a region historically known as the Basque Country."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Many place names throughout northern Spain retain traces of ancient Basque origin."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "The Basque people have maintained a distinct cultural identity for many centuries within the Iberian Peninsula."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Basque has borrowed a number of words from neighbouring Spanish and French over the centuries."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Researchers have proposed numerous theories linking Basque to ancient languages, though none have been conclusively proven."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve sonraki cümledeki örneği doğru şekilde hazırlayan tek seçenek budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-g63-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "PARAGRAPH GAP-FILL (BIOLOGICAL ADAPTATION)", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Tardigrades, microscopic creatures often called water bears, are famous for their extraordinary ability to survive conditions that would be lethal to nearly every other form of life. When faced with extreme dehydration, they can expel almost all of the water in their bodies and enter a dormant state known as cryptobiosis. ---- In this state, tardigrades have survived exposure to temperatures near absolute zero, intense radiation, and even the vacuum of outer space. Once conditions improve and water becomes available again, they can rehydrate and resume normal biological function within hours.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "During cryptobiosis, tardigrades continue to move and feed normally, showing no outward signs of dormancy."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Tardigrades are unable to survive any significant loss of water, making dehydration one of the greatest threats to their survival."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Once a tardigrade enters cryptobiosis, it can never return to normal biological activity again."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Cryptobiosis in tardigrades has only ever been observed under carefully controlled laboratory conditions."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "In this remarkably resilient state, their metabolism slows to nearly undetectable levels, allowing them to endure extreme environments."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "Parçadaki anlam bütünlüğünü sağlayan ve sonraki cümleyle mantıksal olarak örtüşen tek seçenek budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t64-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - RELATIVE CLAUSE + DOUBLE RESULT", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Unlike what most people expect, many orb-weaving spiders consume their old web every day, which allows them to recycle the silk proteins and build a fresh web each night.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Pek çok insanın beklediğinin aksine, birçok yuvarlak ağ ören örümcek eski ağını her gün yer; ancak bu, ipek proteinlerini geri dönüştürmesini engeller ve her gece yeni bir ağ örmesini zorlaştırır."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Birçok yuvarlak ağ ören örümcek, pek çok insanın beklediğinin aksine eski ağını haftada bir kez yer; bu da ipek proteinlerini geri dönüştürmesini sağlar."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Pek çok insanın beklediğinin aksine, birçok yuvarlak ağ ören örümceğin eski ağını yemesi, onu diğer örümcek türlerinden daha güçlü kılar."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Birçok yuvarlak ağ ören örümcek, eski ağını her gün yediği için pek çok insanın beklediğinin aksine yeni ağ örmeyi bırakır."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Pek çok insanın beklediğinin aksine, birçok yuvarlak ağ ören örümcek eski ağını her gün yer; bu da ipek proteinlerini geri dönüştürmesini ve her gece yeni bir ağ örmesini sağlar."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki tüm bilgileri (karşılaştırma, sonuç ve ek detay) hiçbir ekleme ya da çıkarma yapmadan doğru şekilde aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t65-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - HISTORICAL ORIGIN + EPONYM", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "The Braille reading system became widely adopted after Louis Braille, a blind French teenager, developed a method of representing letters using raised dots.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Braille okuma sistemi, kör bir Fransız genci olan Louis Braille'in harfleri kabartma noktalarla temsil eden bir yöntem geliştirmesinin ardından yaygın olarak benimsenmiş, ancak günümüzde artık kullanılmamaktadır."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Louis Braille, harfleri kabartma noktalarla temsil eden bir yöntem geliştirdiği için kör olmuştur."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Braille okuma sistemi, gören bir Fransız genci olan Louis Braille'in harfleri kabartma noktalarla temsil eden bir yöntem geliştirmesinin ardından yaygın olarak benimsenmiştir."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Braille okuma sistemi, kör bir İngiliz genci olan Louis Braille'in harfleri kabartma noktalarla temsil eden bir yöntem geliştirmesinin ardından yaygın olarak benimsenmiştir."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Braille okuma sistemi, kör bir Fransız genci olan Louis Braille'in harfleri kabartma noktalarla temsil eden bir yöntem geliştirmesinin ardından yaygın olarak benimsenmiştir."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki kişi, olay ve sonucu hiçbir ekleme, çıkarma ya da yer/tarih değişikliği yapmadan doğru şekilde aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t66-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - CHAIN OF CAUSATION", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Long-term exposure to air pollution inflames the tissue of the lungs, which in turn reduces the efficiency of oxygen exchange and increases the risk of respiratory disease.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Hava kirliliğine uzun süre maruz kalmak, akciğer dokusunu iyileştirir; bu da oksijen değişiminin verimliliğini artırır ve solunum hastalığı riskini azaltır."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Solunum hastalığı riskinin artması, hava kirliliğine uzun süre maruz kalmanın akciğer dokusunu iltihaplandırmasına neden olur ve bu da oksijen değişiminin verimliliğini azaltır."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Hava kirliliğine uzun süre maruz kalmak, akciğer dokusunu iltihaplandırır; bu da oksijen değişiminin verimliliğini artırır ve solunum hastalığı riskini azaltır."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Hava kirliliğine uzun süre maruz kalmak, akciğer dokusunu iltihaplandırır; bu da oksijen değişiminin verimliliğini azaltır, solunum hastalığı riskini artırır ve bağışıklık sistemini tamamen güçlendirir."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Hava kirliliğine uzun süre maruz kalmak, akciğer dokusunu iltihaplandırır; bu da oksijen değişiminin verimliliğini azaltır ve solunum hastalığı riskini artırır."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki nedensellik zincirini (X, Y'ye yol açar; bu da Z'yi tetikler) hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya bilgi eklemeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t67-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - EMBEDDED CLAUSE + STATISTICS + PURPOSE", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "In Canada, where public health data shows that opioid-related deaths have increased substantially over the past five years, several cities are opening supervised injection sites in an effort to reduce fatal overdoses.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Halk sağlığı verilerinin, opioid kaynaklı ölümlerin son beş yılda önemli ölçüde azaldığını gösterdiği Kanada'da, birkaç şehir denetimli enjeksiyon merkezleri açıyor."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Kanada'da, birkaç şehrin denetimli enjeksiyon merkezleri açmasının ardından, opioid kaynaklı ölümlerin son beş yılda önemli ölçüde arttığı ortaya çıkmıştır."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Halk sağlığı verilerinin, opioid kaynaklı ölümlerin son beş yılda önemli ölçüde arttığını gösterdiği Kanada'da, birkaç şehir ölümcül doz alımlarını artırmak amacıyla denetimli enjeksiyon merkezleri kapatıyor."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Halk sağlığı verilerinin, opioid kaynaklı ölümlerin son beş yılda önemli ölçüde arttığını gösterdiği Kanada'da, birkaç şehir ölümcül doz alımlarını azaltmak amacıyla denetimli enjeksiyon merkezleri açıyor ve opioid krizi tamamen sona ermiştir."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Halk sağlığı verilerinin, opioid kaynaklı ölümlerin son beş yılda önemli ölçüde arttığını gösterdiği Kanada'da, birkaç şehir ölümcül doz alımlarını azaltmak amacıyla denetimli enjeksiyon merkezleri açıyor."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki istatistiksel veriyi, amaç ifadesini ve yapılan eylemi hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya değiştirmeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t68-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - PARTICIPLE CLAUSE + DEFINITION", "seviye": "orta", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "Held every year in the Nevada desert, the Burning Man festival brings together artists and free spirits from around the world to build a temporary community centred on creativity.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Her yıl Arizona çölünde düzenlenen Burning Man festivali, dünyanın dört bir yanından sanatçıları ve özgür ruhları yaratıcılık odaklı geçici bir topluluk kurmak üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "İki yılda bir Nevada çölünde düzenlenen Burning Man festivali, dünyanın dört bir yanından sanatçıları ve özgür ruhları yaratıcılık odaklı geçici bir topluluk kurmak üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Her yıl Nevada çölünde düzenlenen Burning Man festivali, yalnızca profesyonel sanatçıları yaratıcılık odaklı geçici bir topluluk kurmak üzere bir araya getirir."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Her yıl Nevada çölünde düzenlenen Burning Man festivali, dünyanın dört bir yanından sanatçıları ve özgür ruhları yaratıcılık odaklı geçici bir topluluk kurmak üzere bir araya getirir ve etkinlik sonunda kalıcı bir yerleşim inşa edilir."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Her yıl Nevada çölünde düzenlenen Burning Man festivali, dünyanın dört bir yanından sanatçıları ve özgür ruhları yaratıcılık odaklı geçici bir topluluk kurmak üzere bir araya getirir."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki sıklık, yer ve amaç bilgilerini hiçbir yönünü değiştirmeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: E."}, {"id": "ydtozg9-t69-10", "ders": "ydtIngilizce", "konu": "TRANSLATION (ENG-TUR) - APPOSITIVE + REPORTED FINDING", "seviye": "zor", "kaynak": "özgün", "metin": "A new study examining the reasons for the decline of Cahokia, one of the largest pre-Columbian settlements north of Mexico, has revealed that repeated flooding combined with resource depletion strained the city's ability to sustain its population.", "siklar": [{"harf": "A", "metin": "Meksika'nın kuzeyindeki Kolomb öncesi en büyük yerleşimlerden biri olan Cahokia'nın gerilemesinin ardından, tekrarlanan sellerin ve kaynak tükenmesinin şehrin nüfusunu artırdığı ortaya çıkmıştır."}, {"harf": "B", "metin": "Meksika'nın kuzeyindeki Kolomb öncesi en büyük yerleşimlerden biri olan Cahokia'nın gerileme nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, tek bir büyük yangın şehrin nüfusunu sürdürme kapasitesini zorladı."}, {"harf": "C", "metin": "Meksika'nın kuzeyindeki Kolomb öncesi en büyük yerleşimlerden biri olan Cahokia'nın gerileme nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, tekrarlanan seller ve kaynak tükenmesi şehrin nüfusunu artırma kapasitesini geliştirdi."}, {"harf": "D", "metin": "Meksika'nın kuzeyindeki Kolomb öncesi en büyük yerleşimlerden biri olan Cahokia'nın gerileme nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, tekrarlanan seller ve kaynak tükenmesi şehrin nüfusunu sürdürme kapasitesini zorladı ve şehir bir gecede tamamen terk edildi."}, {"harf": "E", "metin": "Meksika'nın kuzeyindeki Kolomb öncesi en büyük yerleşimlerden biri olan Cahokia'nın gerileme nedenlerini inceleyen yeni bir araştırmaya göre, tekrarlanan seller ve kaynak tükenmesi şehrin nüfusunu sürdürme kapasitesini zorladı."}], "dogru": "E", "aciklama": "İngilizce cümledeki uygarlık, konum ve çöküş nedenini hiçbir yönünü tersine çevirmeden veya bilgi eklemeden aktaran tek çeviri budur. Cevap: E."}]};
